          "content": {
            "mimeType": "application/json",
            "text": "[{\"description\":\"Thursdays 7.15 - 9.15pm, online, £220 for the course\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":120,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\" Hebrew Advanced 1 with Ronit First-Kavisky [Online]\",\"instanceDates\":\"8 January-26 March\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"575201ABKCSTLVSCLKGDJPKMPPDRLNPLR\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-01-08T19:15:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-01-08T19:15:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-03-26T19:15:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-03-26T19:15:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Languages\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Languages\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"Ronit First-Kavisky\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false},{\"description\":\"Mondays, 7.15pm-9.15pm, £220, online // \",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":120,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\" Hebrew Intermediate 3 (Term 2) with Reuven Vazan [Online]\",\"instanceDates\":\"5 October-5 October\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"647401ACTSRNDDMMTBBCVLJTKHGMKVJJQ\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-10-05T19:15:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-10-05T18:15:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-10-05T19:15:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-10-05T18:15:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false,\"attribute_Genre\":\"Languages\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"True\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Languages\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"Reuven Vazan\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"10am-12noon, free, in building // 18+ // Are you looking for a new job but unsure how to stand out in today’s competitive market?\\r\\n\\r\\nJoin Resource’s interactive free workshop at JW3 on Thursday, 05 March 2026 from 10am - 12pm and gain the skills and confidence to take your job search to the next level. In this engaging session, their experts with over 33 years of experience will guide you through:\\r\\nCrafting a standout CV and covering letter\\r\\nSharpening your interview techniques to impress employers\\r\\nMastering networking to open doors\\r\\nWhether you’re just starting your job search or looking to refine your approach, this workshop will simplify the process and give you practical strategies you can apply immediately.\\r\\n \\r\\nWho should attend?\\r\\nAnyone looking for a job in the near future -  no age limit or prior experience required. All are welcome!\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":120,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\" Land Your Next Job: Expert Tips on CVs, Networking & Interviews\",\"instanceDates\":\"5 March-5 March\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"585601AKRNLNMGNDHPVVKTQJNNDPNNPPP\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-03-05T10:00:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-03-05T10:00:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-03-05T10:00:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-03-05T10:00:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Talks & Discussions\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false},{\"description\":\"7-8.45pm, building, £18 // Be part of history as the London Jewish Male Choir begins its 100th-anniversary celebrations! \\r\\nEstablished in the heart of London's East End in 1926, the LJMC is a living legacy, proudly holding its place as one of the oldest continuously performing Jewish choirs globally.\\r\\nFor a hundred years, their voices have resonated, bridging communities and entertaining audiences. The concert at JW3 is the grand opening of a year-long celebration, showcasing the very best of their past and present repertoire in a performance that tells the choir's remarkable story.\\r\\nPrepare for a delightful evening with a program that promises something for everyone: from powerful cantorial showcases and beloved musical theatre numbers to the timeless beauty of Yiddish song, the energy of Israeli folk music, and popular secular classics by celebrated Jewish composers.\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":105,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"100 Years of the London Jewish Male Choir\",\"instanceDates\":\"22 February-22 February\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"564601AGCLHRHBJSRHMHHVHQNRSQQHDQD\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-02-22T19:00:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-02-22T19:00:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-02-22T19:00:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-02-22T19:00:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Music\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Arts & Culture\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false},{\"description\":\"\\\"7.30pm-8.30pm, £15, in building, 16+, Wednesday 3 June 2026 // “Seasoned mischief-makers ensure that even the most hare-brained rule gets a fair (and funny) trial.” - **** One4Review\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nComedians put the world to rights - because somebody has to! - in the hit panel show and podcast, 101 Rules for a Better World (by Comedians).\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nFollowing a sold-out Edinburgh Fringe run, host Leslie Gold (as seen at the Comedy Store) and Producer Nick bring the show to JW3, inviting guest comedians to present ideas to improve the world - imagine the opposite of Room 101. It’s an interactive show with an audience vote to choose which rules are adopted - and which get the chop. \\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nThe result is often silly, occasionally profound, and always funny! \\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nComedian panellists to be announced soon - follow @101_rules_pod on Instagram for the latest news.\\\"\\r\\n\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":60,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"101 Rules for a Better World (by Comedians)\",\"instanceDates\":\"3 June-3 June\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"604001AKSKBKDDHTBVGGLMHSQHQJSSSPR\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-06-03T19:30:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-06-03T18:30:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-06-03T19:30:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-06-03T18:30:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Comedy\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Arts & Culture\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false},{\"description\":\"When David Hockney's beautiful lover, Peter Schlesinger, breaks up with him, it leaves David a complete emotional wreck. An artist, he suddenly finds himself unable to create anything, and is awash in depression and loneliness. After a time, David is able to find inspiration in his backyard swimming pool, and he begins a portrait of it. This unique docudrama presents a semi-fictionalized account of the story behind one of Hockney's most popular paintings. Duration: 101 minutes Rating: 15 Director: Jack Hazan Cast: David Hockney, Peter Schlesinger, Celia Birtwell Year: 1974 Language: English https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=m2sEkXKxQs8&pp=ygUdYSBiaWdnZXIgc3BsYXNoIGRhdmlkIGhvY2tuZXk%3D\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":106,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"A Bigger Splash\",\"instanceDates\":\"8 July-8 July\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"640601ABMCJDPRJQPMTSPSBDCLGJCMTCC\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-07-08T13:30:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-07-08T12:30:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-07-08T13:30:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-07-08T12:30:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false,\"attribute_Genre\":\"Cinema\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"7-8.30pm, building, £20 // Join Hayley Mills at JW3 for a fully illustrated in conversation with George McGhee and hear out all about her life’s journey.\\r\\n\\r\\nWinner of many awards including a special Oscar, Hayley Mills rose from child star in such classic films as Tiger Bay, Pollyanna, Whistle Down the Wind and The Parent Trap.\\r\\n\\r\\nShe later appeared on stage as J M Barrie’s Peter Pan, as Anna in The King & I, in Noel Coward's Two Keys and in Sondheim's A Little Night Music. She featured on TV in Good Morning Miss Bliss and Wild at Heart amongst many other performances.\\r\\n\\r\\nAs the youngest daughter of one of Britain's most distinguished actors, Sir John Mills, Hayley had to set her sights high to become Disney's biggest female star ever.\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":90,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"A Conversation with Hayley Mills\",\"instanceDates\":\"16 February-16 February\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"557201AGDKNRGHQVQSJVCJRTGKPDCHDPV\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-02-16T19:00:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-02-16T19:00:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-02-16T19:00:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-02-16T19:00:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Talks & Discussions\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Adult Education\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false},{\"description\":\"7.30pm-9pm, building only, £20 // Following three highly successful annual Cricketing Evenings at JW3, please join us for A Fourth Annual Cricket Evening  which Daniel Lightman will be in conversation with a panel including Mike Brearley OBE, who thrice captained England to Ashes victory and Test Match Special commentator Daniel Norcross.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nDaniel Lightman, co-author of Cricket Grounds from the Air, co-curated the first ever exhibition on Jews and Cricket at the MCC Museum, and his articles in Wisden, The Cricketer and Nightwatchman have revealed previously unknown stories of the lives of Jewish (and Jew-ish) cricketers.\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":90,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"A Fourth Annual Cricket Evening\",\"instanceDates\":\"18 May-18 May\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"593203AVNKSPRJLJBRMTRJGHLPNDHSCJB\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-05-18T19:30:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-05-18T18:30:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-05-18T19:30:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-05-18T18:30:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Talks & Discussions\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Adult Education\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false},{\"description\":\"10.30am-12.30pm, 3 & 10 February, £35 for both sessions, in building // \\r\\n\\r\\nDo you have a grandchild with autism? Would you like to understand more about autism and learn practical tools and strategies that can make an impact? If so, this 2 part-workshop, led by Norwood specialists, is for you. \\r\\n\\r\\nJoin us to learn about what autism is, how to support family members diagnosed with autism and meet other grandparents in a welcoming & supportive setting.  \\r\\n\\r\\nAbout Norwood:\\r\\n\\r\\nAt Norwood we provide a range of early intervention groups and services, specialist help and advice to children and families in the Jewish community and beyond. Our experienced team offers emotional, therapeutic and specialist advice and guidance. We provide a range of group and individual support to help parents manage supporting their children who may be neurodivergent or have learning disabilities. \\r\\n\\r\\nFOR WEBSITE: \\r\\n\\r\\nDo you have a grandchild with autism? Would you like to understand more about autism and learn practical tools and strategies that can make an impact? If so, this 2 part-workshop, led by Norwood specialists, is for you. \\r\\n\\r\\nKey topics will include: \\r\\n\\r\\nWhat is Autism? \\r\\n\\r\\nCommunication \\r\\n\\r\\nSensory needs \\r\\n\\r\\nEmotional regulation \\r\\n\\r\\nBuilding relationships as a supportive grandparent \\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nAbout Norwood \\r\\n\\r\\nAt Norwood we provide a range of early intervention groups and services, specialist help and advice to children and families in the Jewish community and beyond. Our experienced team offers emotional, therapeutic and specialist advice and guidance. We provide a range of group and individual support to help parents manage supporting their children who may be neurodivergent or have learning disabilities.\\r\\n\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":120,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"A Grandparent's Guide to Autism\",\"instanceDates\":\"3 February-10 February\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"563001ARHDMMBGKCQTQDLBBDTCDHJHVVT\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-02-03T10:30:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-02-03T10:30:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-02-10T10:30:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-02-10T10:30:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Classes & Courses\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"True\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Adult Education\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"Norwood\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false},{\"description\":\"7pm-9pm, £15, in building, age 13+, Monday 11 May 2026 // A life remembered through photographs. Presented by his grandson, journalist Darren Richman, A Life in 13 Pictures explores Holocaust survivor Zigi Shipper’s story through images that reveal the personal, the unexpected, and the extraordinary legacy he left behind.   Photographs have a unique power: they capture a single moment, yet hold entire lives within them.   In A Life in 13 Pictures, journalist Darren Richman presents the story of his late grandfather, Holocaust survivor Zigi Shipper, through thirteen carefully chosen images. Each photograph opens a window onto a moment in Zigi’s life, revealing personal, unexpected, and deeply human details behind a remarkable story of survival, rebuilding, and achievement.  The evening is shaped as a shared conversation. Alongside Darren, invited guests and contributors help bring these photographs to life, offering different perspectives on Zigi’s journey and the impact he had on those around him. Together, they reveal moments that are intimate, surprising, and deeply human, allowing us to see not only the history Zigi lived through, but the person he was. Through these images, we are offered a glimpse into a life marked by resilience, determination, and achievement, and into the enormous sweep of history embodied in one individual story.   A Life in 13 Pictures is both an act of remembrance and a celebration of a life lived with meaning.\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":90,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"A Life in 13 Pictures\",\"instanceDates\":\"11 May-11 May\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"595002AJPVVQCJQQJTPRDMLPRPDJGNGTL\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-05-11T19:00:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-05-11T18:00:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-05-11T19:00:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-05-11T18:00:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Talks & Discussions\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Holocaust Learning\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false},{\"description\":\"When renowned psychiatrist Lilian Steiner learns of the death of one of her patients, she is convinced it was murder and takes it upon herself to investigate… Duration: 107 minutes Rating: 15 Director: Rebecca Zlotowski Cast: Jodie Foster, Daniel Auteuil, Mathieu Amalric, Virginie Efira Year: 2025 Language: French Subtitles: English https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=2JabG5C6IU8\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":103,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"A Private Life\",\"instanceDates\":\"10 July-29 July\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"640801ALSHPSJKJPMCKLQKJDMBLCPQGBK\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-07-10T10:30:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-07-10T09:30:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-07-29T13:00:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-07-29T12:00:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false,\"attribute_Genre\":\"Cinema\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"11am-12noon, hybrid, £20 // On Easter Eve 1144 the dead body of a young skinner’s apprentice named William was found in a wood near Norwich. It was rumoured that he had been crucified by the Jewish community after synagogue service on the second day of Passover, in mockery of the  Passion of Jesus. Find out how this extraordinary story developed into an accusation which was to blight the Jews of Europe.\\r\\n\\r\\nJill Stern is an historian. Aged twenty she graduated with first class honours in History from King’s College London. Much of her working life was spent as a teacher at Wycombe Abbey School and as chairman of a Health Authority in West London and vice-chairman of North Thames Regional Health Authority. Returning to academic study she gained an MA (Distinction) and a doctorate in seventeenth century Dutch history at University College London.  \\r\\n\\r\\nAs a doctoral student she was awarded the prestigious Pollard Prize for History. She has a book and many published articles to her credit. She has lectured in Britain, the Netherlands and New York. History is her lifelong passion and she is keen to share that passion.\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":60,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"A Ritual Murder: Norwich 1144\",\"instanceDates\":\"25 March-25 March\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"560601AQBTQRCQKHQSSNKPTNVSRGNTSVS\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-03-25T11:00:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-03-25T11:00:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-03-25T11:00:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-03-25T11:00:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Talks & Discussions\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Adult Education\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"Jill Stern\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false},{\"description\":\"From the Coen Brothers, A Serious Man follows Larry Gopnik as he seeks advice from three rabbis to cope with his family life. //\\r\\n\\r\\nWith a filmed introduction by Richard Kind and in-conversation with Dr Julia Wagner and journalist Darren Richman, this is set to be a very special screening. // 15, 1h 46m\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":106,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"A Serious Man\",\"instanceDates\":\"16 August-16 August\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"627601ABTDGBMKVMLQTKQDSSLBKRRVTNC\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-08-16T18:00:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-08-16T17:00:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-08-16T18:00:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-08-16T17:00:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":true,\"attribute_Genre\":\"Cinema\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Coming of Age Film Season\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"11:00 // 18 Nov 2026 // £12 // Sleep is like an old friend I’ve not seen for a long time. She’s stopped returning my calls. But some nights feel sort of magic – just you and me, watching a new day being born.\\r\\nBlending drama and multi-sensory play in a relaxed, beautifully designed environment, this is a celebration of the wonder and challenges of new parenthood, with a guided Stay and Play session after the show. \\r\\nFor parents with babies aged 0–18 months. Supported by Arts Council England.\\r\\n\\r\\n\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":60,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"A Tale of Us\",\"instanceDates\":\"18 November-18 November\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"633802ABQHCJBGJLSDPTGRDMGHGGBLSJR\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-11-18T11:00:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-11-18T11:00:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-11-18T11:00:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-11-18T11:00:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false,\"attribute_Genre\":\"Families & Youth\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"2.30-4.30pm, £20, in building //  Join Stephen Burstin in his virtual tour of Hampton Court Palace, exploring the magnificent home of the notorious King Henry VIII and his six (unfortunate) wives. From award-winning gardens, notorious royal banquets to a corridor whispered to be haunted by one of Henry’s wives.  Learn also about its amazing Jewish connections, including King Henry turning to Jewish sages to secure one divorce, a Jewish hero who saved a King from an assassin’s bullet, the Jewish financier who helped secure another Palace royal resident the crown of England and uncover more Jewish anecdotes along the way. \\r\\n\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":90,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"A Virtual Tour of Hampton Court Palace…with enthralling Jewish connections!\",\"instanceDates\":\"10 February-10 February\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"556001AJLVGRBVBKMTDMMVMDJNDLSQLHC\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-02-10T14:30:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-02-10T14:30:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-02-10T14:30:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-02-10T14:30:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Walks\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"Stephen Burstin\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false},{\"description\":\"1.30pm-2.30pm, Thursdays, in building, £7 per session // This weekly debating series is organised by students, who select the topics for discussion and the debaters for each side. Students determine the structure and the subjects. Join them to hear your peers’ perspectives and to contribute your own.\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":60,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Abraham Debating Club Summer 2026\",\"instanceDates\":\"23 April-25 June\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"599602ANVSGKGMNJTPBSKVJGTKTRGJRLV\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-04-23T13:30:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-04-23T12:30:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-06-25T13:30:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-06-25T12:30:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false,\"attribute_Genre\":\"Classes & Courses\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"False\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Adult Education Classes & Courses\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"1.30pm-2.30pm, £7 // Come and join JW3's regular students who organise this weekly debate choosing the topics and debater on each side.  Hear their voices and add your own.\\r\\n\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":60,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Abraham Debating Club Winter 2026\",\"instanceDates\":\"8 January-26 March\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"561003AHKNKRRHHJMKMMDQGPSCRRPGSKK\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-01-08T13:30:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-01-08T13:30:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-03-26T13:30:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-03-26T13:30:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false,\"attribute_Genre\":\"Classes & Courses\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"True\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Adult Education\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"A deeply moving portrait of an architect tested by the impossible choices between career, country and motherhood. \\r\\n\\r\\n \\r\\n\\r\\nAda Karmi Melamede is one of the most accomplished architects in the world, but very little is known about her outside her home country of Israel. ADA – MY MOTHER THE ARCHITECT is a deeply moving portrait of an extraordinary woman directed by her daughter, filmmaker, and former architect, Yael Melamede. Ada is a true pioneer who, like many successful working mothers of her time, was forced to make impossible choices. Despite personal sacrifices, Ada's work gave physical form to some of Israel’s most important civic institutions, most notably in the acclaimed Supreme Court building in Jerusalem, the Open University, Ben Gurion University, and the Institute for Democracy, to name a few. ADA explores the impossible tensions between professional ambition and private life, and the ongoing challenge of holding onto ideals in a country increasingly drifting away from them.\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":120,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"ADA - My Mother the Architect\",\"instanceDates\":\"29 April-13 May\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"613802AGKTLMCMHLPLCNQCSTDMJTRMJPH\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-04-29T19:30:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-04-29T18:30:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-05-13T12:45:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-05-13T11:45:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Cinema\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false},{\"description\":\"4.30-6.30pm, £30, building // The final Programme of this fourth Series features three of our regulars whom our audience have most enjoyed. The inspired Finnish violinist, Sini Simonen and captivatingly imaginative Scottish pianist Alasdair Beatson join our Artistic Director, David Waterman, for forty-two years cellist of the Endellion Quartet, in a programme centring around Schubert’s Trio in E flat, one of his great, mature masterworks. If the Trout is Schubert’s most joyous piece, this trio is one of his most tragic and moving. The extremely evocative slow movement, which was inspired by a Swedish folksong, “The Sun has Set”, and has been used in many a film score, was first performed on the anniversary of the death of Beethoven, revered by Schubert. \\r\\n\\r\\nBeethoven’s own early piano trio, full of life, energy and sheer happiness, was part of a set of three in what must be the most distinguished, immortal Opus 1 ever issued by a composer. The concert opens with a violin and piano Sonatina by the great Jean Sibelius, the most wonderfully expressive composer from Sini Simonen’s native land. // Sibelius   Sonatina Op 80 in E for Violin and Piano  (23m)\\r\\n\\r\\nBeethoven  Piano trio in G   Op 1 no 2   (37m)\\r\\n\\r\\nInterval  (20m)\\r\\n\\r\\nSchubert  Piano trio in E flat Op 100 (30m)\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":120,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Alasdair Beatson, Sini Simonen, David Waterman\",\"instanceDates\":\"21 March-21 March\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"650601AKGSKMVNMVHCQTCHBLTKLMJJGTV\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2027-03-21T16:30:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2027-03-21T16:30:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2027-03-21T16:30:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2027-03-21T16:30:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false,\"attribute_Genre\":\"Music\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Classical Music Series\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"7.15-8.15pm, hybrid, £20 // Following the recent results of the US Mid-term elections, political expert Jonathan Paris will delve into their groundbreaking significance for the future of Trump’s presidency, his likely Republican successor, the Democratic Party and America itself. Join Paris in his engaging, clear and accessible talk to understand the unique position America faces internationally and the potential outcomes on its democratic and political future. \",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":60,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"American Midterm Election Update\",\"instanceDates\":\"4 November-4 November\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"636802AGKQSCLKVNQSLGTVGDQTHSPPQGQ\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-11-04T19:15:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-11-04T19:15:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-11-04T19:15:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-11-04T19:15:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false,\"attribute_Genre\":\"Talks & Discussions\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Adult Education\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"Jonathan Paris\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"Walking tour, 11am-1pm, £20 // Join Rachel Kolsky and discover the stories behind the East End Village.\\r\\n\\r\\nWalking from Mile End, Stepney Green always comes as a revelation to visitors with its attractive terraced houses and green spaces. En route you visit the campus of Queen Mary College with its fascinating history, and historic Sephardi Novo cemetery and discover hidden memories of the Jewish community with the old age home, Stepney Jewish School, Rothschild Dwellings, your guide’s favourite anarchist, pioneering women and so much more. \",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":120,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"An East End Village: Mile End and Stepney\",\"instanceDates\":\"20 October-20 October\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"636001ABTRCBKRRTSDGQMPSRVNJQJNJCS\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-10-20T11:00:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-10-20T10:00:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-10-20T11:00:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-10-20T10:00:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false,\"attribute_Genre\":\"Walks\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Walking Tours\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"Rachel Kolsky\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"6-9pm, £20 // Join us for a special evening exploring the powerful interconnection between food and Jewish identity.\\r\\n\\r\\nA panel of culinary experts will share how food is not only nourishment but also a vital thread that brings us together, strengthens our resilience, and preserves our heritage.\\r\\n\\r\\nDiscover how cherished recipes have been passed down from generation to generation (l’dor v’dor), carrying with them stories, traditions, and inspiration that continue to shape our communities and conversations today.\\r\\n\\r\\nCookbooks will be available to buy on the night.\\r\\n\\r\\nFeaturing Alissa Timoshkina (author of the cookbook Kapusta), Sephardi chef Linda Dangoor (author of From the Tigris to the Thames) and Helen Graham, a chef and food writer. The conversation will be chaired by food and culture writer Adrienne Katz Kennedy. \\r\\n\\r\\nLinda is the author of two cookbooks. The first one, Flavours of Babylon is an exploration and a celebration of the flavours and recipes of her Baghdadi heritage. Her second book. From the Tigris to the Thames recounts leaving her Baghdadi home and her journey living in various countries and discovering their various dishes. \\r\\n\\r\\nHelen is a celebrated chef and food writer based in London. Drawing on her Jewish diasporic roots, she pioneers innovative vegetable-forward cooking inspired by cuisines across the Middle East, Eastern Europe and North Africa. She has worked at several prominent Middle Eastern restaurants including the Palomar, the Barbary and the Ottolenghi Test Kitchen. Helen was Executive Chef at renowned London vegetarian restaurant Bubala for 5 years, helping take the business from pop-up to two critically acclaimed sites before leaving in 2023 to go solo. In 2022, Helen was selected as a rising star by Jay Rayner, and she made her debut television appearance on Sunday Brunch. She has since also appeared on Saturday Kitchen. Her recipes have been featured in Great British Chefs, House & Garden, The Guardian, Vogue, Delicious Magazine, Ocado Life Magazine, the Financial Times, and The Observer.\\r\\nwww.helengraham.co.uk\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":90,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"An Evening of Edible Memory: Food, Identity, and Jewish Life Across Generations\",\"instanceDates\":\"20 May-20 May\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"557601AVSNKLKKJQSPKRKHKGNDLVSJCQV\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-05-20T19:30:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-05-20T18:30:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-05-20T19:30:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-05-20T18:30:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Talks & Discussions\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Adult Education\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"Linda Dangoor\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false},{\"description\":\"7-9pm, £10, hybrid // Evening to mark the Departure and Expulsion of Jews from Arab Countries and Iran. JW3 in partnership with Harif is hosting the official UK Commemoration of the Departure and Exodus of Jews from Arab countries and Iran, in the presence of communal leaders and diplomats.\\r\\nThis year our theme will be : Jews of Egypt: 70 years since Suez .\\r\\n\\r\\nThe evening will feature testimonies of Jews who resettled in Britain following the expulsion. Guy Schalom and his band will transport us back to the cosmopolitan atmosphere of the 1950s with music popular throughout the Middle East.\\r\\n\\r\\nVisitors to JW3 are invited to browse the spectacular Harif exhibition at the entrance. It celebrates Sephardi culture in London and explains  the Henna ceremony widely practised by Jews from Arab countries to bestow blessings of happiness and fertility on a forthcoming marriage.\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":120,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"An Evening to commemorate the Exodus of Jews from Arab countries and Iran\",\"instanceDates\":\"19 November-19 November\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"645602AVNSJCVGJSPCRGJLLLGPLLCRKNP\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-11-19T19:00:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-11-19T19:00:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-11-19T19:00:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-11-19T19:00:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false,\"attribute_Genre\":\"Talks & Discussions\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"19:00 // 24 Sep 2026 // £23 // JW3 favourite Jeremy Sassoon returns following the acclaimed release of his 2026 album Older and Wiser. Fresh from worldwide performances aboard luxury cruise ships, Jeremy presents album tracks and highlights from Legends of Voice and Piano, written for the new Four Seasons yacht.\\r\\n\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":150,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"An evening with Jeremy Sassoon\",\"instanceDates\":\"24 September-24 September\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"631401AMPJTCHRSMGCLDJHDLHTGBJKBDL\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-09-24T19:00:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-09-24T18:00:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-09-24T19:00:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-09-24T18:00:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false,\"attribute_Genre\":\"Music\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"Jeremy Sassoon\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"7pm-8.30pm, £10, hybrid // Since October 7th, relationships between Muslims and Jews across the world have been strained. Many have stopped speaking; some have turned on one another. Yet in the midst of this turmoil, a Rabbi and an Imam have managed not only to preserve their friendship, but to deepen it. Their commitment to dialogue has inspired a bi-weekly podcast that explores how genuine conversation can bridge even the most painful divides.\\r\\n\\r\\nJoin us for an evening with Imam Nasser Kurdy MBE and Rabbi Dovid Lewis, two faith leaders who despite significant disagreements, continue to speak to one another in good faith while conflict exists thousands of miles away.\\r\\n\\r\\nImam Nasser Kurdy MBE, originally from Jordan, is a Manchester-based surgeon and lay Imam. Rabbi Dovid Lewis is a native Mancunian who has led the South Manchester Jewish Community since 2011. Friends since 2012, their bond strengthened after Nasser survived a stabbing outside his mosque in 2017, an event widely reported at the time. Since October 7th, they have partnered on dozens of interfaith initiatives across schools and even Premier League football clubs throughout the North West. Most recently, they jointly led an assembly for local teenagers on navigating difficult conversations about Israel–Palestine.\\r\\n\\r\\nImam Nasser Kurdy MBE:\\r\\n\\r\\n“The Israeli–Palestinian conflict affects relationships within our local communities. Jews and Muslims are having great difficulty speaking to each other. There’s no dialogue. Hence the podcast it’s about dialogue.”\\r\\n\\r\\nRabbi Dovid Lewis:\\r\\n“In our own communities, we might like to think we are influential: Nasser leads the mosque, I lead the synagogue. However, neither of us can make a direct difference to what’s happening in Israel, Palestine, Gaza, the West Bank. But what is our responsibility? It is to make sure that it doesn’t spill over into our communities, into the friendships we have built with one another.”\\r\\n\\r\\nThis special evening will explore their story, their podcast, and their mission: to show that agreement isn’t required, but conversation, the simple power of talk is.\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":90,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"An Evening with The Rabbi and The Imam\",\"instanceDates\":\"26 April-26 April\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"590601AVMSDTPMDSJDSNQHLJVKNLHSNHC\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-04-26T19:00:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-04-26T18:00:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-04-26T19:00:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-04-26T18:00:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Talks & Discussions\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false},{\"description\":\"11am-12pm, hybrid, £20 // Victoria was queen for over 60 years (1837-1901) and her reign sees a changing pattern of art and the arguments surrounding it. A new world of patrons and galleries emerges. Come along and experience Victorian Art from the final works of Turner, the Pre-Raphaelites and their followers to the Nocturnes of Whistler. No previous knowledge required. \\r\\n\\r\\nJill Stern is an historian by training. Her master’s degree was in the Art and Culture of the Dutch Golden Age and Art History also featured in her doctoral thesis and subsequent book. She is currently teaching two classes of Victorian Art for the University of the Third Age. \",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":60,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"An Introduction to Victorian Art\",\"instanceDates\":\"23 September-23 September\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"636601AKLDDCSTDTQBGRNHTGVKTNQBDCL\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-09-23T11:00:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-09-23T10:00:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-09-23T11:00:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-09-23T10:00:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false,\"attribute_Genre\":\"Talks & Discussions\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Adult Education\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"Jill Stern\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"In this powerful Israeli drama, six-year-old Annu and her beloved grandmother Sana share a quiet life in a Druze village—until one night Annu collapses and whispers a cryptic message about finding her “children in Syria.” Convinced her granddaughter channels her long-lost sister, Sana defies disbelief and danger to follow the clue into war-scarred territory. As she crosses borders, confronts old wounds, and navigates political and emotional terrain, Sana discovers not just the meaning of Annu’s words but the hidden threads of love, loss, and identity that bind generations. | This film is Arabic and Hebrew with English subtitles. | Duration: 1h 26m\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":86,\"imageUrl\":\"https://system.spektrix.com/jw3/files/179c13af-f908-49a7-b293-ad335864d50b.jpg\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Annu\",\"instanceDates\":\"12 May-12 May\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"https://system.spektrix.com/jw3/files/179c13af-f908-49a7-b293-ad335864d50b-thumbnail.jpg\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"617802ARSLPDSMMKBRRGVGHCPQJTVSSKC\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-05-12T17:30:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-05-12T16:30:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-05-12T17:30:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-05-12T16:30:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Cinema\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Seret Film Festival\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false},{\"description\":\"7-8.30pm, building, £20 // The Annual Spiro Tribute Lecture celebrates the tremendous work of Robin (z\\\"l) and Nitza Spiro and their contribution to Jewish cultural life in Britain over the last 40+ years. This year we are honoured to welcome actress, writer and producer Bat-El to the stage.\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":90,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Annual Spiro Tribute 2026\",\"instanceDates\":\"11 February-11 February\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"559801APNQVSMMVTNSGPPLHVCGDCSVRGD\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-02-11T19:00:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-02-11T19:00:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-02-11T19:00:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-02-11T19:00:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Talks & Discussions\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Adult Education\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false},{\"description\":\"Tuesdays, 7.15pm-9.15pm, £220, in building //\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":120,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Arabic Beginners with Micheline Antonian\",\"instanceDates\":\"6 October-6 October\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"649401ABRRGRMHVQPKMGMHQDSNDKHVSQT\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-10-06T19:15:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-10-06T18:15:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-10-06T19:15:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-10-06T18:15:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false,\"attribute_Genre\":\"Languages\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"True\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Languages\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"Micheline Antonian\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"Tuesdays, 7.15pm-9.15pm, £220, in building // \",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":120,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Arabic Not Quite Beginners (Term 2) with Micheline Antonian\",\"instanceDates\":\"21 April-14 July\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"610003ALCHJQBKDKTQNQGRBVSCRTLCKPN\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-04-21T19:15:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-04-21T18:15:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-07-14T19:15:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-07-14T18:15:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Languages\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"True\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Languages\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"Micheline Antonian\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false},{\"description\":\"Tuesdays, 7.15pm-9.15pm, £220, in building // \",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":120,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Arabic Not Quite Beginners with Micheline Antonian\",\"instanceDates\":\"6 January-24 March\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"571801AMTMKBPNKKDMCJBNLTSDDCJRLDG\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-01-06T19:15:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-01-06T19:15:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-03-24T19:15:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-03-24T19:15:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Languages\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"True\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Languages \",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"Micheline Antonian\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false},{\"description\":\"Wednesdays, 1pm-3pm, £220, in building // \",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":120,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Arabic Total Beginners with Micheline Antonian [NEW]\",\"instanceDates\":\"7 October-7 October\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"650201APJTNGJQBHKVJVTPJNLTGCTNLRC\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-10-07T13:00:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-10-07T12:00:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-10-07T13:00:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-10-07T12:00:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false,\"attribute_Genre\":\"Languages\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"True\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Languages\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"Micheline Antonian\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"12noon-2pm, £20, Sunday 31 May 2026 // Join London-based architect Ittai Frank for a captivating walking tour through Hampstead, exploring the lasting legacy of Jewish émigré architects and their vital contribution to British Modernist architecture. Back by popular demand, this tour highlights remarkable local buildings and stories of innovation, identity and resilience. This walk offers a unique opportunity to reflect on the enduring impact of Jewish immigrants on London’s architectural landscape.\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":120,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Architectural Walk in Hampstead\",\"instanceDates\":\"31 May-12 July\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"516801AGVBPMCTGJDHDHNKGQGNHNLKNHH\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-05-31T12:00:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-05-31T11:00:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-07-12T12:00:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-07-12T11:00:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Walks\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Walking Tours\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"Ittai Frank\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false},{\"description\":\"Walking tour, 12-2pm, £20 // Join London-based architect Ittai Frank for a captivating walking tour through Hampstead, exploring the lasting legacy of Jewish émigré architects and their vital contribution to British Modernist architecture. Back by popular demand, this tour highlights remarkable local buildings and stories of innovation, identity and resilience. This walk offers a unique opportunity to reflect on the enduring impact of Jewish immigrants on London’s architectural landscape.\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":120,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Architectural Walk in Hampstead\",\"instanceDates\":\"18 October-18 October\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"635801ANBBPQGJLHVKMLGRPDGHTNRDBNQ\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-10-18T12:00:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-10-18T11:00:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-10-18T12:00:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-10-18T11:00:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false,\"attribute_Genre\":\"Walks\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Walking Tours\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"Ittai Frank\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"2pm-4.15pm, £20, Sunday 21 June 2026 // To mark Refugee Week 2026, learn about the story of Fred Uhlman, a Jewish refugee lawyer turned artist, who settled with his English wife, Diana, in Downshire Hill in 1938.  Discover how they together formed the artist refugee committee to rescue Jewish artists trapped in Czechoslovakia and about how their Hampstead house became a refuge during WWII.  Hear about the organisations that he was involved in; visit sites he was known to frequent; discuss the role of his artistic friends and neighbours and find out about other Jewish refugee artists and designers who also settled in Hampstead. \\r\\n\\r\\nMarilyn Greene is a museum curator and educator. She was Curator of Hampstead Museum, Burgh House between 1998 & 2006 and worked in adult and community initiatives at the Victoria and Albert Museum from 2000-2013, primarily with faith and intercultural groups. In 2019/20 she assisted with administration for the Insiders Outsiders Festival which organises events about refugees from Nazi Europe and their contribution to the arts. She has worked on organisational and curatorial projects at London Transport Museum and is currently a Hidden London Guide for them. She is a qualified City of London Guide and Westminster Guide and also leads mudlarking tours on the Thames foreshore and school tours for the Charles Dickens Museum.\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":135,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Art & Refugees in Hampstead\",\"instanceDates\":\"21 June-21 June\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"598601ATHMLRDNVGLJLSCMBSLNKCHVDHV\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-06-21T14:00:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-06-21T13:00:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-06-21T14:00:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-06-21T13:00:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Walks\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Walking Tours\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"Marilyn Greene\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false},{\"description\":\"7pm-8.30pm, £18, hybrid // What is AI? And what is Jewish thought? \\r\\n\\r\\n \\r\\nJoin us for an engaging taster session exploring what artificial intelligence is and how we can make sense of it in today’s fast-changing world.  \\r\\n\\r\\nTogether, we will unpack the basics of AI, the different forms it can take and some bigger ideas like machine learning and superintelligence. Drawing on Jewish thought and practice, we will also explore how these perspectives can offer powerful insights into understanding this transformative technology and its radical impact on our world. \\r\\n\\r\\nWho should attend? \\r\\nThis course is for anyone curious about AI & tech and anyone interested in understanding our future - no prior knowledge nor tech background needed! \\r\\n\\r\\n \\r\\nWho teaches the course? \\r\\n\\r\\nDr Asher Kessler completed his PhD at the London School of Economics focusing on the intellectual history of ‘Big Tech’. His research focuses specifically upon Facebook/Meta, examining how high-level actors in and around the company came to think and speak about time, space, and their ability to change the world around them. Other than this, Asher has worked on questions of how Jewish thought might be used to navigate contemporary technological transformations.\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":90,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Artificial Intelligence and Jewish Thought [In-Building]\",\"instanceDates\":\"19 March-19 March\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"564201AQBHLSLPGKTTGMKTNJKKGVPGCNM\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-03-19T19:00:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-03-19T19:00:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-03-19T19:00:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-03-19T19:00:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Talks & Discussions\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Adult Education\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"Asher Kessler\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false},{\"description\":\"7pm-8.30pm, £18, hybrid // What is AI? And what is Jewish thought? \\r\\n\\r\\n \\r\\nJoin us for an engaging taster session exploring what artificial intelligence is and how we can make sense of it in today’s fast-changing world.  \\r\\n\\r\\nTogether, we will unpack the basics of AI, the different forms it can take and some bigger ideas like machine learning and superintelligence. Drawing on Jewish thought and practice, we will also explore how these perspectives can offer powerful insights into understanding this transformative technology and its radical impact on our world. \\r\\n\\r\\nWho should attend? \\r\\nThis course is for anyone curious about AI & tech and anyone interested in understanding our future - no prior knowledge nor tech background needed! \\r\\n\\r\\n \\r\\nWho teaches the course? \\r\\n\\r\\nDr Asher Kessler completed his PhD at the London School of Economics focusing on the intellectual history of ‘Big Tech’. His research focuses specifically upon Facebook/Meta, examining how high-level actors in and around the company came to think and speak about time, space, and their ability to change the world around them. Other than this, Asher has worked on questions of how Jewish thought might be used to navigate contemporary technological transformations.\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":90,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Artificial Intelligence and Jewish Thought [Online]\",\"instanceDates\":\"19 March-19 March\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"562802AJNKKHVJHNDPSSSVLLNSKQHDJLC\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-03-19T19:00:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-03-19T19:00:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-03-19T19:00:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-03-19T19:00:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Talks & Discussions\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Adult Education\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"Asher Kessler\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false},{\"description\":\"11am-1pm, £20, Monday 11 May 2026 // Join Rachel Kolsky and discover the stories behind the famous Rothschild family. \\r\\n\\r\\nPiccadilly became 'Rothschild Row' when they made their money in the City but spent it on opulent homes in London's West End. Join popular tour guide and author, Rachel Kolsky, and discover sites linked to the homes of NM, the founder of the company plus Lionel, Leo, Ferdy and Alfred, Along the way ‘meet’ their famous neighbours including the Duke of Wellington and Disraeli and hear the stories of business and charity, love and marriage including the church where Hannah married the future prime minister, Lord Rosebery.\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":120,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"At Home with the Rothschilds\",\"instanceDates\":\"11 May-11 May\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"596601ALNTPMHVBMSMTNJDCVTMBHRKKTR\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-05-11T11:00:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-05-11T10:00:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-05-11T11:00:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-05-11T10:00:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Walks\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Walking Tours\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"Rachel Kolsky\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false},{\"description\":\"Walking tour, 5-7pm, £20 // Discover the mysterious atmosphere to Hampstead on a tour after-dark where the streets are lit by old-fashioned lamps. We will wind through the narrow back streets and catch glimpses of its fascinating history from the glow of lamps and lit buildings. This tour is particularly stunning over the Festive season where subtle Christmas lights add to the effect. \\r\\n\\r\\n \\r\\n\\r\\nMarilyn Greene is a museum curator and educator. She was Curator of Hampstead Museum, Burgh House between 1998 & 2006 and worked in adult and community initiatives at the Victoria and Albert Museum from 2000-2013, primarily with faith and intercultural groups. In 2019/20 she assisted with administration for the Insiders Outsiders Festival which organises events about refugees from Nazi Europe and their contribution to the arts. She has worked on organisational and curatorial projects at London Transport Museum and is currently a Hidden London Guide for them. She is a qualified City of London Guide and Westminster Guide and also leads mudlarking tours on the Thames foreshore and school tours for the Charles Dickens Museum. \",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":120,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Atmospheric Lamplit Hampstead\",\"instanceDates\":\"25 October-25 October\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"635402ASRDSPTJLSNBVCRDSPQLSBJSJRL\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-10-25T17:00:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-10-25T17:00:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-10-25T17:00:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-10-25T17:00:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false,\"attribute_Genre\":\"Walks\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Walking Tours\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"Marilyn Greene\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"4.30-6.30pm, £30, building // From New York to Sydney, to Vienna and London, the Aviv Quartet has captivated audiences with its exceptional performances at the world’s most prestigious venues, such as Carnegie Hall, the Concertgebouw, l’Auditorium du Louvre, Wigmore Hall, and the Konzerthaus Berlin. It has also been invited by festivals such as Verbier, Davos, Aix-enProvence, Lubéron, and les Folles Journées de Nantes. // Purcell Fantasias \\r\\nBeethoven “Harp Quartet “ Op 74\\r\\nMendelssohn Op 13\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":210,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Aviv Quartet\",\"instanceDates\":\"24 January-24 January\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"650001AQTKQJHQJJQSDLBTHCPPTNCJGRN\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2027-01-24T16:30:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2027-01-24T16:30:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2027-01-24T16:30:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2027-01-24T16:30:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false,\"attribute_Genre\":\"Music\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Classical Music Series\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"When David Hockney's beautiful lover, Peter Schlesinger, breaks up with him, it leaves David a complete emotional wreck. An artist, he suddenly finds himself unable to create anything, and is awash in depression and loneliness. After a time, David is able to find inspiration in his backyard swimming pool, and he begins a portrait of it. This unique docudrama presents a semi-fictionalized account of the story behind one of Hockney's most popular paintings. Duration: 101 minutes Rating: 15 Director: Jack Hazan Cast: David Hockney, Peter Schlesinger, Celia Birtwell Year: 1974 Language: English https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=m2sEkXKxQs8&pp=ygUdYSBiaWdnZXIgc3BsYXNoIGRhdmlkIGhvY2tuZXk%3D\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":106,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Babykino: A Bigger Splash\",\"instanceDates\":\"6 July-6 July\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"641001AHTDBPQDPCTNKCKLJNHBBQGTVLT\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-07-06T10:30:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-07-06T09:30:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-07-06T10:30:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-07-06T09:30:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false,\"attribute_Genre\":\"Cinema\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"Set on Vancouver Island in the late 1990s, Blue Heron follows eight-year-old Sasha and her Hungarian immigrant family as they attempt to build a new life, only to be destabilised by the increasingly dangerous behaviour of her older brother, Jeremy. Drawing on her own memories, filmmaker Sophy Romvari shapes a deeply personal portrait of childhood, family fractures, and the fragility of recollection. Duration: 90 minutes Rating: 12A Director: Sophy Romvari Cast: Eylul Guven, Edik Beddoes, Iringó Réti Year: 2026 Language: English and Hungairan Subtitles: English https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=6qAK9GwWRe0\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":91,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Babykino: Blue Heron\",\"instanceDates\":\"27 July-27 July\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"641201AQLGTJCGRDDRSTBJRGRBBQKQMJL\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-07-27T11:00:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-07-27T10:00:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-07-27T11:00:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-07-27T10:00:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false,\"attribute_Genre\":\"Cinema\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"For parents and carers with babies under the age of one // \\tEgypt's most adored actor, George Fahmy (Fares Fares) is pressured to star in a film commissioned by the highest authorities. He reluctantly accepts the role and finds himself thrown into the inner circle of power. Like a moth drawn to the flame, he begins an affair with the mysterious wife of the general overseeing the film. This is director Tarik Saleh's final film of his Cairo Trilogy. // Duration: 129 minutes Rating: 15 Director: Tarik Saleh Cast: Fares Fares, Amr Waked, Lyna Khoudri Year: 2025 Language: Arabic Subtitles: English\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":129,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Babykino: Eagles of the Republic\",\"instanceDates\":\"15 June-15 June\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"628801ASJNVDVLQSKGCMRGNDJSHTJHCJN\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-06-15T10:30:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-06-15T09:30:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-06-15T10:30:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-06-15T09:30:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Cinema\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false},{\"description\":\"For parents and carers with babies under the age of one // Enzo, 16, defies his bourgeois family's expectations by starting a masonry apprenticeship, a path far removed from the prestigious life they had envisioned for him. \\r\\n\\r\\n \\r\\n\\r\\nIn their chic villa in the sun-drenched South of France, tensions simmer as relentless questions and pressures weigh on Enzo's future and dreams. On the construction sites, however, Vlad, a charismatic Ukrainian colleague, shakes up Enzo's world and opens the door to unexpected possibilities. \\r\\n\\r\\n \\r\\n\\r\\nDuration: 93 minutes \\r\\n\\r\\nRating: 15 \\r\\n\\r\\nDirector: Robin Campillo \\r\\n\\r\\nCast: Eloy Pohu, Maksym Slivinskyi, Pierfrancesco Favino  \\r\\n\\r\\nYear: 2025 \\r\\n\\r\\nLanguage: French / Ukrainian \\r\\nSubtitles: English \",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":93,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Babykino: Enzo\",\"instanceDates\":\"29 June-29 June\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"630001AVTHPGTBNTJQHTJHRDJTRGJRDNS\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-06-29T10:30:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-06-29T09:30:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-06-29T10:30:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-06-29T09:30:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Cinema\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false},{\"description\":\"In an afterlife where souls have one week to decide where to spend eternity, Joan is faced with the impossible choice between the man she spent her life with and her first love, who died young and has waited decades for her to arrive. | This screening is exclusively for parents or carers with a baby under one. | Duration: 1h 54m, Rating: 15\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":114,\"imageUrl\":\"https://system.spektrix.com/jw3/files/850e91e5-fa16-43a6-8c4d-a9190e742c82.jpg\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Babykino: Eternity\",\"instanceDates\":\"5 January-5 January\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"https://system.spektrix.com/jw3/files/850e91e5-fa16-43a6-8c4d-a9190e742c82-thumbnail.jpg\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"580601AQCHRPMVVKVHNKQQBPQNRTMNSVH\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-01-05T10:30:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-01-05T10:30:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-01-05T10:30:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-01-05T10:30:00Z\",\"altText\":\"Eternity\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Cinema\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Babykino\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false},{\"description\":\"The powerful story of love and loss that inspired the creation of Shakespeare’s timeless masterpiece, Hamlet. | This screening is exclusively for parents or carers with a baby under one. | Duration: 2h 5m, Rating: 12A  \",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":125,\"imageUrl\":\"https://system.spektrix.com/jw3/files/19916ba7-c43f-40fe-b33c-16d8a2cee12c.jpg\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Babykino: Hamnet\",\"instanceDates\":\"26 January-2 March\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"https://system.spektrix.com/jw3/files/19916ba7-c43f-40fe-b33c-16d8a2cee12c-thumbnail.jpg\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"579602AJHPSNBCGRNJHSDRRGBMLMRMRHM\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-01-26T10:30:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-01-26T10:30:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-03-02T10:30:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-03-02T10:30:00Z\",\"altText\":\"Hamnet\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Cinema\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Babykino\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false},{\"description\":\"Disowned at birth by his obscenely wealthy family, blue-collar Becket Redfellow will stop at nothing to reclaim his inheritance, no matter how many relatives stand in his way. | Duration: 1h 45m, Rating: 15 Credits Rating: 15 Genre: Dark Comedy Director: John Patton Ford Stars: Glen Powell, Margaret Qualley, Jessica Henwick https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=BxBof_p3_es&pp=ygUgaG93IHRvIG1ha2UgYSBraWxsaW5nIFVLIHRyYWlsZXI%3D\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":105,\"imageUrl\":\"https://system.spektrix.com/jw3/files/1f8327ba-eb98-43da-875c-bbdf0090b4fa.jpg\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Babykino: How to Make A Killing\",\"instanceDates\":\"20 April-20 April\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"https://system.spektrix.com/jw3/files/1f8327ba-eb98-43da-875c-bbdf0090b4fa-thumbnail.jpg\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"617001ABRLVMPHHJDRMQBHBHRRGLJJQPM\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-04-20T11:00:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-04-20T10:00:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-04-20T11:00:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-04-20T10:00:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Cinema\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false},{\"description\":\"In 1950s New York, Marty Mauser, a young man with a dream no one respects, goes to hell and back in pursuit of greatness. | This screening is exclusively for parents or carers with a baby under one. | Duration: 2h 30m, Rating: 15\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":150,\"imageUrl\":\"https://system.spektrix.com/jw3/files/f252ed39-3d2e-441a-8a15-fe259e895d43.jpg\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Babykino: Marty Supreme\",\"instanceDates\":\"19 January-23 February\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"https://system.spektrix.com/jw3/files/f252ed39-3d2e-441a-8a15-fe259e895d43-thumbnail.jpg\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"581601ARLNHQPKQDKHQSBCPQLRPLVNCKC\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-01-19T10:30:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-01-19T10:30:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-02-23T10:30:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-02-23T10:30:00Z\",\"altText\":\"Babykino: Marty Supreme\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Cinema\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Babykino\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false},{\"description\":\"From the team behind 'Finding Your Feet' and 'Fisherman's Friends' comes Mother's Pride, a story about the Harley family who after losing their matriarch, must come together to save their pub and village through the art of beer-brewing. | Duration: 1h 30m, Rating: 12A \",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":90,\"imageUrl\":\"https://system.spektrix.com/jw3/files/bc6e3042-d532-4893-871f-caacb39519a4.jpg\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Babykino: Mother's Pride\",\"instanceDates\":\"23 March-23 March\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"https://system.spektrix.com/jw3/files/bc6e3042-d532-4893-871f-caacb39519a4-thumbnail.jpg\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"605401ABSPDTDQPPQJSCNPKDDPLPQMLLV\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-03-23T10:30:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-03-23T10:30:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-03-23T10:30:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-03-23T10:30:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Cinema\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Babykino\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false},{\"description\":\"For parents and carers with babies under the age of one // Heartfelt and funny, the film follows three sisters who return to their childhood home for a momentous weekend: the third wedding of their twice-widowed mother, Diana Frost (Kristin Scott Thomas).  \\r\\n\\r\\n \\r\\n\\r\\nThe three daughters are from vastly different walks of life: Katherine (Scarlett Johansson) is a Captain in the Royal Navy; Victoria (Sienna Miller) is a Hollywood star; and Georgina (Emily Beecham) is a hospice nurse. Over the weekend, the family gathers to celebrate the new marriage, but mother and daughters alike are forced to revisit the past and confront the future, all with help from a colourful group of unexpected wedding guests.  //\\r\\n\\r\\n \\r\\n\\r\\nDuration: 95 minutes \\r\\n\\r\\nRating: 15 \\r\\n\\r\\nDirector: Kristin Scott Thomas \\r\\n\\r\\nCast: Scarlett Johansson, Sienna Miller, Emily Beecham \\r\\n\\r\\nYear: 2025 \\r\\n\\r\\nLanguage: English \",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":95,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Babykino: My Mother's Wedding\",\"instanceDates\":\"22 June-22 June\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"629601ADKJJQLVTTVCJNKCTHRMDGRTKKL\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-06-22T11:00:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-06-22T10:00:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-06-22T11:00:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-06-22T10:00:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Cinema\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false},{\"description\":\"In 18th century Venice, 20-year-old violin virtuoso Cecilia lives at the Pièta orphanage, where, despite her talent, she remains confined, knowing that marriage is the only way out. Yet, her life takes a turn after she meets Antonio Vivaldi, a brilliant and ambitious composer who becomes the new violin teacher. Guided by Vivaldi and his music, Cecilia finds the strength to challenge the destiny that once seemed inevitable. | This film is in Italian with English subtitles. | Duration:1h 51m, Rating: 15 Credits\\r\\nRating: 15\\r\\nGenre: Drama\\r\\nDirector: Damiano Michieletto \\r\\nStars: Michele Riondino, Tecla Insolia, Fabrizia Sacchi https://youtu.be/J-fEjuVy5cQ\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":110,\"imageUrl\":\"https://system.spektrix.com/jw3/files/85e341cc-e2f2-41cb-a285-908c167bed2a.jpg\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Babykino: Primavera\",\"instanceDates\":\"18 May-18 May\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"https://system.spektrix.com/jw3/files/85e341cc-e2f2-41cb-a285-908c167bed2a-thumbnail.jpg\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"623401ABPSHNVBBPHKRJDQCTKHDCGDMQK\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-05-18T10:30:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-05-18T09:30:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-05-18T10:30:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-05-18T09:30:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Cinema\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false},{\"description\":\"Set in modern-day Tokyo, Rental Family follows an American actor who struggles to find purpose until he lands an unusual gig: working for a Japanese \\\"rental family\\\" agency, playing stand-in roles for strangers. As he immerses himself in his clients’ worlds, he begins to form genuine bonds that blur the lines between performance and reality. Confronting the moral complexities of his work, he rediscovers purpose, belonging, and the quiet beauty of human connection. | Duration: 2h 19m, Rating: 12A Credits\\r\\nRating: 12A\\r\\nGenre: Comedy, Drama\\r\\nDirector: Hikari\\r\\nStars: Brendan Fraser, Takehiro Hira, Mari Yamamoto\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":109,\"imageUrl\":\"https://system.spektrix.com/jw3/files/6820993c-3e3b-43a9-9995-e93834fa04cd.jpg\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Babykino: Rental Family\",\"instanceDates\":\"16 February-16 February\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"https://system.spektrix.com/jw3/files/6820993c-3e3b-43a9-9995-e93834fa04cd-thumbnail.jpg\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"586801ASRGRVSGNTBSPGKHCDVBGVBLGPC\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-02-16T10:30:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-02-16T10:30:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-02-16T10:30:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-02-16T10:30:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Cinema\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false},{\"description\":\"For parents or carers with babies under the age of one. // What is the value of art? Does it reside in personal expression? Cultural longevity? Financial worth? These questions fuel Steven Soderbergh’s gloriously entertaining comedy. Julian Sklar (McKellen) was once a star of London’s 1960’s and 70’s pop art explosion, but he hasn’t painted in decades and has been broke for years. His two estranged children (James Corden, Jessica Gunning), desperate for an inheritance, hire Lori, an art restorer and former forger (Coel), to pose as a prospective assistant in order to access unfinished canvases Julian has buried deep in storage. A sharp and remarkable tale of creativity, legacy, and avarice. //Rating: 15, Director: Steven Soderbergh, Stars: Ian McKellen, Michaela Coel, Jessica Gunning https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=7CB2nsSBqs0&pp=ygUbdGhlIGNocmlzdG9waGVycyB1ayB0cmFpbGVy\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":100,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Babykino: The Christophers\",\"instanceDates\":\"1 June-1 June\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"627801AQJRNNKKKVQTPMSSVRGKJPGVPPL\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-06-01T11:00:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-06-01T10:00:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-06-01T11:00:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-06-01T10:00:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Cinema\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false},{\"description\":\"Joe and Angela's marriage is on thin ice. When they invite their enigmatic upstairs neighbors for a dinner party, the night spirals into unexpected places. Have they reignited the spark or lit the match that burns it all down? Duration: 107 minutes Rating: 15 Director: Olivia Wilde Cast: Seth Rogan, Olivia Wilde, Edward Norton, Penélope Cruz Year: 2026 https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=7YIHRhRMn94&pp=ygUVdGhlIGludml0ZSB1ayB0cmFpbGVy\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":107,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Babykino: The Invite\",\"instanceDates\":\"20 July-20 July\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"641401ATJJDJLHMPNNPCLBJHCSKLJMLQV\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-07-20T11:00:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-07-20T10:00:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-07-20T11:00:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-07-20T10:00:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false,\"attribute_Genre\":\"Cinema\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"The riveting biography of 102-year-old CIA spymaster Peter Sichel who passed away earlier this year, revealing for the first time the epic and unvarnished history of the US foreign intelligence service from the inside. With a good dose of wit and humor to boot, Sichel unpacks the obscured roots of conflicts that plague today's world and the toll espionage took on his personal life. | Duration: 1h 31m, Rating: 15 Credits Rating: 15 Genre: Documentary Director: Katharina Otto-Bernstein Stars: Scott Anderson, Erick Arbenz, Carl Bernstein https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=IYB2lKY4yQY&pp=ygUXdGhlIGxhc3Qgc3B5IFVLIHRyYWlsZXI%3D\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":106,\"imageUrl\":\"https://system.spektrix.com/jw3/files/0def24d0-8ecf-4d05-b4cf-c36714f34979.jpg\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Babykino: The Last Spy\",\"instanceDates\":\"27 April-27 April\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"https://system.spektrix.com/jw3/files/0def24d0-8ecf-4d05-b4cf-c36714f34979-thumbnail.jpg\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"616802ABDCRMCQHHHNBTCCDCKCJDKVLQL\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-04-27T10:30:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-04-27T09:30:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-04-27T10:30:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-04-27T09:30:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Cinema\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false},{\"description\":\"While people across 1990's Iraq struggle to survive, 9-year old Lamia has been selected to prepare a cake to celebrate the President's birthday. In a landscape of fear and scarcity, where basic ingredients are nearly impossible to find, Lamia sets out on a determined journey throughout the big city in search of eggs, flour, and sugar. Accompanied by her grandmother, her loyal friend Saeed, and her pet rooster Hindi, she navigates vendors and police officers along the way. | This film is in Arabic with English subtitles | Duration: 1h 45m, Rating: 12A \",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":105,\"imageUrl\":\"https://system.spektrix.com/jw3/files/f396cba8-2e06-44ee-90ac-b0e4c0263861.jpg\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Babykino: The President's Cake\",\"instanceDates\":\"16 March-16 March\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"https://system.spektrix.com/jw3/files/f396cba8-2e06-44ee-90ac-b0e4c0263861-thumbnail.jpg\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"605601ANVMJKVPVBPHDBHPCQBQNKNGPPR\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-03-16T10:30:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-03-16T10:30:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-03-16T10:30:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-03-16T10:30:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Cinema\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Babykino\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false},{\"description\":\"Elliot Green (Jeremy Steyn) finds himself caught up in a whirlwind of caterers, guest lists, hairdressers and Torah study as Maria Charles’ endearingly fussy matriarch Rita prepares him for the most important day of his life.\\r\\n\\r\\nExhausted dad Victor (Bernard Spear) and elder sister Lesley (Adrienne Posta) take a more serene approach, but Eliot’s about to experience an acute case of cold feet.\\r\\n\\r\\nAffectionately satirising the rituals of Jewish community and debunking the myth of adulthood, Jack Rosenthal’s witty time capsule of 1970s Britain holds a near‑mythical status in British Jewish culture and remains a landmark of UK television drama.\\r\\n\\r\\n// Special Screening: Thursday 28 May @ 6.30pm\\r\\nOn Thursday 28 May, join us for a special screening of the beloved classic. The screening will be preceded by an introduction, as well as a screening of the short film Beshert (2025), and will be followed by an in‑conversation discussion.\\r\\n\\r\\nWe will welcome Jason Solomons, film critic and presenter-turned-film producer whose debut production is the award-winning short Beshert. Alongside playwright Amy Rosenthal, Jack Rosenthal’s daughter, they will reflect on the award-winning screenwriter’s celebrated body of work and the enduring legacy of Bar Mitzvah Boy.\\r\\n\\r\\nAudiences on Thursday 28 May will also receive a copy of Dr Julia Wagner’s essay Bar Mitzvah Boy, which was originally published with the BFI Blu‑ray edition of the film, distributed with the kind permission of both the BFI and the author.\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":75,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Bar Mitzvah Boy\",\"instanceDates\":\"28 May-31 May\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"625201AGVTBCQQPRTGQTLKDKPNTRVSJCG\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-05-28T18:30:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-05-28T17:30:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-05-31T18:20:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-05-31T17:20:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Arts & Culture\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Coming of Age Film Season\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false},{\"description\":\"7.15pm-8.30pm, £20, in building, Wednesday 1 July 2026 // A pioneer of modernism, Barbara Hepworth (1903-1975) was one of the most important sculptors of the 20th century. \\r\\n\\r\\nHer organic shapes, \\\"pierced\\\" holes, and fascination with colour, reflect a deep connection between human figures and the natural world.\\r\\n\\r\\nCoinciding with the exhibition Hepworth in Colour at the Courtauld Gallery (12 June- 06 September 2026), this talk will explore how her body of work engaged with Jewish artists who migrated to Britain.\\r\\n\\r\\nTogether with Jacob Epstein, Naum Gabo, László Moholy-Nagy, and Lucie Rie, Hepworth fostered new visions to expand the story of art.\\r\\n\\r\\nSophie is an art historian, writer, and lecturer, with a special interest in visual culture and architecture. She has worked with leading institutions in the culture and heritage sectors across Europe and brings a rich, interdisciplinary perspective to her talks.\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":75,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Barbara Hepworth: Carving New Spaces\",\"instanceDates\":\"1 July-1 July\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"594601ATVTKMMRGBLTDRMGQTCNMQCQSNV\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-07-01T19:15:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-07-01T18:15:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-07-01T19:15:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-07-01T18:15:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Talks & Discussions\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Adult Education\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"Sophie Lachowsky\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false},{\"description\":\"6pm-9.30pm, £12, in building // applicants should be 12+ // \",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":210,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Battle of the Bands\",\"instanceDates\":\"8 March-8 March\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"546401AQPTBQMJRTRPLDKLVVNTRGSGBKC\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-03-08T18:00:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-03-08T18:00:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-03-08T18:00:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-03-08T18:00:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Families & Youth\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false},{\"description\":\"7-8pm, building, £9 // Calling all poets and poetry lovers to join our Open Mic Poetry Night, hosted by Judy Karbritz, co-founder of the Jewish Poetry Society and Harrow’s Community Poet.\\r\\n\\r\\nTo mark JW3’s 13th birthday, join us for a relaxed evening of poetry, where participants are invited to share original pieces or favourite poems exploring themes of schooldays, growing up and independence. Whether you are an experienced poet or simply want to come along and listen, all our welcome to this communal night of poetry.\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":60,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Becoming Ourselves: Poems of Growing Up and Beyond\",\"instanceDates\":\"11 March-11 March\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"566401ANHTHCLJBCLKJVLSQHLCNLGGPTG\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-03-11T19:00:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-03-11T19:00:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-03-11T19:00:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-03-11T19:00:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Talks & Discussions\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Arts & Culture\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"Judy Karbritz\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false},{\"description\":\"Victoria Wood remains one of Britain's most cherished entertainers -- a comic genius whose work reshaped the landscape of British humor. But behind the joyous persona -- the singer, the satirist, the sharp-witted writer -- lay a young woman navigating insecurity, anger, and self-doubt. Told in her own words and through the voices of those who knew her best, the film uncovers the formative experiences and personal battles that powered Victoria's unmatched ability to make the nation laugh. | Duration: 2h 12m, Rating: 15 | Films may be preceded by up to 20 minutes of advertisements and trailers. Specific timings will vary with each screening. We always recommend arriving on time.\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":90,\"imageUrl\":\"https://system.spektrix.com/jw3/files/56817741-43aa-4ab0-9827-cfd9001788b5.jpg\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Becoming Victoria Wood\",\"instanceDates\":\"1 February-5 February\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"https://system.spektrix.com/jw3/files/56817741-43aa-4ab0-9827-cfd9001788b5-thumbnail.jpg\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"586802ALDTMJHQQDTQMGJLNGNBKHHPHKB\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-02-01T17:40:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-02-01T17:40:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-02-05T13:30:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-02-05T13:30:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Cinema\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false},{\"description\":\"11am-12.30pm, £15, online // Over 80 years after the Holocaust, children of survivors and refugees will explore together how it has affected their lives.\\r\\n\\r\\nThis online event is exclusively for members of the second generation, whether they reside in the UK or abroad.\\r\\n\\r\\nThis workshop will be led by Gaby Glassman, a psychologist and psychotherapist who has facilitated second generation groups since the 1980s.; 80 years after the Holocaust, children of survivors and refugees will explore together how it has affected their lives.\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":90,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Being Second Generation\",\"instanceDates\":\"22 March-22 March\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"589601AGJQCNMMCTPQPKRHGPHGMJQGSJG\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-03-22T11:00:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-03-22T11:00:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-03-22T11:00:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-03-22T11:00:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Talks & Discussions\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Holocaust Learning\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false},{\"description\":\"11am - 12.30pm, £15, online only // Eighty years after the Holocaust, the children of Holocaust survivors and refugees come together to explore the lasting legacy of their parents' experiences and how these have influenced their own lives. Through shared discussion and reflection, participants will have the opportunity to connect with others who understand the unique challenges, responsibilities, and strengths that can come with being part of the second generation.\\r\\n\\r\\nThis online workshop will be led by Gaby Glassman, a psychologist and psychotherapist who has facilitated second-generation groups since the 1980s.\\r\\n\\r\\nPlease note that this event is exclusively for second-generation participants, the children of Holocaust survivors and refugees, whether resident in the UK or abroad.\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":90,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Being Second Generation\",\"instanceDates\":\"11 October-11 October\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"651601ARMPVJSCDJJTKLGRBCNPTSJQQDQ\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-10-11T11:00:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-10-11T10:00:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-10-11T11:00:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-10-11T10:00:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false,\"attribute_Genre\":\"Talks & Discussions\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"Gaby Glassman\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"19:30 // 27 Oct 2026 // £15 // You know what it's like when everything’s going well? Bennett doesn’t. He was in the Top Ten Jokes of The Fringe and he’s BAFTA shortlisted, yet life still laughs at him. \\r\\n\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":75,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Bennett Arron - I Regret This Already \",\"instanceDates\":\"27 October-27 October\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"632401AMLRSPDTTDHTMVNVDNLKGCTSTLD\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-10-27T19:30:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-10-27T19:30:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-10-27T19:30:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-10-27T19:30:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false,\"attribute_Genre\":\"Comedy\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"2-3.30pm, building only, £20 // The art dealer Weill is the subject of an exhibition which has travelled from New York to Montreal and be at the Musee de l'Orangerie  in Paris over the winter months. Born into a poor Jewish family and without social connections or physical allure, Berthe Weill had few advantages in life other than courage and a brilliant eye for artistic talent. She was the first Paris dealer to show the work of both Picasso and Matisse and the only dealer to offer a one man show to Modigliani in his life time. With her motto of \\\"Make way for the young\\\" she offered support for many of the best artists active in Paris between 1900 and the forced closure of her gallery in 1940. In his lecture Patrick Bade will be celebrating the life and career of this remarkable woman. \",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":90,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Berthe Weill: A Courageous Spirit\",\"instanceDates\":\"8 January-8 January\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"556401AVCMRKJVTNQVJMDRHGLCQPVDLKH\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-01-08T14:00:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-01-08T14:00:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-01-08T14:00:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-01-08T14:00:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Classes & Courses\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Adult Education\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"Patrick Bade\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false},{\"description\":\"6.30-8.30pm, £18, in building // Life rarely gives us a clean pause between one chapter and the next.  \\r\\n\\r\\nBetween Chapters: Re-imagining the Road Ahead creates that pause - an intentional space to step back, reflect and re-imagine what comes next.  \\r\\n\\r\\nThrough guided creative exercises, you will explore your values, clarify the direction you want to move in the world and reconnect with what feels meaningful to you. Rather than rushing toward answers, the session invites you to creatively and intentionally map out who you are becoming.  \\r\\n\\r\\n2. Session Outline: \\r\\n\\r\\nDuring the taster session, participants will explore these questions using a sequence of creative tasks, including: \\r\\n\\r\\nGuided visualisation \\r\\n\\r\\nCreative prompts \\r\\n\\r\\nCollaging and creating a collection of images to guide your road ahead \\r\\n\\r\\n \\r\\n\\r\\n3. What You’ll Learn: \\r\\n\\r\\nBy the end of the session, participants will gain: \\r\\n\\r\\nGreater clarity about what matters to them at this moment \\r\\n\\r\\nA feeling of being more connected to yourself as you move forward \\r\\n\\r\\nLanguage or images that help you describe where you are and where you might go next \\r\\n\\r\\n4. Who It’s For: \\r\\n\\r\\nThis taster session is for anyone who feels they are between chapters - finishing one phase of life \\r\\n\\r\\n \\r\\n\\r\\n (perhaps of the year too? Where one stage is coming to an end, and what’s next isn’t clear yet’) and not yet ready to define the next - and who would like a guided and creative way to reflect and re-imagine the road ahead. \\r\\n\\r\\nNo artistic experience is needed: the emphasis is on the process. \\r\\n\\r\\n \\r\\n\\r\\n5. Who Delivers It? \\r\\n\\r\\nRachel Davies is an ICF accredited coach working in leadership development and coaching. She is fascinated by creativity and how it enhances our lives. She founded the course Creative Journeys to help people explore their creativity, and has published ‘Life, In Shorts’, a book of poetry about her time in Zambia, makes ceramics and loves to paint. \",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":120,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Between Chapters: Re–imagining the Road Ahead\",\"instanceDates\":\"28 September-28 September\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"636801AKPBQQCKSHVMSBCKKTQCQQBTSHD\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-09-28T18:30:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-09-28T17:30:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-09-28T18:30:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-09-28T17:30:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false,\"attribute_Genre\":\"Talks & Discussions\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Adult Education\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"Rachel Davies\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"For the special screening on Sunday 26th July, we invite you to a conversational cinema experience, sharing your stories from your second chapter. Have you started something new later in life? Changed direction? Followed a long-held dream? Reinvented yourself? We'd love to hear your second-chapter stories, to be shared pre- and post- screening, alongside a social in our Cafe afterwards. // A cantor in a crisis of faith finds his world turned upside down when his grade school music teacher re-enters his life as his new adult Bat Mitzvah student. // 15, 1h 51m\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":180,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Between the Temples\",\"instanceDates\":\"26 July-30 July\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"627401AKDKLCTPNDKGNGCLDSVDSJRVRGH\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-07-26T18:00:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-07-26T17:00:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-07-30T17:30:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-07-30T16:30:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":true,\"attribute_Genre\":\"Cinema\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Coming of Age Film Season\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"2-3.30pm, £20, hybrid // The biggest radio, recording and movie star around the world for 40 years Bing had it all but let’s look at his life and career in more detail - films include the Road titles, Blue Skies and White Christmas. \\r\\n\\r\\nGeorge McGhee has over 35 years of experience, latterly at the BBC, where he oversaw all feature films and international TV series acquisitions. \",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":90,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Bing Crosby\",\"instanceDates\":\"16 November-16 November\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"637601AHRCGMVGRSDVBRRTJTQMTRMBKKR\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-11-16T14:00:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-11-16T14:00:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-11-16T14:00:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-11-16T14:00:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false,\"attribute_Genre\":\"Talks & Discussions\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Adult Education\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"George McGhee\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"The love story of London-based Lebanese journalist and Syrian-based activist/cameraman over thirteen years of revolutions, war and exile. From besieged Aleppo to the confines of a London newsroom, Lebanese journalist Janay Boulos and Syrian activist /cameraman Abd Alkader Habak retrace their love story, using their vast personal archives stretching over 13 years of revolutions, war and exile. Can their love survive distance, danger, and differences? Duration: 85 minutes Rating: TBC Director: Janay Boulos, Abd Alkader Habak Year: 2026 Language: Arabic and English Subtitles: English https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=NUR79tVVOv0\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":85,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Birds of War\",\"instanceDates\":\"20 July-23 July\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"641601ADJGDKTSNNVGGTCSQMSCDLKGJDH\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-07-20T14:00:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-07-20T13:00:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-07-23T15:40:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-07-23T14:40:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false,\"attribute_Genre\":\"Cinema\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"Set on Vancouver Island in the late 1990s, Blue Heron follows eight-year-old Sasha and her Hungarian immigrant family as they attempt to build a new life, only to be destabilised by the increasingly dangerous behaviour of her older brother, Jeremy. Drawing on her own memories, filmmaker Sophy Romvari shapes a deeply personal portrait of childhood, family fractures, and the fragility of recollection. Duration: 90 minutes Rating: 12A Director: Sophy Romvari Cast: Eylul Guven, Edik Beddoes, Iringó Réti Year: 2026 Language: English and Hungairan Subtitles: English https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=6qAK9GwWRe0\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":91,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Blue Heron\",\"instanceDates\":\"24 July-31 July\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"641202ADTMRPSPRQVDMKSQCKGSMRQTHJT\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-07-24T13:15:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-07-24T12:15:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-07-31T13:00:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-07-31T12:00:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false,\"attribute_Genre\":\"Cinema\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"Book available for purchase: Not Only for Ourselves: The Past, Present and Future of JCORE\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\t<h2>Book: Not Only for Ourselves: The Past, Present and Future of JCORE</h2>Purchase your copy of the book with your ticket.\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":90,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Book: Not Only for Ourselves: The Past, Present and Future of JCORE\",\"instanceDates\":\"17 June-17 June\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"605201AMSDTLLRTRGHLBCSNKJBTBTMGHK\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-06-17T19:00:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-06-17T18:00:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-06-17T19:00:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-06-17T18:00:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Talks & Discussions\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Adult Education Programme\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false},{\"description\":\"Supplementary event for Robert Peston in conversation with Gabriel Pogrund. This is Robert Peston's book The Kill Switch. \",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\t<h2>Book: The Kill Switch by Robert Peston</h2>Purchase your copy of the book with your ticket (RRP £16.99).\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":75,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Book: The Kill Switch\",\"instanceDates\":\"16 July-16 July\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"630401APCJTLQLVBMRGCJQVRQQNQMSHGK\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-07-16T19:30:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-07-16T18:30:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-07-16T19:30:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-07-16T18:30:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Talks & Discussions\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false},{\"description\":\"1.15pm-2.15pm, Thursdays, in building, £8.50 per session // Join us for our monthly reading circle! Led by Naomi Grant, we will meet to explore, discuss and debate a range of fiction and non-fiction texts of your choice.   \\r\\n\\r\\nEach month, we choose the next book together during our session, so everyone has a voice in what we read. There’s no pressure to finish the book - enjoy it at your own pace and come ready to share whatever stood out to you.   \\r\\n\\r\\nFor the circle on 30th April, the group have chosen Women Without Men by Shahrnush Parsipur.\\r\\n\\r\\nHere’s what to do next:  \\r\\n\\r\\nGet your copy: Please aim to have your copy of Women Without Men before the discussion. You can order it online here or visit your local bookshop or library.\\r\\nRead at your pace: Feel free to read ahead, dip in and out, or go through it steadily.   \\r\\nInvite a friend: If you know someone who enjoys reading and lively discussions, let them know about our group.   \\r\\nBrainstorm: Come with a book recommendation you’d like to suggest to the group for the next session (Thursday 4 June). \\r\\nNaomi Grant is an artist and teacher living and working in London. She graduated from the University of Cambridge with a first-class degree in English before joining the Masterclass Programme at the Jerusalem Studio School in Israel. Following this, she completed the Postgraduate Programme at the Royal Drawing School in London. She is a regular contributor to the London Review of Books. \",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":60,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Books & Bagels Reading Circle Summer 2026\",\"instanceDates\":\"30 April-2 July\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"601201AQGQBJDHGBLRNLGLLMGCTMTMSNJ\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-04-30T13:15:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-04-30T12:15:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-07-02T13:15:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-07-02T12:15:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Classes & Courses\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Creative Courses\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"Naomi Grant\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false},{\"description\":\"Thursdays once per month, 1.15pm-2.15pm, £8.50 per session // Book for 19 Mar: My Grandmother Sends Her Regards and Apologies, written by Fredrik Backman and translated by Henning Koch // \\r\\n\\r\\n \\\"Join us for the launch of our new Books & Bagels reading circle. Led by Naomi Grant, we will meet once a month to explore, discuss and debate a range of fiction and non-fiction texts of your choice. Accompanied by delicious free bagels, everyone is welcome!  \\r\\n\\r\\nNaomi Grant is an artist and teacher living and working in London. She graduated from the University of Cambridge with a first-class degree in English before joining the Masterclass Programme at the Jerusalem Studio School in Israel. Following this, she completed the Postgraduate Programme at the Royal Drawing School in London. She is a regular contributor to the London Review of Books.; Join us for the launch of our new Books & Bagels reading circle. Led by Naomi Grant, we will meet once a month to explore, discuss and debate a range of fiction and non-fiction texts of your choice. Accompanied by delicious bagels, everyone is welcome!  \\r\\n\\r\\nNaomi Grant is an artist and teacher living and working in London. She graduated from the University of Cambridge with a first-class degree in English before joining the Masterclass Programme at the Jerusalem Studio School in Israel. Following this, she completed the Postgraduate Programme at the Royal Drawing School in London. She is a regular contributor to the London Review of Books.\\\"\\r\\n\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":60,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Books & Bagels Reading Circle Winter 2026\",\"instanceDates\":\"15 January-19 March\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"561002AHQQRDLKSPCVNKHCLDKHLVJQLCR\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-01-15T13:15:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-01-15T13:15:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-03-19T13:15:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-03-19T13:15:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Classes & Courses\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"True\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Creative Courses\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"Naomi Grant\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false},{\"description\":\"7.30-9.30pm, £30, building // Boris Giltburg is lauded across the globe as a deeply sensitive, insightful and\\r\\ncompelling interpreter for his narrative-driven approach to performance. Critics have\\r\\npraised his \\\"interplay of spiritual calm and emphatic engagement\\\" as \\\"gripping... one\\r\\ncould not wish for a more illuminating, lyrical or more richly phrased interpretation”\\r\\n(Suddeutsche Zeitung) // Part I \\r\\n\\r\\nJ.S. Bach (1685–1750)  \\r\\n\\r\\nSelections from The Well-Tempered Clavier, Book I \\r\\n\\r\\nLudwig van Beethoven (1770–1827) \\r\\n\\r\\nPiano Sonata No. 21 in C major, Op. 53 ‘The Waldstein’ \\r\\n\\r\\nI. Allegro con brio \\r\\n\\r\\nII. Introduzione: Adagio molto \\r\\n\\r\\nIII. Rondo: Allegretto moderato – Prestissimo  \\r\\n\\r\\nInterval of 25 minutes \\r\\n\\r\\nPart II \\r\\n\\r\\nSergei Rachmaninov (1873–1943) \\r\\n\\r\\nPreludes (A Selection) \\r\\n\\r\\nMaurice Ravel (1875–1937) \\r\\n\\r\\nGaspard de la nuit, M.55  \\r\\n\\r\\nI. Ondine \\r\\n\\r\\nII. Le Gibet \\r\\n\\r\\nIII. Scarbo \",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":110,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Boris Giltburg\",\"instanceDates\":\"30 September-30 September\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"646202ADLSCQLLHNDLQVJPGTSMRNPVPPD\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-09-30T19:30:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-09-30T18:30:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-09-30T19:30:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-09-30T18:30:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false,\"attribute_Genre\":\"Music\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Classical Music Series\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"7.30-8.30pm, building, £7, age 16+ // A thrilling new play full of humour that brings to the stage Israel’s most relatable conflicts, alongside moments of laughter, emotion, and self-discovery. \\r\\n\\r\\nAviel, a religious-nationalist, and Itai, a secular-liberal, are paired together for the final navigation exercise of their non-commissioned officer course — a mission that will soon lead them to become commanders in the IDF. \\r\\n\\r\\nWhat begins as a struggle between two soldiers from opposite sides of Israeli society gradually turns into a journey of mutual discovery and unity. \\r\\n\\r\\nThey learn that it is precisely their differences that allow them to grow and face the challenges ahead. \\r\\nThis play emphasises that the only way for us to thrive as a people is to be bound together as one nation. \\r\\n\\r\\nA new Israeli play written by two IDF combat commanders, Ben Zablodovsky and Shmulik Bahlou.\\r\\n\\r\\nPresented by the Israeli House. \",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":60,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Bound By Duty\",\"instanceDates\":\"1 February-1 February\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"568401ADPCLTVDQCTSQJCJCSTNLCHVVTM\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-02-01T19:30:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-02-01T19:30:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-02-01T19:30:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-02-01T19:30:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Families & Youth\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Festival of Spoken Ivrit\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false},{\"description\":\"Thursdays, 2.15pm-4pm, £147 for 11 week block // Discover the world’s most popular, social and strategic card game.  This 11-week course will teach you the basic principles of the game as well as tips to help you improve. Led by Victor Lesk, who works full time in bridge as an umpire, organiser and technologist.   By the end, you'll be ready to sit at any table with confidence and continue your bridge journey. // \\r\\nWhat You’ll Learn - By the end of this course, you’ll be able to: \\r\\nLearn how the game works: suits, ranks, tricks and the play sequence, Understand partnerships & scoring, Learn tips for success in social or club games // \\r\\n\\r\\nWho It’s For - Total beginners – no experience needed.  // \\r\\n\\r\\nYour Teacher - Victor is director of Bridge at the Royal Automobile Club and populariser of the well-known Café Bridge format which combines a bridge competition with a restaurant crawl, this 11-week course will help you learn the basics of bidding, play and strategy while having fun and meeting new people. No partner or experience needed - just your curiosity. // All materials are provided\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":105,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Bridge for Beginners\",\"instanceDates\":\"8 January-26 March\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"578201ARNTHJMQKJKDCCHQPVMLMGRQGCS\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-01-08T14:15:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-01-08T14:15:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-03-26T14:15:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-03-26T14:15:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Classes & Courses\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"True\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Body & Mind Courses\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"Victor Lesk\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false},{\"description\":\"Thursdays, 2.15pm - 4pm, £14 per session or £133 for the course // Join us for our intermediate Bridge class and take your Bridge game to the next level.  \\r\\n\\r\\nThis course will refine your Bridge skills and play. Through guided teaching and focused practice, you’ll learn how to play with confidence, instinct and strategies. \\r\\n\\r\\nWhat You’ll Learn \\r\\n\\r\\nBy the end of this course, you’ll be able to: \\r\\n\\r\\nLearn more sophisticated techniques to maximize trick-taking. \\r\\nStrengthen partnership communication through signalling and strategic planning. \\r\\nWho It’s For \\r\\n\\r\\nThose who already have some knowledge of the bridge game. \\r\\nThose who want to learn about the modern style of Acol bidding. \\r\\nThose who enjoy the social aspect of being part of a friendly group whose members are all keen to improve their game. \\r\\nYour Teacher \\r\\n\\r\\nAlan Brown moved to London four years ago. He was previously the joint owner of the successful Grimsby Bridge Academy with partner, England international Brian Smith. He taught bridge there for many years whist still pursuing his profession of school teacher. He has won numerous bridge trophies throughout a long-playing career and represented his county for many years. He loves teaching bridge. \\r\\n\\r\\nPractical Details\\r\\n\\r\\nAll materials are provided \\r\\nJW3 Accessibility information can be found here \",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":105,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Bridge: Intermediate\",\"instanceDates\":\"23 April-14 May\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"613401ATDNTTPPKHPLJMRBVHGRVJDDGNK\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-04-23T14:15:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-04-23T13:15:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-05-14T14:15:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-05-14T13:15:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Classes & Courses\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"True\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Adult Education\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"Alan Brown\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false},{\"description\":\"Tuesdays, 2.30pm-4.30pm, £133 for the 10-week course // Play and improve your skills at bridge, the world’s most popular, social and strategic card game. \\r\\n\\r\\nThis 10-week course will help you learn the basics of bidding, play and strategy while having fun and meeting new people. No partner or experience needed - just your curiosity.   \\r\\n\\r\\nExpand your comfort zone and take your place in the community of bridge-lovers. \\r\\n\\r\\nCourse Format\\r\\n\\r\\nPlay casual bridge with others who are a similar level and are eager to learn more\\r\\nAsk questions ad lib during the auction and play to the teacher on hand \\r\\nLearn tips for success in social or club games  \\r\\nWho It’s For  \\r\\n\\r\\nThose who know just the rules of bridge and some basic conventions \\r\\nThose who have more experience or are enrolled in JW3's intermediate course \\r\\nThose who played bridge in the past and want to get back in to it \\r\\nYour Teacher \\r\\n\\r\\nVictor is director of Bridge at the Royal Automobile Club and populariser of the well-known Café Bridge format which combines a bridge competition with a restaurant crawl, this 11-week course will help you learn the basics of bidding, play and strategy while having fun and meeting new people. No partner or experience needed - just your curiosity. \\r\\n\\r\\nPractical Details\\r\\n\\r\\nAll materials are provided \\r\\nJW3 Accessibility information can be found here \",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":120,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Bridge: Supervised Play\",\"instanceDates\":\"6 October-6 October\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"644202AMNHMNGQDPVCMDTMPLLSKKRHTMK\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-10-06T14:30:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-10-06T13:30:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-10-06T14:30:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-10-06T13:30:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false,\"attribute_Genre\":\"Classes & Courses\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"True\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"Tuesdays, 2.30pm-4.30pm, £14 per session, £133 for the course // Play and improve your skills at bridge, the world’s most popular, social and strategic card game.  \\r\\n\\r\\nExpand your comfort zone and take your place in the community of bridge-lovers. \\r\\n\\r\\nCourse Format\\r\\n\\r\\nPlay casual bridge with others who are a similar level and are eager to learn more\\r\\nAsk questions ad lib during the auction and play to the teacher on hand \\r\\nLearn tips for success in social or club games  \\r\\nWho It’s For  \\r\\n\\r\\nThose who know just the rules of bridge and some basic conventions \\r\\nThose who have more experience or are enrolled in JW3's intermediate course \\r\\nThose who played bridge in the past and want to get back in to it \\r\\nYour Teacher \\r\\n\\r\\nVictor is director of Bridge at the Royal Automobile Club and populariser of the well-known Café Bridge format which combines a bridge competition with a restaurant crawl, this 11-week course will help you learn the basics of bidding, play and strategy while having fun and meeting new people. No partner or experience needed - just your curiosity. \\r\\n\\r\\nPractical Details\\r\\n\\r\\nAll materials are provided \\r\\nJW3 Accessibility information can be found here \",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":120,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Bridge: Supervised Play Spring 2026\",\"instanceDates\":\"21 April-14 July\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"613201ADPBTPQCLMDJNGDTKQPSBVCLBJQ\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-04-21T14:30:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-04-21T13:30:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-07-14T14:30:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-07-14T13:30:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false,\"attribute_Genre\":\"Classes & Courses\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"True\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Adult Education\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"Victor Lesk\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"A bold documentary portrait of the inimitable singer, songwriter and icon: Marianne Faithfull.\\r\\nA survivor, provocateur, and true original, Marianne has spent more than six decades defying expectations — releasing over 35 albums while constantly reinventing herself. Made with her full involvement, Broken English is an intimate and unflinching exploration of a fractured yet unbreakable life shaped by fame, creativity and relentless public scrutiny.\\r\\nThe film unfolds within The Ministry of Not Forgetting — an imagined, cinematic institution where memory and mythology collide. Featuring a cast led by Tilda Swinton and George MacKay, alongside Sophia Di Martino, Zawe Ashton and Calvin Demba. With powerful, intimate performances from friends and collaborators including Nick Cave & Warren Ellis, Jehnny Beth, Courtney Love, Suki Waterhouse and Beth Orton.\\r\\nBroken English is a genre-defying act of resilience and rebellion. Marianne Faithfull’s final fearless declaration — her defiant swan song. | Duration: 1h 38m, Rating: 15 Credits\\r\\nRating: 15\\r\\nGenre: Biography, Documentary, Music\\r\\nDirectors: Ian Forsyth, Jane Pollard\\r\\nStars: Marianne Faithful, Tilda Swinton, George MacKay https://youtu.be/k7h6QkAfhjU?si=TOVOtr5YLHCVva37\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":99,\"imageUrl\":\"https://system.spektrix.com/jw3/files/1f6fe247-db09-4c8b-a774-2d0f07a80ecf.jpg\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Broken English\",\"instanceDates\":\"14 May-17 May\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"https://system.spektrix.com/jw3/files/1f6fe247-db09-4c8b-a774-2d0f07a80ecf-thumbnail.jpg\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"623601ARTVNQDCDHQJNGJPSJKHHBGKQRG\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-05-14T10:30:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-05-14T09:30:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-05-17T13:30:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-05-17T12:30:00Z\",\"altText\":\"Broken English\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Cinema\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false},{\"description\":\"Anand, a 30-something city dweller compelled to spend a 10-day mourning period for his father in the rugged countryside of western India, tenderly bonds with a local farmer who is struggling to stay unmarried. As the mourning ends, forcing his return, Anand must decide the fate of his relationship born under duress. Duration: 112 minutes Rating: 15 Director: Rohan Kanawade Cast: Bhushaan Manoj, Suraaj Suman, Jayshri Jagtap Year: 2025 Language: Marathi Subtitles: English https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ssjeFH1oyxY&pp=ygUUY2FjdHVzIHBlYXJzIHRyYWlsZXI%3D\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":112,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Cactus Pears\",\"instanceDates\":\"3 July-14 July\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"640202APVHTKQSNLCSJCTMBRBKBJTGMKB\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-07-03T10:30:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-07-03T09:30:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-07-14T10:30:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-07-14T09:30:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false,\"attribute_Genre\":\"Cinema\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"7pm-10pm, £18 // A sharp, and hilariously awkward comedy. Aviram Zissu, the Special Ops unit’s self-important, rule-dodging sergeant, has spent decades perfecting a cushy, semi-corrupt double life on base. His carefully built world unravels when his insecure son, Rani, is drafted as the new canteen operator. Stuck in a unit he never meant to join, and serving under the father he can’t stand, Rani faces a nightmare of drills, egos, and family baggage. In a place built for action heroes, the real battle is father vs. son.\\r\\n\\r\\nPremiere screening of three episodes, followed by a Q&A with Liraz Chamami & Eliana Beiker\\r\\n\\r\\nIn collaboration with SERET intl. Israeli film festival\\r\\nDistributed by yes. Studios\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":170,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Canteen Commando\",\"instanceDates\":\"24 February-24 February\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"583001ANBNMMHJKCDSPLBKNTQMKRRDQDV\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-02-24T19:00:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-02-24T19:00:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-02-24T19:00:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-02-24T19:00:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Talks & Discussions\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false},{\"description\":\"7.15-8.45pm, building, £35 including a signed copy of Miriam’s Table – the authentic Bukharian Cookbook // Introducing Lilian Cordell, Jewish Chef and Author of Miriam’s Table.\\r\\n\\r\\nSharing with you the stories from her mother’s recipes that were never written, and now lovingly noted down in her book for the next generation.\\r\\n\\r\\nA menu of Dushpara, the vegetarian, option. This is the classic ravioli or tortellini with mushrooms then cooked in a delicious tomato, mushroom and chickpea broth.\\r\\n\\r\\nWatch how it is made and listen to the stories and of course taste the delicious result, in our demo kitchen.\\r\\n\\r\\nPlease note the food is Kosher but not supervised\\r\\n\\r\\nEnding with a signed copy of the book\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":90,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Celebrating Bukharian Food: A Cooking Class\",\"instanceDates\":\"3 December-3 December\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"637802ALMKSCJPKDRBNTSQHCJQSPKVLMV\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-12-03T14:30:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-12-03T14:30:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-12-03T19:15:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-12-03T19:15:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false,\"attribute_Genre\":\"Talks & Discussions\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Adult Education\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"Lilian Cordell\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"10.30am-12noon, Thursdays, building // £54 for the course // This course celebrates the breakthroughs that transformed films and how we experience them.  \\r\\n\\r\\nFocusing on landmark transformations in sound, colour and vision, we will explore how each breakthrough expanded what cinema could express, who it could reach and how audiences could see, think & feel.  \\r\\n\\r\\nThrough iconic films and class discussion, join Julia to learn about cinema’s past and its enduring source of inspiration, creativity and cultural power. \\r\\n\\r\\nWhat You’ll Learn: \\r\\n\\r\\nIdentify pivotal moments that transformed cinema history \\r\\n\\r\\nUnderstand how sound, colour, and vision reshaped cinematic storytelling \\r\\n\\r\\nBuild a sense of community through discussing cinema’s impact.  \\r\\n\\r\\nWho It’s For: \\r\\n\\r\\nThis course is for anyone who loves film and wants to understand cinema better. Whether you’re interested in film and the arts or simply curious about how cinema became what it is today, please join us. No prior film knowledge is needed - just an open mind and a love of watching films. \\r\\n\\r\\nWho Delivers It? \\r\\n\\r\\nDr Julia Wagner is a lecturer and writer specialising in Jewish-interest film and television. She holds a PhD in Film Studies and is a member of the London Film Critics’ Circle. Her writing has been published widely, including by the BFI, Sight & Sound and The Jewish Chronicle. From 2017-23, she curated JW3/BFI archive project, Jewish Britain on Film. Julia founded Casting Jewish consultancy and is author of Hester Street (BFI Film Classics/Bloomsbury, forthcoming 2025). \",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":90,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Celebrating Cinema's Defining Moments\",\"instanceDates\":\"25 June-25 June\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"600801ARCPHRCJDJBLMRNGVGVNTHVMRRJ\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-06-25T10:30:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-06-25T09:30:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-06-25T10:30:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-06-25T09:30:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Classes & Courses\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"True\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"History & Politics Courses\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"Dr Julia Wagner\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false},{\"description\":\"7.30-9.30pm, building, £22 // 1st half - 40min (7:30-8:10pm)\\r\\nInterval - 15min (8:10-8:25pm)\\r\\n2nd half - 40min (8:25-9:05pm) // An evening of live music and performance with West End actors to celebrate the Brill Building Sound. \\r\\n\\r\\nThis era of new music included many great Jewish songwriters and Producers  including pairings such as Gerry Goffin and Carole King, Barry Mann and Cynthia Weil and Geoff Barry and Emily Greenwich. The work shaped a new era of pop music with greater melodical sophistication, building on the established work and style of the ‘Tin Pan Alley’ songwriters. \",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":90,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Celebrating the Brill Building Sound\",\"instanceDates\":\"15 February-15 February\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"565601AJCCCMPSMHQDJPVPLPDPBHLBVBJ\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-02-15T19:30:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-02-15T19:30:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-02-15T19:30:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-02-15T19:30:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Music\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Arts & Culture\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false},{\"description\":\"7.30pm-9.30pm, £15, in building // Join us in the JW3 Cinema for a special evening with electronic composer and Klezmer-raised artist Chaia, as she bridges the past and the dancefloor.\\r\\n\\r\\nPerforming live from her Roland sampler, Chaia blends archival Yiddish recordings with the hypnotic pulse of techno and ambient frameworks. This unique event features a live performance integrating accordion, vocals, and electronic samples, interspersed with an intimate conversation exploring her contemporary takes on traditional pieces and her extensive research with historical archives.\\r\\n\\r\\nRaised in the Klezmer tradition and mentored by Yiddish music pioneers, Chaia works closely with institutions like the YIVO Institute and the Yiddish Book Center to resurrect ancestral sounds within global rave culture. Don’t miss this deeply ritualistic exploration of intergenerational memory, electronic innovation, and cultural liberation.\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":120,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Chaia: Yiddish Electronic (Live & In Conversation)\",\"instanceDates\":\"28 June-28 June\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"626601AMGLDPBMTNBDGKMTBQVKGBDCNTN\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-06-28T19:30:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-06-28T18:30:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-06-28T19:30:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-06-28T18:30:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":true,\"attribute_Genre\":\"Music\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"14:00 // 29 Nov 2026 // Adults £10, Children £12, babes in arms go free // Celebrate the season with our Chanukah Family Extravaganza – a day of festive fun for children and families.  Enjoy a building full of creativity, movement and music, with hands on activities and plenty of chances to play and explore.\\r\\n\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":180,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Chanukah Funukah 2026\",\"instanceDates\":\"29 November-29 November\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"632601ATPHKQKLCLJJRBQJCQBQJGTRDMB\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-11-29T14:00:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-11-29T14:00:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-11-29T14:00:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-11-29T14:00:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false,\"attribute_Genre\":\"Families & Youth\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"2pm-3.15pm, £20, in building, Thursday 18 June 2026 // Cher is one of a kind: a singer, actress, fashionista, gossip magnet, and LGBTQ+ icon who has been a star since the mid-1960s. Her extraordinary career includes a multitude of triumphs and failures from marriages to television programmes to films, albums, and concert tours. Throughout it all, Cher has held fast to her identity while also reinventing her image and career, defying those that wrote her off at numerous times in her career. She has hosted one of the top television shows in America (The Sonny and Cher Show), released best-selling albums, appeared on Broadway, won an Academy Award (for Moonstruck), advocated for political causes, fundraised for charitable foundations, and has written part one of her memoir (Cher: The Memoir, Part One; part two will be released in 2026). \\r\\n\\r\\n \\r\\n\\r\\nThis talk will focus on Cher’s extensive multimedia career, considering how she rose from being part of the Sonny and Cher duo in her twenties to becoming a film and solo music star in her thirties and forties to her greatest ‘comeback’ in her fifties (with the single, ‘Believe’) to her contemporary icon status as she turns 80 in 2026. \\r\\n\\r\\n \\r\\n\\r\\nDr Julie Lobalzo Wright is an Associate Professor in Film and Television Studies at the University of Warwick. She has taught and researched film and television stardom for many years, publishing work and giving talks on various stars, including Judy Garland, Elvis Presley, David Bowie and Barbra Streisand. Her next project is a book length study of Barbra Streisand that will focus on the authorship of her star image throughout her career. \",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":75,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Cher: Multimedia star, Cultural Icon, Living Legend\",\"instanceDates\":\"18 June-18 June\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"593601ACDVCJVCCRKQHGJGDKTKQRGLPDN\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-06-18T14:00:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-06-18T13:00:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-06-18T14:00:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-06-18T13:00:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Talks & Discussions\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Adult Education\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"Dr Julie Lobalzo Wright\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false},{\"description\":\"7-8pm, £10, building, age 13+ // Set against the haunting landscapes of the Łódź Ghetto, the second largest ghetto in Nazi-occupied Poland, and Chełmno nad Nerem, the first Nazi extermination camp, Chicken Soup with Tears explores life and loss in the shadow of Auschwitz.   Told through two interwoven narratives, the novel follows Zenon, a disillusioned teacher searching for meaning within a fractured society, and Mendel, a survivor whose journey through persecution, from Belgium to the Łódź Ghetto and Chełmno, has profoundly shaped his understanding of the world.   As their lives intersect, the story becomes an exploration of memory, moral awakening, and the fragile yet enduring power of compassion.   Author Alan Walters will be in conversation, reflecting on the historical inspiration behind the novel, the characters at its heart, and the questions the story leaves us with today.   About the author:   Born in East London, Alan Walters studied Russian and History at London and Cambridge universities before a long teaching career across the UK and Europe. His deep interest in the Holocaust led him to focus on the fate of Jews in lesser-known extermination camps, particularly Chelmno nad Nerem, the first of its kind. His writing is driven by a commitment to uncovering and preserving these lesser known yet important histories. \",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":60,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Chicken Soup with Tears\",\"instanceDates\":\"7 September-7 September\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"638401ABQTPQQSLJBBHDRCTLCSTSTNLST\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-09-07T19:00:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-09-07T18:00:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-09-07T19:00:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-09-07T18:00:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false,\"attribute_Genre\":\"Talks & Discussions\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Holocaust Learning\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"Alan Walters\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"7.30-8.45pm, £20, building // We are delighted to welcome acclaimed historian Marc David Baer for the launch of his latest book, Children of Abraham. From the prophet Muhammad's first interactions with Jewish Arabs in the seventh century to the ongoing conflict in the Middle East, this timely and urgent new book presents a nuanced analysis of Muslim-Jewish relations. Spanning 1400 years of history,  Bauer gives a balanced view of the extensive conflict and cooperation between these two communities, whose relations will continue to shape global politics for decades to come.\\r\\n\\r\\n \\\"A revelatory picture of both coexistence and conflict ... a story so little known and totally relevant to our world today.\\\"\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nBio\\r\\n\\r\\nMarc David Baer (PhD, History, University of Chicago, 2001) is Professor of International History at the London School of Economics and Political Science. His books have won the Albert Hourani Prize (2008) and the Dr. Sona Aronian Book Prize for Excellence in Armenian Studies (2020), and shortlisted for the Wolfson History Prize (2022)\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":75,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Children of Abraham: The Story of Muslim-Jewish Relations\",\"instanceDates\":\"22 September-22 September\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"639001AQVRJHLJTMDMNPVDGLNQKKVRMJQ\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-09-22T19:30:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-09-22T18:30:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-09-22T19:30:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-09-22T18:30:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false,\"attribute_Genre\":\"Talks & Discussions\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Adult Education\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"Marc David Baer\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"7.30-9pm, hybrid, £20 // To celebrate the paperback version of Chutzpah: A memoir of faith, sexuality and daring to stay we are delighted to welcome author Yehudis Fletcher in conversation with Toby Lichtig\\r\\n\\r\\nAs the daughter of a rabbi raised in an Orthodox Jewish community, Yehudis struggled to conform to the strict expectations placed upon her and her siblings. Outspoken, curious and desperate to know more about G-d, she felt fenced in by what she saw as arbitrary rules and questions left unanswered.\\r\\n\\r\\nAs Yehudis grew older, these restrictions intensified and her questions for G-d hung heavier than ever. Repeatedly let down by those who were supposed to protect her and pushed on a path that seemed to take her further away from who she really was, she began to yearn for a life in which she could embrace all facets of herself.\\r\\n\\r\\nWhen Yehudis’s sexuality came up against the expectations of her family and her community, the pressure to inhabit a binary position reached fever pitch. Confronted with either losing the faith she loved or losing herself, Yehudis made the most daring decision of all: she decided to stay.\\r\\n\\r\\nBooks will be available for purchase and signing on the night.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nToby Lichtig is a journalist, broadcaster and the Fiction and Politics Editor of the Times Literary Supplement. He writes for a range of publications, including the TLS, Wall Street Journal, Jewish Chronicle and New Humanist, and has appeared as a guest critic on various television and radio programmes. He has also worked as a documentary producer, specialising in arts and serious factual.\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":90,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Chutzpah: Yehudis Fletcher in conversation with Toby Lichtig\",\"instanceDates\":\"26 March-26 March\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"560801ACKPGTLQVPMLDCQBLJKLDNJRKQQ\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-03-26T19:30:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-03-26T19:30:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-03-26T19:30:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-03-26T19:30:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Talks & Discussions\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Adult Education\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"Yehudis Fletcher\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false},{\"description\":\"Approx 2 hours including interval // Preview Tickets: 7 - 9 December, £15 per person // Off Peak Tickets: 11-19 December & 2-4 January  £17 child & £27 adult // Peak Tickets: 20 - 31 December £20 child & £32 adult // Relaxed Performance Dates\\r\\n\\r\\nRelaxed performances are ideal for people with learning disabilities or autism, or anyone who would benefit from a more relaxed environment.\\r\\n\\r\\nThese performances are of course still open for anyone to book. During our relaxed performances, we will be making the following changes:\\r\\n\\r\\nHouse lights remaining switched on at a low level throughout the performance\\r\\nNoise from the performance will be reduced throughout the performance\\r\\nNo sudden flashes or lighting changes\\r\\nRelaxed Performances will be shown on the following dates and times:\\r\\n\\r\\nWednesday 17 December @ 6pm; \\r\\nMonday 22 December @ 1pm; \\r\\nWednesday 31 December @ 11am\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":120,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Cinderella and the Matzo Ball\",\"instanceDates\":\"2 January-4 January\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"472801AGBRGQGRPKMJNPTHSCLTMJDNMLP\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-01-02T11:00:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-01-02T11:00:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-01-04T18:00:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-01-04T18:00:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Special Events\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Chanukah\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false},{\"description\":\"Thu 05 February 2026 // 19:30 // Curious about how much we should trust artificial intelligence? Join us for an eye-opening evening with Prof. Claudia Goldman-Shenhar, Associate Professor at the Hebrew University of Jerusalem, as she explores how humans interact with and learn to trust intelligent machines.\\r\\nDiscover how AI shapes the way we make decisions, how trust can be built (and lost) between humans and algorithms, and what it really takes to make AI systems work for society rather than against it.\\r\\nExpect an engaging, thought-provoking talk that blends psychology, technology, and ethics — all delivered by one of the leading voices in human–AI interaction.\\r\\nWhether you’re an AI enthusiast, tech sceptic, or just curious about our digital future, this is a session you won’t want to miss.\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":75,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Click here, if you’re not a robot: AI in today's age\",\"instanceDates\":\"5 February-5 February\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"574801ACVJRBQHMLMQBGHDKBLHPBVVCPJ\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-02-05T19:30:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-02-05T19:30:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-02-05T19:30:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-02-05T19:30:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Talks & Discussions\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Adult Education\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"Prof. Claudia Goldman-Shenhar\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false},{\"description\":\"Brought together by the unexpected inheritance of an abandoned house in rural Normandy, four cousins discover they share a mysterious family history. In 1895, their ancestor Adèle, then aged 21, leaves her hometown to search for her mother in Paris. She discovers a city on the cusp of modernity, bustling with new-found avant-garde creativity, with the rise of photography and the birth of Impressionist painting. As her descendants retrace her steps, they unravel Adèle's surprising past. The two timelines of 1895 and 2024 intertwine and collide, confronting the cousins’ contemporary attitudes with life in late 19th century Paris, leaving everyone’s future forever changed. | This film is in French with English subtitles. | Duration: 2h 4m, Rating: 15 Credits\\r\\nRating: 15\\r\\nGenre: Comedy, Drama\\r\\nDirector: Cédric Klapisch\\r\\nStars: Suzanne Lindon, Abraham Wapler, Vincent Macaigne https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=nthdYa9sSXE&pp=ygUaY29sb3VycyBvZiB0aW1lIHVrIHRyYWlsZXI%3D\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":124,\"imageUrl\":\"https://system.spektrix.com/jw3/files/f1b94295-ba3c-4e61-a0d4-cac77cc11f16.jpg\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Colours of Time\",\"instanceDates\":\"17 May-21 May\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"https://system.spektrix.com/jw3/files/f1b94295-ba3c-4e61-a0d4-cac77cc11f16-thumbnail.jpg\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"623801ARNMNCSBVCPDRDDRCRMVTBSJJTC\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-05-17T11:00:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-05-17T10:00:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-05-21T11:00:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-05-21T10:00:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Cinema\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false},{\"description\":\"Invitation only event // The climate and nature crisis is an existential threat to our way of life. As a Jewish community, our foundational values compel us to care deeply about the vulnerable, the prospects for future generations, and the preservation of our Earth, and all of this is in jeopardy. At the same time, we have the opportunity to think positively and shape the transition to a more sustainable world.\\r\\n \\r\\nThe National Emergency Briefing campaign seeks to raise awareness of these issues, and we are keen to participate. We invite you to join us for a private screening of the 50-minute National Emergency Briefing film, followed by a facilitated discussion with fellow community leaders. The core purpose of this gathering is to explore what the film tells us and, crucially, how we could best engage the wider Jewish community on this vitally important issue.\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":105,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Community Crises: a screening and strategy discussion\",\"instanceDates\":\"23 June-23 June\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"626801ASDQKNJGTPQQJQSCHNNLRTCMBDK\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-06-23T19:00:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-06-23T18:00:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-06-23T19:00:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-06-23T18:00:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Talks & Discussions\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false},{\"description\":\"2pm-3pm, free, in building // Yoga for everyone! \\r\\n\\r\\nLed by Yael Flexer, join our free trial Yoga class designed for all ages and abilities. Move, stretch, and breathe at your own pace in a friendly & supportive environment. No experience needed - just bring yourself and an open mind. \\r\\n\\r\\nIn this class, you will: \\r\\n\\r\\nStretch and strengthen your body. \\r\\n\\r\\nImprove balance and flexibility, helping you feel more agile and confident. \\r\\n\\r\\nLearn mindful breathing and relaxation techniques to reduce stress and boost focus. \\r\\n\\r\\nPractice at your own pace in a supportive & judgment-free environment. \\r\\n\\r\\n \\r\\n\\r\\nYael Flexer is an award-winning choreographer, teacher and artistic director of Flexer & Sandiland, creating internationally touring dance and digital dance works. Yael is also senior lecturer and Reader in Dance at The University of Chichester, where she curates the 'What Dance Can Do' conference on intergenerational and 60+ dance.  \\r\\n\\r\\nYael is currently training to be a Yoga teacher with Intelligent Yoga, a Scaravelli inspired Yoga Teacher training and is British Wheel of Yoga student teacher member \",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":60,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Community Yoga: Free Trial\",\"instanceDates\":\"5 March-5 March\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"585401ABSDDMTCLVGQDHDLQLQKGGKVTMJ\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-03-05T14:00:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-03-05T14:00:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-03-05T14:00:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-03-05T14:00:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Classes & Courses\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false},{\"description\":\"10.30-11.30am, 1-2pm, building, £15 for baby and carer, age 0-3 // Two sheep think they know everything about sleep. \\r\\nThey’re experts in the field. \\r\\nBut tonight they’re wide awake.\\r\\n​\\r\\nSnuggle up and join two sheep on a journey through the joys and frustrations of everything bedtime. A touching, musical adventure filled with sensory play, for 0-3 year olds and their (very tired) grown ups.\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":60,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Counting Sheeps\",\"instanceDates\":\"10 March-10 March\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"567401ATVVJKVPLPVHVSPVMQVHMVHTQNR\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-03-10T10:30:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-03-10T10:30:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-03-10T13:00:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-03-10T13:00:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Families & Youth\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Families\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false},{\"description\":\"11:30 // 8 Nov 2026 // £14 // Get cosy ahead of Chanukah at this relaxed candle painting workshop. Brighten up the winter with your own colourful designs and spend the afternoon meeting new people over a warm, creative activity.\\r\\n\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":120,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Craft Café: Candle Painting\",\"instanceDates\":\"8 November-8 November\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"633401ADLVRLLCDBGCKHLQMCBMCRPBGJK\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-11-08T11:30:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-11-08T11:30:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-11-08T11:30:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-11-08T11:30:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false,\"attribute_Genre\":\"Young Professionals\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"MANOMAKE\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"10am-12noon, £10, in building // Crossing Borders: A Conversation on Co-Productions\\r\\nWith Eran Riklis & Jonny Persey\\r\\nHow are international co-productions shaping the future of storytelling?\\r\\n\\r\\nDate & Time: Friday 8 May, 10:00 AM\\r\\nLocation: NW London (exact address will be shared upon registration)\\r\\nJoin renowned filmmaker Eran Riklis and Executive Producer Jonny Persey for an in-depth conversation on navigating global partnerships, creative collaboration, and what it takes to bring films to life across borders, with insights into co-production links between the UK and Israel.\\r\\n\\r\\nLight refreshments will be served.\\r\\n\\r\\nAbout the Speakers\\r\\n\\r\\nEran Riklis is one of Israel’s most acclaimed filmmakers. His award-winning films were released worldwide to critical acclaim and commercial success and were presented in numerous film festivals including Berlin, Venice, Toronto, Telluride, Locarno, London, San Sebastian and many more. His films include Reading Lolita in Tehran (2025), The Syrian Bride, Lemon Tree, The Human Resources Manager, A Borrowed Identity, Zaytoun, Spider in the Web, Shelter, Playoff, Cup Final, Zohar, Vulcan Junction and more. He is a graduate of the National Film School, Beaconsfield, UK. \\r\\n\\r\\nJonny Persey is an experienced film producer and educator. He is Chair of MetFilm Studio, a boutique, vertically integrated film company, which produces, distributes and sells fiction and documentary films for cinema and television. Over a period of some thirty years, Jonny has produced or exec-produced over 30 feature films and television programmes as well as numerous short form projects. His credits reveal an eclectic mix of thought-provoking, inquisitive and entertaining titles, with numerous commercial successes, critical accolades, award wins and festival prizes. Meanwhile, as Director of MetFilm School, he is the proud custodian of the learning journey of over 17,000 graduates over the last two decades, and an unashamed show-off about their success in the industry.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n*This event is presented in collaboration with FIC - Friends of Israeli Culture, with a special thanks to the Cultural Department of the Israeli Embassy in London.\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":120,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Crossing Borders: A Conversation on Co-Productions\",\"instanceDates\":\"8 May-8 May\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"621801AVTRQQGDHBNNNVJVTMGKMKJMKCM\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-05-08T10:00:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-05-08T09:00:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-05-08T10:00:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-05-08T09:00:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Arts & Culture\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Seret Film Festival\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false},{\"description\":\"Test course\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":120,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"CultureSuite Test Course\",\"instanceDates\":\"18 May-18 May\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"589201AQQVGTSLHVPQSQPMKRQVKDCLVGB\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-05-18T10:30:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-05-18T09:30:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-05-18T10:30:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-05-18T09:30:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Classes & Courses\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false},{\"description\":\"Cup Final (Gmar Gavi’a) (1991) is a powerful, genre-bending war drama from early in Eran Riklis’s celebrated career, blending suspense, character study and humanity in an unforgettable story set during Israel’s 1982 invasion of Lebanon. The film follows Cohen, a young Israeli soldier taken hostage by a small group of Palestinian fighters as the conflict unfolds. \\r\\nAmid the rubble and tension of war, an extraordinary and surprising connection emerges: both Cohen and his captors share an ardent love for football — especially their support for the Italian team in the 1982 FIFA World Cup — and this common passion gradually breaks down the barriers of nationalism and enmity. \\r\\nFeaturing a standout performance by Muhammad Bakri as the Palestinian commander Ziad, this heartfelt tribute celebrates Bakri’s legacy and Riklis’s gift for portraying the fragile, often ironic humanity that can arise even in the most brutal of conflicts. | This film is in English, Hebrew and Arabic with English subtitles. | Duration: 1h 10m\\r\\n\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":110,\"imageUrl\":\"https://system.spektrix.com/jw3/files/b84d4a09-1e0a-4496-bb7a-3a17e499bfa8.jpg\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Cup Final + Q&A\",\"instanceDates\":\"10 May-10 May\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"https://system.spektrix.com/jw3/files/b84d4a09-1e0a-4496-bb7a-3a17e499bfa8-thumbnail.jpg\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"618401ATKRMJBMSHLNMBRGTNLNTSSKKBP\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-05-10T17:30:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-05-10T16:30:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-05-10T17:30:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-05-10T16:30:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Cinema\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Seret Film Festival\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false},{\"description\":\"Mondays, 2-3.30pm, £20 per session or £180 for the 10-week course // Join Paula Kitching as she brilliantly and irreverently tackles current affairs each week. Topics are chosen by you and the major issues of the day.  \\r\\n\\r\\nWhat You’ll Learn: \\r\\n\\r\\nBy the end of this course, you will be able to: \\r\\n\\r\\nDevelop a deeper understanding of UK & global current affairs  \\r\\n\\r\\nRead a variety of news stories, analyzing different perspectives, viewpoints, and media coverage.  \\r\\n\\r\\nParticipate in engaging and informed discussions.  \\r\\n\\r\\nWho It’s For: \\r\\n\\r\\nThis course is for anyone who wants to better understand the major political, social and economic issues affecting our world.  No prior knowledge of politics or international relations is needed – just a desire to learn and engage in conversation.  \\r\\n\\r\\nWho Delivers It: \\r\\n\\r\\nPaula Kitching is a historian and writer. She is the project manager and historian for a project that is building a digital archive on the Jewish experience of the First World War. Paula is a regular contributor to the Historian magazine of the Historical Association and has written articles for commemorative publications for the Royal British Legion, the MOD and JW3. \",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":90,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Current Affairs for Autumn 2026 [In Building]\",\"instanceDates\":\"5 October-14 December\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"643402ASSSJJKSTGKHCMJLBJKJMDSKQQG\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-10-05T14:00:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-10-05T13:00:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-12-14T14:00:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-12-14T14:00:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false,\"attribute_Genre\":\"Classes & Courses\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"Paula Kitching\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"Mondays, 2-3.30pm, £20 per session or £180 for the 10-week course // Join Paula Kitching as she brilliantly and irreverently tackles current affairs each week. Topics are chosen by you and the major issues of the day. What You’ll Learn: By the end of this course, you will be able to: Develop a deeper understanding of UK & global current affairs Read a variety of news stories, analyzing different perspectives, viewpoints, and media coverage. Participate in engaging and informed discussions. Who It’s For: This course is for anyone who wants to better understand the major political, social and economic issues affecting our world. No prior knowledge of politics or international relations is needed – just a desire to learn and engage in conversation. Who Delivers It: Paula Kitching is a historian and writer. She is the project manager and historian for a project that is building a digital archive on the Jewish experience of the First World War. Paula is a regular contributor to the Historian magazine of the Historical Association and has written articles for commemorative publications for the Royal British Legion, the MOD and JW3.\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":90,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Current Affairs for Autumn 2026 [Online]\",\"instanceDates\":\"5 October-14 December\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"643601AMDLVBDRNBTGTGGKBCGDPRTGGHG\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-10-05T14:00:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-10-05T13:00:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-12-14T14:00:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-12-14T14:00:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false,\"attribute_Genre\":\"Classes & Courses\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"Paula Kitching\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"Mondays, 2pm-3.30pm, hybrid // £20 per session, £180 for 10 weeks // Join Paula Kitching as she brilliantly and irreverently tackles current affairs each week. Topics are chosen by you and the major issues of the day.  \\r\\n\\r\\nWhat You’ll Learn: \\r\\n\\r\\nBy the end of this course, you will be able to: \\r\\n\\r\\nDevelop a deeper understanding of UK & global current affairs  \\r\\n\\r\\nRead a variety of news stories, analysing different perspectives, viewpoints and media coverage.  \\r\\n\\r\\nParticipate in engaging and informed discussions.  \\r\\n\\r\\nWho It’s For: \\r\\n\\r\\nThis course is for anyone who wants to better understand the major political, social and economic issues affecting our world.  No prior knowledge of politics or international relations is needed – just a desire to learn and engage in conversation.  \\r\\n\\r\\nWho Delivers It: \\r\\n\\r\\nPaula Kitching is a historian and writer. She is the project manager and historian for a project that is building a digital archive on the Jewish experience of the First World War. Paula is a regular contributor to the Historian magazine of the Historical Association and has written articles for commemorative publications for the Royal British Legion, the MOD and JW3. \",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":90,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Current Affairs for Summer 2026 [In Building]\",\"instanceDates\":\"20 April-13 July\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"597001AVMGDTQHJNHTGCLNSLHQPBLMHMC\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-04-20T14:00:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-04-20T13:00:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-07-13T14:00:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-07-13T13:00:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Classes & Courses\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"True\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"History & Politics Courses\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"Paula Kitching\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false},{\"description\":\"Mondays, 2pm-3.30pm, hybrid // £20 per session, £180 for 10 weeks // Join Paula Kitching as she brilliantly and irreverently tackles current affairs each week. Topics are chosen by you and the major issues of the day. What You’ll Learn: By the end of this course, you will be able to: Develop a deeper understanding of UK & global current affairs Read a variety of news stories, analysing different perspectives, viewpoints and media coverage. Participate in engaging and informed discussions. Who It’s For: This course is for anyone who wants to better understand the major political, social and economic issues affecting our world. No prior knowledge of politics or international relations is needed – just a desire to learn and engage in conversation. Who Delivers It: Paula Kitching is a historian and writer. She is the project manager and historian for a project that is building a digital archive on the Jewish experience of the First World War. Paula is a regular contributor to the Historian magazine of the Historical Association and has written articles for commemorative publications for the Royal British Legion, the MOD and JW3.\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":90,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Current Affairs for Summer 2026 [Online]\",\"instanceDates\":\"20 April-13 July\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"597201AJHLPHDTTGHNPDRSRPSCQKBMJNT\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-04-20T14:00:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-04-20T13:00:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-07-13T14:00:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-07-13T13:00:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Classes & Courses\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"True\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"History & Politics Courses\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"Paula Kitching\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false},{\"description\":\"Mondays, 2pm-3.15pm, £20 per session, or £198 for 11 weeks, hybrid // Join Paula as she brilliantly and irreverently tackles current affairs each week. Topics are chosen by you and the issues of the day. Paula is a historian and writer. She is the project manager and historian for a project that is building a digital archive on the Jewish experience of the First World War. Paula is a regular contributor to the Historian magazine of the Historical Association and has written articles for commemorative publications for the Royal British Legion, the MOD and JW3.\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":90,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Current Affairs for Winter 2026 [In-Building]\",\"instanceDates\":\"5 January-23 March\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"559001ADHHKRPVGVVGSVPGSQVQGPNMMRB\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-01-05T14:00:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-01-05T14:00:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-03-23T14:00:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-03-23T14:00:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Classes & Courses\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"True\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"History & Politics Courses\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"Paula Kitching\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false},{\"description\":\"Mondays, 2pm-3.15pm, £20 per session, or £198 for 11 weeks, hybrid // Join Paula as she brilliantly and irreverently tackles current affairs each week. Topics are chosen by you and the issues of the day. Paula is a historian and writer. She is the project manager and historian for a project that is building a digital archive on the Jewish experience of the First World War. Paula is a regular contributor to the Historian magazine of the Historical Association and has written articles for commemorative publications for the Royal British Legion, the MOD and JW3.\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":90,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Current Affairs for Winter 2026 [Online]\",\"instanceDates\":\"5 January-23 March\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"558801ADNHNHQCGLCVLQHKJPQGSPLNMMR\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-01-05T14:00:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-01-05T14:00:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-03-23T14:00:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-03-23T14:00:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Classes & Courses\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"True\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"History & Politics Courses\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"Paula Kitching\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false},{\"description\":\"This is a venue hire, customers should email mayasamson@sky.com directly to book // Get ready for a high-energy, feel-good class!\\r\\nStep into a safe and supportive space where you can learn, grow, and challenge yourself—free from judgment and pressure.\\r\\nFeel empowered, relieve stress, and let loose as you move to your favorite songs.\\r\\nImmerse yourself in an infectious community vibe that will leave you feeling unstoppable.\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":60,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":false,\"name\":\"Dance Classes with Maya\",\"instanceDates\":\"10 April-1 May\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"502401AHPCJBCSCGNTBTMTQJBHKBPVJVT\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-04-10T18:00:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2025-04-10T17:00:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-05-01T18:00:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2025-05-01T17:00:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Families & Youth\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Venue Hire\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false},{\"description\":\"Aya’s routine life is shaken after a random encounter at the airport. She impulsively picks up a man she doesn’t know, but after a brief, intense connection, he disappears without a trace. This sudden exit leaves Aya with a \\\"gnawing hunger\\\"— an emotional void she didn't know existed.\\r\\nAs she tries to find that feeling again, her relationship with her husband, Aviad (a linguist who studies ancient, dead languages), begins to show its cracks. While he focuses on the words of the past, Aya is looking for a new way to communicate her deepest desires in the present.\\r\\nDead Language is a beautiful and quiet film about how we often feel most seen by the people we know the least. With powerful performances by Sarah Adler and Yehezkel Lazarov, it explores the thin line between the life we have and the life we secretly crave. | This film is in Czech, Hebrew and English with English subtitles. | Duration: 1h 50m\\r\\n\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":110,\"imageUrl\":\"https://system.spektrix.com/jw3/files/05bae93d-7a40-4a40-8413-dd9fc450a14f.jpg\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Dead Language\",\"instanceDates\":\"11 May-11 May\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"https://system.spektrix.com/jw3/files/05bae93d-7a40-4a40-8413-dd9fc450a14f-thumbnail.jpg\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"619001ADCJSCHSKMTTGDLJRDKDQBTRVKJ\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-05-11T17:00:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-05-11T16:00:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-05-11T17:00:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-05-11T16:00:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Cinema\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Seret Film Festival\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false},{\"description\":\"2pm-3pm, Free, in building, Thursday 30 April 2026 // JW3 hosts its sixth Death Café – an intimate space for a lightly facilitated conversation about death and dying. \\r\\n\\r\\nAnd at JW3, there’ll be a Jewish twist. There is no formal agenda, and this is not a grief support or counselling session. \\r\\n\\r\\nWhile it is difficult to talk about death and dying, Death Café offers participants the opportunity to share their thoughts about life-and-death in a relaxed and non-judgemental setting. More general information about the concept is here.\\r\\n\\r\\nThe group will be facilitated by Sally Berkovic, author of Death Duties: The Chevra Kadisha – what being around the dead taught me about life.\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":60,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Death Café\",\"instanceDates\":\"30 April-30 April\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"591601ATJCDJNPLCKHBHRJVSGSNSQRVPQ\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-04-30T14:00:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-04-30T13:00:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-04-30T14:00:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-04-30T13:00:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Talks & Discussions\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Adult Education\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"Sally Berkovic\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false},{\"description\":\"7-8.30pm, building, £15, age 13+ // Defeating Hate brings together Katja Hoyer’s Weimar and Julia Franck’s Worlds Apart to explore how Germany has confronted fascism, silence and divided memory.   Hoyer’s Weimar traces ordinary lives in a town on the edge of catastrophe: a place associated with Goethe, Schiller and Bauhaus, but also with the rise of fascism and the creation of Buchenwald. Franck’s Worlds Apart offers a deeply personal account of childhood, displacement, neglect and the search for belonging in East Germany.   Through film clips and conversation, this event asks how ordinary people are shaped by history, how silence passes through families and societies, and what it takes to face the past with honesty, responsibility and compassion.   In partnership with the Goethe-Institut London.\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":90,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Defeating Hate?\",\"instanceDates\":\"29 October-29 October\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"636004AMQLCMJGPVRNQSCKBBQQQHQRHMD\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-10-29T19:00:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-10-29T19:00:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-10-29T19:00:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-10-29T19:00:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false,\"attribute_Genre\":\"Talks & Discussions\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Holocaust Learning\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"Julia Franck, Kate Hoyer\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"Approx 2 hours including interval // Preview Tickets: 6-7 December, £15 per person // Off Peak Tickets: 8-17 December £17 child & £27 adult // Peak Tickets: 18 December - 3 January £20 child & £32 adult // \",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":120,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Dick Whittingberg Gets Into a Pickle\",\"instanceDates\":\"6 December-3 January\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"582601APDRVPLNPGDDHKGVQNJLQNQNJVS\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-12-06T17:00:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-12-06T17:00:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2027-01-03T17:30:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2027-01-03T17:30:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Performance\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false},{\"description\":\"Mondays, 10:30am-12noon, £198 for the 11 week course, in building // Just like the early teen years in the life of an individual, those living through the Holocaust were confronted with new chances, new choices, new challenges. The evil of Nazism led many to defy the regime in ways that varied according to their situation, to the possibility of effective action and to their own values. The resisters and the righteous included men, women and children; religious and secular; Jewish and Gentile. Their actions took the form of attacks, escapes, uprisings, fraud, theft, hiding and being hidden, keeping chronicles, teaching and learning, leaving a legacy of knowledge and ideas, and even praying. All these actions raise big moral issues connected to personal and communal risk and ask the ultimate question: can we do a bad thing for a good reason? But the boisterousness and the bravado are undeniable, as are the intuition and the ingenuity involved. It was chutzpah at its most creative, its most courageous. Angela Gluck has worked as a teacher, trainer and consultant to schools and local authorities. She has written over 40 books on aspects of religion and history, and broadcasted on these subjects. She devotes part of her work to teaching children, young people and adults in cross-communal settings. She is an active trustee of The Separated Child Foundation.\\r\\n\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":90,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Dilemmas of the Deep: Resistance and ‘The Righteous’\",\"instanceDates\":\"5 January-23 March\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"560401AQBJRMDPLNSVGDMCJDJTNVQVGPC\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-01-05T10:30:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-01-05T10:30:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-03-23T10:30:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-03-23T10:30:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Classes & Courses\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"True\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"History & Politics Courses\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"Angela Gluck\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false},{\"description\":\"If you found out we weren't alone, if someone showed you, proved it to you, would that frighten you? This summer, the truth belongs to eight billion people. Today is... Disclosure Day. Duration: 145 minutes Rating: 12A Director: Steven Spielberg Cast: Emily Blunt, Josh O’Connor, Colin Firth, Eve Hewson Year: 2025 https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=VCPhAydaRBc&pp=ygUZZGlzY2xvc3VyZSBkYXkgdWsgdHJhaWxlcg%3D%3D\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":145,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Disclosure Day\",\"instanceDates\":\"6 July-21 July\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"641801ASHKMMTBNVHPBDVSTTHNQMCSVPH\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-07-06T17:10:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-07-06T16:10:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-07-21T13:00:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-07-21T12:00:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false,\"attribute_Genre\":\"Cinema\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"7-8.15pm, building, £15, age 13+ // We all dream, but what was it like to dream under Nazism?\\r\\n\\r\\nIn the years after 1933, journalist Charlotte Beradt secretly collected the dreams of ordinary people living in Nazi Germany. These striking accounts show how fear, pressure and uncertainty entered even the most private spaces of life, revealing moments of inner questioning, defiance and the struggle to maintain a sense-of-self.\\r\\n\\r\\nJournalist and broadcaster Amanda Rubin is joined by dream researcher Melinda Powell, co-founder of the Dream Research Institute and author of The Hidden Lives of Dreams, and psychotherapist Robin Shohet, author of Dream Sharing.\\r\\n\\r\\nTogether they will reflect on the difficult choices people faced as the regime invaded their inner lives, and how moments of awareness, doubt and courage could shape the possibility of resistance. Offering a rarely explored perspective on Holocaust history, encounter the emotional reality of the period through the dreams of those who lived it, while exploring how propaganda, surveillance and self-censorship shaped everyday life, and how questions of conformity, belonging and resistance continue to resonate today.\\r\\n\\r\\n“The stronger a person’s power of moral and political resistance was, the more positive, less absurd, their dreams were... These stand in direct contrast to the dreams where the dreamer has lost their ability to act, even while asleep.” – Charlotte Beradt\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":75,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Dreaming and Resisting: What We Know and What We Deny\",\"instanceDates\":\"30 March-30 March\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"563601ASPDLQDPTLHNKGMKVNSDJMRRVTB\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-03-30T19:00:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-03-30T18:00:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-03-30T19:00:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-03-30T18:00:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Talks & Discussions\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Holocaust Learning\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false},{\"description\":\"7-8.15pm, building, £15, age 13+ // What can dreams tell us about life under Nazism? Journalist and filmmaker Amanda Rubin joins historian and psychoanalyst Professor Daniel Pick to explore an extraordinary archive of dreams collected by Charlotte Beradt in 1930s Nazi Germany. These dreams, often unsettling, sometimes surreal, reveal how fear, propaganda, and control seeped into the unconscious lives of ordinary people.  Together they will reflect on how political power can shape not just our actions and words, but even what we dare to imagine. Beradt’s work still resonates today, raising timely questions about truth, illusion, and the hidden effects of propaganda.   Daniel Pick is a leading historian and psychoanalyst whose work bridges history, psychology, and culture. Author of The Pursuit of the Nazi Mind (OUP), he leads the Wellcome Trust project Hidden Persuaders on Cold War fears of brainwashing, and is a familiar voice on BBC radio and television.\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":75,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Dreaming Under Dictatorship\",\"instanceDates\":\"29 January-29 January\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"562402ASSLPDDJRCCSKJCJQKCDSPRVPCQ\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-01-29T19:00:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-01-29T19:00:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-01-29T19:00:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-01-29T19:00:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Talks & Discussions\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Holocaust Learning\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false},{\"description\":\"Ducks, An Urban Legend is a bold Israeli dark comedy that follows five unforgettable characters navigating life on the “wrong” side of Tel Aviv. Yossi desperately tries to hold his relationship and wedding dreams together; Asaf and his partner Anna resort to absurd measures to unlock his grandfather’s pension; and Elias, a lonely Palestinian awaiting a heart transplant, is forced into cooperation with the Israeli security services. As their lives collide in tales of love, loss, survival and grace, the film blends sharp humor with poignant humanity, offering a quirky yet deeply moving portrait of resilience and redemption in the urban landscape. Winner of Best Script at the Tallinn Black Nights Film Festival, this ensemble piece showcases standout performances from Roi Miller, Diana Abramov, Erez Drigues, Rinat Matatov and Sarel Piterman, bringing heart and wit to every story thread. | This film is in Hebrew with English subtitles. | Duration 1h 40m\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":100,\"imageUrl\":\"https://system.spektrix.com/jw3/files/fbf11f12-c5a2-4c61-998f-87af3e6f118f.jpg\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Ducks, An Urban Legend\",\"instanceDates\":\"13 May-13 May\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"https://system.spektrix.com/jw3/files/fbf11f12-c5a2-4c61-998f-87af3e6f118f-thumbnail.jpg\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"618802ANKBBRCVRGHNVSRRSHLNTQBJVLR\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-05-13T17:30:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-05-13T16:30:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-05-13T17:30:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-05-13T16:30:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Cinema\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Seret Film Festival\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false},{\"description\":\"Egypt's most adored actor, George Fahmy (Fares Fares) is pressured to star in a film commissioned by the highest authorities. He reluctantly accepts the role and finds himself thrown into the inner circle of power. Like a moth drawn to the flame, he begins an affair with the mysterious wife of the general overseeing the film. This is director Tarik Saleh's final film of his Cairo Trilogy.  //\\r\\n\\r\\nDuration: 129 minutes \\r\\nRating: 15 \\r\\nDirector: Tarik Saleh \\r\\nCast: Fares Fares, Amr Waked, Lyna Khoudri \\r\\nYear: 2025 \\r\\nLanguage: Arabic \\r\\nSubtitles: English \",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":129,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Eagles of the Republic\",\"instanceDates\":\"14 June-18 June\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"628601APNJNKGMHRNVJMRRRJCNVTDKDTJ\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-06-14T10:30:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-06-14T09:30:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-06-18T10:20:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-06-18T09:20:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Cinema\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"True\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false},{\"description\":\"After a devastating loss, witty and proudly troublesome Eleanor Morgenstein, 94, tells a tale that takes on its own dangerous life. | Duration: 1h 38m, Rating: 12A | Films may be preceded by up to 20 minutes of advertisements and trailers. Specific timings will vary with each screening. We always recommend arriving on time.\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":98,\"imageUrl\":\"https://system.spektrix.com/jw3/files/0a7afe64-5f07-46fb-a49c-71c50e720ab8.jpg\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Eleanor the Great \",\"instanceDates\":\"1 February-12 February\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"https://system.spektrix.com/jw3/files/0a7afe64-5f07-46fb-a49c-71c50e720ab8-thumbnail.jpg\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"577801AGGPPBJMLKSNBDGKTKQDBKQTTMD\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-02-01T12:30:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-02-01T12:30:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-02-12T15:00:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-02-12T15:00:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Cinema\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false},{\"description\":\"6.30pm - 7.30pm, free, followed by a screening of EPiC: Elvis Presley in Concert at 7.30pm\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\t<h2>Elvis Karaoke Hour</h2>Dust off your blue suede shoes, and join us for a free Elvis karaoke hour before the film begins! \\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":60,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Elvis Karaoke Hour - EPiC: Elvis Presley in Concert\",\"instanceDates\":\"12 March-12 March\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"607401ASQBLRHKLSBTBJNMLNGQSTLJDPD\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-03-12T18:30:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-03-12T18:30:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-03-12T18:30:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-03-12T18:30:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Special Events\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false},{\"description\":\"Enzo, 16, defies his bourgeois family's expectations by starting a masonry apprenticeship, a path far removed from the prestigious life they had envisioned for him. \\r\\n\\r\\n \\r\\n\\r\\nIn their chic villa in the sun-drenched South of France, tensions simmer as relentless questions and pressures weigh on Enzo's future and dreams. On the construction sites, however, Vlad, a charismatic Ukrainian colleague, shakes up Enzo's world and opens the door to unexpected possibilities. \\r\\n\\r\\n \\r\\n\\r\\nDuration: 93 minutes \\r\\n\\r\\nRating: 15 \\r\\n\\r\\nDirector: Robin Campillo \\r\\n\\r\\nCast: Eloy Pohu, Maksym Slivinskyi, Pierfrancesco Favino  \\r\\n\\r\\nYear: 2025 \\r\\n\\r\\nLanguage: French / Ukrainian \\r\\nSubtitles: English \",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":93,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Enzo\",\"instanceDates\":\"30 June-9 July\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"629802ATBJNVBDCBHBRNQHPGMCHQLCSBP\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-06-30T13:15:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-06-30T12:15:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-07-09T16:00:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-07-09T15:00:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false,\"attribute_Genre\":\"Cinema\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"Elvis sings and tells his story like never before in a new cinematic experience from visionary filmmaker Baz Luhrmann. | Duration: 1h 31m, Rating: 12A Credits\\r\\nRating: 12A\\r\\nGenre: Documentary\\r\\nDirector: Baz Luhrmann\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":96,\"imageUrl\":\"https://system.spektrix.com/jw3/files/1c9f77b3-c4c4-4d53-bd14-79d5740042d7.jpg\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"EPiC: Elvis Presley in Concert\",\"instanceDates\":\"8 March-12 March\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"https://system.spektrix.com/jw3/files/1c9f77b3-c4c4-4d53-bd14-79d5740042d7-thumbnail.jpg\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"605801AKTPLCHJGMLTLLCJGNDKHKGLMLM\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-03-08T14:30:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-03-08T14:30:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-03-12T19:30:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-03-12T19:30:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Cinema\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false},{\"description\":\"In an afterlife where souls have one week to decide where to spend eternity, Joan is faced with the impossible choice between the man she spent her life with and her first love, who died young and has waited decades for her to arrive. | Duration: 1h 54m, Rating: 15 \",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":114,\"imageUrl\":\"https://system.spektrix.com/jw3/files/b4684877-b3bb-43f1-82ed-143bc94bbd16.jpg\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Eternity\",\"instanceDates\":\"5 January-8 January\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"https://system.spektrix.com/jw3/files/b4684877-b3bb-43f1-82ed-143bc94bbd16-thumbnail.jpg\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"580401ACPBHHHDVVHDGDVBSSRRNCBSHSS\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-01-05T19:10:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-01-05T19:10:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-01-08T17:50:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-01-08T17:50:00Z\",\"altText\":\"Eternity\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Cinema\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false},{\"description\":\"12.30pm-7pm, £36, in building // Join us for the UK Premiere of Etty, a 6‑part mini‑series by Hagai Levi. \\r\\n\\r\\nIn Nazi‑occupied Amsterdam, a young woman begins therapy. Her name is Etty Hillesum. At 27, fuelled by an intense passion for life, she embarks on a profound spiritual and emotional journey documented meticulously in her diaries.\\r\\n\\r\\nThese writings reveal her turbulent relationship with psycho-chirologist Julius Spier, a love affair that becomes the catalyst for her radical inner transformation—one intensified by the mounting threat she faces as a Jewish woman. Her path ultimately leads her to an extraordinary act of solidarity.\\r\\n\\r\\nFirst published forty years after her death, Hillesum’s diaries have since been translated into more than twenty languages and sold millions of copies worldwide. Told in an unconventional form, the series creates a dialogue between past and present, showing how Etty’s search for meaning resonates powerfully today and posing a timely question: How do we find hope in a hopeless world?\\r\\n\\r\\nWe will be screening the complete 6-part series, including scheduled comfort breaks throughout. \",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":390,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Etty\",\"instanceDates\":\"12 April-12 April\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"595801AQMBGKKQDGJPBKJMGBKBKKVMGBD\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-04-12T12:30:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-04-12T11:30:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-04-12T12:30:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-04-12T11:30:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Arts & Culture\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Arts & Culture\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false},{\"description\":\"7.30-8.30pm, hybrid, £20 // As Ukraine marks its 4th year since Russia launched a full-scale invasion, security and political analyst Jonathan Paris will offer an essential update on the developments of this contemporary European war. This panel discussion will analyse Ukrainian defences against Russian advances and the potential implications for Ukraine’s future and sovereignty as the war continues to develop. Expect a comprehensive analysis of the war’s current trajectory and its far-reaching implications for Europe and the world.\\r\\n\\r\\nJonathan Paris is a London-based Middle East analyst and former fellow at the Council on Foreign Relations in New York. He is currently Senior Fellow at the Center for Advanced Studies on Terrorism (CAST) and Senior Advisor Emeritus at the Chertoff Group. He appears regularly on Sky News and Al Arabiya and has been quoted in the New York Times and other publications.\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":60,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Europe at a Crossroads\",\"instanceDates\":\"9 February-9 February\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"559402ANHLJTDVSRPDLBDHKTHJCSGDQPK\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-02-09T19:30:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-02-09T19:30:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-02-09T19:30:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-02-09T19:30:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Talks & Discussions\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Adult Education\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"Jonathan Paris\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false},{\"description\":\"Frida Kahlo is a phenomenon. She is arguably the world’s favourite female artist – beloved by young and old. Exhibition on Screen’s award-winning film is back by popular demand with an exciting new addition from the blockbuster transatlantic exhibition from Tate Britain and MFA Houston 'Frida Kahlo: the Making of an Icon'. Back in the cinemas in May 2026, one month before the Tate exhibition opens, allowing audiences to watch both the film and see the show. \\r\\nWho was Frida Kahlo? Everyone knows her face but who was the woman behind the bright colours, the big brows and the floral crowns? Take a journey through the life of a true icon, discover her art, and uncover the true story of her rebellious, passionate and turbulent life. \\r\\nMaking use of the latest technology to deliver previously unimaginable quality, we take an in-depth look at key works throughout her career. Using letters Kahlo wrote to guide us, this definitive film reveals her deepest emotions and unlocks the secrets and symbolism contained within her art. \\r\\nExhibition on Screen’s trademark combination of interviews with those who knew her and world experts, commentary and a detailed exploration of her art, combined with new special bonus footage from the 2026 Tate exhibition, delivers a treasure trove of colour and emotion. This personal and intimate film offers privileged access to her works, her home, her studio and highlights the source of her feverish creativity, her resilience and her unmatched lust for life, beauty and revolution. \\r\\nCreated in close collaboration with world experts and those who knew her. | Duration: 1h 30m, Rating: 12A \",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":90,\"imageUrl\":\"https://system.spektrix.com/jw3/files/7bc94451-0edf-443f-a44f-ccc28fa02912.jpg\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Exhibition on Screen: Frida Kahlo\",\"instanceDates\":\"19 May-6 July\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"https://system.spektrix.com/jw3/files/7bc94451-0edf-443f-a44f-ccc28fa02912-thumbnail.jpg\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"625401ARTNNNKPCLLHJGMBLHNNSHQLJHV\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-05-19T19:30:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-05-19T18:30:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-07-06T20:00:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-07-06T19:00:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Cinema\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false},{\"description\":\"Exhibition on Screen were deeply saddened to hear of the death of brilliant artist David Hockney, who they worked closely with to make a film about his work back in 2017. As a tribute to David Hockney this film has been made theatrically available again at certain cinemas & galleries. Widely considered Britain’s most popular artist, David Hockney was a global sensation with exhibitions in London, New York, Paris and beyond, attracting millions of visitors worldwide. Featuring intimate and in-depth interviews with Hockney, this revealing film focuses on two blockbuster exhibitions held in 2012 and 2016 at the Royal Academy of Art in London. Director Phil Grabsky secured privileged access to craft this cinematic celebration of a 21st century master of creativity. Duration: 30 minutes Director: Phil Grabsky Year: 2017 https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=WGRjOzQ-S40\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":85,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Exhibition on Screen: Remembering David Hockney\",\"instanceDates\":\"3 July-16 July\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"641802ANCGMMPMCJLDBVTGMKLKMCKDQJS\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-07-03T14:00:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-07-03T13:00:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-07-16T16:00:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-07-16T15:00:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false,\"attribute_Genre\":\"Cinema\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"Celebrating the 250th anniversary of their births, this unmissable new documentary explores Turner and Constable’s intertwined lives and legacies alongside the groundbreaking Tate exhibition.Two of Britain’s greatest painters, J.M.W. Turner and John Constable were also the greatest of rivals. Born within a year of each other, both used landscape painting to reflect the changing world around them. Tate Britain is bringing these two greats together for a groundbreaking exhibition, in London from November 2025 to April 2026, and Exhibition on Screen once again has exclusive and privileged access to bring their extraordinary art and remarkable stories to the big screen in February so that you can enjoy both film and exhibition together. Discover unexpected sides to both artists with intimate views of sketchbooks and personal items and insights from leading experts. | Duration: 1h 31m, Rating: PG \",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":91,\"imageUrl\":\"https://system.spektrix.com/jw3/files/f6019fc0-698f-4813-b833-ed5bfceadcbb.jpg\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Exhibition on Screen: Turner & Constable\",\"instanceDates\":\"10 March-22 April\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"https://system.spektrix.com/jw3/files/f6019fc0-698f-4813-b833-ed5bfceadcbb-thumbnail.jpg\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"607601AMDPBNJRHNDGRBNVGJJJDGQPCCM\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-03-10T19:30:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-03-10T19:30:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-04-22T16:15:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-04-22T15:15:00Z\",\"altText\":\"Exhibition on Screen: Turner & Constable\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Cinema\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false},{\"description\":\"16:00 // 11 Oct 2026 // £12 // Join a facilitated, confidential sharing space to reflect on the complexities of Jewish identity since October 7th, through guided conversation and creative expression using art materials. Together, we’ll process experiences, build resilience and explore ways to navigate an increasingly challenging world.\\r\\n\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":150,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Exploring our Jewish Identities in a Topsy Turvy World\",\"instanceDates\":\"11 October-11 October\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"633601AGLQKBKSJNHHNNSJMNTLKSDVBQP\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-10-11T16:00:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-10-11T15:00:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-10-11T16:00:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-10-11T15:00:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false,\"attribute_Genre\":\"Young Professionals\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"Sargam Picker\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"Ruth (Kathleen Chalfant), a retired cook, prepares breakfast in her sunny and cozy kitchen -- a dish she seems to have made many times before, although small and puzzling errors now punctuate her comfortable routine.  \\r\\n\\r\\n \\r\\n\\r\\nWhen her son (H. Jon Benjamin) arrives to dine with her, she mistakes him for a suitor. Their \\\"date\\\" takes them to an assisted living facility, which Ruth does not remember that she had previously selected for herself. Among her fellow memory care residents, Ruth feels lost and adrift, certain she has found herself somewhere she does not belong. As she slowly begins to accept the warmth and support of care workers Vanessa (Carolyn Michelle) and Brian (Andy McQueen), she finds new ways to ground herself in her body, even as her mind embarks on a journey all its own. Writer-director Sarah Friedland's coming-of-old-age feature compassionately follows the winding path of octogenarian Ruth's shifting memories and desires while remaining rooted in her sage perspective. //\\r\\n\\r\\nDuration: 90 minutes \\r\\nRating: 12A \\r\\nDirector: Sarah Friedland \\r\\nCast: Kathleen Chalfant, H. Jon Benjamin, Carolyn Michelle \\r\\nYear: 2024 \\r\\nLanguage: English \",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":90,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Familiar Touch\",\"instanceDates\":\"21 June-26 June\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"628002AGMNJHGSJDLCDVSQTPBSTKQGPKV\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-06-21T11:00:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-06-21T10:00:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-06-26T15:30:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-06-26T14:30:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Cinema\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false},{\"description\":\"2pm-3.30pm, £7 child £5 adult babes in arms free, all ages // Kick off the summer holidays with a splash of excitement at JW3 Beach for an hour of non-stop seaside fun. Richie Rich Parties is bringing their signature high-energy entertainment to the sand, offering a celebration specially designed to keep children fully engaged and parents smiling.\\r\\n\\r\\nYou can expect a vibrant atmosphere filled with circus skills, professional bubble displays, and plenty of music to keep everyone dancing. The session is packed with interactive games and big energy, ensuring bags of fun for both kids and grown-ups alike.\\r\\n\\r\\nThis event is the ultimate summer holiday treat for families looking to kick back and make unforgettable memories together by the water. We invite you to join in the laughter and experience the magic of a Richie Rich party right here at the beach.\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":90,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Family Beach Party\",\"instanceDates\":\"26 July-26 July\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"603201ANBNBTSGTJRSRPGSKHLBGPBNLDD\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-07-26T14:00:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-07-26T13:00:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-07-26T14:00:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-07-26T13:00:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Families & Youth\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Families\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"Richie Rich\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false},{\"description\":\"11.00am-12pm, £7 child, £5 adult, babes in arms free // Get get ready to jump, jive, wiggle, giggle, shimmy, and shake at the Lanaland Family Disco on the beach!\\r\\n\\r\\nWe'll also have crafting and beach fun activities with some book giveaways from PJ Library too! \\r\\n\\r\\nJoin us for an uplifting, all-ages dance party where little ones and grown-ups can let loose together. With bubbles, rainbows, parachute games, pom poms  and a specially curated playlist to satisfy all ages this isn’t just a disco — it’s a celebration of family fun.\\r\\n\\r\\nLed by JW3 fan favourite Ilana Banana, the Lanaland Family Disco creates a safe, joyful space where everyone’s welcome on the dance floor— from crawling babies to boogying grandparents! Sing alongs, dance along, and immerse yourself in musical, sensory delight and feel-good vibes for all.\\r\\n\\r\\nThis event is geared towards under 7s, but all ages are welcome!\\r\\n\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":60,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Family Disco on the Beach\",\"instanceDates\":\"9 August-9 August\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"622001ARRLSHMDQGRRHCMBBLHRRCBTMMM\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-08-09T11:00:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-08-09T10:00:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-08-09T11:00:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-08-09T10:00:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false,\"attribute_Genre\":\"Families & Youth\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Families\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"Ilana Banana\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"A feature film in the form of a triptych. The three stories all concern the relationships between adult children, their somewhat distant parent (or parents), and each other. | Duration: 2h 13m, Rating: 12A Credits\\r\\nRating: 12A\\r\\nGenre: Comedy, Drama\\r\\nDirector: Jim Jarmusch\\r\\nStars: Tom Waits, Adam Driver, Mayim Bialik, Charlotte Rampling, Cate Blanchett https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=PA07EmbZ0b0&pp=ygUnZmF0aGVyIG1vdGhlciBzaXN0ZXIgYnJvdGhlciBVSyB0cmFpbGVy\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":122,\"imageUrl\":\"https://system.spektrix.com/jw3/files/a49401da-25ce-4f6f-8109-6f5b2f5492de.jpg\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Father Mother Sister Brother\",\"instanceDates\":\"26 April-7 May\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"https://system.spektrix.com/jw3/files/a49401da-25ce-4f6f-8109-6f5b2f5492de-thumbnail.jpg\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"616001ASVKNRJHRQCKQLJSSNTTLNDKGSM\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-04-26T10:30:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-04-26T09:30:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-05-07T16:00:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-05-07T15:00:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Cinema\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false},{\"description\":\"7.30pm, tentative duration 2hrs, £33 adult £16.50 student, in-building // The Fibonacci Quartet have burst onto the international stage after winning first prize in numerous competitions including the prestigious Borciani International Competition in Italy. Audiences love the immediacy and warmth of their communication both with one another and with the listener. \\r\\nLuba Tunnicliffe is one of the UK’s finest and most musicianly young violists and played for several years in the Ruisi Quartet. \\r\\n// \\r\\nThere are only a handful of major string sextets but they are all wonderfully sonorous and warm. The extra viola and cello added to the string quartet add a lot of colour and richness, and also liberate the first viola and cello to share melodies with the first violin.  It is perhaps not an accident that all these three gorgeous pieces are part of the late Romantic era. This is a rare chance to hear them together.\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":120,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Fibonacci String Quartet with Luba Tunicliffe and David Waterman\",\"instanceDates\":\"15 January-15 January\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"493601AMLKBDVGSMCMTQDNKCCBMGQRCBR\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-01-15T19:30:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-01-15T19:30:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-01-15T19:30:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-01-15T19:30:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Arts & Culture\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Classical Music Series\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false},{\"description\":\"Free exhibition, no booking required, 19 Jan–11 Feb, age 13+ // From 1940 to 1941 around 70,000 adults with mental and physical disabilities living in institutions across Germany and Austria were systematically killed under a Nazi state-led programme called Aktion-T4. The victims were deemed to have ‘lives unworthy of life’.  This exhibition tells the previously unknown story of the 13 British-born victims of this murderous assault on disabled people. Most of them were from the families of German and Austrian immigrants who moved to Britain to work in the early twentieth century before fatefully returning to Germany before the Second World War. Others were from mixed marriages between British and German or Austrian nationals.  An international team of researchers led by Dr Helen Atherton from the University of Leeds have meticulously and painstakingly reconstructed the lives of these people, as well as telling the story of the T4 programme in which they were caught up and its aftermath.\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":660,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":false,\"name\":\"Finding Ivy: A Life Worthy of Life (Exhibition)\",\"instanceDates\":\"19 January-11 February\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"562601ASHJKQTKCHCBTJVSBHRGNCVSSHR\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-01-19T10:00:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-01-19T10:00:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-02-11T21:00:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-02-11T21:00:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Special Events\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Holocaust Learning\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false},{\"description\":\"7-8.15pm, building, £15 //   Between 1940 and 1941, 13 British-born adults with disabilities were among the thousands murdered under Nazi Germany’s Aktion T4 programme, a history that has remained largely hidden until now.  Join Helen Atherton (University of Leeds), Simon Jarrett (Birkbeck, Open University), and theatre director Stephen Unwin, former Chair of “KIDS”, a national charity supporting disabled young people and their families, as they bring these stories to light and honour the lives of the victims.  The panel will also reflect on disability today, highlighting resilience, visibility, and inclusion, while remembering the past.\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":75,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Finding Ivy: A Life Worthy of Life (Panel Discussion)\",\"instanceDates\":\"5 February-5 February\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"562201ANGHCDCMBJHQHGPRRBDTKPLLQPQ\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-02-05T19:00:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-02-05T19:00:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-02-05T19:00:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-02-05T19:00:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Talks & Discussions\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Holocaust Learning\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false},{\"description\":\"2-4pm, £20, off-site //\\r\\nJoin Boaz Tal and step into history with a walking tour through central London, where the story of modern Zionism took shape in the early 20th century.\\r\\n\\r\\nFollow in the footsteps of Chaim Weizmann as we wander past the houses and streets where he met the leading figures who helped turn the dream of a Jewish state into reality – from the Rothschild family to Herbert Samuel, from Lord Balfour to Lady Astor.\\r\\n\\r\\nAt every stop, you’ll discover the fascinating role each of these individuals played, and how ideas, friendships, and political influence came together to spark the historic Balfour Declaration. Imagine Weizmann himself knocking on doors, holding late-night discussions, and persuading Britain’s decision-makers – and feel how these moments became stepping stones towards the creation of the State of Israel.\\r\\n\\r\\nThis tour will not depart from JW3; the meeting location will be provided upon booking.\\r\\n\\r\\nPlease wear comfortable shoes and dress for the weather! \",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":120,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Following the Footsteps of Dr. Chaim Weizmann and the Balfour Declaration\",\"instanceDates\":\"22 March-26 April\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"556201AGPMPCVTCHDNKHJNJSCRQDVRNJK\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-03-22T14:00:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-03-22T14:00:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-04-26T14:00:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-04-26T13:00:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Walks\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Walking Tours\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"Boaz Tal\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false},{\"description\":\"7pm-8.15pm, £10, in building // ages 13+ // What does football reveal about life, power and survival in a concentration camp? \\r\\n\\r\\nThis event explores the little known history of football in and around Mauthausen concentration camp, from the teams and matches connected to the SS, to the ways in which football also became part of prisoners’ daily reality. We will be joined by Bernhard Kolbe from the Mauthausen Memorial, whose research sheds light on this complex and unsettling chapter of camp history \\r\\n\\r\\nAt the heart of the evening will be the testimony of Eva Clarke, who was born in Mauthausen in April 1945, just days before liberation. Her extraordinary story brings the history of the camp into deeply personal focus, reminding us of the human lives behind the historical record. \\r\\n\\r\\nThe event has been developed together with JW3’s Austrian volunteer, who will also reflect on what it means to grow up in Austria today, and how a younger generation navigates the difficult legacy of the Nazi past. \\r\\n\\r\\nBringing together history, testimony and personal reflection, this evening asks how we confront a painful past,  and how memory can be carried forward with honesty, sensitivity and responsibility. \",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":75,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Football in Mauthausen: Memory, Testimony and Responsibility\",\"instanceDates\":\"16 July-16 July\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"630601ANNJRRCDBVPSLRTDNVHLKRHSHVP\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-07-16T19:00:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-07-16T18:00:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-07-16T19:00:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-07-16T18:00:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Talks & Discussions\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false},{\"description\":\"Mondays, 10.30am-12.30pm, £240, in building\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":120,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"French Advanced Conversation with Patricia Zerah\",\"instanceDates\":\"13 April-13 July\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"608401AJMVCCVJSRKRSBQCTVJNJBBHKKC\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-04-13T10:30:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-04-13T09:30:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-07-13T10:30:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-07-13T09:30:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Languages\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"True\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Languages\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"Patricia Zerah\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false},{\"description\":\"Mondays, 1pm-3pm, £240, in building // \",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":120,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"French Advanced Conversation with Patricia Zerah\",\"instanceDates\":\"13 April-13 July\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"608801ANHLBRMJMCRVGLJJSQQTQMSDSHS\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-04-13T13:00:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-04-13T12:00:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-07-13T13:00:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-07-13T12:00:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Languages\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"True\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Languages\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"Patricia Zerah\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false},{\"description\":\"Mondays, 10.30am-12.30pm, £220, in building \",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":120,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"French Advanced Conversation with Patricia Zerah\",\"instanceDates\":\"5 October-5 October\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"645601ALHGKKGPLJPTDBHDLJQMKGRRRML\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-10-05T10:30:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-10-05T09:30:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-10-05T10:30:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-10-05T09:30:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false,\"attribute_Genre\":\"Languages\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"True\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Languages \",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"Patricia Zerah\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"Mondays, 1pm-3pm, £220, in building\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":220,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"French Advanced Conversation with Patricia Zerah\",\"instanceDates\":\"5 October-5 October\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"646001AQKBTSMQKVRGHNMDGJJTKSMGDVN\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-10-05T13:00:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-10-05T12:00:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-10-05T13:00:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-10-05T12:00:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false,\"attribute_Genre\":\"Languages\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"True\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Languages \",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"Patricia Zerah\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"Tuesdays, 10.30am-12.30pm, £220, in building // \",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":120,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"French Intermediate with Patricia Zerah\",\"instanceDates\":\"6 January-24 March\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"570401ANGPPKNVVNCMDLHHHLDVBDCSQDG\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-01-06T10:30:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-01-06T10:30:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-03-24T10:30:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-03-24T10:30:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Languages\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"True\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Languages \",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"Patricia Zerah\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false},{\"description\":\"Tuesdays, 10.30am-12.30pm, £240, in building // \",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":120,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"French Intermediate with Patricia Zerah\",\"instanceDates\":\"14 April-14 July\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"610201AJQVBVGPBLLVLKCKGKNPBHMJKDV\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-04-14T10:30:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-04-14T09:30:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-07-14T10:30:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-07-14T09:30:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Languages\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"True\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Languages\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"Patricia Zerah\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false},{\"description\":\"Tuesdays, 10.30am-12.30pm, £220, in building // \",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":120,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"French Intermediate with Patricia Zerah\",\"instanceDates\":\"6 October-6 October\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"647601ALDHQBRQBBVNTQKPRLHKLGSDRKS\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-10-06T10:30:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-10-06T09:30:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-10-06T10:30:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-10-06T09:30:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false,\"attribute_Genre\":\"Languages\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"True\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Languages\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"Patricia Zerah\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"7.30-9pm, building, £18 // From Ash to Promise is a powerful triple bill of contemporary ballets exploring layered themes of personal and national identity, with a focus on Jewish narratives. The programme features three works that reflect on heritage, memory, and transformation, guiding audiences through fractured histories and into a recontexualized future. \\r\\n\\r\\nLot’s Wife – Marika Brussel's feminist reimagining of the biblical figure who looked back. Originally scheduled for stage in 2020, it premiered as a film during lockdown. This performance marks its long-awaited live debut. Watch the film \\r\\n\\r\\nMr. Greentree (My wish was my command) – A multimedia solo work by Richard Bermange inspired by Austrian-Jewish cabaret artist and anti-fascist Fritz Grünbaum. Incorporating archival audio and sound design, it explores creativity and resistance.  \\r\\n\\r\\nSlant of the Earth – Choreographed by Marika Brussel, this evocative UK premiere reimagines the ancient story of Abraham, Sarah, and Hagar through contemporary ballet. Set against a backdrop of shifting landscapes and timeless questions, the piece delves into themes of love, power, exile, and generational legacy. Brussel's choreography weaves emotional nuance and physical intensity, exploring the intimate and often fraught dynamics between the three central figures. Slant of the Earth invites audiences to reflect on the human cost of faith, the complexity of chosen paths, and the echo of ancient decisions in the modern world. \",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":90,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"From Ash to Promise\",\"instanceDates\":\"8 February-8 February\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"565401ANKRHPSRJDDNHMGVMMVVTTVQDMR\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-02-08T19:30:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-02-08T19:30:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-02-08T19:30:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-02-08T19:30:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Performance\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Arts & Culture\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false},{\"description\":\"1pm - 2.30pm for all ages, 3.30pm - 5pm for ages 13+ // £8 per child, £6 per adult, babes in arms free //  \",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":90,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"From Bin to Brilliant: Family Upcycling Workshop\",\"instanceDates\":\"26 April-26 April\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"601601ADLVGJKHDDHBKVTTPSKVRBSJMTJ\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-04-26T13:00:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-04-26T12:00:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-04-26T15:30:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-04-26T14:30:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Families & Youth\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Families\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"Miki Shaw\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false},{\"description\":\"Spanning from the Yom Kippur War to the horrors of October 7th, Major General Doron Almog’s life is a timeline of Israeli tragedy. Yet, surrounded by five decades of bereavement, this Israel Prize laureate refuses to despair. A profound portrait of a leader transforming relentless personal grief into a legacy of national hope. | This film is in Hebrew with English subtitles | Duration: 1h 7m\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":67,\"imageUrl\":\"https://system.spektrix.com/jw3/files/9fa1d31a-092e-4c2a-8f55-b55adc1efb0a.jpg\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"From October 6th to October 7th\",\"instanceDates\":\"8 May-8 May\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"https://system.spektrix.com/jw3/files/9fa1d31a-092e-4c2a-8f55-b55adc1efb0a-thumbnail.jpg\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"617801ADCCPBRLNRCVLMMPQRVKDSLRQVG\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-05-08T10:30:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-05-08T09:30:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-05-08T10:30:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-05-08T09:30:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Cinema\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Seret Film Festival\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false},{\"description\":\"A movement workshop to release, reconnect and build community. Through guided explorations, we’ll engage the creative body, imagination and sense of play, discovering moments of connection and collective joy. No experience needed, just openness to move.\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":90,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Gathering in Movement\",\"instanceDates\":\"18 October-18 October\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"633202AGBPGQGRMGPDLJQSSNQVQSMKMNC\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-10-18T11:00:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-10-18T10:00:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-10-18T11:00:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-10-18T10:00:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false,\"attribute_Genre\":\"Young Professionals\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"Delicia Sefiha\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"When soon-to-be-dad comedian Irmy learns his sole inheritance is a tiny parcel of land in the occupied Palestinian territories, he also discovers it’s been seized by extreme-right settlers who turned it into a winery. Joined by his father, he challenges the settlers, the army, and the Israeli government to reclaim the land. What begins as a personal mission becomes a provocative, funny, and activist journey that reveals the mechanisms of occupation, confronting ideological taboos and exposing the complex realities of land, power, and resistance in the West Bank. | This film is in Hebrew with English subtitles. | Duration: 1h 10m\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":70,\"imageUrl\":\"https://system.spektrix.com/jw3/files/1a37f77b-a323-4be4-b173-2f4bd8b1bd32.jpg\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Get the Land Back\",\"instanceDates\":\"11 May-11 May\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"https://system.spektrix.com/jw3/files/1a37f77b-a323-4be4-b173-2f4bd8b1bd32-thumbnail.jpg\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"618801AHNGKJJRQQCBNBBLRMJHNQVNMCQ\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-05-11T15:00:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-05-11T14:00:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-05-11T15:00:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-05-11T14:00:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Arts & Culture\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Seret Film Festival\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false},{\"description\":\"9am-5pm, in-building // JW3 is hosting the NHS blood donation team. Donating blood can be done in under an hour and can potentially save a life. To donate blood, you must book in advance through www.blood.co.uk. No walk-ins allowed. Please note that JW3 is not handling bookings so please do not contact our Box Office.\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":480,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":false,\"name\":\"Give Blood @ JW3\",\"instanceDates\":\"18 May-18 May\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"477201ATKVQLMMGTPTQGNVHLSVCVJDGMK\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-05-18T09:00:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-05-18T08:00:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-05-18T09:00:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-05-18T08:00:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Special Events\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false},{\"description\":\"9am-5pm, in-building // JW3 is hosting the NHS blood donation team. Donating blood can be done in under an hour and can potentially save a life. To donate blood, you must book in advance through www.blood.co.uk. No walk-ins allowed. Please note that JW3 is not handling bookings so please do not contact our Box Office.\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":480,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":false,\"name\":\"Give Blood @ JW3\",\"instanceDates\":\"19 January-19 January\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"477401ABNRRPMMRBKJMMDTKBRHRJPLMLQ\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-01-19T09:00:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-01-19T09:00:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-01-19T09:00:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-01-19T09:00:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Special Events\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false},{\"description\":\"7.30pm-8.30pm, hybrid, £20 // In this talk, Middle East and geopolitical analyst Jonathan Paris will delve into the latest news on the Middle East, tracking the impact of the Iran War on great power geopolitics and the Region. Hear from Paris’ expert analysis on Iran, the Gulf and Israel and their global impact. \",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":60,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Global Geopolitics and the Middle East\",\"instanceDates\":\"14 October-14 October\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"637201AKSJSLQQNBJCSSHGMQTHMJCPLKM\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-10-14T19:30:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-10-14T18:30:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-10-14T19:30:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-10-14T18:30:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false,\"attribute_Genre\":\"Talks & Discussions\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Adult Education\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"Jonathan Paris\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"7.30-8.45pm, £15, building // To mark International Day of the Girl, this conversation explores the theme of modern femininity at the heart of Zoe's book, Good Slut.\\r\\n Zoe's widely-discussed book is an exploration, and passionate defence, of girls' and women's freedom and power in the West today: that which we already have and that which we can grasp. Less about sex and more about everything, Zoe argues that whatever problems remain, do not go out into the world feeling like a marked victim.  To think power not as fixed- held in absolute terms by men, or some other group, but as something fluid that you can grab too. To think of yourself as a powerful machine - more powerful than you think - who has a lot more to you than appearance. Don't be embarrassed or try to curb your appetites (well, unless they're physically harmful) – for money, success, career. 'Having it all' has been hugely discredited but it is something you should happily aim for, if you want.\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":75,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Good Slut: Live \",\"instanceDates\":\"8 October-8 October\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"639201AJRVMDHLMKBHKQRQMTJQCRPVTSD\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-10-08T19:30:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-10-08T18:30:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-10-08T19:30:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-10-08T18:30:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false,\"attribute_Genre\":\"Talks & Discussions\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Adult Education\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"Zoe Strimpel\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"2-3.30pm, hybrid, £20 // Grace rose from fashion model to become one of the top stars of the 1950’s before marrying a prince and retiring to Monaco . During her short career she starred opposite some of Hollywoods biggest names including Gary Cooper, Clark Gable &  Frank Sinatra . Let’s look at her life and career. With clips from High Noon, Dial M For Murder, High Society and Mogambo .\\r\\n\\r\\nGeorge McGhee has over 35 years of experience, latterly at the BBC, where he oversaw all feature films and international TV series acquisitions.\\r\\n\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":90,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Grace Kelly\",\"instanceDates\":\"20 January-20 January\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"556801ATBCPBHMDDNMJTPQKLKNDBNJLKV\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-01-20T14:00:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-01-20T14:00:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-01-20T14:00:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-01-20T14:00:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Talks & Discussions\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Adult Education\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"George McGhee\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false},{\"description\":\"7.30pm-10pm, Thursday 4 June 2026 // Join 10cc’s legendary songwriter and Hall of Famer Graham Gouldman for an intimate evening in conversation with renowned DJ Gary Crowley. From the chart-topping hits of 10cc like \\\"I’m Not In Love\\\" to the classics he penned for The Hollies and The Yardbirds, Gouldman reflects on the ten pivotal songs that shaped his life, revealing the stories and inspirations behind a truly remarkable career. A rare chance to hear one of Britain’s most distinguished songwriters discuss the music that made him who he is today.\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":90,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Graham Gouldman: 10 Songs that Changed My Life\",\"instanceDates\":\"4 June-4 June\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"590801AVLHSLSDVHVJSVCRLKSHRJMQKHK\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-06-04T19:30:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-06-04T18:30:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-06-04T19:30:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-06-04T18:30:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Music\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Arts & Culture\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false},{\"description\":\"H is for Hawk follows Helen, who, after the sudden death of her father, loses herself in the memories of their time birding and exploring the natural world together and turns the ancient art of falconry--rooted in European tradition--training a wild goshawk named Mabel to navigate her profound loss. But as she teaches Mabel to hunt and fly free, Helen discovers how deeply she has neglected her own emotions and life. What begins as an act of endurance transforms into an intimate journey of resilience and healing. | Duration: 2h 0m, Rating: 15 \\r\\n| Films may be preceded by up to 20 minutes of advertisements and trailers. Specific timings will vary with each screening. We always recommend arriving on time.\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":114,\"imageUrl\":\"https://system.spektrix.com/jw3/files/3e96e4fa-f28f-4ea2-9af6-c8f3b6871075.jpg\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"H is for Hawk\",\"instanceDates\":\"8 February-12 February\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"https://system.spektrix.com/jw3/files/3e96e4fa-f28f-4ea2-9af6-c8f3b6871075-thumbnail.jpg\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"587201ACQGLBPMKSGCTDHPVMDCDPNPHVL\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-02-08T13:20:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-02-08T13:20:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-02-12T17:20:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-02-12T17:20:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Cinema\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false},{\"description\":\"10.30am-12noon, 12.30pm-2pm, 3pm-5pm // £10 per head to cover the cost of supplies // \",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":90,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Half Term Foodbank Volunteering for Families: Cooking with Everyday Spices\",\"instanceDates\":\"17 February-17 February\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"585201AMMKTBHNQMLNJVTHCVLQDTBCMLM\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-02-17T10:30:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-02-17T10:30:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-02-17T15:00:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-02-17T15:00:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Families & Youth\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Families\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false},{\"description\":\"Shakespeare’s most enduring tragedy finds bold new life in Aneil Karia’s fierce, full-blooded adaptation, set in present-day London’s vibrant South Asian community. Anchored by a resonant and complex performance from Riz Ahmed in the title role, this is Hamlet as you’ve never seen it. | Duration: 1h 54m, Rating: 15\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":104,\"imageUrl\":\"https://system.spektrix.com/jw3/files/54e307e7-fd2b-4541-85fe-48e936c05921.jpg\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Hamlet\",\"instanceDates\":\"2 March-5 March\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"https://system.spektrix.com/jw3/files/54e307e7-fd2b-4541-85fe-48e936c05921-thumbnail.jpg\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"607001AQNGRRHMQCDCQQQBCBVNJKTDBKJ\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-03-02T13:30:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-03-02T13:30:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-03-05T15:30:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-03-05T15:30:00Z\",\"altText\":\"Hamlet\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Cinema\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false},{\"description\":\"The powerful story of love and loss that inspired the creation of Shakespeare’s timeless masterpiece, Hamlet. | Duration: 2h 5m, Rating: 12A | Films may be preceded by up to 20 minutes of advertisements and trailers. Specific timings will vary with each screening. We always recommend arriving on time.\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":125,\"imageUrl\":\"https://system.spektrix.com/jw3/files/d3112666-be30-4514-9711-2aae17080f27.jpg\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Hamnet\",\"instanceDates\":\"25 January-4 March\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"https://system.spektrix.com/jw3/files/d3112666-be30-4514-9711-2aae17080f27-thumbnail.jpg\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"581801ATHGTDHKVMHLRQSKVRRMQBMMMNR\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-01-25T17:20:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-01-25T17:20:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-03-04T13:30:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-03-04T13:30:00Z\",\"altText\":\"Hamnet\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Cinema\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false},{\"description\":\"Young newlyweds Arthur and Jenny Fitton want nothing more than to get their marriage started on the right foot. But before they can depart for their honeymoon in Spain, they have to spend their first night together at the home of Arthur's parents, Ezra and Lucy. The couple are prevented from having any intimacy, but it only gets worse. They find out that their trip to Spain is canceled, which sets the tone for a rocky few weeks. | Duration: 1h 55m, Rating: 12 | Films may be preceded by up to 20 minutes of advertisements and trailers. Specific timings will vary with each screening. We always recommend arriving on time.\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":115,\"imageUrl\":\"https://system.spektrix.com/jw3/files/4f0ffa52-facf-4e43-9f8b-9fe45ec2cc10.jpg\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Hayley Mills: The Family Way\",\"instanceDates\":\"22 February-24 February\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"https://system.spektrix.com/jw3/files/4f0ffa52-facf-4e43-9f8b-9fe45ec2cc10-thumbnail.jpg\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"587401AVBSPTVPTBLQKCPVLPMJBDDBLVJ\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-02-22T14:50:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-02-22T14:50:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-02-24T11:00:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-02-24T11:00:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Cinema\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false},{\"description\":\"A heartfelt documentary honoring Amir Fisher’s journey from aspiring footballer abroad to courageous IDF lone soldier. Through intimate interviews and personal footage, the film celebrates his dedication, bonds with his unit, and ultimate sacrifice defending Kibbutz Kfar Aza on October 7, 2023.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nA Heart of a Warrior is a powerful and moving documentary tribute to the life and legacy of Amir Fisher, a young man whose journey led him from international dreams to ultimate sacrifice.\\r\\nBorn in Israel but raised much of his life abroad, Amir grew up chasing a future as a professional footballer, even playing overseas. But a visit to Israel changed everything — overnight he made the life-altering decision to return alone, immigrate to Israel, and dedicate himself to service in the IDF. Choosing to rise above personal ambition, he enlisted as a lone soldier and found deep purpose serving in Unit Duvdevan. His dedication, courage, and bond with his team defined who he became — until October 7, 2023, when he fell defending the residents of Kibbutz Kfar Aza, shielding them with his own body.\\r\\n\\r\\nThis documentary weaves Amir’s personal story with the collective narrative of his Duvdevan unit and the fierce battle in Kfar Aza on that fateful day. Through intimate interviews with his family, his partner, his friends, and his brothers-in-arms, and enriched with archival footage, photos, and moments from Amir’s life and service, the film captures a young man defined by resilience, excellence, unwavering loyalty, friendship, and love for Israel — values that became his compass until the end.\\r\\n\\r\\nA Heart of a Warrior celebrates a life lived with courage, purpose, and heart — and honours a warrior whose spirit continues to inspire. | This film is in Hebrew with English subtitles. | Duration: 1h 34m\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":94,\"imageUrl\":\"https://system.spektrix.com/jw3/files/4e4d1890-a687-45d9-930b-275d7bd73bb4.jpg\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Heart of a Warrior\",\"instanceDates\":\"14 May-14 May\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"https://system.spektrix.com/jw3/files/4e4d1890-a687-45d9-930b-275d7bd73bb4-thumbnail.jpg\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"620201AKRVMPVBVJSNQKCKSJMJRSDVCHB\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-05-14T16:30:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-05-14T15:30:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-05-14T16:30:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-05-14T15:30:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Cinema\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Seret Film Festival\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false},{\"description\":\"Heaven & Earth is a suspenseful and emotionally charged Israeli drama that follows Maya and Aviv Berger, a couple who appear to have everything: a strong partnership, successful careers and a devoted young son. But when a routine test reveals a shocking truth that challenges their understanding of family and identity, their picture-perfect life begins to crack. \\r\\nAs Maya digs deeper for answers, long-buried secrets emerge, forcing both partners to confront their own assumptions and the fragile foundations of trust they built their life upon. With a story that deftly blends family drama and psychological intrigue, Sky & Earth immerses audiences in a world where the boundary between certainty and doubt dissolves, and where love must be re-evaluated in the face of uncertainty. | This film is in Hebrew with English subtitles. | Duration: 1h 46m\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":106,\"imageUrl\":\"https://system.spektrix.com/jw3/files/e9cc8753-6a4c-41cd-b488-23b590c32cf5.jpg\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Heaven & Earth\",\"instanceDates\":\"12 May-12 May\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"https://system.spektrix.com/jw3/files/e9cc8753-6a4c-41cd-b488-23b590c32cf5-thumbnail.jpg\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"619002ANRBMGGKCPVVKHCCVVNCRKMJHDC\",\"firstInstanceDa