\n</div>\",\"duration\":120,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Hebrew Very Advanced with Nurit Gance\",\"instanceDates\":\"15 April-15 July\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"611801AMNHMTSSLPNRDTSRHVBBDRLHMTB\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-04-15T19:30:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-04-15T18:30:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-07-15T19:30:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-07-15T18:30:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Languages\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"True\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Languages \",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"Nurit Gance\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false},{\"description\":\"Wednesdays, 7.30pm-9.30pm, £220, in building // \",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":120,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Hebrew Very Advanced with Nurit Gance\",\"instanceDates\":\"7 October-7 October\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"648202ASTDJTBBHJCGLVJPCRHLVLVCCVP\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-10-07T19:30:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-10-07T18:30:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-10-07T19:30:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-10-07T18:30:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false,\"attribute_Genre\":\"Languages\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"True\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Languages\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"Nurit Gance\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"Wednesdays, 10.30am-12.30pm, £220, in building //\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":120,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Hebrew Very Advanced with Nurit Gance\",\"instanceDates\":\"7 October-7 October\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"649802APHVJJBDPJKLNBMNPKVRGVLGDVC\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-10-07T10:30:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-10-07T09:30:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-10-07T10:30:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-10-07T09:30:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false,\"attribute_Genre\":\"Languages\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"True\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Languages\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"Rina Gurvitz\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"Wednesdays during term time, Mini Moves Creative Dance (3+): 4:30-5:00 ; Prep/Primary Ballet and Modern (6+): 5:00-5:45 // Venue Hire, bookings made at hedanceacademy.co.uk \",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":45,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":false,\"name\":\"Helena Elizabeth Dance Academy\",\"instanceDates\":\"7 January-8 July\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"614601ALSVJDQTNLCSNDHTGGDMCMNGNQD\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-01-07T16:30:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-01-07T16:30:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-07-08T16:30:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-07-08T15:30:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false},{\"description\":\"7.30pm-9pm, £15, hybrid // In partnership with the Jewish Leadership Council, join us for a special evening with globally recognised digital influencer, speaker, educator and author, Hen Mazzig. \\r\\n\\r\\nWith almost 1M followers across his social media platforms and over 100 million users interacting with his content every month, Hen has become one of the most visible and compelling Jewish voices since October 7th. Alongside his advocacy combatting antisemitism, Hen also puts significant energy into proactive positive messaging about being proudly Jewish in our turbulent world. In a recent Jewish News article discussing his podcast series of And They’re Jewish, Hen shared “…after two years defined by grief and division, I wanted to remind people that Jewish identity isn’t just about survival or trauma, it’s about joy, creativity, and life...we’re not here to defend our existence; we’re here to revel in it.” \\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nCome and hear Hen share what has worked best for him to change hearts and minds when both fighting the good fight, and flipping the script to remind the world that Jewish identity is all about joy, creativity and life!\\r\\n\\r\\nHen will be in conversation with Noa Hoffman. Noa Hoffman is a triple-award-winning journalist about to making waves as the newest political correspondent at The Spectator. Fresh from a four-year stint at The Sun, she has emerged as one of the most influential young reporters with a reputation for breaking major stories including the Chris Pincher scandal to failures in asylum, prison release procedures, and government cybersecurity. Hoffman was 2022's British Journalism Awards New Journalist of the Year and London Press Club Awards Young Journalist of the Year, and in 2023 was recognized by the MHP Group's 30 to Watch as one of the most talented and influential journalists under 30 working in the media\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":90,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Hen Mazzig in conversation with Noa Hoffman\",\"instanceDates\":\"6 May-6 May\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"604601AHKDGSKPGVNTTRMHRVJVDBQBMSQ\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-05-06T19:30:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-05-06T18:30:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-05-06T19:30:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-05-06T18:30:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Talks & Discussions\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"Hen Mazzig\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false},{\"description\":\"Theodor Herzl: The man behind Israel, is a bold and timely new documentary that traces the visionary, conflicted, and ultimately tragic life of the man who imagined a Jewish homeland long before it became a reality.  \\r\\n\\r\\nHerzl’s journey is narrated by David Baddiel, with Stephen Fry voicing the words of Herzl. Alongside archival materials and expert commentary, the documentary includes powerful testimonies from both Palestinians and those who witnessed and survived the Holocaust, offering viewers a broad, human lens on a history that continues to shape lives today.  \\r\\n\\r\\nThe film brings together a diverse range of voices: historians, writers, diplomats, survivors, and everyday citizens who help trace the echo of Herzl’s vision into the present. The team travelled across continents to build a documentary that is as visually compelling as it is emotionally resonant. | Duration: 1h, Rating: TBC \",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":60,\"imageUrl\":\"https://system.spektrix.com/jw3/files/652ddd0b-94f6-4159-8dcc-c247bddd949d.jpg\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Herzl: The man behind Israel\",\"instanceDates\":\"1 March-9 March\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"https://system.spektrix.com/jw3/files/652ddd0b-94f6-4159-8dcc-c247bddd949d-thumbnail.jpg\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"607801ATHRDGTTHSQNJLGBKGCPBPNJLJM\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-03-01T20:30:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-03-01T20:30:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-03-09T20:15:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-03-09T20:15:00Z\",\"altText\":\"Herzl\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Cinema\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false},{\"description\":\"10.30am-12noon, hybrid, free, age 13+ //  The theme for Holocaust Memorial Day 2026, ‘Bridging Generations’, a reminder that the responsibility of remembrance does not end with those who survived. It is carried forward by their children, their grandchildren, and by all of us.  This event invites us to engage with personal testimony, reflect on the lessons of the past, and explore how we can each play a role in building bridges, between memory and action, between history and hope.  Join us as we honour the past and commit to a future shaped by empathy, understanding, and a shared responsibility to remember.  In partnership with Generation2Generation (G2G)\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":90,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Holocaust Memorial Day\",\"instanceDates\":\"23 January-23 January\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"562001ACNDNRQDGNBVDGJVVLGRQDPPMKJ\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-01-23T10:30:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-01-23T10:30:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-01-23T10:30:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-01-23T10:30:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Talks & Discussions\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Holocaust Learning\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false},{\"description\":\"How to Live on Earth is a visionary feature documentary that explores our vital connection to nature and its role in our future. Presented by Benedict Cumberbatch, this ultimate 'how-to guide' features inspirational, cutting-edge stories and powerful cinematography from around the world to reveal how humans are learning to team up with nature to solve our biggest challenges. Heart-warming, entertaining, energising, the film presents a hopeful vision of a future within reach – one in which nature thrives, and so do we. Duration: 95 minutes Rating: 12A Director: Fredi Devas Cast: Benedict Cumberbatch, Xiye Bastida, Sam Kass Year: 2026 https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Be4Y2gJONSQ\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":96,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"How to Live on Earth\",\"instanceDates\":\"21 July-30 July\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"642001AQJSLDCMLPLRVLLNKLJKDTLVDGR\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-07-21T15:50:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-07-21T14:50:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-07-30T10:30:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-07-30T09:30:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false,\"attribute_Genre\":\"Cinema\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"Disowned at birth by his obscenely wealthy family, blue-collar Becket Redfellow will stop at nothing to reclaim his inheritance, no matter how many relatives stand in his way. | Duration: 1h 45m, Rating: 15 Credits\\r\\nRating: 15\\r\\nGenre: Dark Comedy\\r\\nDirector: John Patton Ford \\r\\nStars: Glen Powell, Margaret Qualley, Jessica Henwick https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=BxBof_p3_es&pp=ygUgaG93IHRvIG1ha2UgYSBraWxsaW5nIFVLIHRyYWlsZXI%3D\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":105,\"imageUrl\":\"https://system.spektrix.com/jw3/files/340fd109-48c4-408e-a3bf-d62ba4a7adc8.jpg\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"How to Make A Killing\",\"instanceDates\":\"13 April-15 April\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"https://system.spektrix.com/jw3/files/340fd109-48c4-408e-a3bf-d62ba4a7adc8-thumbnail.jpg\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"615601AHLLVGSDTQQMQBBTVMVHTGTNTNK\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-04-13T19:30:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-04-13T18:30:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-04-15T16:15:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-04-15T15:15:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Cinema\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false},{\"description\":\"With her life crashing down around her, Linda attempts to navigate her child's mysterious illness, her absent husband, a missing person, and an increasingly hostile relationship with her therapist. | Duration: 1h 53m, Rating: 15 \",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":113,\"imageUrl\":\"https://system.spektrix.com/jw3/files/eb54e70d-8a19-4ddc-ba8d-b35343a8aac2.jpg\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"If I Had Legs I'd Kick You\",\"instanceDates\":\"22 March-26 March\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"https://system.spektrix.com/jw3/files/eb54e70d-8a19-4ddc-ba8d-b35343a8aac2-thumbnail.jpg\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"606001APVCLVBGNBDGTHDRTCHKPLPPVKJ\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-03-22T14:30:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-03-22T14:30:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-03-26T16:20:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-03-26T16:20:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Cinema\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false},{\"description\":\"7.30pm - 9pm, £20, hybrid // We are delighted to welcome back Rick Sopher and Dr Abdulla Galadari (online) as they launch their new book, Illuminating Scriptural Connections. They will be interviewed by Daisy Scalchi, head of Religion at the BBC. \\r\\nFor the first time, the Torah's fifty-four weekly portions are viewed through the lens of the Qur'an, uncovering both the variations between the two texts as well as the shared stories, prophets, principles, and visions that illuminate a deeper spiritual kinship between Judaism and Islam.\\r\\nIt opens new spaces for interfaith understanding and connection, showing that the spiritual DNA of Judaism and Islam are intertwined far more closely than centuries of misunderstanding have allowed us to see.\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":90,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Illuminating Scriptural Connections: A Qur'anic Commentary on the Torah\",\"instanceDates\":\"15 September-15 September\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"652001AJRCKGGLNQMCMSNQJJLQCHHMPBL\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-09-15T19:30:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-09-15T18:30:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-09-15T19:30:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-09-15T18:30:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false,\"attribute_Genre\":\"Talks & Discussions\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"Rick Sopher and Dr Abdulla Galadari\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"7.30-9pm, building, £20 // We are delighted to welcome back to JW3 Professor Philippe Sands KC, a barrister and advocate who has appeared before many international courts and tribunals, and author of the groundbreaking East West Street, which traces his family’s history within the former Pale of Settlement. He will be joined by Deborah Posel, whose remarkable book A Darker Shade of Pale uncovers the hidden story of global migration at the turn of the twentieth century, from Lithuania to the British colony of South Africa. Through the story of her grandfather, Maurice Posel, she illuminates the struggles and aspirations of countless others, using the intimacy of a single narrative to explore much broader historical themes.\\r\\n\\r\\nThis conversation will complement the exhibition exploring Jewish life in Lithuania before the Holocaust. The project brings together photographs, letters, and personal stories shared by members of the UK Jewish community of Lithuanian descent. It traces a vibrant and deeply rooted society, follows the largest wave of Jewish migration in modern history between 1881 and 1914, and reflects on how the Lithuanian Jewish diaspora continues to shape life in Britain today. The exhibition will also explore themes of memory, belonging, and the act of remembering—how stories are preserved, transmitted, and reimagined across generations.\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":90,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"In conversation with Philippe Sands and Deborah Posel\",\"instanceDates\":\"4 November-4 November\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"636803AJTHKDLRVSDQGBTNTSBJKDHRBJL\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-11-04T19:30:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-11-04T19:30:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-11-04T19:30:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-11-04T19:30:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false,\"attribute_Genre\":\"Talks & Discussions\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Adult Education\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"Philippe Sands and Deborah Posel\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"Thursdays 2.15pm-4pm, £147 for 11 week block // Join us for our first Intermediate Bridge class & take your Bridge game to the next level.  \\r\\n\\r\\nThis 11-week course will refine your Bridge skills and play. Through guided teaching and focused practice, you’ll learn how to play with confidence, instinct and strategies.   \\r\\n\\r\\n \\r\\n\\r\\nWhat You’ll Learn \\r\\n\\r\\nBy the end of this course, you’ll be able to: \\r\\n\\r\\nLearn more sophisticated techniques to maximize trick-taking. \\r\\n\\r\\nStrengthen partnership communication through signalling and strategic planning. \\r\\n\\r\\n \\r\\n\\r\\nWho It’s For \\r\\n\\r\\nFollowing from our Beginner’s Bridge class, this course is designed for players who know the basics and are ready for deeper strategies, sharper card plays and more competitive bidding. \\r\\n\\r\\nYour Teacher \\r\\n\\r\\nAlan Brown moved to London four years ago. He was previously the joint owner of the successful Grimsby Bridge Academy with partner, England international Brian Smith. He taught bridge there for many years whist still pursuing his profession of school teacher. He has won numerous bridge trophies throughout a long-playing career and represented his county for many years. He loves teaching bridge. \\r\\n\\r\\n \\r\\n\\r\\nPractical Details: \\r\\n\\r\\nAll materials are provided \",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":105,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Intermediate Bridge Class\",\"instanceDates\":\"8 January-26 March\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"578401ASRNKCMKRTCGGTBCLPHRCNKPNTD\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-01-08T14:15:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-01-08T14:15:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-03-26T14:15:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-03-26T14:15:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Classes & Courses\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"True\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Body & Mind Courses\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"Alan Brown\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false},{\"description\":\"10am-3pm, free, venue hire, bookings made at www.investandescape.com // \",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":300,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":false,\"name\":\"Invest & Escape: Cyprus Property\",\"instanceDates\":\"22 March-22 March\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"608001ARSMSGVNJGNCGLLKVGPGQCVRJQB\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-03-22T10:00:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-03-22T10:00:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-03-22T10:00:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-03-22T10:00:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Talks & Discussions\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false},{\"description\":\"4.30-6.30pm, £30, building // French-Korean violinist Duval, coming to us for a second time, won the hearts of the JW3 audience with her spontaneity, warmth and naturalness.  Her playing effortlessly brings music fully to life. She will lead a string quintet including two outstanding violists Ami-Louise Johnsson ( Swedish-Japanese) and Emma Wernig (German-American), violist of the distinguished Doric Quartet; Tim Crawford, violinist in the thrilling Valo Quartet and Teyber Trio, and in hot demand at chamber music festivals all over Europe; and our Artistic Director, David Waterman, for 42 years cellist of the Endellion Quartet. \\r\\n\\r\\nMozart found that the addition of a second viola to a string quartet releases myriad possibilities of captivating colours and warmth, and his two quintets in this programme bear ample witness to this.  The D major, in particular, is one of his great late masterpieces and is comparable to any of his great operas. Beethoven’s Quintet finds him at his most delightfully genial, warm-hearted and affectionate, and it ends with a dramatic, virtuosic and exciting Finale. // Mozart Quintet in C minor K406 \\r\\n\\r\\nBeethoven Quintet in C Op 29 \\r\\n\\r\\nInterval  \\r\\n\\r\\nMozart   Quintet in D major K 593\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":120,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Irène Duval, Tim Crawford, Ami-Louise Johnsson, Emma Wernig, David Waterman\",\"instanceDates\":\"21 February-21 February\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"649803ABPHRBHNNQCGQLKCLSNSVJNCBNR\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2027-02-21T16:30:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2027-02-21T16:30:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2027-02-21T16:30:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2027-02-21T16:30:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false,\"attribute_Genre\":\"Music\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Classical Music Series\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"As their marriage quietly unravels, Alex faces middle age and an impending divorce, seeking new purpose in the New York comedy scene while Tess confronts the sacrifices she made for their family--forcing them to navigate co-parenting, identity, and whether love can take a new form. | Duration: 2h 23m, Rating: 15 | Films may be preceded by up to 20 minutes of advertisements and trailers. Specific timings will vary with each screening. We always recommend arriving on time.\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":121,\"imageUrl\":\"https://system.spektrix.com/jw3/files/abfa0d33-dfea-4a90-903b-da3cc28c1e48.jpg\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Is This Thing On?\",\"instanceDates\":\"22 February-26 February\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"https://system.spektrix.com/jw3/files/abfa0d33-dfea-4a90-903b-da3cc28c1e48-thumbnail.jpg\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"587601ASLGGHJLJHMBLHJCPGBQQRNJHCV\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-02-22T20:00:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-02-22T20:00:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-02-26T19:30:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-02-26T19:30:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Cinema\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false},{\"description\":\"6.30pm-8pm, building only, £20 // We are delighted to welcome back journalists Jonathan Harounoff and David Patrikarakos for a timely and in-depth conversation exploring what is really happening inside Iran, and how events there intersect with Israel, the region and the wider world. They will be joined in conversation by Efrat Sopher.\\r\\nJonathan Harounoff is a British-Iranian journalist who now serves as Israel’s International Spokesperson to the United Nations. His book Unveiled: Inside Iran’s #WomenLifeFreedom Revolt examines the profound gulf between the brutal Islamic Republic and the resilient Iranian people, who for more than 46 years have repeatedly risen up in pursuit of freedom and peace.\\r\\nDavid Patrikarakos is an internationally recognised journalist and author who has written for leading publications in the UK and United States. His book War in 140 Characters: How Social Media Is Reshaping Conflict in the 21st Century was published to international acclaim and is taught at Sandhurst, West Point and NATO, and used by the UK Ministry of Defence. In February 2022, The Wall Street Journal named it one of “7 books to read to understand why Russia wants Ukraine.” He is also the author of Nuclear Iran: The Birth of an Atomic State and the host of the Daily Mail’s Apocalypse Now podcast. David has lectured widely at universities and think tanks including Harvard, Yale, Oxford and Cambridge, and appears regularly on television and radio.\\r\\nTogether, the speakers will unpack Iran’s internal dynamics, its regional ambitions, and what the current moment means for Israel, Iran and global security.\\r\\nIn partnership with the Jewish News\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":90,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Israel & Iran Unpacked\",\"instanceDates\":\"29 April-29 April\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"594802APSCRKDDHSPDPHTRBCTMHNCHSJP\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-04-29T18:30:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-04-29T17:30:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-04-29T18:30:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-04-29T17:30:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Talks & Discussions\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Adult Education\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false},{\"description\":\"2pm-3pm, £20, hybrid, Wednesday 29 April 2026 // Join Jonathan Paris in his timely briefing on Israel’s upcoming elections this year. Paris will explore Israel’s pressing issues, its key political players and the potential outcomes of this pivotal election.\\r\\n\\r\\nJonathan will explore these key questions: \\r\\nHow could Trump, Iran and other regional security issues help Netanyahu whilst the ultra-Orthodox military exemption could cost him the election? \\r\\n\\r\\nHow will the election impact growing voices in Jewish diaspora for Aliyah as well as rising numbers of Israelis emigrating abroad?\\r\\n\\r\\nWill Israel's resilient economy, if it continues, help Netanyahu win?\\r\\n\\r\\nJonathan Paris is a London-based Middle East analyst and former fellow at the Council on Foreign Relations in New York. He is currently Senior Fellow at the Center for Advanced Studies on Terrorism (CAST) and Senior Advisor Emeritus at the Chertoff Group. He appears regularly on Sky News and Al Arabiya and has been quoted in the New York Times and other publications\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":60,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Israel’s Approaching Election: Will Netanyahu survive?\",\"instanceDates\":\"29 April-29 April\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"591202AVRRHSQTCVDPSPNGDPVLSQPBTNK\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-04-29T14:00:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-04-29T13:00:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-04-29T14:00:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-04-29T13:00:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Talks & Discussions\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Adult Education\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"Jonathan Paris\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false},{\"description\":\"7.30pm-8.30pm, £10, online only // This year's election in Israel is one of the most high-stakes in years. Join two of the UK's most notable journalists on Israel as they discuss likely outcomes and scenarios, and respond to your questions. Anshel Pfeffer is The Economist's Israel correspondent. Before that he was a columnist and senior correspondent at Ha'aretz. He is author of the book Bibi: The Turbulent Life & Times of Benjamin Netanyahu. Jonathan Freedland is a columnist for The Guardian. He co-presents the podcast Unholy with Israeli news anchor and journalist Yonit Levi.\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":60,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Israeli Election Update\",\"instanceDates\":\"28 July-28 July\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"644001ARMSCQNHGTJCTCHRJLHSVMMJDMQ\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-07-28T19:30:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-07-28T18:30:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-07-28T19:30:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-07-28T18:30:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false,\"attribute_Genre\":\"Talks & Discussions\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"Vahid, an Azerbaijani auto mechanic, was once imprisoned by Iranian authorities. During his sentence, he was interrogated blindfolded. One day, a man named Eqbal enters his workshop. His prosthetic leg creaks, and Vahid thinks he recognizes one of his former torturers. | Duration: 1h 43m, Rating: 12A \",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":103,\"imageUrl\":\"https://system.spektrix.com/jw3/files/292b5192-4d54-485b-990e-12ff79901475.jpg\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"It Was Just an Accident\",\"instanceDates\":\"4 January-8 January\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"https://system.spektrix.com/jw3/files/292b5192-4d54-485b-990e-12ff79901475-thumbnail.jpg\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"579801ADTSMMNMTBNQQTSDLCPRNJDSBVD\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-01-04T12:30:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-01-04T12:30:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-01-08T11:00:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-01-08T11:00:00Z\",\"altText\":\"It Was Just an Accident\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Cinema\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false},{\"description\":\"2pm-3.30pm, £20, hybrid, Monday 11 May 2026 // Jack Lemmon was one of the most versatile Hollywood actors from the 1950’s to the 1990’s.\\r\\nHe starred in 50 films ranging from comedies like “Some Like It Hot & The Odd Couple” to Dramas like “The China Syndrome & Glen Garry Glen Ross” winning two Oscar’s along the way. Let’s look at his life and his amazing career.\\r\\n\\r\\nGeorge McGhee has over 35 years of experience, latterly at the BBC, where he oversaw all feature films and international TV series acquisitions.\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":90,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Jack Lemmon\",\"instanceDates\":\"11 May-11 May\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"592001APBBHPSVLJDKNBJVKQGBHQDTTNM\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-05-11T14:00:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-05-11T13:00:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-05-11T14:00:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-05-11T13:00:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Talks & Discussions\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Adult Education\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"George McGhee\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false},{\"description\":\"7pm-8.30pm, £20, in building // Join us as John Steinberg launches his compelling new novella, Jacob Returns. \\r\\n\\r\\nJohn will be in conversation with a panel of distinguished thinkers as they discuss the personal and universal themes behind his latest work. The evening will explore the ways in which the novella mirrors John's own spiritual journey. \\r\\n\\r\\nThe panel will feature: \\r\\nJohn Steinberg, Author of Jacob Returns \\r\\nDr Tali Lowenthal, Associate Professor,Dept. of Hebrew & Jewish Studies, UCL \\r\\nPatricia Pitchon, Author, freelance journalist & retired psychotherapist \\r\\nRabbi Dr Harvey Belovski, Organisational psychologist & Rabbinic Head, University Jewish Chaplaincy\\r\\n\\r\\nIn partnership with Spiro Ark.\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":90,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Jacob Returns\",\"instanceDates\":\"22 April-22 April\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"579201ACSDTTBVPNBTPDTHQRMCMRRGTKN\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-04-22T19:00:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-04-22T18:00:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-04-22T19:00:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-04-22T18:00:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Talks & Discussions\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"John Steinberg\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false},{\"description\":\"7.30pm-9pm, £15 // Recommended ages 13+ // Please note a change in line-up from originally advertised, with the event now chaired by Elte Rauch // James Joyce's novel follows Jewish Dubliner Leopold Bloom on his odyssey around the city on 16th June 1904.Joyce famously described his book as 'a novel of two peoples', the Irish and the Jewish. For Joyce enthusiasts worldwide, 16th June marks Bloomsday.\\r\\n\\r\\nJoin us for the first ever 'kosher' Bloomsday at JW3, in partnership with Jewish Literary Foundation and London Irish Centre. Elte Rauch shares her Joyce enthusiasm with Zachary Leader whose recent Ellmann's Joyce: The Biography of a Masterpiece and its Maker was a Times Literary Supplement Book of the Year, and award-winning Irish novelist Eimear McBride who counts Ulysses as one of her biggest inspirations.\\r\\n\\r\\nEimear McBride is the author of four novels: ‘A Girl is a Half-formed Thing’, ‘The Lesser Bohemians,’ ‘Strange Hotel’ and ‘The City Changes Its Face’, as well as the non-fiction work ‘Something Out of Place: Women & Disgust’ and the short plays ‘Mouthpieces.’ She held the inaugural Creative Fellowship at the Beckett Research Centre, University of Reading and, in 2022, wrote and directed A Very Short Film About Longing (DMC Films/BBC), which screened in the London Film Festival. She is the recipient of the Women’s Prize for Fiction, Goldsmiths Prize, Geoffrey Faber Memorial Prize, Kerry Group Irish Novel of the Award, and the James Tait Black Memorial Prize.She lives in London with her Irish-Jewish family.\\r\\n\\r\\nZachary Leader is an Emeritus Professor of English Literature at the University of Roehampton in London and is the author or editor of a dozen books on modern British and American literature and English Romantic Poetry, among them biographies of the novelists Kingsley Amis and Saul Bellow and the recently published Ellmann’s Joyce: The Biography of a Masterpiece and Its Maker. He is the General Editor of The Oxford History of Life-Writing, a seven-volume series, and a Fellow of the Royal Society of Literature, has dual UK/US citizenship, and lives in London.\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":90,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"James Joyce's Ulysses - A Novel of Two Peoples\",\"instanceDates\":\"16 June-16 June\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"595201APPMVDDHMLPTSTPSLVTHNGLNRBC\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-06-16T19:30:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-06-16T18:30:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-06-16T19:30:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-06-16T18:30:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Talks & Discussions\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Adult Education\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false},{\"description\":\"7.15-8.30pm, £20, building // One of the leading members of the Impressionists, Renoir (1841–1919) was celebrated for his intimate portraits and light-filled hubs of Modernity.   \\r\\n\\r\\nMore than any of his contemporaries, he was committed to chronicling fleeting moments of love, candid domesticity, and the sociability of dance halls and theatres. \\r\\n\\r\\nTo coincide with the exhibition at the National Gallery, Renoir and Love (3 October 2026- 31 January 2027), this talk will examine Renoir’s complex relationship with his Jewish patrons and his transition from Impressionist style to more classical sculptural compositions. \\r\\n\\r\\nSophie Lachowsky is an art historian, lecturer and writer, working with leading institutions and private galleries in the culture and heritage sectors. \\r\\n \\r\\nShe graduated from the Courtauld Institute with an MA in History of Art, with a focus on post-war abstraction, on which she has published in academic journals and exhibition catalogues. \\r\\n \\r\\nSophie strongly believes in the power of art, to shape our thinking.  She is enthusiastic about creating a rich, interdisciplinary perspective that appeals to a multigenerational audience. \",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":75,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Jewish Patrons: The Career Choices of Pierre-Auguste Renoir\",\"instanceDates\":\"18 November-18 November\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"637402AKJJNGJTNDBKSTDPVQVTCBLBTTJ\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-11-18T19:15:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-11-18T19:15:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-11-18T19:15:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-11-18T19:15:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false,\"attribute_Genre\":\"Talks & Discussions\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Adult Education\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"Sophie Lachowsky\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"Tuesdays, 2-3.30pm, £20 per session or £60 for 3 sessions // This three-part course explores some of the most radical and creative responses to modernity in recent Jewish history.   \\r\\n\\r\\n \\r\\n\\r\\nSession 1: Tuesday 6 Oct — Jewish Diasporism  \\r\\n\\r\\nWhat does it mean to live as a people dispersed yet connected? We begin by exploring Jewish diasporism as both a religious and secular idea —examining how thinkers and communities reimagined Jewish life beyond nationalism. From 70CE and the destruction of the temple through to Melanie Kaye/Kantrowitz and R.B. Kitaj we’ll look at how diasporism has evolved as a movement.   \\r\\n\\r\\n \\r\\n\\r\\nSession 2: Tuesday 3 Nov — Hasidism  \\r\\nBorn in the 18th century and often seen as inward-looking, Hasidism was in fact a bold spiritual revolution. We’ll trace its development from the Ba’al Shem Tov to its 19th-century golden age, asking how it responded to modernity, and why it continues to resonate today through Neohasidism and Jewish Renewal.   \\r\\n\\r\\n \\r\\n\\r\\nSession 3: Tuesday 1 Dec — The Bund and Other Jewish Movements  \\r\\nFrom mysticism to political action: we turn to the Jewish Labour Bund and other movements that redefined Jewish identity through socialism, culture, and activism. How did they challenge tradition and normative politics—and what legacies do they leave behind?  \\r\\n\\r\\n  \\r\\n\\r\\nAcross three sessions, we’ll uncover a rich landscape of ideas, debates, and experiments in Jewish life—many of which still shape our world today.  \\r\\n\\r\\n \\r\\n\\r\\nYael Roberts is a Jewish educator, artist, and community builder. She is a PhD student in Creative and Critical Practice at Sussex University, where she has received the Morris & Bessie Emanuel Scholarship in Modern Jewish History and Culture. Her research explores the 19th century Hasidic homilies of Izbica/Radzyn. Outside of her studies, she is a visiting service leader and educator at Exeter Synagogue, and an educator for the Jewish Learning Collaborative. Originally from St. Louis, Missouri, she has lived in the UK for over a decade. She has taught across the UK at Limmud UK and Azara Yeshiva, and has worked at Alyth Synagogue, Westminster Synagogue, and Reform Judaism.  \",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":90,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Jewish Revolutionary Movements [In Building]\",\"instanceDates\":\"6 October-1 December\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"644201ABPVQKKQKLBHLTBMCPCGTRHCQDL\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-10-06T14:00:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-10-06T13:00:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-12-01T14:00:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-12-01T14:00:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false,\"attribute_Genre\":\"Classes & Courses\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"Yael Roberts\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"Tuesdays, 2-3.30pm, £20 per session or £60 for 3 sessions // This three-part course explores some of the most radical and creative responses to modernity in recent Jewish history. Session 1: Tuesday 6 Oct — Jewish Diasporism What does it mean to live as a people dispersed yet connected? We begin by exploring Jewish diasporism as both a religious and secular idea —examining how thinkers and communities reimagined Jewish life beyond nationalism. From 70CE and the destruction of the temple through to Melanie Kaye/Kantrowitz and R.B. Kitaj we’ll look at how diasporism has evolved as a movement. Session 2: Tuesday 3 Nov — Hasidism Born in the 18th century and often seen as inward-looking, Hasidism was in fact a bold spiritual revolution. We’ll trace its development from the Ba’al Shem Tov to its 19th-century golden age, asking how it responded to modernity, and why it continues to resonate today through Neohasidism and Jewish Renewal. Session 3: Tuesday 1 Dec — The Bund and Other Jewish Movements From mysticism to political action: we turn to the Jewish Labour Bund and other movements that redefined Jewish identity through socialism, culture, and activism. How did they challenge tradition and normative politics—and what legacies do they leave behind? Across three sessions, we’ll uncover a rich landscape of ideas, debates, and experiments in Jewish life—many of which still shape our world today. Yael Roberts is a Jewish educator, artist, and community builder. She is a PhD student in Creative and Critical Practice at Sussex University, where she has received the Morris & Bessie Emanuel Scholarship in Modern Jewish History and Culture. Her research explores the 19th century Hasidic homilies of Izbica/Radzyn. Outside of her studies, she is a visiting service leader and educator at Exeter Synagogue, and an educator for the Jewish Learning Collaborative. Originally from St. Louis, Missouri, she has lived in the UK for over a decade. She has taught across the UK at Limmud UK and Azara Yeshiva, and has worked at Alyth Synagogue, Westminster Synagogue, and Reform Judaism.\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":90,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Jewish Revolutionary Movements [Online]\",\"instanceDates\":\"6 October-1 December\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"644401AJCGSDKTKHTSHBMDMCDMPGJLCPN\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-10-06T14:00:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-10-06T13:00:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-12-01T14:00:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-12-01T14:00:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false,\"attribute_Genre\":\"Classes & Courses\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"Yael Roberts\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"11am-1pm, £20, Tuesday 30 June 2026 // Explore London’s theatreland and discover connections with Jewish actors, impresarios, writers and producers, not forgetting the theatres (and cinemas) themselves. The cast for this fun and entertaining walk includes Lionel Bart, Lord Delfont, Barbra Streisand, Henry Goodman, Alfred Marks, Vivian van Damm and many more. Credits are also due to Lyons for the refreshments and Freed for the dance shoes.\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":120,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Jewish Theatreland\",\"instanceDates\":\"30 June-30 June\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"516402ALMBJBPDKKMTLDDCGGPQQKGMPQR\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-06-30T11:00:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-06-30T10:00:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-06-30T11:00:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-06-30T10:00:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Walks\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Walking Tours\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"Rachel Kolsky\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false},{\"description\":\"7.30pm-8.45pm, £20, in building, Thursday 25 June 2026 // Join us for an enlightening evening exploring the remarkable world of 20th-century Jewish hairdressers with Zuleika Rodgers and Leslie Cavendish.\\r\\n\\r\\nZuleika Rodgers, Associate Professor in Jewish Studies and Director of the Centre for Jewish Studies, will discuss her forthcoming book—a history of the profound influence Jewish hairdressers had on fashion throughout the 20th century. Her personal connection to this story runs deep: her father was the first Vidal Sassoon stylist to come to Dublin.\\r\\nWe will also hear from Leslie Cavendish, The Beatles’ hairdresser from 1967 to 1975. Cavendish left school at just 15, with no formal artistic training, to pursue a career in hairdressing. He went on to work with iconic 1960s stylist Vidal Sassoon and soon counted many of the era’s biggest stars among his clients, including Keith Moon, the Bee Gees, the Dave Clark Five, James Hunt, Terence Stamp, Jane Asher, James Taylor, and many more. But the highlight of his career was styling four of the most famous heads of hair in history: The Beatles.\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":75,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Jews in Hairdressing\",\"instanceDates\":\"25 June-25 June\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"594001ANQLRGGJQVCGCGHJCHBBRVLDKCD\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-06-25T19:30:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-06-25T18:30:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-06-25T19:30:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-06-25T18:30:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Talks & Discussions\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Adult Education\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"Zuleika Rodgers\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false},{\"description\":\"3-5.30pm, £12 early bird | £15 pre-sale | £18 door | £12 students & under 18 // Early bid tickets end 15 Jan // Join us at JW3 on 29 March 2026 for a vibrant evening of live music featuring the JMI Youth Big Band - a group of dedicated young musicians aged 11–19 exploring Jewish music through jazz and creative improvisation. Under the guidance of bandleader Sam Eastmond, the ensemble brings fresh energy to traditional melodies, offering a unique and heartfelt take on Jewish musical heritage. It’s a chance to hear how the next generation is engaging with culture, creativity, and collaboration. \\r\\n\\r\\nThis special concert is a joint event with NYJO (National Youth Jazz Orchestra) Under 18s, showcasing a wide range of musical talent from across both ensembles. Together, they’ll present an exciting mix of styles and influences, highlighting the richness and diversity of youth music today.\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":150,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"JMI Youth Big Band x NYJO: The Future of Jazz\",\"instanceDates\":\"15 March-15 March\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"565001ALDNRGDTJQQNQGSDSHPHHJGQHLH\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-03-15T15:00:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-03-15T15:00:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-03-15T15:00:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-03-15T15:00:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Music\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Arts & Culture\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false},{\"description\":\"19:00 // 22 Oct 2026 // £20 // Go behind the scenes with Emmy and BAFTA-winning maestro John Altman. This intimate musical retrospective blends hilarious, star-studded anecdotes - from Bob Marley to Amy Winehouse - with live piano reimagining his iconic hits from Titanic, Life of Brian, and George Michael.\\r\\n\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":150,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"John Altman: The Hidden Man\",\"instanceDates\":\"22 October-22 October\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"631601ARMRLNBMJGHDMQTTRRMQSBJJRCP\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-10-22T19:00:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-10-22T18:00:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-10-22T19:00:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-10-22T18:00:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false,\"attribute_Genre\":\"Music\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"\\\"7pm-8.50pm, £18, in building, 12+, Sunday 21 June 2026 // A night of new Jewish writing about coming out, being proud and feeling guilty for missing Friday night dinner\\r\\n\\r\\nEchoes Theatre co. and THE JEWish CABARET present a night of Jewish joy. Leave the politics behind and enjoy new short comedic plays and original musical theatre songs all about the joys (and oys) of being LGBTQ+ and Jewish.\\r\\n\\r\\nSupported by The Shoresh Charitable Trust, The Hirschel Foundation and Ann & Charles Kessler\\\"\\r\\n\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":110,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Joyfully Jewish: Rainbows on Rye\",\"instanceDates\":\"21 June-21 June\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"592801ASSDSKSRBGVQPBBNHPDNHRBSHJJ\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-06-21T19:00:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-06-21T18:00:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-06-21T19:00:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-06-21T18:00:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Performance\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Arts & Culture\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false},{\"description\":\"\\\"19:00 // 1 Nov 2026 // £18 // Echoes Theatre Co. and THE JEWish CABARET present a night of Jewish Joy! A night of new Jewish writing all about leaving home, settling in and finding the perfect beigel.\\r\\n\\r\\nSupported by Shoresh Charitable Trust, The Hirschel Foundation and Ann & Charles Kessler\\\"\\r\\n\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":110,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Joyfully Jewish: Strangers in a Strange Land\",\"instanceDates\":\"1 November-1 November\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"632801AJJHGBMHTTPCNCVVKLPNLHVDGTP\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-11-01T19:00:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-11-01T19:00:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-11-01T19:00:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-11-01T19:00:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false,\"attribute_Genre\":\"Performance\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"TBC\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":240,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":false,\"name\":\"JW3 Annual Gala 2026\",\"instanceDates\":\"14 October-14 October\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"630801AJCHRPDCSCTLTJRKQKRMGHQDCQS\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-10-14T18:30:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-10-14T17:30:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-10-14T18:30:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-10-14T17:30:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Special Events\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false},{\"description\":\"\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":120,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":false,\"name\":\"JW3 Annual Property Breakfast 2026\",\"instanceDates\":\"24 September-24 September\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"628203AJHNCLRNPHBBHLMVHVRJMHVMPSS\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-09-24T07:30:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-09-24T06:30:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-09-24T07:30:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-09-24T06:30:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Special Events\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false},{\"description\":\"Monthly, 7.30-9.30pm, £17 (£12 as of May 2026), age 16+ // JW3 Comedy Club is back showcasing the best in Jewish Comedy. We’re bringing you Jewish and Jew-ish comics, from rising stars to names you'll recognise, and not just from sitting next to them at your niece's bat mitzvah! Be aware, you might hear one or two words that your Bubbe only said in Yiddish, hoping you wouldn't understand...   Line Ups will be announced through JW3’s socials and mailing list so make sure not to miss out.\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":120,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"JW3 Comedy Club\",\"instanceDates\":\"26 May-11 November\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"564401AHRHMPHHMKJNRGDTPNKTBVHCNVH\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-05-26T19:30:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-05-26T18:30:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-11-11T19:30:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-11-11T19:30:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Comedy\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Comedy\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false},{\"description\":\"1pm - 3pm, free // Join us for a warm and welcoming afternoon of shared food, community connection, and celebration. Hear inspiring stories and help us recognise our amazing volunteers.\\r\\n\\r\\nWhether you’re a long-time volunteer, new to the community, or simply want to take part, everyone is welcome. This is a wonderful opportunity to meet others, connect, and celebrate the spirit of giving back together.\\r\\n\\r\\nThis gathering forms part of two national celebrations: Volunteers’ Week 2026 and The Big Lunch.\\r\\n\\r\\nVolunteers’ Week is a UK-wide campaign recognising the incredible contributions of volunteers. Since its launch in 1984, it has spent over 40 years shining a light on the people who give their time, energy, and care to strengthen our communities. This year, as the campaign continues with a fresh and vibrant identity, we are proud to honour the diversity, unity, and impact of volunteering right here at JW3. \\r\\n\\r\\nVolunteers’ Week is all about gratitude and togetherness, and there’s no better way to mark the occasion than by gathering around the table.\\r\\n\\r\\nTaking place on the first weekend in June, The Big Lunch is the UK’s annual get-together for neighbours and communities. Since 2009, millions of people have come together to share friendship, food, and fun—with over 10 million participants in 2025 alone.\\r\\n\\r\\nLet’s eat, connect, and celebrate the people who make our community thrive.\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":120,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"JW3's Big (Bagel) Lunch\",\"instanceDates\":\"7 June-7 June\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"625801AGVMSKRRQKJMQLBSTBGTBVQRGDN\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-06-07T13:00:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-06-07T12:00:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-06-07T13:00:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-06-07T12:00:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Social Action\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false},{\"description\":\"2pm-6pm, £10 adult (16+), £7 child (under 16s) // It’s JW3’s Bar Mitzvah year — we’re throwing a party and you’re invited. This is more than a moment; it’s a milestone, marked with music, laughter, great food, and even better company.\\r\\nThroughout the afternoon enjoy workshops and tasters to see what JW3 is all about. There will be music and memories from across the years as we toast to growth, development and our entrance into adulthood.\\r\\nWith activities for everyone aged 1–101, plus plenty of dancing, this is a celebration of how far we’ve come and an exciting look toward what’s next. Join us as we toast to growth, development, and our step into adulthood.\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":240,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"JW3's B'Mitzvah Party\",\"instanceDates\":\"28 June-28 June\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"622201AMGVGVMKKSKDRKBQLLGPKMSMBLD\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-06-28T14:00:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-06-28T13:00:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-06-28T14:00:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-06-28T13:00:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Special Events\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false},{\"description\":\"Keith Jarrett's legendary performance in January 1975 nearly didn't happen.  \\r\\n\\r\\n \\r\\n\\r\\nBased on a true story, Köln 75 follows how the concert was conceived and orchestrated by the efforts of a teenage up and coming concert promoter, Vera Brandes, (played by German actress Mala Emde). Her enthusiasm set her to multitasking -- from organizing the concert venue (the Cologne Opera House), promoting the event, and selling the tickets, to convincing Jarrett to perform when he almost dropped out when the Bösendorfer Imperial Grand piano he was promised was nowhere to be found. John Magaro plays Jarrett with his own intensity, a sublime counterpoint to Mala Emde's joyful portrayal of the enthusiastic and unstoppable Vera.  \\r\\n\\r\\n \\r\\n\\r\\nKöln 75 captures the compelling, entertaining and, until now, unknown back story about Jarrett's one-hour, entirely improvised concert, which became the best-selling solo album in jazz history. // \\r\\n\\r\\n \\r\\n\\r\\nDuration: 117 minutes \\r\\n\\r\\nRating: 15 \\r\\n\\r\\nDirector: Ido Fluk \\r\\n\\r\\nCast: Mala Emde, John Magaro, Michael Chernus \\r\\n\\r\\nYear: 2025 \\r\\n\\r\\nLanguage: German & English \\r\\nSubtitles: English \",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":117,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Köln 75\",\"instanceDates\":\"26 June-2 July\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"629801ALRGTCQHLNPTQKPMMJJGKQJJRJK\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-06-26T10:30:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-06-26T09:30:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-07-02T13:00:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-07-02T12:00:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Cinema\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false},{\"description\":\"8pm-9pm, £15, Thursday 11 June 2026 // Hugo Max’s films, paintings and performances draw upon collective history and religious practices, offering an absurdist reflection on Jewish identity.\\r\\n\\r\\nFollowing screenings and performances at the Austrian Filmmuseum, London’s BFI Southbank and Prince Charles Cinema, Max joins us for a programme of his experimental short films interspersed with live music and a Q&A.\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":60,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Kosher Giraffes & Other Tails\",\"instanceDates\":\"11 June-11 June\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"591001AGTLTLPLQJGHGCMQNSQSSGCRJVM\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-06-11T20:00:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-06-11T19:00:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-06-11T20:00:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-06-11T19:00:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Music\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Arts & Culture\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false},{\"description\":\"7-8.15pm, free, hybrid //  JW3’s Kristallnacht commemorative event centres on Michael Moritz’s Ausländer, a deeply personal exploration of family, flight and inherited memory.  Sorting through papers and photographs after his mother’s death, Moritz uncovers the history of close family members murdered by the Nazis. His search takes him into a past marked by tragedy, grief and the dark shadows cast on Jewish life by the Holocaust.  His parents left Germany as child refugees, escaping to London before later settling in Cardiff after the war. Yet the idea of being a stranger or outsider ‘an Ausländer” continued to haunt the family, running through Moritz’s childhood and resurfacing in his adopted home of California, where he became one of Silicon Valley’s most celebrated investors.  This commemorative evening will include conversation, music and time for reflection, marking Kristallnacht while considering the continuing urgency of Moritz’s story: what happens when ordinary people give license to despots, and how the lessons of the past continue to resonate today.\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":75,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Kristallnacht Commemoration: Ausländer\",\"instanceDates\":\"5 November-5 November\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"646401ABDHQJLNMGCGJRQNBTSQGQBGCSP\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-11-05T19:00:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-11-05T19:00:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-11-05T19:00:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-11-05T19:00:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false,\"attribute_Genre\":\"Talks & Discussions\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Holocaust Learning\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"Sir Michael Moritz\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"7pm-10pm, £15, Sunday 7 June 2026 // Content warning: This event includes strong language, sexual references, and explicit imagery, which some audience members may find challenging. // Running order\\r\\n18:00 – Exhibition\\r\\n19:00 – Punk Play, Poetry and Interviews\\r\\n21:00 – Social\\r\\n21:30 – End// The relationship between Jewish culture and punk rock is as enduring as it is influential. From the genre’s explosive emergence in the mid-1970s to its contemporary incarnations, figures with Jewish roots have been present at pivotal moments in punk history.\\r\\n\\r\\nThis one-off event brings together some of those key voices alongside forever-punk Mark Jay and music historian Alain Dein to trace a neon thread through five decades of rebellion and reinvention.\\r\\n\\r\\nIn true punk spirit, expect a cut-and-paste happening: live interviews, DJ sets, a photo exhibition, poetry, film, and a very special punk play. Raise a glass - and some chaos -with us.\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":180,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"L'Chaim / L'Chaos: 50 Years of Jewish Punk\",\"instanceDates\":\"7 June-7 June\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"591201AQDPTMLCHSJJRLVBRSGJVPPLJHQ\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-06-07T18:00:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-06-07T17:00:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-06-07T18:00:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-06-07T17:00:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Music\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Arts & Culture\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false},{\"description\":\"7.30pm-9.30pm, £20, in building, Tuesday 7 July 2026, filmed with English subtitles // Le cose non dette - things left unsaid // Following its successful screenings in Rome and Milan, Harif and JW3 are proud to present  the London premiere of this documentary directed by Hamos Guetta. Set in Libya under Colonel Gaddafi, the film tells the story of a remarkable Jewish man and the courage and heroism of a Jewish woman.\\r\\nThe film will be followed by a Q&A with the director, Hamos Guetta, who will be joining us from Rome.\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":81,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Le cose non dette\",\"instanceDates\":\"7 July-7 July\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"594201AKSMGHJQQRBBGBPMDKKNGTHVKSB\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-07-07T19:30:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-07-07T18:30:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-07-07T19:30:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-07-07T18:30:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Talks & Discussions\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Adult Education\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false},{\"description\":\"Lemon Tree (2008) is a poignant and deeply human drama from Eran Riklis that uses a simple yet revealing story to illuminate the complexities of life on the Israeli-Palestinian border. The film centers on Salma, a Palestinian widow whose peaceful existence tending her family’s lush lemon grove is shattered when the Israeli Defense Minister moves into a fortified home right next door and declares her trees a security threat. \\r\\nRefusing to surrender her heritage, Salma launches a courageous legal fight — taking her case all the way to the Israeli Supreme Court — with the help of a young lawyer and unexpected sympathy from the minister’s own lonely wife. Through rich performances and Riklis’s finely calibrated storytelling, Lemon Tree reveals how courage, empathy and quiet resistance can flourish even amid deep political divides, turning a fight over fruit trees into a resonant human drama. | This film is in Hebrew and Arabic with English subtitles | Duration: 1h 46m\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":106,\"imageUrl\":\"https://system.spektrix.com/jw3/files/e1358ce6-c856-476d-bf64-5921d1d62d58.jpg\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Lemon Tree + Q&A\",\"instanceDates\":\"10 May-10 May\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"https://system.spektrix.com/jw3/files/e1358ce6-c856-476d-bf64-5921d1d62d58-thumbnail.jpg\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"618201ASBHBTBTPBLRNSLLDHDDPRBKGJR\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-05-10T14:30:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-05-10T13:30:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-05-10T14:30:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-05-10T13:30:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Cinema\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Seret Film Festival\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false},{\"description\":\"Defiant, brilliant, and untamable, Leonora Carrington refused to live by anyone’s rules but her own.  \\r\\n\\r\\n \\r\\n\\r\\nIn the charged atmosphere of 1930s Paris, she falls under the spell of the Surrealist movement—and into a passionate, volatile love affair with the German artist Max Ernst. Together, they create a world where art and life blur, surrounded by icons like André Breton and Salvador Dalí, and build an otherworldly refuge in the south of France filled with sculpted creatures and strange, living dreams.  \\r\\n\\r\\n  \\r\\n\\r\\nLeonora in the Morning Light is the epic true story of a woman who turned trauma into transcendence, creating beauty from chaos and forging a legacy that changed the history of modern art. //\\r\\n\\r\\n \\r\\n\\r\\nDuration: 103 minutes \\r\\n\\r\\nRating: 15 \\r\\n\\r\\nDirector: Thor Klein & Lena Vurma \\r\\n\\r\\nCast: Olivia Vinall, Alexander Scheer, Cassandra Ciangherotti, Ryan Gage, Istvan Teglas, Luis Gerardo Mendez \\r\\n\\r\\nYear: 2025 \\r\\n\\r\\nLanguage: English \",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":103,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Leonora in the Morning Light\",\"instanceDates\":\"21 June-24 June\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"629201ALCTHCJDNBNSNQGQJTQTCQDLVQN\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-06-21T13:15:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-06-21T12:15:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-06-24T17:00:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-06-24T16:00:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Cinema\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false},{\"description\":\"8pm-9.15pm, £12 // On October 7, ordinary lives were violently disrupted. \\r\\n\\r\\nThis special evening brings together five Israelis, all connected through the Hapoel Rishon football club, whose lives were shaped by that day in profoundly different ways. \\r\\n\\r\\nAmong them are a hostage who survived 491 days in captivity; a soldier whose life-threatening injuries required five emergency operations in 48 hours; a survivor of the Nova music festival; a volunteer police officer; and an investigator in the Missing Persons Unit who spent 300 days searching for missing civilians. \\r\\n\\r\\nTogether, they will share deeply personal stories of trauma, resilience, survival and courage, and reflect on how October 7 continues to shape their lives today. \\r\\n\\r\\nIn conversation with Rachel Riley MBE, this will be a thoughtful and deeply human evening exploring loss, endurance, and what comes next. \\r\\n\\r\\n \\r\\n\\r\\nOur special guest speakers are: \\r\\n\\r\\nOr Levy – held hostage for 491 days after being kidnapped from the Nova festival, where his wife was murdered \\r\\n\\r\\nDoron Mizrahi – survived the Nova Festival, helping evacuate wounded festival goers \\r\\n\\r\\nSaar Nechemia – suffered life threatening injuries after being attacked by terrorists \\r\\n\\r\\nIdo Stern - 300 days reserve duty in the Missing Persons Unit searching for missing civilians \\r\\n\\r\\nMeital Gabby - volunteer in the Israeli Police; brother survived Nova Festival \",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":75,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Lives Interrupted: Voices of Heroism and Survival from October 7 \",\"instanceDates\":\"24 May-24 May\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"626001ALLVVGBRTLQJHLHPPRJRGLJLSPP\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-05-24T20:00:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-05-24T19:00:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-05-24T20:00:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-05-24T19:00:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Talks & Discussions\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false},{\"description\":\"7.30pm-8.30pm, £15, in building, 13+, Wednesday 24 June 2026 // YIDDISH THEATRE REBOOTED\\r\\nThe London Yiddish Players, London’s first Yiddish theatre company in 30 years, bring the traditions of Yiddish theatre kvetching and screaming into 2026 with their debut performance: a hilarious and moving mishmash of new writing and sketches alongside extracts from Yiddish classics such as Ansky’s The Dybbuk and the works of Sholem Aleykhem, writer of what later became Fiddler On The Roof.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nDirected by comedian/writer David Schneider, together with theatre artist/Yiddish educator Tamara Micner, and East End historian/singer Vivi Lachs, the company consists of professional and non-professional performers, Yiddish speakers and non-Yiddish speakers. \\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nNo knowledge of Yiddish is necessary to attend and enjoy. Though by the time you leave, you may well feel, to use a Yiddish word, like a maven.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nNone of this would be possible without the support of the Yiddish Cafe Trust and its chair Stephen Ogin; UCL’s Department of Hebrew & Jewish Studies and Associate Professor of Yiddish Studies, Sonia Gollance; and the generosity of the Shoresh Charitable Trust.\\r\\n\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":75,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"London Yiddish Players: Yiddish Theatre Reboot\",\"instanceDates\":\"24 June-24 June\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"593001ALCRCJLNJBKLSPRQHDPDKLTTKRC\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-06-24T19:30:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-06-24T18:30:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-06-24T19:30:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-06-24T18:30:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Performance\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Arts & Culture\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false},{\"description\":\"Walking tour, 2-4pm, £20 // Join us for an enlightening walking tour to explore 1000 years of Jewish history. This experience is for everyone interested in London’s extraordinary culture and heritage! \\r\\n\\r\\nStarting in Aldgate and crossing the historic City of London, you will discover the fascinating story of London’s Jewish population from medieval times to the present day. Learn about the Jews brought to England by William the Conqueror after 1066, the expulsion under Edward I in 1290, the resettlement under Cromwell in 1656, and subsequent Jewish immigration up to the present day. \\r\\n\\r\\nDuring our walk, you will see many of the most important sites in the City – including those connected to London’s rich and complex Jewish history. Hear about various London Jewish personalities over the years, and about Jewish life in Britain and beyond. Don’t miss this opportunity to delve into centuries of Jewish and general history in London. \",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":120,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"London’s Jewish History over the Centuries\",\"instanceDates\":\"8 November-8 November\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"635403AMJDKQGTDRBQHLHMTVRGSQKKJMM\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-11-08T14:00:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-11-08T14:00:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-11-08T14:00:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-11-08T14:00:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false,\"attribute_Genre\":\"Walks\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Walking Tours\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"Marc Gardiner\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"2pm-4pm, £20, Sunday 19 July 2026 // Step into the footsteps of brilliant minds who shaped the modern world. This fascinating walking tour along the scenic Regent’s Canal unveils the stories of visionary scientists, engineers, and innovators whose groundbreaking work transformed transportation, medicine, electronics, and AI.\\r\\n\\r\\nAs you stroll through this historic area—often compared to Amsterdam’s charming canal life—you’ll uncover the hidden history behind world-changing discoveries and inventions. Led by expert guide Boaz Tal, this tour offers a unique blend of history, science, and culture, bringing the past to life in the very place where innovation thrived.\\r\\n\\r\\nThe meeting location will be provided upon booking confirmation.\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":120,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Londoners Who Changed the World\",\"instanceDates\":\"19 July-19 July\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"517201ABJCHBRQVTBLJQDJGGLBCJDNHQQ\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-07-19T14:00:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-07-19T13:00:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-07-19T14:00:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-07-19T13:00:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Walks\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Walking Tours\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"Boaz Tal\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false},{\"description\":\"Walking tour, 2-4pm, £20 // Step into the footsteps of brilliant minds who shaped the modern world. This fascinating walking tour along the scenic Regent’s Canal unveils the stories of visionary scientists, engineers, and innovators whose groundbreaking work transformed transportation, medicine, electronics, and AI. \\r\\n\\r\\nAs you stroll through this historic area—often compared to Amsterdam’s charming canal life—you’ll uncover the hidden history behind world-changing discoveries and inventions. Led by expert guide Boaz Tal, this tour offers a unique blend of history, science, and culture, bringing the past to life in the very place where innovation thrived. \\r\\n\\r\\nThe meeting location will be provided upon booking confirmation. \",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":120,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Londoners Who Changed the World\",\"instanceDates\":\"22 November-22 November\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"636201ANPQRQBKMPBLSGBHKBGLVRDQPKB\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-11-22T14:00:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-11-22T14:00:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-11-22T14:00:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-11-22T14:00:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false,\"attribute_Genre\":\"Walks\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Walking Tours\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"Boaz Tal\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"3pm-5pm, £20, Sunday 17 May 2026 // London's Jewish History over the Centuries\\r\\n\\r\\nJoin us for an enlightening walking tour to explore 1000 years of Jewish history. This experience is for everyone interested in London’s extraordinary culture and heritage!\\r\\n\\r\\nStarting in Aldgate and crossing the historic City of London, you will discover the fascinating story of London’s Jewish population from medieval times to the present day. Learn about the Jews brought to England by William the Conqueror after 1066, the expulsion under Edward I in 1290, the resettlement under Cromwell in 1656, and subsequent Jewish immigration up to the present day.\\r\\n\\r\\nDuring our walk, you will see many of the most important sites in the City – including those connected to London’s rich and complex Jewish history. Hear about various London Jewish personalities over the years, and about Jewish life in Britain and beyond. Don’t miss this opportunity to delve into centuries of Jewish and general history in London.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nLocation: Starting point will be provided upon booking.\\r\\nPlease wear comfortable shoes and dress for the weather!\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":120,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"London's Jewish History over the Centuries\",\"instanceDates\":\"8 November-8 November\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"455401AMHJVTKCLNLVQKLVCSSGSMMTQQV\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-11-08T14:00:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-11-08T14:00:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-11-08T14:00:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-11-08T14:00:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Walks\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Walking Tours\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"Marc Gardiner\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false},{\"description\":\"7.30-8.45pm, £20, building // Meet Max and Eliana: an uncircumcised liberal Jewish comedian and the modern Orthodox woman he's fallen for. After making an instant 3am connection in a bar in Edinburgh, Max discovers a devastating truth: that despite his upbringing, he's not quite the \\\"right\\\" kind of Jewish. And if he wants to marry the love of his life, he's in for a rollercoaster of a journey. \\r\\nFor everything you ever wanted to know about Orthodox conversion, from rabbis to relationships and even that infamous date with a scalpel... join this hilarious and determined couple for a talk at JW3, following the publication of Max Olesker's memoir Making the Cut.\\r\\n\\r\\nBooks will be available to buy and be signed on the night\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":75,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Making the Cut\",\"instanceDates\":\"20 October-20 October\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"639401AQJJDSDHCCVDKLLLVCPPRMSTQGG\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-10-20T19:30:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-10-20T18:30:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-10-20T19:30:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-10-20T18:30:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false,\"attribute_Genre\":\"Talks & Discussions\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Adult Education\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"Max Olesker\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"7pm - 8.15pm, £12, in building // Maksim Herkin was taken hostage by Hamas terrorists on October 7, 2023, during the attack on the Nova Festival. For 738 days, he was held in Gaza, cut off from his family and the outside world. Born in the Donbas region of Ukraine, he was 35-year-old father to a 3-year-old daughter when he was kidnapped, and was the primary provider for his mother and 11-year-old brother. \\r\\n\\r\\nIn this intimate and powerful conversation, Maksim will share his personal story. From the final messages he sent to his family that morning, to the choices he made in captivity to protect his identity, and the resilience that sustained him through nearly two years of uncertainty. \\r\\n\\r\\nNow free, Maksim will also reflect on what he has carried with him since his return. What it means to rebuild, what has stayed with him, and what he wants this community to hear and understand. \\r\\n\\r\\nIn conversation with Danyelle Neuman, Chief Development Officer at The Jewish Agency for Israel, this will be a deeply moving evening and a rare opportunity to hear directly from someone who lived through these events. There will be an opportunity to ask questions and join the conversation. \",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":75,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Maksim Herkin: A Personal Story of Survival and Strength\",\"instanceDates\":\"22 June-22 June\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"622801AGQGPDJTKMHBPQGTGTHLGPCDQKR\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-06-22T19:00:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-06-22T18:00:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-06-22T19:00:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-06-22T18:00:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Talks & Discussions\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false},{\"description\":\"2-3.30pm, hybrid, £20 // Margaret Lockwood was one of Britain’s biggest female stars from the late 1930’s to the 50’s in such films as The Lady Vanishes, The Man in Grey , Love Story and the Wicked Lady. George will trace her life and career.   \\r\\n\\r\\n \\r\\n\\r\\nGeorge McGhee has over 35 years of experience, latterly at the BBC, where he oversaw all feature films and international TV series acquisitions. \",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":90,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Margaret Lockwood: Not a Wicked Lady\",\"instanceDates\":\"12 October-12 October\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"637001AHVJHKMRKHHJBVLLTPGNQCCQCMQ\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-10-12T14:00:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-10-12T13:00:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-10-12T14:00:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-10-12T13:00:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false,\"attribute_Genre\":\"Talks & Discussions\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Adult Education\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"George McGhee\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"7.30pm, approx 2hr duration including a 15-min interval, £33 adult £16.50 student, in-building //Whether playing concerti, chamber music or unaccompanied violin, or directing orchestras such as Chamber  Orchestra of Europe or the Royal Northern Sinfonia, Polish-born Maria Włoszczowska captivates her audiences with her liveliness, charm, and finesse and her palpable love of music and of the violin. Alasdair Beatson’s charisma and expressiveness is already well known to JW3 audiences. // The programme includes two unsurpassable major masterpieces from the piano trio repertoire by Schumann and Brahms.  The two middle movements of the Schumann trio are amongst the most overwhelmingly moving in the trio literature. The concert opens with Mendelssohn’s marvellous F major violin and piano sonata. \",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":129,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Maria Włoszczowska, David Waterman, and Alasdair Beatson\",\"instanceDates\":\"12 February-12 February\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"493801AJMGJBVQDLNMHLKCTRKMNMRVPTL\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-02-12T19:30:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-02-12T19:30:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-02-12T19:30:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-02-12T19:30:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Arts & Culture\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Classical Music Series\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false},{\"description\":\"In 1950s New York, Marty Mauser, a young man with a dream no one respects, goes to hell and back in pursuit of greatness. | Duration: 2h 30m, Rating: 15 | Films may be preceded by up to 20 minutes of advertisements and trailers. Specific timings will vary with each screening. We always recommend arriving on time.\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":150,\"imageUrl\":\"https://system.spektrix.com/jw3/files/062f7571-7e3f-45d7-aaa2-224e4404a633.jpg\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Marty Supreme\",\"instanceDates\":\"18 January-5 March\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"https://system.spektrix.com/jw3/files/062f7571-7e3f-45d7-aaa2-224e4404a633-thumbnail.jpg\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"581401AMRQQCRMCRCTVDDNRBSRNGCDHDM\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-01-18T19:15:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-01-18T19:15:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-03-05T11:00:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-03-05T11:00:00Z\",\"altText\":\"Marty Supreme\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Cinema\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false},{\"description\":\"3pm-5pm, £20, off site // Walk with us through Mayfair, one of London's most prestigious and affluent neighbourhoods, known for its magnificent Georgian houses and squares, royal parks, and grand avenues. \\r\\n\\r\\nDiscover the area’s fascinating history, from its origins as a swampy field used for the annual May Fair celebrations in the 17th century, to its more recent status as the most expensive property on the London Monopoly board! Also, learn about Mayfair’s long association with the United States - including its connections with four different American presidents.\\r\\n\\r\\nMayfair also has its own Jewish history, with former residents including prominent Victorian Anglo-Jewish figures such as Benjamin Disraeli, Sir Moses Montefiore and Alfred de Rothschild, and later some famous 20th century musicians, movie stars – and hairdressers! Hear their stories and many others which form part of 1,000 years of Jewish history in Britain. \\r\\n\\r\\nJoin us as we explore magnificent Mayfair, enjoying its geography and learning about its history - both general and Jewish. This tour is for everybody!\\r\\n\\r\\nThis tour will not depart from JW3; the meeting location will be provided upon booking.\\r\\n\\r\\nPlease wear comfortable shoes and dress for the weather! \",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":120,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Mayfair Walk - with a Jewish Twist\",\"instanceDates\":\"1 March-1 March\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"554202AQVDJKKSCNLMGNJBQLTSDVDDMCN\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-03-01T15:00:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-03-01T15:00:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-03-01T15:00:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-03-01T15:00:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Walks\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Walking Tours\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false},{\"description\":\"Walking tour, 3-5pm, £20 // Walk with us through Mayfair, one of London's most prestigious and affluent neighbourhoods, known for its magnificent Georgian houses and squares, royal parks, and grand avenues.   \\r\\n\\r\\nDiscover the area’s fascinating history, from its origins as a swampy field used for the annual May Fair celebrations in the 17th century, to its more recent status as the most expensive property on the London Monopoly board! Learn about Mayfair’s long association with the United States, including its connections with four different American presidents.  \\r\\n\\r\\n  \\r\\n\\r\\nMayfair also has its own Jewish history, with former residents including prominent Victorian Anglo-Jewish figures such as Benjamin Disraeli, Sir Moses Montefiore and Alfred de Rothschild, and later some famous 20th century musicians, movie stars – and hairdressers! Hear their stories and many others which form part of 1,000 years of Jewish history in Britain.   \\r\\n\\r\\nJoin us as we explore magnificent Mayfair, enjoying its geography and learning about its history - both general and Jewish. This tour is for everybody! \",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":120,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Mayfair Walk – with a Jewish Twist!\",\"instanceDates\":\"11 October-11 October\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"635601AMGBLTSQHLVKHMDGKSTMLPRSCGH\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-10-11T15:00:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-10-11T14:00:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-10-11T15:00:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-10-11T14:00:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false,\"attribute_Genre\":\"Walks\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Walking Tours\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"Marc Gardiner\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"Founded in 1930, Troisgros has held three Michelin stars for 55 years. The children of the fourth generation, Marie-Pierre and Michel’s sons are continuing the family business: César runs the Michelin-starred restaurant, Le Bois sans feuilles (The Leafless Wood), and Léo is in charge of one of the other two Troisgros restaurants, La Colline du colombier (The Dovecote Hill). From the daily market to the cheese maturing cellars, via the vineyard, the cattle farm and the vegetable garden adjacent to the restaurant, Menus-Plaisirs is an intimate, sensory journey through the kitchens of one of the world’s most prestigious restaurants. | Duration: 4h, Rating: PG \",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":240,\"imageUrl\":\"https://system.spektrix.com/jw3/files/26dc83cd-18b9-4ab0-bdc8-82c600dbfd35.jpg\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Menus-Plaisirs – Les Troisgros\",\"instanceDates\":\"13 January-14 January\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"https://system.spektrix.com/jw3/files/26dc83cd-18b9-4ab0-bdc8-82c600dbfd35-thumbnail.jpg\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"581201ATQCRHDHNVVTQNMBJTLTVTSJSHV\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-01-13T14:00:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-01-13T14:00:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-01-14T12:10:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-01-14T12:10:00Z\",\"altText\":\"Menus-Plaisirs – Les Troisgros\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Cinema\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false},{\"description\":\"Spanning three decades, Merrily We Roll Along charts the turbulent relationship between composer Franklin Shepard and his two lifelong friends: writer Mary and lyricist and playwright Charley. Originally produced on Broadway in 1981, then becoming an inventive cult classic ahead of its time, the musical features some of Stephen Sondheim's most celebrated and personal songs. The 2023-2024 Broadway production, directed by Maria Friedman, redefined the show for a new era, bringing Stephen Sondheim's intricate score and George Furth's book to vivid life with extraordinary depth and clarity. Merrily We Roll Along garnered the most five-star reviews in West-End history. | Duration: 2h 25m, Rating: 15 \",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":145,\"imageUrl\":\"https://system.spektrix.com/jw3/files/3f244ace-63a2-40a9-bb1a-0f04d57f0cc8.jpg\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Merrily We Roll Along\",\"instanceDates\":\"2 January-4 January\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"https://system.spektrix.com/jw3/files/3f244ace-63a2-40a9-bb1a-0f04d57f0cc8-thumbnail.jpg\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"579601ANLTGKKVMDBVRDRRTNKRHQPCCRD\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-01-02T11:00:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-01-02T11:00:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-01-04T14:45:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-01-04T14:45:00Z\",\"altText\":\"Merrily We Roll Along\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Cinema\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false},{\"description\":\"2-3pm, hybrid, £20 // Join Middle East analyst Jonathan Paris for a thought-provoking exploration of the region's ever-more complex geopolitical landscape. This talk will unpack the global consequences of recent conflicts, shed light on the evolving roles of international actors in the region and investigate the potential political shifts which could shape the future of the Middle East.\\r\\n\\r\\nJonathan Paris is a London-based Middle East analyst and former fellow at the Council on Foreign Relations in New York. He is currently Senior Fellow at the Center for Advanced Studies on Terrorism (CAST) and Senior Advisor Emeritus at the Chertoff Group. He appears regularly on Sky News and Al Arabiya and has been quoted in the New York Times and other publications.\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":60,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Middle East 2026\",\"instanceDates\":\"21 January-21 January\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"557401AVBNVGMTCDLPDGRCKNLJNKQGDDH\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-01-21T14:00:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-01-21T14:00:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-01-21T14:00:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-01-21T14:00:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Talks & Discussions\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Adult Education\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"Jonathan Paris\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false},{\"description\":\"7.30pm-8.30pm, £20, hybrid, Tuesday 23 June 2026 // Hear from Middle East analyst Jonathan Paris about the politics, current affairs and geopolitical issues which shape the Middle East today. \\r\\n\\r\\nJonathan will explore these key questions: \\r\\n\\r\\nWill Iran's Islamic regime survive the year? \\r\\n\\r\\nWill Israel and Syria overcome their disagreements and make peace?\\r\\n\\r\\nWill Hamas and Hezbollah disarm? \\r\\n\\r\\nWill Trump continue to show robust support for Israel against their adversaries?\\r\\n\\r\\nJonathan Paris is a London-based Middle East analyst and former fellow at the Council on Foreign Relations in New York. He is currently Senior Fellow at the Center for Advanced Studies on Terrorism (CAST) and Senior Advisor Emeritus at the Chertoff Group. He appears regularly on Sky News and Al Arabiya and has been quoted in the New York Times and other publications.\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":60,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Middle East Update\",\"instanceDates\":\"23 June-23 June\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"593801ACVSJTPNCBCGHQBSCCTGRBVTQPC\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-06-23T19:30:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-06-23T18:30:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-06-23T19:30:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-06-23T18:30:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Talks & Discussions\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Adult Education\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"Jonathan Paris\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false},{\"description\":\"A stirring meditation on faith, commitment, and the enduring power of love, as a longtime couple takes a life-changing trip to Amsterdam. | Duration: 2h 12m, Rating: 12 Credits\\r\\nRating: 12A\\r\\nGenre: Drama\\r\\nDirector: Polly Findlay\\r\\nStars: Lesley Manville, Ciarán Hinds https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=CbyNeGn3ZCE&pp=ygUabWlkd2ludGVyIGJyZWFrIFVLIHRyYWlsZXI%3D\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":90,\"imageUrl\":\"https://system.spektrix.com/jw3/files/8cdda19e-d396-4c21-a928-7a502de39c4a.jpg\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Midwinter Break\",\"instanceDates\":\"19 April-23 April\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"https://system.spektrix.com/jw3/files/8cdda19e-d396-4c21-a928-7a502de39c4a-thumbnail.jpg\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"616201ARKLJLVCBDMPLBBSPNHPDRNKNDL\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-04-19T10:30:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-04-19T09:30:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-04-23T16:45:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-04-23T15:45:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Cinema\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false},{\"description\":\"Join artist and author Miriam Ellia ahead of her talk, Moses and the 613 Health and Safety Commandments, for an informal drinks reception and book signing.\\r\\nCome along from 6pm to meet Miriam, enjoy a complimentary glass of wine, and purchase a signed copy of her latest book before the evening talk begins.\\r\\nThis free event offers a chance to chat, browse the book, and settle in before the main event at 7pm.\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":60,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Miriam Ellia Book Signing & Drinks Reception\",\"instanceDates\":\"24 May-24 May\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"626201AMGQNVQJLPPSTCRMSHCQJNKRSBN\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-05-24T18:00:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-05-24T17:00:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-05-24T18:00:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-05-24T17:00:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Talks & Discussions\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Adult Education\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false},{\"description\":\"1pm-4pm, £10 per person, Partnering with Pier Point, following the successful Chanukah Funukah event, an escape room for families (9+ ideal age) - The Premise: It is exactly 60 minutes before the B’mitzvah begins. The venue is set, the guests are arriving, but disaster has struck! The guest of honor’s prepared speech and the ceremonial Torah pointer (Yad) have been locked inside a \\\"security vault\\\" by a confused relative, and the code has been forgotten.\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":180,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Mitzvah Mission: Impossible!\",\"instanceDates\":\"31 May-31 May\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"602401AVVTRGTHJHVCHNGQPSBBBMLMMBH\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-05-31T13:00:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-05-31T12:00:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-05-31T13:00:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-05-31T12:00:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Families & Youth\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Families\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false},{\"description\":\"11:00 // 15 Nov 2026 // £35 // To launch our new Young JW3 Modern Ashkenazi Cooking series, join us for a hands-on Chanukah cooking workshop. Learn to make latkes, sweet fritters and schmears with a twist, before enjoying lunch, a Q&A and book signing with the chef afterwards.\\r\\n\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":180,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Modern Ashkenazi Cooking: A Taste Of Chanukah\",\"instanceDates\":\"15 November-15 November\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"633002ARCPGSHKBBNTPMHVVVTBCMCSVSJ\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-11-15T11:00:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-11-15T11:00:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-11-15T11:00:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-11-15T11:00:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false,\"attribute_Genre\":\"Young Professionals\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"Alissa Timoshkina\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"Thursdays, 10.30am-12.30pm, £180 for the 10-week course // Join us as we celebrate the work of Tom Stoppard with a selection of texts exploring the writer’s life, art and world. We will launch the term by considering the impact of Stoppard’s Jewish identity on his plays and will conclude by drawing comparisons with his contemporary, Harold Pinter. Along the way, we will look at the prose of Simon Mawer and Helen Epstein whose writing informs and enriches our understanding of the great playwright’s concerns.  \\r\\n\\r\\n \\r\\n\\r\\nWhat You’ll Learn: \\r\\n\\r\\nDiscover the bold, witty and engaging voices who define modern Jewish Literature.  \\r\\n\\r\\nUnderstand & discuss themes of Jewish identity, alienation and community.  \\r\\n\\r\\nGain insight into the workings of language, form and structure. \\r\\n\\r\\nExplore a range of writing styles and literary genres.  \\r\\n\\r\\n \\r\\n\\r\\nWho It’s For: \\r\\n\\r\\nJW3's Modern Jewish Literature course is designed for curious readers who want to dive into the writers, stories and ideas which have shaped our understanding of Jewish life, culture & society.   \\r\\n\\r\\nIt’s perfect for those who enjoy discovering new voices, understanding different perspectives and discussing thought-provoking and relevant writing. If you are excited to deepen your understanding of Jewish Literature in a welcoming & inspiring way, this course is for you.  \",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":120,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Modern Jewish Literature [In Building]\",\"instanceDates\":\"8 October-8 October\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"645001AKKKSRRDJGSHRHVCBBRPTHVBRRS\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-10-08T10:30:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-10-08T09:30:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-10-08T10:30:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-10-08T09:30:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false,\"attribute_Genre\":\"Classes & Courses\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"True\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"Naomi Grant and Aviva Dautch\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"Thursdays, 10.30am-12.30pm, £180 for the 10-week course // Join us as we celebrate the work of Tom Stoppard with a selection of texts exploring the writer’s life, art and world. We will launch the term by considering the impact of Stoppard’s Jewish identity on his plays and will conclude by drawing comparisons with his contemporary, Harold Pinter. Along the way, we will look at the prose of Simon Mawer and Helen Epstein whose writing informs and enriches our understanding of the great playwright’s concerns. What You’ll Learn: Discover the bold, witty and engaging voices who define modern Jewish Literature. Understand & discuss themes of Jewish identity, alienation and community. Gain insight into the workings of language, form and structure. Explore a range of writing styles and literary genres. Who It’s For: JW3's Modern Jewish Literature course is designed for curious readers who want to dive into the writers, stories and ideas which have shaped our understanding of Jewish life, culture & society. It’s perfect for those who enjoy discovering new voices, understanding different perspectives and discussing thought-provoking and relevant writing. If you are excited to deepen your understanding of Jewish Literature in a welcoming & inspiring way, this course is for you.\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":120,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Modern Jewish Literature [Online]\",\"instanceDates\":\"8 October-8 October\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"645201AHSNPLGLDDKPTNQQJQBDGTVJKTL\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-10-08T10:30:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-10-08T09:30:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-10-08T10:30:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-10-08T09:30:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false,\"attribute_Genre\":\"Classes & Courses\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"True\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"Naomi Grant and Aviva Dautch\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"10.30am-12.30pm, Thursdays, hybrid // £20 per session, £162 for the course // Join us for as this season we explore the writing of the Jewish East End through the plays of Arnold Wesker and the poetry and prose of Emanuel Litvinoff. In the second half of term, we will consider the impact of short stories, including Isaac Babel & Grace Paley’s work, before concluding with a celebration of Dorothy Parker. We will also be joined by Aviva Dautch on the 4th June who will be looking at the winner of the 2026 Wingate Prize. \\r\\n\\r\\n \\r\\n\\r\\nWhat You’ll Learn: \\r\\n\\r\\nDiscover the bold, witty and engaging voices who define modern Jewish Literature.  \\r\\n\\r\\nUnderstand & discuss themes of Jewish identity, alienation and community.  \\r\\n\\r\\nGain insight into the workings of language, form and structure. \\r\\n\\r\\nExplore a range of writing styles and literary genres.  \\r\\n\\r\\n \\r\\n\\r\\nWho It’s For: \\r\\n\\r\\nJW3's Modern Jewish Literature course is designed for curious readers who want to dive into the writers, stories and ideas which have shaped our understanding of Jewish life, culture & society.   \\r\\n\\r\\nIt’s perfect for those who enjoy discovering new voices, understanding different perspectives and discussing thought-provoking and relevant writing. If you are excited to deepen your understanding of Jewish Literature in a welcoming & inspiring way, this course is for you.  \\r\\n\\r\\n \\r\\n\\r\\nWho Delivers It?  \\r\\n\\r\\nNaomi Grant is an artist and teacher living and working in London. She graduated from the University of Cambridge with a first class degree in English before joining the Masterclass Programme at the Jerusalem Studio School in Israel. Following this, she completed the Postgraduate Programme at the Royal Drawing School in London. She is a regular contributor to the London Review of Books. \\r\\n\\r\\n \\r\\n\\r\\nCourse Outline: \\r\\n\\r\\n30th April: The plays of Arnold Wesker (Part1) \\r\\n\\r\\n7th May: The plays of Arnold Wesker (Part 2) \\r\\n\\r\\n14th May: The poetry and prose of Emanuel Litvinoff  \\r\\n\\r\\n21st May: The short stories of Isaac Babel \\r\\n\\r\\n28th May (Half term) \\r\\n\\r\\n4th June: Wingate Prize 2026 (with Aviva Dautch) \\r\\n\\r\\n11th June: The short stories of Grace Paley (Part1) \\r\\n\\r\\n18th June: The short stories of Grace Paley (Part 2) \\r\\n25th June: The Collected Dorothy Parker (Part1) \\r\\n2nd July:  The Collected Dorothy Parker (Part 2) \\r\\n \",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":120,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Modern Jewish Literature Spring 2026 [In Building]\",\"instanceDates\":\"30 April-2 July\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"601001ASLLPMMTQTLQVJCDGMBSBSLBRQV\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-04-30T10:30:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-04-30T09:30:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-07-02T10:30:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-07-02T09:30:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false,\"attribute_Genre\":\"Classes & Courses\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"True\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Creative Courses\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"Naomi Grant\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"10.30am-12.30pm, Thursdays, hybrid // £20 per session, £162 for the course // Join us for as this season we explore the writing of the Jewish East End through the plays of Arnold Wesker and the poetry and prose of Emanuel Litvinoff. In the second half of term, we will consider the impact of short stories, including Isaac Babel & Grace Paley’s work, before concluding with a celebration of Dorothy Parker. We will also be joined by Aviva Dautch on the 4th June who will be looking at the winner of the 2026 Wingate Prize. What You’ll Learn: Discover the bold, witty and engaging voices who define modern Jewish Literature. Understand & discuss themes of Jewish identity, alienation and community. Gain insight into the workings of language, form and structure. Explore a range of writing styles and literary genres. Who It’s For: JW3's Modern Jewish Literature course is designed for curious readers who want to dive into the writers, stories and ideas which have shaped our understanding of Jewish life, culture & society. It’s perfect for those who enjoy discovering new voices, understanding different perspectives and discussing thought-provoking and relevant writing. If you are excited to deepen your understanding of Jewish Literature in a welcoming & inspiring way, this course is for you. Who Delivers It? Naomi Grant is an artist and teacher living and working in London. She graduated from the University of Cambridge with a first class degree in English before joining the Masterclass Programme at the Jerusalem Studio School in Israel. Following this, she completed the Postgraduate Programme at the Royal Drawing School in London. She is a regular contributor to the London Review of Books. Course Outline: 30th April: The plays of Arnold Wesker (Part1) 7th May: The plays of Arnold Wesker (Part 2) 14th May: The poetry and prose of Emanuel Litvinoff 21st May: The short stories of Isaac Babel 28th May (Half term) 4th June: Wingate Prize 2026 (with Aviva Dautch) 11th June: The short stories of Grace Paley (Part1) 18th June: The short stories of Grace Paley (Part 2) 25th June: The Collected Dorothy Parker (Part1) 2nd July: The Collected Dorothy Parker (Part 2)\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":120,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Modern Jewish Literature Spring 2026 [Online]\",\"instanceDates\":\"30 April-2 July\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"598802ABVLGRKMTPPNTLNSSCJGJTTTBBS\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-04-30T10:30:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-04-30T09:30:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-07-02T10:30:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-07-02T09:30:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false,\"attribute_Genre\":\"Classes & Courses\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"True\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Creative Courses\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"Naomi Grant\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"Thursdays, 10:30am-12:30pm, hybrid, £20 per session or £180 for the 10 week course // Join Naomi as she explores the richness of modern Jewish culture through reading Israeli, European and American literature.\\r\\n\\r\\nTo celebrate JW3’s Bar Mitzvah year, this course will explore the coming-of-age novels of Howard Jacobson, the short stories of Melissa Bank, and the autobiographical essays of Adrienne Rich and Muriel Spark. We will also mark Holocaust Remembrance Week by considering the poetry of Geoffrey Hill and Sylvia Plath.\\r\\n\\r\\nThe second half of the term will be devoted to scenes from the tragedies of Arthur Miller, culminating in our final session led by Aviva Dautch who will teach on the poetry of Adrienne Rich. \\r\\n\\r\\n5 January: The Mighty Walzer, Howard Jacobson\\r\\n22 January: Kalooki Nights, Howard Jacobson\\r\\n29 January: The Poetry of Geoffrey Hill and Sylvia Plath\\r\\n5 February: The Girls’ Guide to Hunting and Fishing, Melissa Bank (Part 1)\\r\\n12 February:The Girls’ Guide to Hunting and Fishing, Melissa Bank (Part 2)\\r\\n19 February: Half Term\\r\\n26 February: Scenes from Arthur Miller (Part 1)\\r\\n5 March: Scenes from Arthur Miller (Part 2)\\r\\n12 March: Scenes from Arthur Miller (Part 3)\\r\\n19 March: Split at the Root, Adrienne Rich & The Gentile Jewesses, Muriel Spark\\r\\n26 March: The Poetry of Adrienne Rich\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":120,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Modern Jewish Literature Winter 2026 [In-Building]\",\"instanceDates\":\"15 January-26 March\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"562801AHHTKCRSVMSGJNPCDMSHTDVCCHG\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-01-15T10:30:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-01-15T10:30:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-03-26T10:30:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-03-26T10:30:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Classes & Courses\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"True\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Creative Courses\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"Naomi Grant\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false},{\"description\":\"Thursdays, 10:30am-12:30pm, hybrid, £20 per session or £180 for the 10 week course // Join Naomi as she explores the richness of modern Jewish culture through reading Israeli, European and American literature.\\r\\n\\r\\nTo celebrate JW3’s Bar Mitzvah year, this course will explore the coming-of-age novels of Howard Jacobson, the short stories of Melissa Bank, and the autobiographical essays of Adrienne Rich and Muriel Spark. We will also mark Holocaust Remembrance Week by considering the poetry of Geoffrey Hill and Sylvia Plath.\\r\\n\\r\\nThe second half of the term will be devoted to scenes from the tragedies of Arthur Miller, culminating in our final session led by Aviva Dautch who will teach on the poetry of Adrienne Rich. \\r\\n\\r\\n5 January: The Mighty Walzer, Howard Jacobson\\r\\n22 January: Kalooki Nights, Howard Jacobson\\r\\n29 January: The Poetry of Geoffrey Hill and Sylvia Plath\\r\\n5 February: The Girls’ Guide to Hunting and Fishing, Melissa Bank (Part 1)\\r\\n12 February:The Girls’ Guide to Hunting and Fishing, Melissa Bank (Part 2)\\r\\n19 February: Half Term\\r\\n26 February: Scenes from Arthur Miller (Part 1)\\r\\n5 March: Scenes from Arthur Miller (Part 2)\\r\\n12 March: Scenes from Arthur Miller (Part 3)\\r\\n19 March: Split at the Root, Adrienne Rich & The Gentile Jewesses, Muriel Spark\\r\\n26 March: The Poetry of Adrienne Rich\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":120,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Modern Jewish Literature Winter 2026 [Online]\",\"instanceDates\":\"15 January-26 March\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"562401ALRJQQMDCNSQHMVQBQGKQKVBJCM\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-01-15T10:30:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-01-15T10:30:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-03-26T10:30:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-03-26T10:30:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Classes & Courses\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"True\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Creative Courses\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"Naomi Grant\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false},{\"description\":\"Tuesdays, 10am-11am, £12 per session, £48 for 4 weeks // Led by Rotem Barak, join our Morning Yoga Class designed for to be adaptable to Older Adults and all abilities. Move, stretch, and breathe at your own pace in a friendly & supportive environment. No experience needed - just bring yourself and an open mind. \\r\\n\\r\\nIn this class, you will: \\r\\n\\r\\nStretch and strengthen your body. \\r\\n\\r\\nImprove balance and flexibility, helping you feel more agile and confident. \\r\\n\\r\\nLearn mindful breathing and relaxation techniques to reduce stress and boost focus. \\r\\n\\r\\nPractice at your own pace in a supportive & judgment-free environment. \\r\\n\\r\\nRotem Barak is a yoga and movement teacher passionate about making movement accessible to everyone. \",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":60,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Morning Yoga\",\"instanceDates\":\"22 September-13 October\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"643403ABQCQJHLSRBSNBJJQHGLVQPRPPM\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-09-22T10:00:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-09-22T09:00:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-10-13T10:00:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-10-13T09:00:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false,\"attribute_Genre\":\"Classes & Courses\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"Rotem Barak\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"7pm-9.30pm, building only, £15 // Join us as artist Miriam Elia is joined by Jewish Culture Month director Liat Rosenthal to discuss the launch of her new book and exhibition commissioned by JW3 for the first Jewish Culture Month. Moses and the 613 Health and Safety Commandments is the latest satirical book by the brilliant artist-author of We Go the Gallery, Piggy Goes to University, and The Diary of Edward the Hamster. Miriam was selected by Marina Abramovic as one of her favourite artists and a whole room in Marina's recent Royal Academy show was dedicated to Miriam's work. A unique limited edition of the book will be available for purchase, signed by the author.\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":150,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Moses and the Health and Safety Commandments (Artist Talk)\",\"instanceDates\":\"24 May-24 May\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"595601AHPDKCNDNPBRDJGCHQDDQHBKMSV\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-05-24T19:00:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-05-24T18:00:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-05-24T19:00:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-05-24T18:00:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Talks & Discussions\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Adult Education\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false},{\"description\":\"14 May - 30 June, free // Celebrate Shavuot with Miriam Elia’s satirical exhibition, Moses and the 613 Health and Safety Commandments. This original JW3 commission offers an affectionate, hilarious look at Jewish law through the lens of modern safety culture.\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":720,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":false,\"name\":\"Moses and the Health and Safety Commandments (Exhibition)\",\"instanceDates\":\"14 May-30 June\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"604401ANSHDRRQHKRGLMVGNHDGLDQLBLQ\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-05-14T10:00:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-05-14T09:00:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-06-30T20:00:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-06-30T19:00:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Special Events\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false},{\"description\":\"At 28, Kate Moss is already the greatest fashion icon of our time.  \\r\\n\\r\\nEndlessly watchable, never predictable, always natural and utterly unpretentious. Kate shaped a generation. Yet she still yearns to be seen, truly seen. In a bold move, Kate enters Lucian Freud's studio. Two British cultural titans converge, and Kate bares herself. Freud's genius explores Kate's hidden depths. Her complexity unfolds. A mesmerizing rapport develops. The wild party scene fades whilst self-discovery takes centre stage. Tension mounts. Truths emerge. Kate finds her voice, her strength, her true self. Kate blossoms from supermodel to eternal muse. This is a journey into the heart of an icon. Vulnerable. Defiant. Reborn.  //\\r\\n\\r\\nDuration: 100 minutes \\r\\nRating: 15 \\r\\nDirector: James Lucas \\r\\nCast: Jasmine Blackborow, Derek Jacobi, Ellie Bamber \\r\\nYear: 2025 \\r\\nLanguage: English \",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":100,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Moss & Freud\",\"instanceDates\":\"1 June-9 June\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"628001AJGRNDVJCSBKDTKTJTHDHCGRCLS\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-06-01T17:15:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-06-01T16:15:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-06-09T11:00:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-06-09T10:00:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Cinema\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false},{\"description\":\"From the team behind 'Finding Your Feet' and 'Fisherman's Friends' comes Mother's Pride, a story about the Harley family who after losing their matriarch, must come together to save their pub and village through the art of beer-brewing. | Duration: 1h 30m, Rating: 12A \",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":90,\"imageUrl\":\"https://system.spektrix.com/jw3/files/47412f68-dfbd-4d8c-a902-91bed2fcf641.jpg\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Mother's Pride\",\"instanceDates\":\"22 March-26 March\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"https://system.spektrix.com/jw3/files/47412f68-dfbd-4d8c-a902-91bed2fcf641-thumbnail.jpg\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"605802AQSCCTTSSHTDMVJSRDPRSCRSVKJ\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-03-22T12:20:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-03-22T12:20:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-03-26T14:00:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-03-26T14:00:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Cinema\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false},{\"description\":\"12.30pm-1.30pm, £12 per session, £40 for the course, in building // Take a break in the middle of your day to refresh your body and reset your mind. This all-ages lunchtime movement class invites you to tune into your body, develop body awareness, and build confidence through playful improvisation, guided exercises and gentle movement exploration. \\r\\n\\r\\nAlongside developing technical and creative skills, these sessions offer a wonderful opportunity to connect socially, move with freedom and add a little joy to your day. \\r\\n\\r\\nClasses also provide exciting opportunities to perform, including a potential London performance in May 2026. More information can be found here:  \\r\\n\\r\\nhttps://www.flexerandsandiland.com/works/an-obscure-camera \\r\\n\\r\\nWho’s It For: \\r\\n\\r\\nLed by Yael Flexer, Artistic Director of Flexer & Sandiland, these movement classes are open to adults of all ages and abilities, whether you're new to movement or have previous dance experience. \\r\\n\\r\\nWho Delivers It:  \\r\\n\\r\\nYael Flexer is an award-winning choreographer, teacher and artistic director of Flexer & Sandiland, creating internationally touring dance and digital dance works. Yael is also senior lecturer and Reader in Dance at The University of Chichester, where she curates the 'What Dance Can Do' conference on intergenerational and 60+ dance.  \\r\\n\\r\\nflexerandsandiland.com  \",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":60,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Move & Reset\",\"instanceDates\":\"22 January-26 March\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"579001AKQPMGPQGPBHKBNJLVPVJPCBQHT\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-01-22T12:30:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-01-22T12:30:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-03-26T12:30:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-03-26T12:30:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Classes & Courses\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"True\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false},{\"description\":\"12.30pm-1.30pm, £12 per session, £60 for the course // Take a break in the middle of your day to refresh your body and reset your mind. This all-ages lunchtime movement class invites you to tune into your body, develop body awareness, and build confidence through playful improvisation, guided exercises and gentle movement exploration. \\r\\n\\r\\nAlongside developing technical and creative skills, these sessions offer a wonderful opportunity to connect socially, move with freedom and add a little joy to your day. \\r\\n\\r\\nClasses also provide exciting opportunities to perform, including a potential London performance in May 2026. More information can be found here:  \\r\\n\\r\\nhttps://www.flexerandsandiland.com/works/an-obscure-camera \\r\\n\\r\\nWho’s It For: \\r\\n\\r\\nLed by Yael Flexer, Artistic Director of Flexer & Sandiland, these movement classes are open to adults of all ages and abilities, whether you're new to movement or have previous dance experience. \\r\\n\\r\\nWho Delivers It:  \\r\\n\\r\\nYael Flexer is an award-winning choreographer, teacher and artistic director of Flexer & Sandiland, creating internationally touring dance and digital dance works. Yael is also senior lecturer and Reader in Dance at The University of Chichester, where she curates the 'What Dance Can Do' conference on intergenerational and 60+ dance.  \\r\\n\\r\\nflexerandsandiland.com \",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":60,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Move & Reset\",\"instanceDates\":\"7 May-21 May\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"604801ACBLGCBJRHGMLNPCNJVPPCPDHGM\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-05-07T12:30:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-05-07T11:30:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-05-21T12:30:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-05-21T11:30:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Classes & Courses\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"True\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Adult Education Classes & Courses\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"Yael Flexer\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false},{\"description\":\"\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":114,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"My Father's Island\",\"instanceDates\":\"31 July-31 July\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"642201ACPLLCHQDRJNRHQKNDGPSKHRDSJ\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-07-31T10:30:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-07-31T09:30:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-07-31T10:30:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-07-31T09:30:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false,\"attribute_Genre\":\"Cinema\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"A poetic, tender portrait of father-son bonds. Framed by the political landscape of 1993 Lagos, the film follows a father and his two young sons as they journey into and around the vibrantly rendered Nigerian metropolis, quietly reckoning with their relationship while navigating a city on the precipice of democratic crisis. Brothers and collaborators Akinola Davis Jr. and Wale Davies bring us a groundbreaking feature debut -- centering an award-winning performance by Sopé Dìrísù -- that reveals the profound depths of what families leave unspoken. | Duration: 1h 59m, Rating: 12A | Films may be preceded by up to 20 minutes of advertisements and trailers. Specific timings will vary with each screening. We always recommend arriving on time.\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":94,\"imageUrl\":\"https://system.spektrix.com/jw3/files/772faa23-0d34-47c1-9108-16a672973469.jpg\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"My Father's Shadow\",\"instanceDates\":\"22 February-26 February\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"https://system.spektrix.com/jw3/files/772faa23-0d34-47c1-9108-16a672973469-thumbnail.jpg\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"588001AKTBKHTVJVSKMSGPTSJVSPDBMQB\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-02-22T17:30:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-02-22T17:30:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-02-26T17:00:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-02-26T17:00:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Cinema\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false},{\"description\":\"Heartfelt and funny, the film follows three sisters who return to their childhood home for a momentous weekend: the third wedding of their twice-widowed mother, Diana Frost (Kristin Scott Thomas).  \\r\\n\\r\\n \\r\\n\\r\\nThe three daughters are from vastly different walks of life: Katherine (Scarlett Johansson) is a Captain in the Royal Navy; Victoria (Sienna Miller) is a Hollywood star; and Georgina (Emily Beecham) is a hospice nurse. Over the weekend, the family gathers to celebrate the new marriage, but mother and daughters alike are forced to revisit the past and confront the future, all with help from a colourful group of unexpected wedding guests. //\\r\\n\\r\\n \\r\\n\\r\\nDuration: 95 minutes \\r\\n\\r\\nRating: 15 \\r\\n\\r\\nDirector: Kristin Scott Thomas \\r\\n\\r\\nCast: Scarlett Johansson, Sienna Miller, Emily Beecham \\r\\n\\r\\nYear: 2025 \\r\\n\\r\\nLanguage: English \",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":95,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"My Mother's Wedding\",\"instanceDates\":\"24 June-30 June\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"628402APDMJGBQTJMCHCVCQTTPMJCDLBT\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-06-24T19:30:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-06-24T18:30:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-06-30T11:00:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-06-30T10:00:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Cinema\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false},{\"description\":\"7.30-9pm, building, £20 // Nadav Schneerson is a drummer, composer and producer based in London. An alumnus of the prestigious jazz programme Tomorrow’s Warriors, Nadav has come up alongside some of the finest jazz talent in London, whilst heavily influenced by previous generations of the program - Nadav individually blends contemporary jazz styles with various influences from around the Middle East. \\r\\n\\r\\n  \\r\\n\\r\\nAt just 25 years old, Nadav has already been making his mark on the London Jazz scene, having performed with the likes of Theon Cross (Sons of Kemet), Charlie Stacey (Yussef Dayes), Steam Down, Dargz, Finn Rees and beyond that, has been involved in projects working with artists such as Jon Batiste, Enny, Allysha Joy and Don Glori to name a few. Having already graced many local UK and international stages such as Montreal Jazz Festival, Montreux Jazz Festival, Jassmine Warsaw, Le Duc des Lombards, WOMAD Gran Canaria and in winter '24/25 spent six weeks playing a residency in China. \\r\\n\\r\\nSchneerson’s debut album, Sheva, features vocalist Afronaut Zu (Steam Down, Rudimental) on lead single ‘Juju Man’, Fellow Tomorrow Warrior’s alumnus Sultan Stevenson on piano and musicians from bands such as Ebi Soda, Levitation Orchestra and Hak Baker to name a few. \\r\\n\\r\\nNadav and his band will come for a single concert to JW3, performing compositions from his debut album, Sheva. \",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":90,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Nadav Schneerson: Sheva\",\"instanceDates\":\"26 March-26 March\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"565201ANBTKMQHJJTKRHBSTGMTCRDKHRT\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-03-26T19:30:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-03-26T19:30:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-03-26T19:30:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-03-26T19:30:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Music\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Arts & Culture\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false},{\"description\":\"7.30-8.45pm, hybrid, £20 // Join us for the Annual Denis Blair Memorial lecture where we will be joined by Natasha Hausdorff, a British barrister, international law specialist, and pro bono legal director of the advocacy group, UK Lawyers for Israel.\\r\\n\\r\\nDennis Blair was a much loved JW3 member and regular Adult Education student who is much missed by all. This annual lecture is sponsored by the Blair Family in memory of Dennis Blair z\\\"l.\\r\\n\\r\\nNicole Lampert is an award-winning British journalist and commentator. She writes extensively about antisemitism and Israel for national newspapers ranging from The Sun to The Telegraph, the New York Post to The Independent, and The Daily Mail to Unherd, commenting on television, publishing her own Substack (Diary From the Diaspora).  \\r\\n \\r\\nThe recent winner of the Pete Newbon Award for the person who has contributed most to the public understanding of antisemitism.\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":75,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Natasha Hausdorff in conversation with Nicole Lampert\",\"instanceDates\":\"24 March-24 March\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"561601AQGKPNPSJBNNBJSQKKNCQSNVSNB\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-03-24T19:30:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-03-24T19:30:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-03-24T19:30:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-03-24T19:30:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Talks & Discussions\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Adult Education\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false},{\"description\":\"Bryan Cranston (Breaking Bad) and Marianne Jean-Baptiste (Hard Truths) feature in this five-star, triumphantly acclaimed new production of Arthur Miller’s classic play, from visionary director Ivo Van Hove (A View from the Bridge).\\r\\nOne family, the heart of the American dream. When wartime delivers profits for Joe, it comes at a price when his partner is charged with criminal manufacturing deals, and his eldest son goes missing in action. Will peacetime bring peace of mind, or will he be confronted by the consequence of his actions?\\r\\nFilmed live from the West End, Paapa Essiedu (I May Destroy You), Tom Glynn-Carney (House of the Dragon), and Hayley Squires (I, Daniel Blake) also feature in this disturbingly prescient play. | This show contains strobe lighting, which may impact customers with photosensitive epilepsy. | Duration: 2h 15m, Rating: 12A\\r\\n\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":135,\"imageUrl\":\"https://system.spektrix.com/jw3/files/c725d41a-f258-4cad-9f94-5458fe892f04.jpg\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"National Theatre Live: All My Sons\",\"instanceDates\":\"16 April-5 July\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"https://system.spektrix.com/jw3/files/c725d41a-f258-4cad-9f94-5458fe892f04-thumbnail.jpg\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"617401ADGVSNMLRGNRVBKCMQJKVQVSPLT\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-04-16T19:15:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-04-16T18:15:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-07-05T17:15:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-07-05T16:15:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":true,\"attribute_Genre\":\"Cinema\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"Something is rotten in the state of Denmark. Are you watching closely?\\r\\n\\r\\nTrapped between duty and doubt, surrounded by power and privilege, young Prince Hamlet dares to ask the ultimate question – you know the one.\\r\\n\\r\\nOlivier Award-winner Hiran Abeysekera (The Father and the Assassin, Life of Pi) is Hamlet in this fearless, contemporary take on Shakespeare’s famous tragedy.\\r\\n\\r\\nNational Theatre Deputy Artistic Director, Robert Hastie (Standing at the Sky’s Edge, Operation Mincemeat) directs this sharp, stylish and darkly funny reimagining. | Duration: 3h including an interval, Rating: 12A\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":180,\"imageUrl\":\"https://system.spektrix.com/jw3/files/7bb6ae88-0178-46f1-b654-c07f1d2031ab.jpg\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"National Theatre Live: Hamlet\",\"instanceDates\":\"8 February-1 March\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"https://system.spektrix.com/jw3/files/7bb6ae88-0178-46f1-b654-c07f1d2031ab-thumbnail.jpg\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"589401ASRLLHTBHJRKVCKLTHBGDGGDNQK\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-02-08T19:00:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-02-08T19:00:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-03-01T12:45:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-03-01T12:45:00Z\",\"altText\":\"National Theatre Live: Hamlet\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Cinema\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false},{\"description\":\"Olivier and Tony Award winner Lesley Manville (Phantom Thread) joins Aidan Turner (Rivals) in a striking new staging of Christopher Hampton’s celebrated adaptation of the classic novel, where among the glittering salons of the super-rich, one misstep can mean ruin. Marquise de Merteuil is a master in the art of survival. Alongside the magnetic Vicomte de Valmont, they turn seduction into strategy and weaponise desire. But when their alliance collapses into rivalry, the battle between them threatens to destroy everyone in their path. Filmed live on stage at the National Theatre, Marianne Elliott (Angels in America) directs this thrilling game of love, lies, and social warfare. Duration: 180 minutes including a 15-minute interval Rating: 15 Director: Marianne Elliott Cast: Lesley Manville, Aidan Turner, Darragh Hand Year: 2026 https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=wq5l5VV51sU&pp=ygUgbGVzIGxpYWlzb25zIGRhbmdlcmV1c2VzIHRyYWlsZXLSBwkJPwsBhyohjO8%3D\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":180,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"National Theatre Live: Les Liaisons Dangereuses\",\"instanceDates\":\"12 July-23 July\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"642202AGRKNVBSLBQKNSRMJBBJVNNJSDV\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-07-12T15:00:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-07-12T14:00:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-07-23T18:30:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-07-23T17:30:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false,\"attribute_Genre\":\"Cinema\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"At the edge of the earth, you could be anyone. \\r\\nPegeen Flaherty’s life is turned upside down when, on a normal day, a young man walks into her pub claiming that he’s killed his father. \\r\\nInstead of being shunned, the killer Christy Mahon becomes a local hero. The welcome murderer wins hearts and races as he beds himself into village life. That is until a second man unexpectedly arrives on the scene…Caitríona McLaughlin directs Nicola Coughlan, Éanna Hardwicke and Siobhán McSweeney in John Millington Synge’s riveting story of youth and self-discovery. | Duration: 2h 30m, Rating: PG \",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":150,\"imageUrl\":\"https://system.spektrix.com/jw3/files/b03661cb-d3fb-4e3c-a13c-4f2d0405e472.jpg\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"National Theatre Live: Playboy of the Western World\",\"instanceDates\":\"28 May-31 May\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"https://system.spektrix.com/jw3/files/b03661cb-d3fb-4e3c-a13c-4f2d0405e472-thumbnail.jpg\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"625601ATVDCKLKDQVLSRHBLDNJJJBLDBV\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-05-28T15:00:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-05-28T14:00:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-05-31T15:00:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-05-31T14:00:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Cinema\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false},{\"description\":\"Returning to cinemas for the first time in over a decade, Helen Mirren plays Queen Elizabeth II in the Olivier and Tony Award-winning hit production. For 60 years, Queen Elizabeth II met with each of her 12 prime ministers in a private weekly meeting. This meeting is known as The Audience. From Winston Churchill to Margaret Thatcher and David Cameron, the Queen advised her prime ministers on matters both public and personal. Through these private audiences, we see glimpses of the woman behind the crown and witness the moments that shaped a monarch. Captured live from London’s West End in 2013. | Duration: 3h, Rating: 12A\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":180,\"imageUrl\":\"https://system.spektrix.com/jw3/files/f5d194ba-0bb8-45b8-9f63-26cfa8268059.jpg\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"National Theatre Live: The Audience\",\"instanceDates\":\"3 March-30 March\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"https://system.spektrix.com/jw3/files/f5d194ba-0bb8-45b8-9f63-26cfa8268059-thumbnail.jpg\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"607201ADNPVMJVHJCJDNNSGRCLJMNJQBK\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-03-03T19:30:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-03-03T19:30:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-03-30T10:30:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-03-30T09:30:00Z\",\"altText\":\"National Theatre Live: The Audience\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Cinema\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false},{\"description\":\"After years in the 12-step program of Alcoholics Anonymous, James becomes a sponsor to newcomer Luka. The pair bond over black coffee, trade stories and build a fragile friendship out of their shared experiences. But as Luka approaches step five -- the moment of confession -- dangerous truths emerge, threatening the trust on which both of their recoveries depend. | Duration: 1h 40m, Rating: 15 \",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":100,\"imageUrl\":\"https://system.spektrix.com/jw3/files/ee3edd37-b872-4554-a371-4475183c03b1.jpg\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"National Theatre Live: The Fifth Step\",\"instanceDates\":\"4 January-22 January\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"https://system.spektrix.com/jw3/files/ee3edd37-b872-4554-a371-4475183c03b1-thumbnail.jpg\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"580201AQMDJBQPLJDPCCRJDRQCSTLPGQM\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-01-04T20:00:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-01-04T20:00:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-01-22T20:30:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-01-22T20:30:00Z\",\"altText\":\"National Theatre Live: The Fifth Step\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Cinema\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false},{\"description\":\"Followed by the screening of The Jazz Singer, and before the screening of Song Sung Blue, join us for a Neil Diamond karaoke hour! This is a free event. \",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":60,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Neil Diamond Karaoke\",\"instanceDates\":\"26 January-26 January\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"582401AMNDJLVPQCPBMSGGVMKPTKPVHSR\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-01-26T18:00:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-01-26T18:00:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-01-26T18:00:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-01-26T18:00:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Performance\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false},{\"description\":\"Featuring a César-winning performance from Théodore Pellerin, Nino is the heartwarming and celebratory story of a young man traversing the streets of Paris as he reconnects with friends, family, and himself after a life-altering diagnosis. Duration: 96 minutes Rating: 15 Director: Pauline Loquès Cast: Théodore Pellerin, William Lebghil, Salomé Dewaels Year: 2025 Language: French Subtitles: English https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=wGGFce0vQoc\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":91,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Nino\",\"instanceDates\":\"24 July-30 July\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"641402AHMBDVMGRBLSVJTJJLKRSRCKRPL\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-07-24T15:30:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-07-24T14:30:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-07-30T13:30:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-07-30T12:30:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false,\"attribute_Genre\":\"Cinema\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"When a man is abruptly laid off by the paper company where he has worked tirelessly for many years, he grows increasingly desperate in his hunt. | Duration: 1h 49m, Rating: 15 | Films may be preceded by up to 20 minutes of advertisements and trailers. Specific timings will vary with each screening. We always recommend arriving on time.\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":139,\"imageUrl\":\"https://system.spektrix.com/jw3/files/6274baab-6a18-4591-824a-907546076d21.jpg\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"No Other Choice\",\"instanceDates\":\"15 February-19 February\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"https://system.spektrix.com/jw3/files/6274baab-6a18-4591-824a-907546076d21-thumbnail.jpg\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"588201APMDJNCPBJTMVTGRHNGHDSBTGBR\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-02-15T12:30:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-02-15T12:30:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-02-19T13:30:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-02-19T13:30:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Cinema\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false},{\"description\":\"7.30-9.30pm, £30, building // This dynamic programme features an array of duo combinations alongside rich trio repertoire. Bohuslav Martinů's work is both exhilarating and inventive, while the Debussy stands as the most beloved of all French violin sonatas. The entire programme is elegantly bookended by two delightful trios by Haydn.\\r\\n\\r\\nGreek-Albanian violinist Jonian Ilias Kadesha is celebrated as one of the world’s most individual and imaginative performers. He is joined by London-based Israeli pianist Noam Greenberg and Vienna-based, Kilburn-born cellist Vashti Hunter - both equally gifted and compelling musicians. // Part I \\r\\n\\r\\nJoseph Haydn (1732–1809) \\r\\n\\r\\nPiano Trio in A major, Hob. XV:18 \\r\\n\\r\\nI. Allegro moderato \\r\\n\\r\\nII. Andante \\r\\n\\r\\nIII. Finale: Allegro \\r\\n\\r\\nBohuslav Martinů (1890–1959) \\r\\n\\r\\nDuo for Violin and Cello No. 1, H. 157 \\r\\n\\r\\nI. Preludium: Andante moderato \\r\\n\\r\\nII. Rondo: Allegro con brio \\r\\n\\r\\nRobert Schumann (1810–1856) \\r\\n\\r\\nPhantasiestücke for Piano Trio, Op. 88 \\r\\n\\r\\nI. Romanze: Nicht schnell, mit innigem Ausdruck \\r\\n\\r\\nII. Humoreske: Lebhaft \\r\\n\\r\\nIII. Duett: Langsam und mit Ausdruck \\r\\n\\r\\nIV. Finale: Im Marschtempo, kräftig \\r\\n\\r\\nInterval of 25 minutes \\r\\n\\r\\nPart II \\r\\n\\r\\nLudwig van Beethoven (1770–1827) \\r\\n\\r\\nSeven Variations on 'Bei Männern, welche Liebe fühlen' from Mozart's The Magic Flute, WoO 46 \\r\\n\\r\\nClaude Debussy (1862–1918) \\r\\n\\r\\nSonata for Violin and Piano in G minor, L. 140 \\r\\n\\r\\nI. Allegro vivo \\r\\n\\r\\nII. Intermède: Fantasque et léger \\r\\n\\r\\nIII. Finale: Très animé \",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":120,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Noam Greenberg, Jonian Kadesha and Vashti Hunter\",\"instanceDates\":\"17 November-17 November\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"649201AKVVMGGGRRQMQDPHGVQRBJGHTBL\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-11-17T19:30:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-11-17T19:30:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-11-17T19:30:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-11-17T19:30:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false,\"attribute_Genre\":\"Music\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Classical Music Series\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"7.00pm-8.30pm, £15, hybrid, Wednesday 17 June 2026 // To celebrate Refugee Week 2026, JW3 is delighted to partner with HIAS+JCORE to launch ‘Not Only for Ourselves’, the history of JCORE. This fascinating book documents the evolution of the organisation and explores its role leading Jewish anti-racism across many decades.\\r\\n \\r\\nNow run as HIAS+JCORE – a partnership with the international refugee protection agency HIAS – the charity’s work challenging hate and welcoming refugees in the UK is more important than ever.\\r\\n\\r\\nWe are excited to be joined by an esteemed panel of guests for this event. You will hear from JCORE’s founder, Dr Edie Friedman, who ran the organisation for 46 years; Rabbi David Mason, who became HIAS+JCORE’s first Executive Director in 2023; the book’s author, Joseph Finlay; Lord Simon Woolley; and Dawn Butler MP. Together they will discuss the organisation’s proud 50-year history, and the future of its work amidst the global context of a rising far-right and hostility to refugees.\\r\\n ‘Not Only for Ourselves’ is published in conjunction with the Parkes Institute at the University of Southampton which houses the JCORE archive.\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":90,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Not Only for Ourselves: The Past, Present and Future of JCORE\",\"instanceDates\":\"17 June-17 June\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"593401ACJRCKVQMRBLQDSMKQTSTSHQVQM\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-06-17T19:00:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-06-17T18:00:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-06-17T19:00:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-06-17T18:00:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Talks & Discussions\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Adult Education\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false},{\"description\":\"Richard Linklater recreates the making of Jean-Luc Godard’s seminal feature debut, penning a nostalgic love letter to the rebellious spirit of the French New Wave. | Duration: 1h 46m, Rating: 12A | Films may be preceded by up to 20 minutes of advertisements and trailers. Specific timings will vary with each screening. We always recommend arriving on time.\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":106,\"imageUrl\":\"https://system.spektrix.com/jw3/files/e2311102-3661-46ec-81ea-1c72a89198e8.jpg\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Nouvelle Vague\",\"instanceDates\":\"15 February-19 February\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"https://system.spektrix.com/jw3/files/e2311102-3661-46ec-81ea-1c72a89198e8-thumbnail.jpg\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"588401AHHDHGNRBMLVRCKPSMTPTSBDBMM\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-02-15T18:30:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-02-15T18:30:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-02-19T11:00:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-02-19T11:00:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Cinema\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false},{\"description\":\"Walking Tour, 2-4pm, £20 // Between the 1880s and 1950, the steep streets of Hampstead and Belsize Park absorbed one of the most concentrated waves of Jewish and Continental intellectuals Britain has ever seen. Viennese analysts, Bauhaus architects, Russian-Jewish translators and Austrian painters arrived, many of them refugees, and in barely a square mile they helped remake what \\\"British\\\" modernism would come to mean. \\r\\n\\r\\nThis walk follows that transformation street by street. You will stand outside the flat where D.H. Lawrence lived in 1915, beside the Jewish translator Samuel Koteliansky, to whom he wrote more letters than to anyone outside his own family. You will reach the bookshop corner where a young George Orwell worked alongside Jon Kimche, who would later smuggle Jewish refugees to Palestine and write a standard history of the Balfour Declaration. You will see the Modernist house that gave a James Bond villain his name, and the garden where Keats wrote \\\"Ode to a Nightingale\\\". \\r\\n\\r\\nIt is not a tidy story. The English writers who lived here held the casual prejudices of their class and time, from the family that created Svengali to Orwell's own diaries. The walk meets that contradiction head on. The friction is the point. So is the fusion. \",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":120,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"NW3: A British–Jewish Cultural Melting Pot\",\"instanceDates\":\"6 September-6 September\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"635201AQPDVLBBNGQNMGTJGNLCRBLPLDC\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-09-06T14:00:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-09-06T13:00:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-09-06T14:00:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-09-06T13:00:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false,\"attribute_Genre\":\"Walks\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Walking Tours\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"Boaz Tal\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"10.30am-12.30pm, £20, Wednesday 6 May 2026 // Step into another fascinating part of London’s East End and hear enthralling stories of notable Jewish figures and the places that shaped their journeys.  \\r\\n\\r\\nDiscover the tiny synagogue dwarfed on all sides by a Mosque; the pub where the order of the day was lager and a latke;  why a monument, dedicated to a King of England, was paid for by the East End’s impoverished Jewish community, and the wine shop that smuggled kosher claret to the mayor of New York during those days of alcohol prohibition.  \\r\\n\\r\\nLearn about the fatal battle between rival Jewish gangs known as the Kosher Nostra;  the manic goings-on at Britain’s most famous Yiddish theatre;  the day Jews and non-Jews united to stop fascists marching through the Jewish East End and how a Jewish immigrant was the only witness to a Jack the Ripper murder.  \\r\\n\\r\\nFinally, meet several colourful Jewish characters, including the wedding photographer bringing Hollywood to the East End;  the Chief Rabbi who ‘saved’ Queen Victoria;  the boxer whose greatest match was outside the ring and the Yiddish actress who insisted the show must go on despite bombs falling all around.  \\r\\n\\r\\nThere are other fascinating sites to see, stories to hear and interesting personalities to meet on this enthralling walking tour. Come join!\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":120,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Old Jewish Quarter: The Wonders of Whitechapel\",\"instanceDates\":\"6 May-6 May\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"517601ANSGTTBTCRCVCGPMQVGKRBSCQMK\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-05-06T10:30:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-05-06T09:30:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-05-06T10:30:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-05-06T09:30:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Walks\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Walking Tours\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"Stephen Burstin\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false},{\"description\":\"Under 7s, £8 per child, £6 per adult // Enjoy a family storytelling afternoon celebrating water and kindness in English (12.30pm), Hebrew (2pm), and Russian (3.30pm). Featuring interactive stories, crafts, and sensory play. One ticket grants access to all three languages and beach-themed activities!\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":240,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"One Beach, Three Languages: A Family Storytelling Day\",\"instanceDates\":\"12 July-12 July\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"603001ACJKPPCNTKRPKKMRKSTBTSQTKMT\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-07-12T12:30:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-07-12T11:30:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-07-12T15:30:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-07-12T14:30:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Families & Youth\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Families\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false},{\"description\":\"One of Us (Echad Mi’shelanu) is a tense 1989 Israeli drama directed by Uri Barbash that explores friendship, duty and moral ambiguity within the Israel Defense Forces. The film centers on three close friends who serve together in an elite paratrooper unit. Years later, after one friend is killed, military policeman Rafa is sent to investigate the suspicious death of a Palestinian detainee. Official reports claim the suspect died escaping, but Rafa uncovers evidence suggesting a deliberate killing covered up by his old comrades. Faced with a crisis of conscience, he must choose between exposing the truth and protecting the bond of brotherhood that has defined his life. \\r\\n\\r\\nThis tribute comes in honour of Alon Abutbul, the celebrated Israeli actor who delivered a memorable performance as Yotam in One of Us and whose prolific career spanned Israeli cinema, international films like The Dark Knight Rises, and television; he died unexpectedly in 2025, leaving a profound legacy in film and theatre. | This film is in Hebrew with English subtitles. | Duration: 1h 54m \",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":114,\"imageUrl\":\"https://system.spektrix.com/jw3/files/8402a418-35e5-486a-a608-415dddfb4265.jpg\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"One of Us\",\"instanceDates\":\"13 May-13 May\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"https://system.spektrix.com/jw3/files/8402a418-35e5-486a-a608-415dddfb4265-thumbnail.jpg\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"619601ADTMDGVTJQVVMRMRPBHDPSGSPGV\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-05-13T15:00:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-05-13T14:00:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-05-13T15:00:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-05-13T14:00:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Cinema\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Seret Film Festival\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false},{\"description\":\"2pm-4.30pm, £25 per session or £276 for 12-week course, in building //  Do you want to explore painting and drawing or develop your skills under expert guidance and tuition? Then this course is for you.   \\r\\n\\r\\nStudents in the Art Studio class receive technical assistance and mentorship for their personal art projects. Topics include colour, composition, proportions, and the history of art. Students are to bring in their own project ideas with source materials (printed images, books, and/or objects.  These will be used to develop a project in drawing then with the possibility of painting.  Please refrain from using images on the iPhone. \\r\\n\\r\\nThe teacher is here for guidance by providing pointers to get you to your artistic goals. \\r\\n\\r\\nWhat You’ll Learn? \\r\\n\\r\\nUnderstand how to use foundational art techniques (like line quality in drawing, paint colour blending and composition/proportions)  \\r\\nExpress ideas visually and develop your own creative work \\r\\nLearn how to work from your initial concept to the completion of an artwork with instructor support \\r\\nWho’s It For? \\r\\n\\r\\nThis class is for anyone who wishes to do art but wants some guidance & inspiration. Everyone is welcome, from beginners to more experienced.  \\r\\n\\r\\nDo I need to bring materials?  \\r\\n\\r\\nThis class provides basic materials, including cartridge and watercolour paper. We also have:  \\r\\n\\r\\nPencils, coloured pencils, charcoal, erasures \\r\\nWatercolours, acrylics, palette paper \\r\\nBasic brushes (including watercolour) and palettes knives \\r\\nAdvanced materials like canvases and specialised paper are not supplied. Students are recommended if they already have a materials at home to bring it in like: paint, canvas, or watercolour paper. Am happy to also recommend where to buy materials.   \\r\\n\\r\\nWho Delivers It? \\r\\n\\r\\nMichael Ajerman is an American artist who focuses on colour in painting and drawing. He has consistently exhibited internationally, recently with the Isabel Sullivan Gallery, New York and SQFT: SPACE Gallery, London. Currently he is exhibiting in the Courtauld Institute’s East Wing Biennial exhibition. \",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":150,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Open Art Studio (Afternoons)\",\"instanceDates\":\"22 April-22 July\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"614201ASMPKTRNPCTMLQTCGRHBBBJQNKT\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-04-22T14:00:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-04-22T13:00:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-07-22T14:00:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-07-22T13:00:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Classes & Courses\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"True\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Adult Education Classes & Courses\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"Michael Ajerman\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false},{\"description\":\"6pm-8.30pm, £25 per session or £207 for the course, in building // Do you want to explore painting and drawing or develop your skills under expert guidance and tuition? Then this course is for you.   \\r\\n\\r\\nStudents in the Art Studio class receive technical assistance and mentorship for their personal art projects. Topics include colour, composition, proportions, and the history of art. Students are to bring in their own project ideas with source materials (printed images, books, and/or objects.  These will be used to develop a project in drawing then with the possibility of painting.  Please refrain from using images on the iPhone. \\r\\n\\r\\nThe teacher is here for guidance by providing pointers to get you to your artistic goals. \\r\\n\\r\\nWhat You’ll Learn? \\r\\n\\r\\nUnderstand how to use foundational art techniques (like line quality in drawing, paint colour blending and composition/proportions)  \\r\\nExpress ideas visually and develop your own creative work \\r\\nLearn how to work from your initial concept to the completion of an artwork with instructor support \\r\\nWho’s It For? \\r\\n\\r\\nThis class is for anyone who wishes to do art but wants some guidance & inspiration. Everyone is welcome, from beginners to more experienced.  \\r\\n\\r\\nDo I need to bring materials?  \\r\\n\\r\\nThis class provides basic materials, including cartridge and watercolour paper. We also have:  \\r\\n\\r\\nPencils, coloured pencils, charcoal, erasures \\r\\nWatercolours, acrylics, palette paper \\r\\nBasic brushes (including watercolour) and palettes knives \\r\\nAdvanced materials like canvases and specialised paper are not supplied. Students are recommended if they already have a materials at home to bring it in like: paint, canvas, or watercolour paper. Am happy to also recommend where to buy materials.   \\r\\n\\r\\nWho Delivers It? \\r\\n\\r\\nMichael Ajerman is an American artist who focuses on colour in painting and drawing. He has consistently exhibited internationally, recently with the Isabel Sullivan Gallery, New York and SQFT: SPACE Gallery, London. Currently he is exhibiting in the Courtauld Institute’s East Wing Biennial exhibition. \",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":150,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Open Art Studio (Evenings)\",\"instanceDates\":\"20 May-24 June\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"614001AQNRPQCDLVVRVQLKQRQBJCCNVSM\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-05-20T18:00:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-05-20T17:00:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-06-24T18:00:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-06-24T17:00:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Classes & Courses\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"True\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Adult Education Classes & Courses\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"Michael Ajerman\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false},{\"description\":\"2-4.30pm, 9 week course, £25 per session or £207 for the course // Do you want to learn to paint and draw or develop your skills under expert guidance and tuition? Then this course is for you. Suitable for all levels from beginners to experienced, students in the Art Studio class receive technical assistance and mentorship for their personal art projects. Topics include colour, composition, proportions, and the history of art. Students are to bring in their own project ideas with source materials (printed images, books, and/or objects). The teacher is here for guidance by providing pointers to get you to your artistic goals. Basic art materials are provided; specialised materials must be purchased independently. Please note that each class has limited numbers to ensure each student has adequate time with the tutor. Michael Ajerman is an American representational painter based in London. He has exhibited his work nationally and internationally. He has taught in a wide variety of educational settings and levels.\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":150,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Open Art Studio Winter 2026 (Afternoons)\",\"instanceDates\":\"7 January-18 March\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"578601AGHBMRGMMRMQCNSTKLQVRTBSDNN\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-01-07T14:00:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-01-07T14:00:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-03-18T14:00:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-03-18T14:00:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Classes & Courses\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"True\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Creative Courses\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"Michael Ajerman\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false},{\"description\":\"6-8.30pm, 8 week course, £25 per session or £184 for the course // Do you want to learn to paint and draw or develop your skills under expert guidance and tuition? Then this course is for you. Suitable for all levels from beginners to experienced, students in the Art Studio class receive technical assistance and mentorship for their personal art projects. Topics include colour, composition, proportions, and the history of art. Students are to bring in their own project ideas with source materials (printed images, books, and/or objects). The teacher is here for guidance by providing pointers to get you to your artistic goals. Basic art materials are provided; specialised materials must be purchased independently. Please note that each class has limited numbers to ensure each student has adequate time with the tutor. Michael Ajerman is an American representational painter based in London. He has exhibited his work nationally and internationally. He has taught in a wide variety of educational settings and levels.\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":150,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Open Art Studio Winter 2026 (Evening)\",\"instanceDates\":\"7 January-18 March\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"578801ATNMCPDDGRDBTCSSBNQLDKKDKQH\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-01-07T18:00:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-01-07T18:00:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-03-18T18:00:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-03-18T18:00:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Classes & Courses\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"True\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Creative Courses\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"Michael Ajerman\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false},{\"description\":\"Operation Grandma (Mivtza Savta) is a beloved 1999 Israeli satirical comedy directed by Dror Shaul that has achieved cult status for its quirky humour and unforgettable lines. The story follows three very different brothers — Alon, a no-nonsense Israeli Army officer; Benni, an inventive electrician; and Idan, a gentle tour guide — as they race against time to bury their adored grandmother in her kibbutz cemetery. When Alon must also launch a secret operation the same day, he treats the funeral like a military mission, leading to a cascade of bureaucratic obstacles, mishaps, and absurd situations.\\r\\nThis tribute is especially poignant in honour of the late Rami Heuberger (1963–2025), whose charismatic performance as Lt. Col. Alon “Krembo” Sagiv helped cement the film in Israeli pop culture. Heuberger, a prolific actor and comedian with an extensive career on stage, screen and television, passed away after a battle with cancer this year, and his role in Operation Grandma remains one of his most memorable contributions to cinema.\\r\\n\\r\\nIn honour of the late Rami Heuberger (1963–2025), Operation Grandma is a cult Israeli satirical comedy about three brothers hilariously planning their grandmother’s kibbutz funeral with military precision amid chaos, showcasing Heuberger’s iconic performance as Lt. Col. Alon “Krembo” Sagiv. | This film is in Hebrew with English subtitles. | Duration: 51m\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":51,\"imageUrl\":\"https://system.spektrix.com/jw3/files/ef328ce1-a78e-4120-96f9-066ee4ea8f06.jpg\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Operation Grandma\",\"instanceDates\":\"14 May-14 May\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"https://system.spektrix.com/jw3/files/ef328ce1-a78e-4120-96f9-066ee4ea8f06-thumbnail.jpg\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"620001AVJLBRQJGKBBMRRJQMGSCJMQGRL\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-05-14T15:00:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-05-14T14:00:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-05-14T15:00:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-05-14T14:00:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Cinema\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Seret Film Festival\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false},{\"description\":\"Walking tour, 10.30am-12.45pm, £20 // Stroll through the City of London exploring the fascinating former Medieval Jewish quarter where the first Jewish community experienced a roller coaster existence 1,000 years ago.  Gazing at incredible structures of various times we also meet enthralling Jewish personalities.\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":135,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Original Jewish London: Hiding in the City’s Square Mile\",\"instanceDates\":\"1 November-1 November\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"636002AQVLVPJLCDGMRQNCKVJKGRBRPQV\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-11-01T10:30:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-11-01T10:30:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-11-01T10:30:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-11-01T10:30:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false,\"attribute_Genre\":\"Walks\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Walking Tours\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"Stephen Burstin\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"Hungary, 1957. A young Jewish boy, raised by his mother with idealized tales of his dead father, has his world turned upside down when a brutish man appears, claiming to be his true parent. | This film is in Hungarian with English subtitles. | Duration: 2h 12m, Rating: 15 Credits\\r\\nRating: 15\\r\\nGenre: Drama\\r\\nDirector: László Nemes\\r\\nStars: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=6Hjo2WyLc80\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":132,\"imageUrl\":\"https://system.spektrix.com/jw3/files/b6cb7982-ad59-4b31-9610-fb80aac1950c.jpg\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Orphan\",\"instanceDates\":\"17 May-26 May\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"https://system.spektrix.com/jw3/files/b6cb7982-ad59-4b31-9610-fb80aac1950c-thumbnail.jpg\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"624001AJLJJJJTKSGVNNNJPQLQMDHKBBV\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-05-17T19:00:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-05-17T18:00:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-05-26T10:30:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-05-26T09:30:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Cinema\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false},{\"description\":\"George Orwell was one of the most visionary authors of the 20th Century, whose novels 1984 and Animal Farm foretold a chilling, all-to-believable authoritarian future. Acclaimed director Raoul Peck, working in collaboration with the Orwell Estate, seamlessly interweaves historical clips, readings from Orwell's diary, cinematic references, and dynamic modern day footage to craft not only a definitive portrait of the writer himself, but an entirely fresh take on how remarkably relevant and prophetic his work has become.\\r\\nPeck doesn't just present the information but shows new ways of seeing it, drawing patterns and connections we might not otherwise realize, championing Orwell as a man from the past who just might hold the key to the world's future. | Duration: 1h 59m, Rating: 15 Credits\\r\\nRating: 15\\r\\nGenre: Documentary \\r\\nDirector: Raoul Peck \\r\\nStars: Damian Lewis https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=5tKAaEqoJq0\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":119,\"imageUrl\":\"https://system.spektrix.com/jw3/files/581f1ef6-18e2-44e8-a947-449635dbeab7.jpg\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Orwell: 2+2=5\",\"instanceDates\":\"6 May-31 May\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"https://system.spektrix.com/jw3/files/581f1ef6-18e2-44e8-a947-449635dbeab7-thumbnail.jpg\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"624201ANCSBLDDBNQQBSSGJTQLNMMQBTD\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-05-06T16:10:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-05-06T15:10:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-05-31T10:30:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-05-31T09:30:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Cinema\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false},{\"description\":\"5.30pm-7pm, £20, Sunday 31 May 2026 // For centuries, the shores of the Golden Horn served as a crucible of cultural exchange. In this special, one-off concert commissioned by JW3, we will bring to life the classical (and often overlooked) musical legacy of Jewish composers - such as Boncukcu, Avram Karaka?, Tanburi Isak, Isak Varon, Karakin Efendi, ?brahim Efendi (Misirli), and Haham Nesim Silviya - who flourished within the Ottoman Empire from the 16th to the 19th centuries.\\r\\n\\r\\nWhile often overlooked in modern histories, these masters were central architects of the Ottoman makam system, weaving Jewish liturgical sensibilities into the refined classical aesthetics of the Imperial court. Through traditional instrumentation and faithful ornamentation, this programme celebrates a vanished era where faith and art coexisted in a singular, harmonious voice.\\r\\n\\r\\nThe Ensemble\\r\\n\\r\\nThe repertoire is brought to life by a quintet of celebrated specialists in the Ottoman tradition:\\r\\n\\r\\nBaha Yetkin: Oud & Vocals\\r\\nJacob Olley: Ney\\r\\nSerdar Y?lmaz: Kanun\\r\\nMuammer Sa?lam: Percussion\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":90,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Ottoman-Jewish Masters: The Lost Sounds of Istanbul\",\"instanceDates\":\"31 May-31 May\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"591401APJBPLLKTHQRHKMCMGHKRMJBQHM\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-05-31T17:30:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-05-31T16:30:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-05-31T17:30:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-05-31T16:30:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Music\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Arts & Culture\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false},{\"description\":\"23 Nov - 7 Dec, free, drop in // Our Freedom: Then and Now is a compelling exhibition and companion podcast series created by a cohort of young artists and professionals.\\r\\n\\r\\nThe Exhibition\\r\\nOur Freedom: Then and Now presents a moving collection of artistic expressions created by participants as part of a nationwide project involving 60 libraries and arts centres. Guided by artist Adam Kammerling, the group explored personal and family histories to honour Holocaust survivors and remember relatives who did not survive, while reflecting on how subsequent generations live with and respond to this legacy. \\r\\n\\r\\nThrough their creative works, participants engage with themes of memory, resilience, and the responsibility to ensure the stories and names of those lost are never forgotten. \\r\\n\\r\\nThis free exhibition offers a powerful, multi-generational perspective on remembrance, identity, and the enduring impact of the Holocaust. \\r\\n\\r\\nThe exhibition will run from 23 November - 7 December at JW3.\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":720,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":false,\"name\":\"Our Freedom: Then & Now\",\"instanceDates\":\"10 December-10 December\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"533801AMMPCPVDHCLNVLSJJKCKPVNCHKH\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-12-10T21:00:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2025-12-10T21:00:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-12-10T21:00:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2025-12-10T21:00:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Young Professionals\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Holocaust Learning\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false},{\"description\":\"26 Mar - 16 April, free // Our Freedom: Then and Now is a vibrant photography exhibition that brings together images from 60 locally-led projects, marking 80 years since the end of the Second World War. A nationwide portrait of people, place and belonging, this exhibition reveals communities’ thoughtful and varied take on freedom across the UK.\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":720,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":false,\"name\":\"Our Freedom: Then & Now\",\"instanceDates\":\"26 March-16 April\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"608201ALPPLKKTCPKTTVSJNQQCTVRMCBL\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-03-26T10:00:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-03-26T10:00:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-04-16T22:00:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-04-16T21:00:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Arts & Culture\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false},{\"description\":\"Out at Six is an intimate, introspective documentary in which director Livi Kessel revisits a formative adolescent relationship that slowly shrank her world to just two people and a few large dogs at the door. Though her partner never physically hurt her, Livi lived with the persistent fear that leaving him would bring something terrible. Interwoven with her personal narrative is a timeline built from research into hundreds of cases where women were murdered by their partners, structured into eight stages that chart a chilling progression from romance to danger. Through candid interviews with those who witnessed her transformation, the film explores the subtle, psychological dynamics of abusive relationships and how communities perceive and respond to them, illuminating the often unseen path from affection to confinement. | This film is in Hebrew with English subtitles. | Duration: 55m\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":55,\"imageUrl\":\"https://system.spektrix.com/jw3/files/bfc7aaea-d6ee-428d-88e8-f8b549cc93d0.jpg\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Out At Six\",\"instanceDates\":\"13 May-13 May\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"https://system.spektrix.com/jw3/files/bfc7aaea-d6ee-428d-88e8-f8b549cc93d0-thumbnail.jpg\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"619801ANLRNRKTTJVDVRKVJCBHLBGRSJP\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-05-13T20:00:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-05-13T19:00:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-05-13T20:00:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-05-13T19:00:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Cinema\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Seret Film Festival\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false},{\"description\":\"2pm-3pm, £7 child £5 adult, all ages // Step into a colourful world of movement, imagination, and connection with Rainbow Flow Story Yoga—a joyful, shared experience created especially for grandparents and their grandchildren, as well as parents and young children.\\r\\nUsing gentle yoga poses woven into an engaging story, Rainbow Flow invites children and adults alike to stretch, move, and explore together. Through music, colour, breathing, and playful relaxation, stories come to life—supporting creativity, wellbeing, and meaningful time across generations.\\r\\nDesigned to be accessible and relaxed, sessions encourage everyone to join in at their own pace. Whether you’re new to yoga or a regular mover, Rainbow Flow offers a welcoming space where togetherness matters more than getting it “right.”\\r\\nThis special session is a perfect May Bank Holiday treat, offering a calm, uplifting activity to enjoy during the school break—an opportunity to slow down, connect, and make memories together.\\r\\nWhat to expect\\r\\n\\r\\nStory‑led yoga inspired by imagination and colour\\r\\nGentle, accessible movement for all ages\\r\\nBreathing and relaxation moments to share\\r\\nLaughter, connection, and quality time together\\r\\n\\r\\nWho it’s for\\r\\n\\r\\nGrandparents with grandchildren\\r\\nParents or carers with young children\\r\\nAnyone who loves stories, movement, and shared experiences\\r\\n\\r\\nNo yoga experience is needed—just curiosity and a willingness to play.\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":60,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Over the Rainbow: Yoga Stories\",\"instanceDates\":\"27 May-27 May\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"602001AJDPPDPPNBSVJPQCVPNRCSCTSCG\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-05-27T14:00:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-05-27T13:00:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-05-27T14:00:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-05-27T13:00:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Families & Youth\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Families\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false},{\"description\":\"3-5.30pm, building, £12 //  Join us for a magical celebration for all ages! Children’s Magic Show – Be amazed as our talented magician brings wonder and giggles to the little ones! Mocktail Hour with a Magician – Tweens and teens can sip stylish mocktails while enjoying close-up magic and mind-blowing tricks! Scavenger hunt mystery trail – Fun for all ages! Work together to solve puzzles, unlock the mystery and win a prize! Crafts Corner – Little hands get creative with Purim-themed crafts! Face Painting & Glitter Tattoos – Sparkle and shine with festive designs for kids of all ages! Costumes encouraged – come dressed to impress! Prizes for our Costume Parade! Let the joy of Purim shine through magic, creativity, and fun for the whole family.\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":150,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Party on Purim 2026\",\"instanceDates\":\"1 March-1 March\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"567201ALNLTCRQPMVJTVMDLCNGJBPTBKM\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-03-01T15:00:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-03-01T15:00:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-03-01T15:00:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-03-01T15:00:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false,\"attribute_Genre\":\"Families & Youth\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Families\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"7pm-8.15pm, £15, in building, age 16+ // Author Anna Hájková discusses \\\"People Without History Are Dust\\\" and the often-overlooked place of queerness in Holocaust history. Drawing on rich archival research, the book brings forward the stories of Jewish victims and survivors from across Germany, the Netherlands, Czechoslovakia, and Poland who were doubly marginalised, persecuted both as Jews and as queer individuals. Together, the conversation reflects on silence, survival, and memory, and why telling these stories matters today.\\r\\n\\r\\nDr Anna Hájková is Reader of modern European continental history at the University of Warwick, UK. She is the author of, among others, The Last Ghetto: An Everyday History of Theresienstadt (2020) and People without History are Dust: Queer Desire in the Holocaust (2025).\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":75,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"People Without History Are Dust: Queer Desire in the Holocaust\",\"instanceDates\":\"26 November-26 November\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"595401AHGVHBQQNMVQPNRNRCNCPNJRVMT\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-11-26T19:00:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-11-26T19:00:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-11-26T19:00:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-11-26T19:00:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Talks & Discussions\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Holocaust Learning\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false},{\"description\":\"A film adaptation of the book, Peter Hujar's Day, by Linda Rosenkrantz. It invites audiences into a single day in 1974 with groundbreaking queer photographer Peter Hujar. Set entirely in one room, the film re-creates the conversation between Hujar and Rosenkrantz, recorded on audio tape nearly fifty years ago and later published as a book. Through their freewheeling, intimate exchange, Hujar shares vivid stories of his interactions with literary and cultural icons like William Burroughs, Candy Darling, Susan Sontag and Allen Ginsberg, while also reflecting on the rhythms of everyday life in 1970s New York. | Duration: 1h 16m, Rating: 12A \",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":76,\"imageUrl\":\"https://system.spektrix.com/jw3/files/2ba80a91-a54c-4efe-b4a4-e22069a36399.jpg\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Peter Hujar's Day\",\"instanceDates\":\"11 January-15 January\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"https://system.spektrix.com/jw3/files/2ba80a91-a54c-4efe-b4a4-e22069a36399-thumbnail.jpg\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"580801ARLSLPRGGRSPPNGGNNBKRSBHTTD\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-01-11T20:00:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-01-11T20:00:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-01-15T19:30:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-01-15T19:30:00Z\",\"altText\":\"Peter Hujar's Day\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Cinema\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false},{\"description\":\"7-9.30pm, hybrid, £15 // Walter Benjamin is one of the most enigmatic thinkers of the 20th-century - a philosopher, critic, and writer whose reflections on history, art, and Judaism resist easy categorisations. His work moves between Marxism and messianic thought, critical theory, the study of language and poetry.  \\r\\n \\r\\nAt the heart of his work are bold and unsettling questions. What if history is not simply a narrative we inherit but something that can be interrupted? What if justice is different to law and power? And how can Judaism be a critical force that can help navigate modern life? \\r\\n \\r\\nIn this short introduction, we will trace how these questions emerge in Benjamin’s thought, and how they invite us to think differently about history, justice and the possibility of change. These questions matter today more than ever. \\r\\n\\r\\nDaniel Weizman is a philosophy lecturer at City Lit and the Mary Ward Centre in London, and the founder of the London School of Continental Philosophy. He holds a PhD from the Centre for Research in Modern European Philosophy (CRMEP), with a focus on philosopher Gilles Deleuze. His teaching spans twentieth- and twenty-first-century continental philosophy, including Michel Foucault, Jacques Derrida, Louis Althusser, Alain Badiou, and Slavoj Žižek, with connections to politics, culture, and aesthetics.\\r\\n\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":150,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Philosophy Taster Night: Walter Benjamin\",\"instanceDates\":\"11 February-11 February\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"558402ABSPBGMNBGCQKLJKTLJMKBHHVDN\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-02-11T19:00:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-02-11T19:00:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-02-11T19:00:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-02-11T19:00:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Talks & Discussions\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Adult Education\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false},{\"description\":\"\\\"7pm-9pm, £20, in building, 16+, Tuesday 9 June 2026 // Southeastern CT, USA, 2026 – Sandra Laub’s 80-minute solo play, Picking Up Stones, her reaction to October 7th, has been hailed as a “remarkable combination of passion, compassion and respect for the facts.” A ‘must see’ show at Edinburgh Fringe Festival 2025, Sandra gives voice to many character perspectives, from Golda Meir to a Palestinian ‘mother of martyrs’, holding up two truths: one can weep for the death of Jewish children and the death of Palestinian children. Her play questions: How can the victims, the innocents on both sides, begin to heal from their trauma? How do diaspora Jews reaffirm their belief in the preservation of Jewish values in the land of Israel? How can people of every faith, denomination, and political persuasion acknowledge the need for peace, now.\\r\\n\\r\\nThe war has ‘ended’ but the peace is fragile. Jews and Muslims worldwide face a sharp spike in Antisemitism and Islamophobia. In America, political left and right swing sharply, debating the issue in the streets and on campus, and the Middle East is re-made as the world watches. Sandra grapples with emotions anyone can recognize in this swirling maelstrom of events.\\\"\\r\\n\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":120,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Picking Up Stones\",\"instanceDates\":\"9 June-9 June\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"592601ARHJLCTMPDVNTQPSBTJJNGSJVMP\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-06-09T19:00:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-06-09T18:00:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-06-09T19:00:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-06-09T18:00:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Performance\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Arts & Culture\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false},{\"description\":\"7-9.30pm, hybrid, £20 // In collaboration with the Royal Academy of Music and the British Library, we are proud to present an evening exploring three extraordinary pianists: Harriet Cohen, Myra Hess and Irene Scharrer. Delve into their navigation of the classical music industry, World Wars, and Jewish identity in the twentieth century. Listen to live performances of significant works from their careers by Academy students, see materials from the British Library’s Music Collections, and hear discussions, from a panel of passionate academics, of their political-musical challenges and achievements. \",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":150,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Play Nice: Jewish Women in 20th Century Classical Music [In Building]\",\"instanceDates\":\"23 February-23 February\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"564801ASTVQLSBVRMCLVSPNBLCMKCNNGS\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-02-23T19:00:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-02-23T19:00:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-02-23T19:00:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-02-23T19:00:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Music\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Arts & Culture\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false},{\"description\":\"7-9.30pm, hybrid, £20 // In collaboration with the Royal Academy of Music and the British Library, we are proud to present an evening exploring three extraordinary pianists: Harriet Cohen, Myra Hess and Irene Scharrer. Delve into their navigation of the classical music industry, World Wars, and Jewish identity in the twentieth century. Listen to live performances of significant works from their careers by Academy students, see materials from the British Library’s Music Collections, and hear discussions, from a panel of passionate academics, of their political-musical challenges and achievements. \",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":150,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Play Nice: Jewish Women in 20th Century Classical Music [Online]\",\"instanceDates\":\"23 February-23 February\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"590001AGGGGKCDRGJCSJLMRJPPLLLMDSM\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-02-23T19:00:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-02-23T19:00:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-02-23T19:00:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-02-23T19:00:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Arts & Culture\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Arts & Culture\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false},{\"description\":\"When Rick (Paul Rudd), a past-his-prime wedding singer, meets fading boy-band star Danny (Nick Jonas) during a gig, the two bond over music and a late-night jam session. \\r\\n\\r\\n \\r\\n\\r\\nBut when Danny turns one of Rick's songs into the hit that reignites his career, Rick sets out to reclaim the recognition he believes he deserves -- even if it means risking everything he cares about.  \\r\\n\\r\\n \\r\\n\\r\\nFrom writer-director John Carney (Sing Street, Once), Power Ballad is a feel-good story about music, self-respect, friendship, and the price of ambition. \\r\\n\\r\\n \\r\\n\\r\\nDuration: 98 minutes \\r\\n\\r\\nRating: 15 \\r\\n\\r\\nDirector: John Carney \\r\\n\\r\\nCast: Paul Rudd, Nick Jonas, Jack Reynor \\r\\n\\r\\nYear: 2025 \\r\\n\\r\\nLanguage: English \",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":98,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Power Ballad\",\"instanceDates\":\"21 June-25 June\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"628802AQJRLRJBVLSLQJLSSPPTCGSKSQN\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-06-21T15:45:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-06-21T14:45:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-06-25T12:30:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-06-25T11:30:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Cinema\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false},{\"description\":\"In 18th century Venice, 20-year-old violin virtuoso Cecilia lives at the Pièta orphanage, where, despite her talent, she remains confined, knowing that marriage is the only way out. Yet, her life takes a turn after she meets Antonio Vivaldi, a brilliant and ambitious composer who becomes the new violin teacher. Guided by Vivaldi and his music, Cecilia finds the strength to challenge the destiny that once seemed inevitable. | This film is in Italian with English subtitles. | Duration:1h 51m, Rating: 15 Credits\\r\\nRating: 15\\r\\nGenre: Drama\\r\\nDirector: Damiano Michieletto \\r\\nStars: Michele Riondino, Tecla Insolia, Fabrizia Sacchi https://youtu.be/J-fEjuVy5cQ\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":110,\"imageUrl\":\"https://system.spektrix.com/jw3/files/4f316c50-52d7-48a1-a4da-bfb027a0f393.jpg\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Primavera\",\"instanceDates\":\"17 May-28 May\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"https://system.spektrix.com/jw3/files/4f316c50-52d7-48a1-a4da-bfb027a0f393-thumbnail.jpg\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"624401ASRMQGDQPVRTTKJPLMPTQHCTTHR\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-05-17T16:30:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-05-17T15:30:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-05-28T10:30:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-05-28T09:30:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Cinema\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false},{\"description\":\"Rt Hon Dame Jacinda Ardern, New Zealand's 40th Prime Minister, led her nation through unprecedented challenges, implemented bold policies, and became the second leader in history to give birth in office, all while championing an inclusive and empathetic leadership style that changed global expectations of what a leader can be. | Duration: 1h 41m, Rating 12A \",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":101,\"imageUrl\":\"https://system.spektrix.com/jw3/files/a3cbfe1f-d8a5-45f0-9225-2a22083d4031.jpg\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Prime Minster \",\"instanceDates\":\"4 January-8 January\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"https://system.spektrix.com/jw3/files/a3cbfe1f-d8a5-45f0-9225-2a22083d4031-thumbnail.jpg\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"580001AKPSQTHNSNJDHCNRPGPSCMLNGBH\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-01-04T17:30:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-01-04T17:30:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-01-08T15:50:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-01-08T15:50:00Z\",\"altText\":\"Prime Minster \",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Cinema\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false},{\"description\":\"7.30pm-9.15pm, £12, ages 14+ // After the dramatic cancellation of her show at the Edinburgh Fringe last year, multi-award-winning comedian Rachel Creeger presents a preview of her brand new show, a brutally warm and darkly funny exploration of racism v Rachism - or when it's paranoia, and when they're really out to get you.\\r\\n\\r\\nThis show will be followed by a Q&A with the performer.\\r\\n\\r\\n★★★★ \\\"Her show is one of the Fringe's big talking points\\\" The Telegraph \\r\\n★★★★ \\\"There is a huge scope for humour around culture and religion. Rachel Creeger is the pinnacle of this.\\\" Funny Women\\r\\n“Clever banter, (and) sharp observation that crosses the religious divide” Fringe Review\\r\\n★★★★ ”Very, very funny” Jewish Chronicle\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":105,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Rachel Creeger: \\\"Queen of the Jews!\\\"\",\"instanceDates\":\"10 June-10 June\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"622601AGCDCTNLBHCMHMQNQRHLDPHTHSG\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-06-10T19:30:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-06-10T18:30:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-06-10T19:30:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-06-10T18:30:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Comedy\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Comedy\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"Rachel Creeger\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false},{\"description\":\"7pm-8.30pm, £20, in building // Join us for a live recording of The Brink, a hugely popular podcast from Daily Telegraph columnist and former Jewish Chronicle editor Jake Wallis Simons and ex-Parachute Regiment officer and geopolitical analyst Andrew Fox.\\r\\nFor this special evening, Jake and Andrew will be joined on stage by Brendan O’Neil, author of After The Pogrom, and well-loved Countdown presenter and campaigner Rachel Riley.\\r\\nAs a foreign correspondent and a frontline soldier respectively, Jake and Andrew have both seen life on the brink first-hand and have found a passion for defending Israel and the West.\\r\\nBrendan and Rachel have both made a name for themselves as tireless activists against antisemitism. Particularly since October 7, they have emerged as crucial voices in the national debate, standing up bravely and unapologetically for Britain’s Jewish minority.\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":90,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Rachel Riley and Brendan O’Neil on The Brink\",\"instanceDates\":\"19 January-19 January\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"534801ACDNPRLPTJRSGPRHVPTQCKKHKHD\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-01-19T19:00:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-01-19T19:00:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-01-19T19:00:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-01-19T19:00:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Talks & Discussions\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false},{\"description\":\"A gently humanist story of the American West from Max Walker-Silverman, Rebuilding follows Dusty (Josh O'Connor), a reserved, divorced father whose ranch has burned down in a devastating wildfire. Now living in a trailer community on a government-run campsite, Dusty finds solace with his new neighbors who have also lost everything, quietly reassembles his life, and starts reconnecting with his ex-wife Ruby (Meghann Fahy) and young daughter Callie-Rose (Lily LaTorre). Filmed against the rapturous backdrop of southern Colorado, Rebuilding is a ruminative, moving portrait of resilience and human connection in the wake of loss. | Duration: 1h 36m, Rating: PG Credits\\r\\nRating: PG \\r\\nGenre: Drama \\r\\nDirector: Max Walker-Silverman\\r\\nStars: Josh O’Connor, Meghann Fahy, Lila LaTorre https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=QkwoapyJjiI&pp=ygUVcmVidWlsZGluZyB1ayB0cmFpbGVy\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":95,\"imageUrl\":\"https://system.spektrix.com/jw3/files/0b62af08-98ce-45ce-8cb4-433972a0505c.jpg\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Rebuilding\",\"instanceDates\":\"12 May-14 May\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"https://system.spektrix.com/jw3/files/0b62af08-98ce-45ce-8cb4-433972a0505c-thumbnail.jpg\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"624601ALVTVHQKSCVTCQVPSDKDBNHBSBS\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-05-12T12:40:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-05-12T11:40:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-05-14T12:35:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-05-14T11:35:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Cinema\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false},{\"description\":\"7-8.15pm, £10, building // Drawing on obituaries, memorial essays and tributes published in the AJR Journal between 1955 and 2025, Refugee Lives : Stories of Exile, Resilience, and Community traces the lives of German-speaking Jewish refugees and émigrés who fled Nazi persecution and built new lives, largely in Britain. Through stories of exile, rebuilding, work, family and community, the book offers a moving portrait of a generation and the lasting impact it had on British Jewish life. Join us and guests for a conversation about memory, resilience and what these lives can still tell us today. \",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":75,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Refugee Lives: Stories of Exile, Resilience, and Community\",\"instanceDates\":\"12 November-12 November\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"637401ANCCTGBJTNDBVPDNTMTMLDCGJRK\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-11-12T19:00:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-11-12T19:00:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-11-12T19:00:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-11-12T19:00:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false,\"attribute_Genre\":\"Talks & Discussions\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Holocaust Learning\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"2-3.30pm, £20, building // In his final years, Rembrandt van Rijn painted some of his most striking self-portraits. \\r\\n\\r\\nPerhaps no artist in the history of Western art has celebrated old age with as much love and respect as Rembrandt. Early in his career he painted a series of deeply moving portraits of an old woman traditionally believed to be his mother. Later on he explored the aging process by looking into the mirror and painting his own portrait. \\r\\n\\r\\n \\r\\n\\r\\nJoin us to explore how artists represent ageing—and how our interpretations shape what we see. \\r\\n\\r\\n \\r\\n\\r\\nPatrick Bade is a Historian, writer and broadcaster. He studied at UCL and the Courtauld and was senior lecturer at Christies Education for many years. He has worked for the Art Fund, Royal Opera House, National Gallery, V&A. He has published on 19th- and early 20th-century painting and on historical vocal recordings. \",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":90,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Rembrandt & Old Age\",\"instanceDates\":\"10 December-10 December\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"638001AMQJMPPSLMBMNQDDBQQHHQHJBTP\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-12-10T14:00:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-12-10T14:00:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-12-10T14:00:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-12-10T14:00:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false,\"attribute_Genre\":\"Talks & Discussions\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Adult Education\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"Patrick Bade\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"7pm-8.15pm, £15, in building // ages 13+ // Extinguished Lives is a short film which has been shown recently at DOC NYC and the Miami Jewish Film Festival. It was directed by award-winning filmmaker Roberta Grossman for the Lost Shtetl Museum, a new Holocaust Museum in Lithuania, which opened in late 2025 after more than a decade of research, planning and building.  During the Second World War, newlywed Frida seeks refuge in her hometown of Šeduva, a shtetl in Lithuania, only to find that fear and betrayal have taken hold. She must confront an unthinkable choice - stay with her family or save herself. Based on survivor testimony, Extinguished Lives tells the little-known story of the Lithuanian Holocaust, exposing how a centuries-old community was erased village by village. A one-night-only screening of the 15-minute film accompanied by a discussion featuring the team behind the Lost Shtetl Museum.\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":75,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Remembering the Holocaust in Lithuania: the stories behind the Lost Shtetl Museum\",\"instanceDates\":\"11 February-11 February\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"583401AGGBJVNTRGNQJHQDKNNDSBPPRPQ\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-02-11T19:00:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-02-11T19:00:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-02-11T19:00:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-02-11T19:00:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Talks & Discussions\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Holocaust Learning\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false},{\"description\":\"Set in modern-day Tokyo, Rental Family follows an American actor who struggles to find purpose until he lands an unusual gig: working for a Japanese \\\"rental family\\\" agency, playing stand-in roles for strangers. As he immerses himself in his clients’ worlds, he begins to form genuine bonds that blur the lines between performance and reality. Confronting the moral complexities of his work, he rediscovers purpose, belonging, and the quiet beauty of human connection. | Duration: 2h 19m, Rating: 12A | Films may be preceded by up to 20 minutes of advertisements and trailers. Specific timings will vary with each screening. We always recommend arriving on time.\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":109,\"imageUrl\":\"https://system.spektrix.com/jw3/files/903f0618-1eda-4f77-99f5-de80189f6bf9.jpg\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Rental Family\",\"instanceDates\":\"17 February-19 February\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"https://system.spektrix.com/jw3/files/903f0618-1eda-4f77-99f5-de80189f6bf9-thumbnail.jpg\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"587402AHTRCHNDNMDMGJCVMTMTTDPRQPR\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-02-17T13:40:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-02-17T13:40:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-02-19T16:10:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-02-19T16:10:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Cinema\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false},{\"description\":\"19:30 // 29 Oct 2026 // £16 // A gentle workshop combining restorative and Hatha yoga with breathwork to support rest, regulation and presence. We’ll finish with a sound healing journey using Alchemy crystal singing bowls to encourage deep relaxation and rejuvenation.\\r\\n\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":90,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Restorative Yoga and Sound Bowls\",\"instanceDates\":\"29 October-29 October\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"633801ANLRGSDVTJQSKHLNTRCNGGBDNQD\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-10-29T19:30:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-10-29T19:30:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-10-29T19:30:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-10-29T19:30:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false,\"attribute_Genre\":\"Young Professionals\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"Sargam Picker\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"Join Robert Peston in conversation with Gabriel Pogrund to discuss his brand-new political thriller.\\r\\n\\r\\nOne of Britain’s most trusted and recognisable journalists, Robert Peston is ITV’s Political Editor and host of the flagship political programme Peston, as well as co-host of the hugely popular podcast The Rest is Money with Steph McGovern, where he continues to help audiences make sense of the rapidly changing worlds of politics, business and finance.\\r\\n\\r\\nPeston is also a bestselling author, and his latest novel, The Kill Switch, a gripping and timely political thriller set at the intersection of media, money and political power is published on 16 July.\\r\\n\\r\\nPeston and Pogrund will discuss the themes behind the novel, the realities of modern political journalism, and the stories shaping Britain today, followed by an audience Q&A.\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":75,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Robert Peston in conversation with Gabriel Pogrund\",\"instanceDates\":\"16 July-16 July\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"630201AQGPPRMMNQPCSVRQGQCCJCRNTMK\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-07-16T19:30:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-07-16T18:30:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-07-16T19:30:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-07-16T18:30:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Talks & Discussions\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Robert Peston\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false},{\"description\":\"11am-12noon, £20, hybrid // If you have ever read Rosemary Sutcliff’s Eagle of the Ninth you will know that it was believed that a Roman legion mysteriously disappeared in the wilds of Scotland. Come and hear the latest evidence about this occurrence and what may really have happened to IX Hispana. An ancient mystery that still excites the world of Roman scholars. \\r\\n\\r\\n  \\r\\n\\r\\nBio: Jill Stern is an historian by training. Her master’s degree was in the Art and Culture of the Dutch Golden Age and Art History also featured in her doctoral thesis and subsequent book. She is currently teaching two classes of Victorian Art for the University of the Third Age. \",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":60,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Roman Britain’s Missing Legion\",\"instanceDates\":\"9 December-9 December\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"638201ALLRMDPPSVHCGPLTHTGRMJNPGQJ\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-12-09T11:00:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-12-09T11:00:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-12-09T11:00:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-12-09T11:00:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false,\"attribute_Genre\":\"Talks & Discussions\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Adult Education\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"Jill Stern\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"2pm-4.15pm, £20, Sunday 9 August 2026 // The City of London has always been home to immigrant communities, with many immigrants making their mark literally through sculptures and reliefs. Wind your way through the City streets, discover these monuments and delve into the tales of the figures who shaped them. \\r\\n\\r\\nWe will discover the first official public sculpture, the Monument which was carved by Caius Gabriel Cibber a Danish immigrant; a drinking fountain by French refugee, Aimé-Jules Dalou; mosaics by Russian born Boris Anrep and perhaps the most significant contribution of sculptures by a number of Jewish refugees from Nazi Europe who settled in the UK such as Naomi Blake, Frank Meisler, Oscar Nemon and Georg Ehrlich.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nMarilyn Greene is a museum curator and educator. She was Curator of Hampstead Museum, Burgh House between 1998 & 2006 and worked in adult and community initiatives at the Victoria and Albert Museum from 2000-2013, primarily with faith and intercultural groups. In 2019/20 she assisted with administration for the Insiders Outsiders Festival which organises events about refugees from Nazi Europe and their contribution to the arts. She has worked on organisational and curatorial projects at London Transport Museum and is currently a Hidden London Guide for them. She is a qualified City of London Guide and Westminster Guide and also leads mudlarking tours on the Thames foreshore and school tours for the Charles Dickens Museum.\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":135,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Sanctuary in the City: Public Art of Immigrants & Refugees\",\"instanceDates\":\"9 August-9 August\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"600401ARSLPTVVQRHKNTVJVQKDLGLDCMK\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-08-09T14:00:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-08-09T13:00:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-08-09T14:00:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-08-09T13:00:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Walks\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Walking Tours\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"Marilyn Greene\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false},{\"description\":\"In 18th-century England, Savage House follows Sir Chauncey Savage (Richard E. Grant), a gloriously unscrupulous social climber propped up by debt and bravado.  \\r\\n\\r\\n \\r\\n\\r\\nWhen invited to host the Duke and Duchess of Devonshire, Chauncey and his razor-sharp wife, Lady Savage (Claire Foy), launch a bid to impress. As preparations spiral into duels, decadence and bloodshed, their performance careens out of control--a darkly comic satire of class, spectacle, and the art of appearing important. //\\r\\n\\r\\n \\r\\n\\r\\nDuration: 114 minutes \\r\\n\\r\\nRating: 15 \\r\\n\\r\\nDirector: Peter Glanz \\r\\n\\r\\nCast: Richard E. Grant, Clare Foy, Jack Farthing  \\r\\n\\r\\nYear: 2025 \\r\\n\\r\\nLanguage: English \",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":114,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Savage House \",\"instanceDates\":\"26 June-1 July\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"627802ATSJDLKCGGMDMBSMPSDCBNHVLPL\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-06-26T13:15:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-06-26T12:15:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-07-01T13:15:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-07-01T12:15:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Cinema\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false},{\"description\":\"Following its record-shattering predecessor, Saving Shuli San reunites Israeli comedy icons Tzion Baruch (Avihu), Shalom Michaelshvili (Nati), and Asi Israelof (Betzalel) in their most absurd adventure yet. When Shuli (David Shaul) is snatched by the Yakuza in Tokyo, the charismatic trio teams up with the sharp and scene-stealing Emma Medding as Shuli’s Tokyo boss, plus a delightfully unpredictable female android, to chase him across Japan. Packed with slapstick comedy, unforgettable chemistry, and laugh-out-loud set pieces, this film delivers nonstop fun from ninjas to fish-out-of-water culture shocks. It’s a joyful, high-energy blend of action and humor that keeps audiences laughing and keeps box offices booming. | This film is in Hebrew with English subtitles. | Duration: 1h 34m\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":100,\"imageUrl\":\"https://system.spektrix.com/jw3/files/99cbe98f-58f7-4c3c-a5ba-9d533d3dd37f.jpg\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Saving Shuli San\",\"instanceDates\":\"14 May-14 May\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"https://system.spektrix.com/jw3/files/99cbe98f-58f7-4c3c-a5ba-9d533d3dd37f-thumbnail.jpg\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"620002AGTGNPRHQHHLDNNLHSNRJRBQHJP\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-05-14T20:00:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-05-14T19:00:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-05-14T20:00:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-05-14T19:00:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Cinema\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Seret Film Festival\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false},{\"description\":\"2pm-3pm, £10, ages 4+ // Philip Simon's hilariously bonkers, award-winning show where children (and maybe even a\\r\\nfew parents) take to the stage to share their favourite jokes.\\r\\nCreated by comedian Philip Simon during lockdown to entertain children (and give parents\\r\\na well-deserved homeschooling break), this is the hilariously silly joke show where your\\r\\nkids are the stars.\\r\\nPhilip holds everything together compering the start of the show, but it’s not long before\\r\\nthe children are given free reign to come up and wreak havoc with their best jokes whilst\\r\\ntheir grown ups cower in their seats, scared of what they might say! Expect silliness,\\r\\ncheeky laughs and almost certainly a few references to poo! Seriously, it's like herding\\r\\ncats, but the laughs your kids will have and get make it all worthwhile!\\r\\nBest Children's Show - Buxton Fringe 2024\\r\\nBest Children's Show - Morecambe Fringe 2022\\r\\nLeicester Comedy Festival Best Kids' Show 2021 (nominee)\\r\\n‘The comedy world's Joe Wicks’ (BBC)\\r\\n‘Philip Simon is never less than hilarious’ (The Stage)\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":60,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"School's Out! Comedy Club\",\"instanceDates\":\"14 June-14 June\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"602601AKMTLQMCQJRQNRQKQLKRNGVPTVD\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-06-14T14:00:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-06-14T13:00:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-06-14T14:00:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-06-14T13:00:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Families & Youth\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Families\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"Philip Simon\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false},{\"description\":\"7.30-9.30pm, £30, building // Schubert’s joyous “Trout” Quintet features utterly charming variations on his song “Die Forelle,” where the addition of a double bass gives the piece its signature buoyancy and verve. Beethoven’s trio is a sheer delight, while the Saint-Saëns is a violinist’s showstopper - radiantly lyrical and thrillingly virtuosic.\\r\\n\\r\\nThe acclaimed Russian-Vietnamese violinist Aylen Pritchin is making major waves across Europe with his stunning playing. He is joined by the marvelous Taiwanese-Canadian pianist Connie Shih, famously known as Steven Isserlis’s regular duo partner.  //  Part I \\r\\n\\r\\nLudwig van Beethoven (1770–1827) \\r\\n\\r\\nString Trio in G major, Op. 9 No. 1 \\r\\n\\r\\nI. Adagio – Allegro con brio \\r\\n\\r\\nII. Adagio ma non tanto e cantabile \\r\\n\\r\\nIII. Scherzo: Allegro \\r\\n\\r\\nIV. Presto \\r\\n\\r\\nCamille Saint-Saëns (1835–1921) \\r\\n\\r\\nIntroduction and Rondo Capriccioso in A minor, Op. 28 \\r\\n\\r\\nInterval of 20 minutes \\r\\n\\r\\nPart II \\r\\n\\r\\nFranz Schubert (1797–1828) \\r\\n\\r\\nPiano Quintet in A major, D. 667 ‘The Trout’ \\r\\n\\r\\nI. Allegro vivace \\r\\n\\r\\nII. Andante \\r\\n\\r\\nIII. Scherzo: Presto \\r\\n\\r\\nIV. Andantino – Allegretto (Theme and Variations) \\r\\n\\r\\nV. Finale: Allegro giusto \\r\\n\\r\\n \",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":105,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Schubert Trout Quintet: Connie Shih, Aylen Pritchin, Ami-Louise Johnsson, David Waterman, Enno Senft\",\"instanceDates\":\"28 October-28 October\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"648801ARQMVBCPDPKHMRDLCKBCQPRCGNS\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-10-28T19:30:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-10-28T19:30:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-10-28T19:30:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-10-28T19:30:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false,\"attribute_Genre\":\"Music\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Classical Music Series\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"6pm-9pm, £20, in building // 12+ // Join us for a live sculpting session by internationally renowned sculptor Frances Segelman as she will be creating a sculpture of Holocaust survivor Harry Olmer MBE in front of an audience.  \\r\\n\\r\\nYad Vashem UK works closely with Frances Segelman producing Holocaust survivor sculptures. This will be the 8th sculpting she has done in a series for Yad Vashem UK. \\r\\n\\r\\nA wonderful opportunity to see Frances Segelman in action, find out more about the process of creating a sculpture as well as meeting Holocaust survivor Harry Olmer and be part of this special occasion. \\r\\n\\r\\nFrances will start sculpting from 6 pm onwards, with a break at 7pm, before resuming at 7:30 pm. There will be a Q&A at 8:15pm.\\r\\n\\r\\nSome light refreshments will be provided.  \",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":180,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Sculpting Lives: An Evening with Frances Segelman and Harry Olmer MBE\",\"instanceDates\":\"13 January-13 January\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"437201AGRLDSLPVJMPLPVRCQKRBSQVPTR\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-01-13T18:00:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2025-01-13T18:00:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-01-13T18:00:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2025-01-13T18:00:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Special Events\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false},{\"description\":\"7-8.19pm, building, £20, age 16+ // \\r\\nThe ritual is broken…or the story is broken…and I don’t know if we’re supposed to fix it.”\\r\\nIn Seder, Adam Kammerling unpacks the tangled stories we carry — and how we choose to tell them — through a performance of spoken word, dance, physical theatre, and live music. \\r\\nRooted in the Jewish ritual of the same name, Seder is a decade in the making. This powerful interdisciplinary performance dives deep into memory and identity — confronting inherited grief, unspoken truths, and the unexpected harmony between heavy metal and Jewish tradition. \\r\\nA dynamic non-linear storytelling experience, Seder is a ritual for now — asking what survival means, in confronting times, and how we pass it on. \",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":70,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Seder\",\"instanceDates\":\"17 February-17 February\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"565801AGJMTDPBLQTRSLMQPBRPSTKMSMP\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-02-17T19:00:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-02-17T19:00:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-02-17T19:00:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-02-17T19:00:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Performance\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Arts & Culture\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false},{\"description\":\"Sisters Nora and Agnes reunite with their estranged father, the charismatic Gustav, a once-renowned director who offers stage actress Nora a role in what he hopes will be his comeback film. When Nora turns it down, she soon discovers he has given her part to an eager young Hollywood star. Suddenly, the two sisters must navigate their complicated relationship with their father -- and deal with an American star dropped right into the middle of their complex family dynamics. | This film is in Norwegian and Swedish with English subtitles. | Duration: 2h 13m, Rating: 15 \",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":133,\"imageUrl\":\"https://system.spektrix.com/jw3/files/1508a985-1cfc-4068-afd5-2b66b128f1dc.jpg\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Sentimental Value\",\"instanceDates\":\"19 January-20 April\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"https://system.spektrix.com/jw3/files/1508a985-1cfc-4068-afd5-2b66b128f1dc-thumbnail.jpg\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"580002AJKMPDQVSNVRBDLBGTKMJSLGNMV\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-01-19T15:30:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-01-19T15:30:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-04-20T13:30:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-04-20T12:30:00Z\",\"altText\":\"Sentimental Value\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Cinema\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false},{\"description\":\"\\\"7pm-8pm, £20, in building, 16+, Tuesday 2 June 2026 // SHADOW PUPPETS\\r\\n\\r\\nA (multi-media) song cycle about celebrity, devised by lyricist Nikki Racklin, with musical director James Cleeve (the songwriting team that brought you BETTE AND JOAN AND BABY JANE, THE MUSICAL).\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nAll lyrics by Nikki Racklin. Music by composers that include Bella Barlow, James Cleeve, Tim Gilvin, Ben Glasstone, Howard Goodall, Michael Tauben and Eden Tredwell.\\\"\\r\\n\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":60,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Shadow Puppets\",\"instanceDates\":\"2 June-2 June\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"592401ARQGRVCJCTBLJGTVMJLDVQVQMGQ\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-06-02T19:00:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-06-02T18:00:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-06-02T19:00:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-06-02T18:00:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Performance\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Arts & Culture\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false},{\"description\":\"\\\"7pm-9.30pm, £20 per class/£75 for the full course, in building, 20s & 30s, 3rd June\\r\\n17th June\\r\\n24th June\\r\\n8th July // Learn to craft cocktails and unleash your creativity with our in-house mixologist, Nini!\\r\\n\\r\\nThis four-part course builds your skills week by week - from mastering the basics of bartending to designing your own signature drink.\\r\\n \\r\\nEach session introduces a new theme, with hands-on recipes, insider tips, and plenty of time to schmooze. While classes can be booked individually, we highly encourage completing the full course for the best experience, culminating in a final showcase and certificate of participation.\\r\\n \\r\\nPlease contact gianina@jw3.org.uk to notify us of any food allergies as soon as possible upon booking. \\r\\n\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":150,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Shake, Stir & Schmooze: Young JW3 Cocktail Making Course\",\"instanceDates\":\"3 June-15 July\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"603401ABCDJTBNNSGRSQLLTNSGMDJSVCD\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-06-03T19:00:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-06-03T18:00:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-07-15T19:00:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-07-15T18:00:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Young Professionals\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"True\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Young JW3\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"Hugo Max\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false},{\"description\":\"1.30-2.30pm & 3.30-4.30pm, building, £7 child, £4 adult, £15 for a family of 3, ages 0 to 9 // Join us for a magical afternoon of music and fun with a professional opera singer and pianist, with sessions in Hebrew and Russian!\\r\\n\\r\\n1.30pm session in Hebrew\\r\\n3.30pm session in Russian\\r\\n \\r\\nEnglish translations of the main spoken parts between the arias will be available during the event.\\r\\n\\r\\nEach session brings classical music to life in a way that’s fun and easy to enjoy for all ages. Children will take part in the show, learn about opera, and discover how much fun classical music can be. Expect famous opera scenes and arias -- some just the way you know them, and some with a playful twist. It’s an immersive experience full of laughter, joy and unforgettable moments.\\r\\n\\r\\nFor children ages 0 to 9. \",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":60,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Shalom, Opera!\",\"instanceDates\":\"29 March-29 March\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"567601ALVKGJHRMDQVCRHHPKQGRDBDBDS\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-03-29T13:30:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-03-29T12:30:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-03-29T15:30:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-03-29T14:30:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Families & Youth\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Families\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false},{\"description\":\"7-8.20pm, building, £16, age 16+ // Sharif شريف is a moving drama about the precarious lives of LGBTQ+ Palestinians, written by Tomer Aldubi.\\r\\nSharif was forced to flee the West Bank as a teen, after his sexual identity has been publicly exposed and his life put in danger. Since then, he’s been trying to survive in Israel, a foreign land, completely alone. Barely speaking the language, and guided by the memory of his secret lover Nour, whom he left behind, he tries to secure a stay permit on the grounds of welfare.\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":80,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Sharif\",\"instanceDates\":\"23 March-23 March\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"566201AJCKVJDRVQPVCBSBBBVVDNHJNGH\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-03-23T19:00:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-03-23T19:00:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-03-23T19:00:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-03-23T19:00:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Performance\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Arts & Culture\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false},{\"description\":\"2pm-3pm, £7 per child, £5 per adult, ages 2-5 // Join Ilana Banana for a joyful Shavuot Learn & Sing Party, a vibrant celebration bursting with songs, stories, movement, and color. We will explore the beautiful tradition of Shavuot by bringing the story of the Jewish people gathering at the foot of the mountain to life through music, play, and imagination.\\r\\n\\r\\nThe session is packed with sensory fun, featuring rainbow ribbons and scarves, musical shakers, and plenty of bubble time. Children will love the high-energy parachute play and the many opportunities for dancing, jumping, and sharing in the collective joy of the holiday.\\r\\n\\r\\nThis is the perfect way for your little ones to celebrate Shavuot through music, movement, friendship, and wonder. We invite you to come learn, come sing, and celebrate the season with Ilana.\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":60,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Shavuot Learn and Sing\",\"instanceDates\":\"24 May-24 May\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"601801AJPCCBSTJSDHMDKDPCPHNVBTHLP\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-05-24T14:00:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-05-24T13:00:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-05-24T14:00:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-05-24T13:00:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Families & Youth\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Families\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"Ilana Banana\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false},{\"description\":\"The special screening on Wednesday 15 July will be accompanied by a brand new set from JW3's beloved comedian Rachel Creeger! Exploring teenage angst, embarrassing moments and making the best of a mishegas! // Shiva Baby is an anxiety-inducing dark comedy about Danielle, a directionless bisexual college student. While attending a traditional Jewish mourning reception (shiva) with her parents, her afternoon spirals into a claustrophobic nightmare when she unexpectedly runs into both her ex-girlfriend and her older, married sugar daddy who is there with his wife and baby. // 15, 1h 7m\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":90,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Shiva Baby\",\"instanceDates\":\"15 July-15 July\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"627201AGTMCBNBBJLBTLSTJMDDJSKKRHT\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-07-15T19:00:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-07-15T18:00:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-07-15T19:00:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-07-15T18:00:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":true,\"attribute_Genre\":\"Cinema\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Coming of Age Film Season\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"Shiva Baby is an anxiety-inducing dark comedy about Danielle, a directionless bisexual college student. While attending a traditional Jewish mourning reception (shiva) with her parents, her afternoon spirals into a claustrophobic nightmare when she unexpectedly runs into both her ex-girlfriend and her older, married sugar daddy who is there with his wife and baby. Duration: 117 minutes Rating: 15 Director: Emma Seligman Cast: Rachel Sennott, Danny Deferrari, Fred Melamed Year: 2020 https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=laJaR_i7c8g\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":78,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Shiva Baby\",\"instanceDates\":\"16 July-19 July\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"642401ARKSBHTLVBSQNBHHSQDKSJMRDVB\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-07-16T14:00:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-07-16T13:00:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-07-19T11:00:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-07-19T10:00:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false,\"attribute_Genre\":\"Cinema\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"INVITATION ONLY EVENT // 8am-10am, free, in building // A joint invitation-only event at JW3 in cooperation with The London Initiative (TLI) // Exploring the potential impact of the 2026 Israeli elections through the lens of TLI’s three imperatives: Promoting Mature Liberal Democracy, Societal Fairness and Partnership Between Israel and World Jewry  //\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":120,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Significance of the Israeli Elections through The London Initiative Prism\",\"instanceDates\":\"13 February-13 February\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"583201AVDQTLRPRVLJKKLVNSKSRMVDNJD\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-02-13T08:00:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-02-13T08:00:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-02-13T08:00:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-02-13T08:00:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Talks & Discussions\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false},{\"description\":\"We are creating the biggest Bar, Bat and B’nei Mitzvah photo album to celebrate this uniquely Jewish rite of passage, loud and proud. We would love to see photos from your simcha, formal or informal, classic or wonderfully wacky, from portraits to dancefloor candids, as well as invitations and menus. From 1926 to 2026, the more the merrier. \\r\\n\\r\\nWe will enlarge a selection of images and display them inside and outside JW3 from this July. While we already have a small number of photographs from the Jewish Museum to get us started, we are inviting you to help us fill JW3 with Bar, Bat and B’nei Mitzvah memories. Tell us who is in the photo and what you remember about the special day. Send your images and memories to barmitzvah@jw3.org.uk \",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":720,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":false,\"name\":\"Simcha Snaps! JW3's Giant B'Mitzvah Photo Album\",\"instanceDates\":\"11 June-27 August\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"615201AGTGHLDCSGJBNDSGRQRCVGGVHQC\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-06-11T10:00:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-06-11T09:00:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-08-27T22:00:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-08-27T21:00:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Special Events\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false},{\"description\":\"5-6pm, building, £7, ages 10+ // Michael has everything — he’s successful, excels at school, has many friends, and is the star of the city’s football team. \\r\\nBut he has a secret: his older brother, Gabriel, is autistic. \\r\\n\\r\\nMichael is terrified of his friends finding out. He decides to hide Gabriel’s existence and lies to everyone about his family. \\r\\nOn the evening of his 13th birthday, his worst nightmare comes true — a surprise party has been planned at his home, where his friends will finally meet his autistic brother. \\r\\n\\r\\nWhat will Michael do to keep his secret from being revealed? \\r\\nA beautiful and moving play inspired by the life story of actor Idan Shkroka, who grew up alongside his autistic brother. \",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":60,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Simply Special\",\"instanceDates\":\"1 February-1 February\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"568201ABLNPSBVTQPKSBQBJNGCVSPPBKL\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-02-01T17:00:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-02-01T17:00:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-02-01T17:00:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-02-01T17:00:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Families & Youth\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Festival of Spoken Ivrit\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false},{\"description\":\"Single week ONLY for the Hebrew Intensive Summer Ulpan // Mon 28 July - Fri 1 Aug // £250 for the single week // Priority will be given to customers booking the full 2 week Ulpan. Customers booking the single week only be able to proceed if there is space. If there is not space, a full refund will be given.\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":300,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Single Week ONLY - Hebrew Summer Ulpan\",\"instanceDates\":\"27 July-3 August\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"631201ARQCLHLVHTNTTBLKSCNPCHKGRQB\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-07-27T10:30:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-07-27T09:30:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-08-03T10:30:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-08-03T09:30:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false,\"attribute_Genre\":\"Languages\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"True\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"7.30pm, tentative duration 2hrs, £33 adult £16.50 student, in-building //Mozart was the first composer to realise the great potential of adding an extra viola to the string quartet, and his exceptionally expressive quintet in g minor is a major masterpiece which resounds through the centuries.  Brahms also enjoys the extra sonorities offered by the medium and his quintet is full of sunlit vitality and warmth.  Bruckner wrote very little chamber music apart from a viola quintet and this Adagio movement at its centre is sublime beyond words.  The programme opens with a wonderful little-known rarity from late Beethoven. // This group includes the inspirational and poetic violinists Simonen and Ruisi, and the superb, richly gifted violists Larivière and Tunnicliffe. \",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":120,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Sini Simonen, Alessandro Ruisi, Sào Soulez Larivière, Luba Tunnicliffe, and David Waterman\",\"instanceDates\":\"4 March-4 March\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"494001AJQGVDBQQRGTJSJQRSTMCLKVMVV\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-03-04T19:30:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-03-04T19:30:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-03-04T19:30:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-03-04T19:30:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Arts & Culture\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Classical Music Series\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false},{\"description\":\"A father and son arrive at a rave deep in the mountains of southern Morocco. They are searching for Mar -- daughter and sister -- who vanished months ago at one of these endless, sleepless parties. Surrounded by electronic music and a raw, unfamiliar sense of freedom, they hand out her photo again and again. Hope is fading, but they push through and follow a group of ravers heading to one last party in the desert. As they venture deeper into the burning wilderness, the journey forces them to confront their own limits. | This film is in Arabic, Spanish and French with English subtitles. | Duration: 1h 54m, Rating: 15 \",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":115,\"imageUrl\":\"https://system.spektrix.com/jw3/files/0eebb4e9-e7e5-4115-a24c-fbe7a766631b.jpg\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Sirāt\",\"instanceDates\":\"29 March-21 April\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"https://system.spektrix.com/jw3/files/0eebb4e9-e7e5-4115-a24c-fbe7a766631b-thumbnail.jpg\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"606202AVCNNDVPPKGSTTCRRNQQNLDKJNP\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-03-29T20:10:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-03-29T19:10:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-04-21T19:15:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-04-21T18:15:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Cinema\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false},{\"description\":\"Screening with Q&A // Celebrate the 20 year anniversary of the British Jewish classic Sixty Six, and 60 years since the iconic World Cup Final of 1966! Jason Solomons in conversation with director Paul Weiland and star Eddie Marsan // \\r\\n\\r\\nComic tale about the agony of a young Jewish boy whose bar mitzvah is scheduled for the day of the 1966 World Cup final at Wembley. Bernie Rubens has been gleefully looking forward to the big day throughout his childhood, but when England book their place in the final against West Germany, will his friends and family be able to resist World Cup fever and make it to the celebration? //\\r\\n\\r\\n12A, 1h 33m plus Q&A\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":150,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Sixty Six\",\"instanceDates\":\"10 June-10 June\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"627001ANVDHLMHLVQSJCBNJVSPDNJMJJH\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-06-10T18:00:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-06-10T17:00:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-06-10T18:00:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-06-10T17:00:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":true,\"attribute_Genre\":\"Cinema\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"\\tComing of Age Film Season\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"Regular screenings // A comic tale about the agony of a young Jewish boy whose bar mitzvah is scheduled for the day of the 1966 World Cup final at Wembley. Bernie Rubens has been gleefully looking forward to the big day throughout his childhood, but when England book their place in the final against West Germany, will his friends and family be able to resist World Cup fever and make it to the celebration? //\\r\\n\\r\\nDuration: 93 minutes \\r\\nRating: 12A \\r\\nDirector: Paul Weiland \\r\\nCast: Helena Bonham Carter, Eddie Marsan, Gregg Sulkin \\r\\nYear: 2006 \\r\\nLanguage: English \",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":93,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Sixty Six\",\"instanceDates\":\"14 June-17 June\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"628401AKGKTQJQSHDTGRHQRDTPPHHSNCJ\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-06-14T13:00:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-06-14T12:00:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-06-17T20:10:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-06-17T19:10:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Cinema\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false},{\"description\":\"3pm-5pm, £20, Sunday 26 July 2026 // Discover four centuries of history and diversity in a walking tour that delves into the rich heritage of Soho - with a Jewish twist! Join us as we explore the quirky streets of central London’s Bohemian playground, and learn about its fascinating and multi-layered history. This includes its Georgian origins; different waves of immigration over the centuries; Soho's musical and theatre heritage; the vice trade; famous restaurants, pubs and clubs; and London's gay village. Furthermore, your guide will describe the area's eclectic Jewish history - from street traders and tailors to musicians, theatre producers and hairdressers - this tour is for everybody!\\r\\n\\r\\nLocation: Starting point will be provided upon booking.\\r\\nPlease wear comfortable shoes and dress for the weather!\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":120,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Soho Tour with a Jewish Twist\",\"instanceDates\":\"26 July-26 July\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"517801ANBJNDJBQQBTPLJRDJGHBNQGGLC\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-07-26T15:00:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-07-26T14:00:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-07-26T15:00:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-07-26T14:00:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Walks\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Walking Tours\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"Marc Gardiner\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false},{\"description\":\"19:00 // 22 Nov 2026 // £20 // Irving Berlin (Annie Get Your Gun/White Christmas), Kurt Weill (Lady In The Dark/Mack The Knife) and Maury Yeston (Nine/Grand Hotel) were all children of revered Cantors – we celebrate their songs with a West End cast, whilst reflecting on the influence growing up around Jewish music made on their work.\\r\\n\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":135,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Son of a Cantor Man - The Music of Irving Berlin, Maury Yeston, Kurt Weill and Harold Arlen\",\"instanceDates\":\"22 November-22 November\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"633001ADRRMBQSHGSQQTSCDBQTHSPKJKL\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-11-22T19:00:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-11-22T19:00:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-11-22T19:00:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-11-22T19:00:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false,\"attribute_Genre\":\"Performance\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"Based on a true story, two down-on-their-luck musicians form a joyous Neil Diamond tribute band, proving it's never too late to find love and follow your dreams. | Duration: 2h 13m, Rating: 12\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":133,\"imageUrl\":\"https://system.spektrix.com/jw3/files/fb800e69-b3d3-4833-86f9-4b7f9a4c73b3.jpg\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Song Sung Blue\",\"instanceDates\":\"25 January-4 March\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"https://system.spektrix.com/jw3/files/fb800e69-b3d3-4833-86f9-4b7f9a4c73b3-thumbnail.jpg\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"582001ASRNMNNMGMLSVTMDNGVLDLGQMVT\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-01-25T20:10:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-01-25T20:10:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-03-04T16:20:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-03-04T16:20:00Z\",\"altText\":\"Song Sung Blue\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Cinema\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false},{\"description\":\"3pm-5pm, £20, Sunday 28 June 2026 // Stroll with us through the Spitalfields area adjacent to the venerable City of London, where magnificent Georgian houses line the side streets of an historic (now trendy and multi-cultural) neighbourhood. \\r\\n\\r\\nOur walk will start in Aldgate at the site of the 2000-year old Roman Wall that defined the original settlement of Londinium, take us past Bevis Marks, London's oldest functioning synagogue opened in 1701, through famous streets such as Petticoat Lane and Brick Lane, and end at Spitalfields - a former Victorian covered market that is now famous for food, fashion, and art. \\r\\n\\r\\nHear about immigrant communities over the centuries that found refuge and work nearby, including French Protestant silk weavers, East European Jewish tailors, and Bangladeshi Muslim restauranteurs.\\r\\n\\r\\nSee historic streets where Yiddish was once the common language, later to be replaced by Bengali. Hear about the vibrant Jewish community that dominated the area in the late 19th and early 20th centuries, and learn about 1000 years of Jewish history in Britain. \\r\\n\\r\\nJoin us to celebrate London's cultural diversity in the heart of this great city!\\r\\n\\r\\nThis tour will not depart from JW3; the meeting location will be provided upon booking.\\r\\n\\r\\nPlease wear comfortable shoes and dress for the weather!\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":120,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Spitalfields: The Historic Jewish East End of London \",\"instanceDates\":\"28 June-28 June\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"492401ALPRVCKJRHQJPPRLHJBPBGJTDRT\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-06-28T15:00:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-06-28T14:00:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-06-28T15:00:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-06-28T14:00:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Walks\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Walking Tours\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"Marc Gardiner\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false},{\"description\":\"This is a venue hire, customers should visit mirimusic.com to book // At the Miriam School of Music, your child can learn, sing, and grow — with inspiring Jewish and secular music taught by conservatoire-trained professionals.\\r\\nLed by Itamar Rashkovsky, violinist at the Royal Welsh College of Music and the Junior Guildhall School of Music\\r\\nEvery teacher is conservatoire-trained — excellence you can trust.\\r\\n•\\tBuild musicianship skills with fun, interactive games\\r\\n•\\tSing Jewish songs in choir \\r\\n•\\tKids of all ages and musical backgrounds welcome!\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":120,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":false,\"name\":\"Summer Music School\",\"instanceDates\":\"15 June-29 June\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"503801AMDLBQCMKGKSGVBRBTRHLKMJGGS\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-06-15T10:30:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2025-06-15T09:30:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-06-29T10:30:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2025-06-29T09:30:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Families & Youth\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Venue Hire\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false},{\"description\":\"Marc Isaacs makes a deal with The Synthetic Sincerity Lab, an AI research project. There, researchers are investigating the possibility of teaching AI characters authenticity, using characters from Isaacs’ documentaries to do so. In return, they allow Isaacs to film the process. Duration: 72 minutes Rating: TBC Director: Marc Isaacs Year: 2025 https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Ml-ZQMF4xfQ\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":71,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Synthetic Sincerity\",\"instanceDates\":\"26 July-29 July\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"641602ALVTGTRGQMHLGCRVJVMRLKHJKHP\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-07-26T11:00:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-07-26T10:00:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-07-29T18:00:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-07-29T17:00:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false,\"attribute_Genre\":\"Cinema\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"7pm-9pm, £16.50, in building // Marc Isaacs (The Filmmaker’s House) made a deal with The Synthetic Sincerity Lab, an AI research project affiliated with the University of Southern England.\\r\\nThere, researchers are investigating the possibility of teaching AI characters authenticity, using characters from Isaacs’ documentaries to do so. In return, they allow Isaacs to film the process.\\r\\nAn AI avatar, created in collaboration with Romanian actress Illinca Manolache (seen in Do Not Expect Too Much from the End of the World by Radu Jude) guides him through this complex research world and sternly instructs him how to behave there. Isaacs films the work of the rebellious AI researcher Lynn, and follows an Uyghur chef who puts himself forward as a subject of study. Can this chef, in AI form, put into words what he is unable to express as a human being?\\r\\nIsaacs’ innovative narrative gradually blurs the line between fact and fiction. Synthetic Sincerity explores the relationship between humans and machines through a blend of documentary, fictional scenes, and gently absurd humor. How does the development of AI influence the way we look at human faces? And how might this technology affect cinema in the future?\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":120,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Synthetic Sincerity: Preview Screening + Director Q&A\",\"instanceDates\":\"22 July-22 July\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"644002ARGSRKQSMRLVPPSBCNRJQPBRSCC\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-07-22T19:00:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-07-22T18:00:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-07-22T19:00:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-07-22T18:00:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false,\"attribute_Genre\":\"Cinema\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"2.30-3.30pm, building, £7 Child, £5 Adult, £15 Family of 3, ages 6-11 // Join us for a calming and joyful one-hour session designed especially for grandparents and their primary school-aged grandchildren. Our instructor, a member of the Tai Chi Union of Great Britain, will guide you through the basics in a welcoming and supportive environment.\\r\\nTogether, you’ll explore the graceful movements of Tai Chi—perfect for all ages and abilities—followed by a relaxing moment to sip on soothing chai tea.\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":60,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Tai Chi & Chai Tea for Grandparents and Grandkids\",\"instanceDates\":\"22 February-22 February\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"567001ACPQGMJRDSMJJMHNHHKKDDCMJLC\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-02-22T14:30:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-02-22T14:30:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-02-22T14:30:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-02-22T14:30:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Families & Youth\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Families\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false},{\"description\":\"Wednesdays 9.30am-10.30am and Fridays 10.30am-11.30am // 15 April - 10 July // Venue Hire, book at hampsteadtaiji@gmail.com or 0783 8339 948 \",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":60,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":false,\"name\":\"Tai Chi Chuan\",\"instanceDates\":\"15 April-10 July\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"474201ABPPJCQSHPHBRQNGNTTLDDHHBHL\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-04-15T09:30:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-04-15T08:30:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-07-10T09:30:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-07-10T08:30:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Classes & Courses\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false},{\"description\":\"2-3/30pm, £20, building // Is it possible to write fiction drawn from lived experiences without sometimes upsetting or alienating friends and family?  \\r\\n\\r\\nFor many writers, the honest answer is no.  \\r\\n\\r\\nStorytelling often borrows from real lives and real conversations - usually without permission. For some Jewish writers, this unease can perhaps feel sharpened by a cultural and religious reluctance to “tell tales”. According to the laws of Lashon Hara, pretty much any commentary on other people’s behavior is frowned upon. \\r\\n\\r\\nThis moral tension - between the urge to tell stories and the responsibility to protect others - sits at the heart of Deborah Freeman’s short story collection, ‘Tell It Not’, which spans forty years and moves between the familiar landscapes of England and the vivid, sunlit settings of Israel.  \\r\\n\\r\\nIn layered and intimate tales, a mother speaks into the night to soothe her screaming baby. A recently released prisoner recounts his journey with the help of two determined volunteers. A woman enters a dressmaker’s studio and is trapped in a room of mirrors – confronted by six silent versions of herself. With characters young and old, caught between cultures, causes and personal crossroads, the stories explore the everyday and the extraordinary: family tensions, political divides, love, loss and the long shadows of history. \\r\\n\\r\\nPresenting her collection of stories, Deborah reflects the quandary of writing fiction that draws on real people and real relationships.  \\r\\n\\r\\nDeborah Freeman, playwright and short story writer, grew up in Bristol and lived in Leeds, Ashkelon, and Manchester, before moving to London in 2013. Plays include Candlesticks, The Song of Deborah and Xanthippe, and radio plays The Bad Samaritan, and Fat. The Song of Deborah was translated into Hebrew and staged at the Khan Theatre, Jerusalem in 2017.   Along the way, she trained and worked as a Psychiatric Social Worker.  She is currently working on a memoir and discussing her latest play, Doors, with a director. \\r\\n\\r\\nShort story collection ‘Tell it Not,’ was first published in 2022 by Red Heifer Press, California, and the current edition was published in 2024 by Wrate Publishers, London.\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":90,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Telling Tales\",\"instanceDates\":\"21 October-21 October\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"639601ANMBVVTBBCNNTDKNKMLQRLTQNHD\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-10-21T14:00:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-10-21T13:00:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-10-21T14:00:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-10-21T13:00:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false,\"attribute_Genre\":\"Talks & Discussions\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Adult Education\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"Deborah Freeman\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"Test Event, testing the new cancellation feature in spek \",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":60,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Test Event For Cancellation \",\"instanceDates\":\"2 April-1 October\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"504201ADCKKKGTRNCRPNMDGNPGMDLKHJC\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-04-02T19:00:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2025-04-02T18:00:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-10-01T11:00:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2025-10-01T10:00:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Classes & Courses\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false},{\"description\":\"Thursdays, 1.30pm-2.30pm, £7 per session // Come and join JW3's regular students who organise this weekly debate choosing the topics and debaters on each side.  Hear their voices and add your own.  \",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":60,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"The Abraham Debating Club for Autumn 2026\",\"instanceDates\":\"10 September-10 December\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"645401APBJDLHHJRGVRMJRMMNGMMNKNVS\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-09-10T13:30:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-09-10T12:30:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-12-10T13:30:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-12-10T13:30:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false,\"attribute_Genre\":\"Classes & Courses\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"7.30pm-10.30pm, £10, in building // An exclusive opportunity for a live networking and watch party with BBC’s The Apprentice star, Lawrence Rosenberg. The event promises to be a unique experience and an exciting opportunity to meet, greet, and mingle with a community member participating in one of the BBC’s biggest reality programs.\\r\\n\\r\\nWith it being the 20th anniversary season, this year’s show is shaping up to be one of the most exciting in memory, with big budget trips, more drama and twists week on week.\\r\\nThe evening will be split into 3 exciting parts, with an opportunity for opening networking with Lawrence and esteemed guests, including former Apprentice candidates, politicians, the press, and leading London business leaders. There will be two opportunities for Q&As with Lawrence, both before and after the show (9-10), with guests able to take pictures with Lawrence before close at 10:30.\\r\\n\\r\\nOpen networking from 1930 until 2030\\r\\nEvent will start with Q&A at 2020\\r\\nWatch party live followed by 15 mins Q&A \\r\\n\\r\\nOur Kosher cocktail bar will be open throughout the evening, serving handcrafted cocktails and drinks.\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":180,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"The Apprentice Live Watch Party with Lawrence Rosenberg\",\"instanceDates\":\"26 February-26 February\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"585801ARCBHKLTDRBRVJLGQHTBHMQNPCD\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-02-26T19:30:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-02-26T19:30:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-02-26T19:30:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-02-26T19:30:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Talks & Discussions\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false},{\"description\":\"Tuesdays, 11am-1pm, £180 for the 10-week course // Learn the art of Hebrew Calligraphy and develop beautiful artwork inspired by text. Work with ink, paint and gold to create beautifully illuminated Hebrew letters, words, quotations and more. \\r\\n\\r\\n What You’ll Learn: \\r\\n\\r\\nHold and use a calligraphy pen correctly \\r\\n\\r\\nForm consistent strokes and letter shapes \\r\\n\\r\\nCreate your own Calligraphic artwork  \\r\\n\\r\\nWho It’s For: \\r\\n\\r\\nThis course is ideal for beginners and also those with art /calligraphy experience. No previous experience or artistic background is required. All are welcome! \\r\\n \\r\\n\\r\\nWho Delivers It: \\r\\n\\r\\nVetta is an artist and calligrapher specialising in Hebrew Calligraphy and painted illumination. She has exhibited widely including at the British Library, The Museum of London and the Jewish Museum.  Vetta is an experienced educator.  \",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":120,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"The Art of Hebrew Calligraphy\",\"instanceDates\":\"22 September-22 September\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"643801ALHBRPGGNQQLKVJLRCHPRVTQHQJ\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-09-22T11:00:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-09-22T10:00:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-09-22T11:00:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-09-22T10:00:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false,\"attribute_Genre\":\"Classes & Courses\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"True\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"Vetta Alexis\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"Tuesdays, 11am-1pm, in building // £180 for the course // Learn the art of Hebrew Calligraphy and develop beautiful artwork inspired by text. Work with ink, paint and gold leaf to create beautifully illuminated Hebrew letters, words, quotations and more.  \\r\\n\\r\\n What You’ll Learn: \\r\\n\\r\\nHold and use a calligraphy pen correctly \\r\\n\\r\\nForm consistent strokes and letter shapes \\r\\n\\r\\nCreate your own words, quotes and artwork  \\r\\n\\r\\nWho It’s For: \\r\\n\\r\\nThis course is ideal for beginners and anyone looking to explore calligraphy as a creative and artistic hobby. No previous experience or artistic background is required. \\r\\n\\r\\nWho Delivers It: \\r\\n\\r\\nVetta is an artist and calligrapher specialising in Hebrew Calligraphy and painted illumination. She has exhibited widely including at the British Library, The Museum of London and the Jewish Museum.\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":120,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"The Art of Hebrew Calligraphy Spring 2026\",\"instanceDates\":\"21 April-14 July\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"599001ACKTRBGQCMVKBTRNCPPNGSNKDMH\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-04-21T11:00:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-04-21T10:00:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-07-14T11:00:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-07-14T10:00:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false,\"attribute_Genre\":\"Classes & Courses\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"True\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Creative Courses\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"Vetta Alexis\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"Tuesdays, 11am-1pm, £20 per session or £162 for the 9 week course, in building // Join artist and calligrapher, Vetta Alexis, to learn Hebrew Calligraphy, and to work with ink, paint and gold to create beautifully illuminated Hebrew Letters, words, quotations and more.  Whether you are a beginner or already on your calligraphy journey, all levels are welcome!\\r\\n\\r\\nVetta is an artist specialising in Hebrew Calligraphy and painted illumination. She has exhibited widely including at the British Library, The Museum of London and the Jewish Museum.\\r\\n\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":120,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"The Art of Hebrew Calligraphy Winter 2026\",\"instanceDates\":\"13 January-24 March\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"561001ALMCSCBSPKNGVPJBQMMCCLMKMDD\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-01-13T11:00:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-01-13T11:00:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-03-24T11:00:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-03-24T11:00:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Classes & Courses\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"True\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Creative Courses\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"Vetta Alexis\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false},{\"description\":\"7pm-8.15pm, £17, in building, Wednesday 27 May 2026 // It’s not just a question of learning the notes. It’s also knowing whether to race ahead or drag one’s feet, march steadily or sway deliciously. It’s knowing how to tease out the dramatic, the delicate, the confident, the fearful, the wit – and how to navigate the emotional journey from first note to last.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nMusician, artist and writer Ruth Waterman explores the options by playing some of Beethoven’s miraculous Bagatelles for piano, showing how a performer attempts to reach the heart of the music.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nIncluded in the book The Great Violinists, Ruth Waterman spent her long career as a solo violinist interpreting the works of the great composers for audiences around the world, including at the Royal Festival Hall and Carnegie Hall’s International Artists series, while pondering the challenging process of bringing music to life. This led to her giving concert talks throughout the UK and abroad, from Germany to South Africa, Russia to Israel, as well as presenting programmes about music and the art of listening on BBC Radio 3 and New York Radio (WNYC).\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nwww.ruthwaterman.com\\r\\n\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":75,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"The Art of Performance with Ruth Waterman\",\"instanceDates\":\"27 May-27 May\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"603801ANTKMNVRQKGBPHBMPDBJNTQDTHJ\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-05-27T19:00:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-05-27T18:00:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-05-27T19:00:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-05-27T18:00:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Music\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Arts & Culture\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"Ruth Waterman\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false},{\"description\":\"The Book of Ruth is an emotional and compelling Israeli drama that draws viewers into the intensely personal world of Ruth and Shmuel Ben David, a young ultra-Orthodox couple whose life is built around tradition, devotion and the joy of family. On the morning they had planned to celebrate their son’s cherished coming-of-age milestone, a devastating accident claims his life, shaking everything they held sacred.\\r\\nAs Ruth struggles with unbearable grief and questions her faith, Shmuel retreats deeper into religious devotion, and the couple’s once-shared path begins to diverge. What unfolds is a powerful exploration of love tested by tragedy, the weight of community expectations, and the fragile journey toward healing. Told with compassion and lyrical grace, this film resonates with anyone who’s grappled with loss and searched for meaning in its wake. | This film is in Hebrew and French with English subtitles. | Duration: 1h 28m\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":88,\"imageUrl\":\"https://system.spektrix.com/jw3/files/619cefcf-9fba-4888-9f4e-b49956febde6.jpg\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"The Book of Ruth\",\"instanceDates\":\"14 May-14 May\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"https://system.spektrix.com/jw3/files/619cefcf-9fba-4888-9f4e-b49956febde6-thumbnail.jpg\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"620401AKHBBTJCRGDQBPMSTQTJVTTCBKR\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-05-14T18:15:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-05-14T17:15:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-05-14T18:15:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-05-14T17:15:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Cinema\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Seret Film Festival\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false},{\"description\":\"The Book of Ruth will be preceded by a screening of the short film, The Butcher's Stain. In The Butcher's Stain, Samir, a Palestinian butcher working at an Israeli supermarket, is accused of tearing down the Israeli hostage posters in the break room. Samir sets out to prove his innocence in order to keep the job he desperately needs. | Duration: 26 minutes. | The Book of Ruth is an emotional and compelling Israeli drama that draws viewers into the intensely personal world of Ruth and Shmuel Ben David, a young ultra-Orthodox couple whose life is built around tradition, devotion and the joy of family. On the morning they had planned to celebrate their son’s cherished coming-of-age milestone, a devastating accident claims his life, shaking everything they held sacred.\\r\\nAs Ruth struggles with unbearable grief and questions her faith, Shmuel retreats deeper into religious devotion, and the couple’s once-shared path begins to diverge. What unfolds is a powerful exploration of love tested by tragedy, the weight of community expectations, and the fragile journey toward healing. Told with compassion and lyrical grace, this film resonates with anyone who’s grappled with loss and searched for meaning in its wake. | These films are in Hebrew, Arabic and French with English subtitles. | Duration: 1h 28m\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":124,\"imageUrl\":\"https://system.spektrix.com/jw3/files/354dd766-5ca7-4e9f-84bb-3e0b3a808fe9.jpg\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"The Book of Ruth & The Butcher's Stain\",\"instanceDates\":\"11 May-11 May\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"https://system.spektrix.com/jw3/files/354dd766-5ca7-4e9f-84bb-3e0b3a808fe9-thumbnail.jpg\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"619201ATJMPQRPTPPTQPDSDHHJLTHRMRT\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-05-11T19:30:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-05-11T18:30:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-05-11T19:30:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-05-11T18:30:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Cinema\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Seret Film Festival\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false},{\"description\":\"The Bride of Belsen tells the extraordinary story of Gena Turgel MBE.  \\r\\n\\r\\n \\r\\n\\r\\nThe youngest of nine children, she survived four Nazi concentration camps. Having walked out of the gas chambers at Auschwitz concentration camp alive, she remained by her mother’s side, doing everything she could to keep her alive. \\r\\n\\r\\nShe was liberated in 1945 by British soldier Norman Turgel. Their love story captured the world’s imagination when they married just months later, Gena in a wedding dress made from a British parachute, now preserved at the Imperial War Museum. \\r\\n\\r\\nKnown as “The Bride of Belsen”, she became one of the most recognised voices of Holocaust education, sharing her testimony with hundreds of thousands and earning an MBE for her service. \\r\\n\\r\\nTold in her own voice, with spellbinding imagery and a powerful soundtrack, this is her testimony. //\\r\\n \\r\\nDuration: 60 minutes \\r\\nRating: 12A \\r\\nLanguage: English \",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":60,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"The Bride of Belsen\",\"instanceDates\":\"15 June-18 June\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"629001ADCKMGNHQLSSSMLQGQQVVSDKQGS\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-06-15T19:00:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-06-15T18:00:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-06-18T17:35:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-06-18T16:35:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Cinema\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false},{\"description\":\"In 1930s Chicago, groundbreaking scientist Dr. Euphronious brings a murdered young woman back to life to be a companion for Frankenstein's monster. What happens next is beyond what either of them could ever have imagined. | Duration: 2h 6m, Rating: 15\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":126,\"imageUrl\":\"https://system.spektrix.com/jw3/files/76cc39c3-9c3d-43e8-97a5-2950f5b88253.jpg\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"The Bride!\",\"instanceDates\":\"29 March-31 March\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"https://system.spektrix.com/jw3/files/76cc39c3-9c3d-43e8-97a5-2950f5b88253-thumbnail.jpg\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"606401AQNKKTNGBSSRTDJPSTMJJGRHRRP\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-03-29T17:20:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-03-29T16:20:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-03-31T16:10:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-03-31T15:10:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Cinema\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false},{\"description\":\"7.30-9pm, £20, building // How did one extraordinary prince create Saudi Arabia?\\r\\nWhy were a million Armenians killed during WWI?\\r\\nHow did an elderly cleric overthrow the Shah and become ruler of Iran?\\r\\nWhy did the Arab Spring fail?\\r\\nCould Trump's peace deal lead to a new Middle East?\\r\\n\\r\\nWe are delighted to welcome back to JW3, international bestselling and multi-award-winning Simon Sebag-Montefiore for the launch of his essential and spellbinding new book, The Cauldron: The Making of the Modern Middle East, exploring all of these questions and more.\\r\\n\\r\\nSimon Sebag Montefiore's prize-winning books have been published in forty-eight languages. Jerusalem: The Biography – A History of the Middle East was a number one Sunday Times (UK) bestseller, a global bestseller and won The Book of the Year Prize from the Jewish Book Council (US) and the Wenjin Book Prize of the National Library of China (People’s Republic of China). In 2025, he was awarded the Blue Metropolis Words to Change Prize (Canada) for “his body of work in humanity and history.’  He read history at Gonville & Caius College, Cambridge University where he received his PhD. He is the presenter of five history series for the BBC and many of his books are being developed for movies or drama series.\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":90,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"The Cauldron: Making of the Modern Middle East\",\"instanceDates\":\"7 September-7 September\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"638601AQRBJJDLRTHRBDVLMTTCVTMSBMM\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-09-07T19:30:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-09-07T18:30:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-09-07T19:30:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-09-07T18:30:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false,\"attribute_Genre\":\"Talks & Discussions\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Adult Education\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"Simon Sebag-Montefiore\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"1916. As war rages on the Western Front, the Choral Society in Ramsden, Yorkshire has lost most of its men to the army. The Choral's ambitious committee, determined to press ahead, decides to recruit local young males to swell their ranks. They must also engage a new chorus master, and despite their suspicions that he has something to hide, their best bet seems to be Dr. Henry Guthrie (Ralph Fiennes) -- driven, uncompromising, and recently returned from a career in Germany. As conscription papers start to arrive, the whole community discovers that the best response to the chaos that is laying waste to their lives is to make music together. | Duration: 1h 53m, Rating: 12A | Films may be preceded by up to 20 minutes of advertisements and trailers. Specific timings will vary with each screening. We always recommend arriving on time. \",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":113,\"imageUrl\":\"https://system.spektrix.com/jw3/files/9f9474fa-3d48-4394-84bf-431143b6c60c.jpg\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"The Choral\",\"instanceDates\":\"9 February-16 February\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"https://system.spektrix.com/jw3/files/9f9474fa-3d48-4394-84bf-431143b6c60c-thumbnail.jpg\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"576201AQKGPDMQHSRHNHQCSCJTBVQLNJR\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-02-09T13:30:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-02-09T13:30:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-02-16T13:30:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-02-16T13:30:00Z\",\"altText\":\"The Choral\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Cinema\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false},{\"description\":\"What is the value of art? Does it reside in personal expression? Cultural longevity? Financial worth? These questions fuel Steven Soderbergh’s gloriously entertaining comedy. Julian Sklar (McKellen) was once a star of London’s 1960’s and 70’s pop art explosion, but he hasn’t painted in decades and has been broke for years. His two estranged children (James Corden, Jessica Gunning), desperate for an inheritance, hire Lori, an art restorer and former forger (Coel), to pose as a prospective assistant in order to access unfinished canvases Julian has buried deep in storage. A sharp and remarkable tale of creativity, legacy, and avarice. | Duration: 1h 40m, Rating: 15 Credits\\r\\nRating: 15\\r\\nGenre: Comedy, Drama\\r\\nDirector: Steven Soderbergh\\r\\nStars: Ian McKellen, Michaela Coel, Jessica Gunning https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=7CB2nsSBqs0&pp=ygUbdGhlIGNocmlzdG9waGVycyB1ayB0cmFpbGVy\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":100,\"imageUrl\":\"https://system.spektrix.com/jw3/files/4531327a-e28a-4c0c-864c-2deb7619620b.jpg\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"The Christophers\",\"instanceDates\":\"24 May-18 June\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"https://system.spektrix.com/jw3/files/4531327a-e28a-4c0c-864c-2deb7619620b-thumbnail.jpg\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"624801ALHDJMVGVBLCDLNKLRHPDMLQDMM\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-05-24T19:00:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-05-24T18:00:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-06-18T15:35:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-06-18T14:35:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Cinema\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false},{\"description\":\"A happily engaged couple is put to the test when an unexpected turn sends their wedding week off the rails. | Duration: 1h 45m, Rating: 15 Credits\\r\\nRating: 15\\r\\nGenre: Dark Comedy \\r\\nDirector: Kristoffer Borgli \\r\\nStars: Zendaya, Robert Pattinson, Alana Haim https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=6zmKcUa4Xxk&pp=ygUUdGhlIGRyYW1hIHVrIHRyYWlsZXI%3D\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":106,\"imageUrl\":\"https://system.spektrix.com/jw3/files/f83ea39c-1727-4ec2-af37-fc04f8839ce2.jpg\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"The Drama\",\"instanceDates\":\"5 May-27 May\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"https://system.spektrix.com/jw3/files/f83ea39c-1727-4ec2-af37-fc04f8839ce2-thumbnail.jpg\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"625001AGQCQTQGPSCKPJCPJPLBGNLLQDB\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-05-05T19:20:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-05-05T18:20:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-05-27T16:00:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-05-27T15:00:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Cinema\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false},{\"description\":\"11am-12noon, £20, hybrid, Wednesday 10 June 2026 // Why did King Edward take this radical step? Were there similar actions in other parts of Europe? Join Jill as she examines the expulsion in the light of the latest research and look at an individual who slipped through the net.\\r\\n\\r\\nJill Stern is an historian. She graduated with first class honours in History from King’s College London. Much of her working life was spent as a teacher at Wycombe Abbey School and as chairman of a Health Authority in West London and vice-chairman of North Thames Regional Health Authority. Returning to academic study she gained an MA (Distinction) and a doctorate in seventeenth century Dutch history at University College London. As a doctoral student she was awarded the prestigious Pollard Prize for History. She has a book and many published articles to her credit. She has lectured in Britain, the Netherlands and New York. History is her lifelong passion and she is keen to share that passion.\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":60,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"The Expulsion of the Jews from England 1290\",\"instanceDates\":\"10 June-10 June\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"593201ABVPRMTSPGRMKGKTLMNKTVQKPCT\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-06-10T11:00:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-06-10T10:00:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-06-10T11:00:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-06-10T10:00:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Talks & Discussions\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Adult Education\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"Jill Stern\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false},{\"description\":\"2-3.30pm, hybrid, £20 // 20th Century Fox had many blonde musical stars (from the 1930’s to the 1960’s) including Shirley Temple, Marilyn Monroe and Alice Faye - let’s chart their course with clips from such films as Rebecca of Sunnybrook Farm, Gentlemen Prefer Blondes and Alexander’s Ragtime Band. \\r\\n\\r\\nGeorge McGhee has over 35 years of experience, latterly at the BBC, where he oversaw all feature films and international TV series acquisitions. \\r\\n\\r\\nBrochure copy:  \\r\\n\\r\\n20th Century Fox had many blonde musical stars ( from the 1930’s to the 1960’s) including Shirley Temple, Marilyn Monroe and Alice Faye - let’s chart their course with clips from such films as Rebecca of Sunnybrook Farm , Gentlemen Prefer Blondes and Alexander’s Ragtime Band . \",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":90,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"The Fox Blondes\",\"instanceDates\":\"1 September-1 September\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"636202ARKVSVDSVKHTBRQBNVBQNCPQBPQ\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-09-01T14:00:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-09-01T13:00:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-09-01T14:00:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-09-01T13:00:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false,\"attribute_Genre\":\"Talks & Discussions\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Adult Education\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"George McGhee\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"7.15pm-8.45pm, £20 (price TBC with book), hybrid, Thursday 28 May 2026 // We are delighted to welcome back to JW3, Aziz Abu Sarah and Maoz Inon as they launch their long awaited book: The Future Is Peace: A Shared Journey Across the Holy Land\\r\\n\\r\\nTwo lifelong peace activists and guides to Israel/Palestine, both of whom have lost family in the conflict, take readers on a revealing life-changing journey across this holy, bloodstained land and discover the mythic, political, and personal history that divides but also binds them and their peoples.\\r\\n\\r\\n“We do not see ourselves as Palestinians and Israelis, or as Jews and Arabs, but as human beings who believe in fostering a culture of dialogue, a culture of forgiveness, and a culture of peace. To those who see only division lines, we say: If you must divide us, let it be as those who believe in peace and equality and those who don’t … yet.”\\r\\n\\r\\nPalestinian Aziz Abu Sarah and Israeli Maoz Inon forged a bond of brotherhood when the world expected them to be enemies. Both have lost family to the conflict. Both have known the bitterness of righteous anger. Yet, they chose a different path.\\r\\n\\r\\nIn The Future Is Peace, Sarah and Inon take readers on a transformative weeklong journey across a sacred and bloodstained land. Facing competing narratives, they explore how compassion and unity can pull humanity back from the precipice of blind hatred. Throughout their travels, they have been constantly asked: In the face of so much loss, how can we ever find hope? Their answer is always the same. One cannot find hope. We must create it.\\r\\n\\r\\nThis book is a rebuttal to a broken world and a bold challenge to the belief that more violence can ever bring security. Told with unflinching honesty, their story is proof that peace is not a naive dream, but a courageous choice—for reconciliation to heal the wounds of revenge, for partnerships to change a destiny of war, and for empathy to save us from drowning in sorrow.\\r\\n\\r\\nPairing unapologetic candor and inspirational prose, Aziz and Maoz are sending an urgent message that the people have the power to make change. Peace is inevitable. For Palestinians, for Israelis, and for the world that awaits their example, it is not just possible—it is the future.\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":90,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"The Future Is Peace: A Shared Journey Across the Holy Land\",\"instanceDates\":\"28 May-28 May\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"595001ALCCTNRSJMMDLPKSPLLDNHQHJBR\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-05-28T19:15:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-05-28T18:15:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-05-28T19:15:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-05-28T18:15:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Talks & Discussions\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Adult Education\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"Aziz Abu Sarah and Maoz Inon\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false},{\"description\":\"3-4pm, building, £7, ages 6-11 //A new play inspired by the bestselling novel by Edmondo De Amicis. \\r\\n\\r\\nMarco sets out on the journey of his life in search of his beloved mother. \\r\\nInside a small travelling theatre, a father and daughter bring to life the story of Marco — a brave boy who crosses continents, faces storms at sea, rides horses, and battles the forces of nature and countless challenges. Yet even in the hardest moments, Marco never gives up — driven by love and the hope of being reunited with his mother. \\r\\n\\r\\nA play filled with humour, adventure, touching moments, and endless inspiration — reminding us that even in the most difficult times, family is the heart that gives us the strength to keep going. \",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":60,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"The Heart\",\"instanceDates\":\"1 February-1 February\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"567802ALSNHSGKKQKPRNCMVSBLRSMPHBQ\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-02-01T15:00:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-02-01T15:00:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-02-01T15:00:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-02-01T15:00:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Families & Youth\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Festival of Spoken Ivrit\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false},{\"description\":\"Two young music students, Lionel and David, attending the Boston Conservatory in 1917, bond over their shared love of folk music. They reconnect a few years later, embarking on a song collecting trip in the backwaters of Maine. | Duration: 1h 2m, Rating: 15 | Films may be preceded by up to 20 minutes of advertisements and trailers. Specific timings will vary with each screening. We always recommend arriving on time.\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":128,\"imageUrl\":\"https://system.spektrix.com/jw3/files/e86230a5-557a-4339-8863-cce6829791e8.jpg\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"The History of Sound\",\"instanceDates\":\"8 February-12 February\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"https://system.spektrix.com/jw3/files/e86230a5-557a-4339-8863-cce6829791e8-thumbnail.jpg\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"588801AKVBMNMJGJMNKDVMBRNKSNDPRGN\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-02-08T16:10:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-02-08T16:10:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-02-12T20:00:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-02-12T20:00:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Cinema\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false},{\"description\":\"Trying to escape her past, Millie accepts a job as a live-in housemaid for the wealthy Nina and Andrew Winchester. But what begins as a dream job quickly unravels into something far more dangerous—a sexy, seductive game of secrets, scandal, and power. | Duration: 2h 11m, Rating: 15\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":131,\"imageUrl\":\"https://system.spektrix.com/jw3/files/922f68ea-d65a-42b5-b27e-0a6251a32152.jpg\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"The Housemaid\",\"instanceDates\":\"12 January-15 January\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"https://system.spektrix.com/jw3/files/922f68ea-d65a-42b5-b27e-0a6251a32152-thumbnail.jpg\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"581001ATPHRLKHHQVVLNMPSMNGPLHVTDM\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-01-12T18:50:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-01-12T18:50:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-01-15T14:20:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-01-15T14:20:00Z\",\"altText\":\"The Housemaid\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Cinema\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false},{\"description\":\"Joe and Angela's marriage is on thin ice. When they invite their enigmatic upstairs neighbors for a dinner party, the night spirals into unexpected places. Have they reignited the spark or lit the match that burns it all down? Duration: 107 minutes Rating: 15 Director: Olivia Wilde Cast: Seth Rogan, Olivia Wilde, Edward Norton, Penélope Cruz Year: 2026 https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=7YIHRhRMn94&pp=ygUVdGhlIGludml0ZSB1ayB0cmFpbGVy\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":107,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"The Invite\",\"instanceDates\":\"17 July-28 July\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"642601AQHGDGHLMRBLDJLRSSMSVDJPLBL\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-07-17T10:30:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-07-17T09:30:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-07-28T11:00:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-07-28T10:00:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false,\"attribute_Genre\":\"Cinema\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"Jess Robin dreams of a career in popular music, but his father, Cantor Rabinovitch, forbids it, insisting Jess live as a traditional Jew and inherit his position at the synagogue. With the help of friend and professional musician Bubba, Jess gets a chance to go to Los Angeles and have famous singer Keith Lennox record one of his songs. Defying both his father and his wife, Jess leaves New York to pursue his dreams. | Duration: 1h 55m, Rating: PG \",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":115,\"imageUrl\":\"https://system.spektrix.com/jw3/files/b632a514-d701-43c9-badd-32a0b97d8c78.jpg\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"The Jazz Singer\",\"instanceDates\":\"26 January-29 January\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"https://system.spektrix.com/jw3/files/b632a514-d701-43c9-badd-32a0b97d8c78-thumbnail.jpg\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"582201ARCRLLVVGCHRPDRPQHNMPTDBVQG\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-01-26T16:00:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-01-26T16:00:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-01-29T14:20:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-01-29T14:20:00Z\",\"altText\":\"The Jazz Singer\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Cinema\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false},{\"description\":\"7.30-9pm, £20, building // Join us for an evening celebrating The Jewish Bakery, the first cookbook from Rinkoff Bakery, a family-run Jewish bakery in London's East End. More than a century in the making, this comprehensive collection brings together recipes inspired by over 100 years and five generations of family baking. Filled with tried-and-tested favourites, the book brings the warmth and joy of the bakery into your own kitchen.\\r\\nIn conversation with Adrienne Katz Kennedy, sisters Jennifer Rinkoff and Debs Rinkoff will discuss the history of the bakery, memories of the old Jewish East End, and the family traditions that have shaped their baking legacy. There may even be an opportunity to sample some delicious treats featured in the book.\\r\\nThe Jewish Bakery celebrates recipes with deep roots, passing on the passion, expertise and experience of a bakery that has served generations of Londoners. From traditional Jewish favourites to beloved family recipes, it offers a unique insight into one of East London's enduring culinary institutions.\\r\\nCopies of the book will be available for purchase on the night, with an opportunity to have them signed by the authors.\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":90,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"The Jewish Bakery: A Century of Rinkoff's\",\"instanceDates\":\"10 September-10 September\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"638402ASLPJKCJPBGCBDCRRRCNGVDVGLL\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-09-10T19:30:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-09-10T18:30:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-09-10T19:30:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-09-10T18:30:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false,\"attribute_Genre\":\"Talks & Discussions\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Adult Education\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"Jennifer Rinkoff\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"7.30-8.45pm, hybrid, £12 // Join Dr Shelley Braude, Jewish Life Coordinator at Clifton College, as she explores the remarkable Jewish history of this pioneering school. Clifton College was the first private school in the UK to admit Jewish students, and in 1878 it established a dedicated Jewish boarding house. Although the boarding house has shut down, the school continues to run a Jewish Life Program and to this day, it remains the only non-Jewish school in the country with its own synagogue on site – complete with an ark and Torah scrolls.\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":75,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"The Jewish History of Clifton College\",\"instanceDates\":\"5 March-5 March\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"560001AVDJPPDLLTSBVDVDBNJDSJBDGJB\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-03-05T19:30:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-03-05T19:30:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-03-05T19:30:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-03-05T19:30:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Talks & Discussions\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Adult Education\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"Dr Shelley Braude\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false},{\"description\":\"Walking tour, 10.30am-12.45pm, £20 // This fascinating tour features the bustling districts of Soho and Fitzrovia which are renowned today as two of the city's most fashionable areas and the centre for entertainment and shopping. But they are also steeped in an enthralling hidden history of a vast Jewish community that once lived there: \\r\\n\\r\\nLearn of the abject poverty that existed in the West End among Jews living just a stone’s throw from the luxury homes of the ultra rich \\r\\n\\r\\nMeet Jewish personalities from the past including the billionaire’s daughter who devoted her life to creating happiness among working class girls; the tailor with 10 daughters who turned to running a pub; the London boy who won the highest civilian gallantry medal during the Second World War; and the Hebrew school pupils studying alongside (and making friends with) Soho’s red light ladies of the streets \\r\\n\\r\\nHear how bitter rivalries split Synagogue congregations and led to a new Jewish religious movement. \\r\\n\\r\\nStroll along famous Berwick Street, Dean Street and Frith Street with plentiful sights of Jewish interest and wonderful stories such as the comical antics of market traders, a kosher restaurant where the most enthusiastic clientele were Hollywood stars; the state school that was Jewish in all but name; and where the Great Tailors’ Strike began 100 years ago involving thousands of Jewish workers. Learn also why a tiny synagogue boasted an astonishing 1,000 congregants \\r\\n\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":135,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"The Jewish West End and its Remarkable Hidden History\",\"instanceDates\":\"23 September-23 September\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"635401AVLSGQKHVQNBHLVCMKSQVHPGDQH\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-09-23T10:30:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-09-23T09:30:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-09-23T10:30:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-09-23T09:30:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false,\"attribute_Genre\":\"Walks\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Walking Tours\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"2-3.30pm, £20, building // Experience Florence as you’ve never seen it before - through the rich, complex and often overlooked history of its Jewish community.  \\r\\n\\r\\n \\r\\n\\r\\nThis talk explores Jewish life in Florence and other Tuscan cities from medieval times to the present, revealing periods of coexistence and flourishing alongside persecution, libels and resilience.  \\r\\n\\r\\n \\r\\n\\r\\nSet against the splendour of Renaissance Florence, discover how deeply embedded Jews were in the city’s cultural and economic success. From the Medici court, where Cosimo the Elder and Lorenzo the Magnificent studied Hebrew with eminent Rabbonim, to scholars, scribes and artists whose work shaped one of history’s most extraordinary periods of creativity.  \\r\\n\\r\\n \\r\\n\\r\\nTracing the community through emancipation under Napoleon, the struggle for Italian independence, and the devastation of Fascism and Nazism, explore how political change reshaped both Jewish lives and the city itself - culminating in the transformation of the ghetto site into today’s Piazza della Repubblica.  \\r\\n\\r\\n \\r\\n\\r\\nEnding with the Florentine Jewish community today, this talk offers a moving portrait of continuity, survival and renewal in a city celebrated for its art and culture. \",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":90,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"The Jews of Florence & Tuscany\",\"instanceDates\":\"17 November-17 November\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"637801ADLCNPQBBLRTMQCKTHBDPCJLCBC\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-11-17T14:00:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-11-17T14:00:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-11-17T14:00:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-11-17T14:00:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false,\"attribute_Genre\":\"Talks & Discussions\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Adult Education\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"Deborah Jay\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"7.30-9.30pm, building, £20 // THE JEWS OF SYRIA (1930-1967) tells the dramatic story of how the Syrian Jewish community in Aleppo and Damascus (along with other Jews in Arab lands) experienced harsh treatment and violence, and were forbidden to travel or emigrate following the partition of Palestine in 1947. Along the way, we learn about the Aleppo Codex, the Great Synagogue of Aleppo, the riots against the Jews, efforts to escape, Rabbi Kalmanowitz and the Jews of Egypt, and Eli Cohen, the renowned Israeli spy.\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":120,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"The Jews of Syria (1930-1967): Screening\",\"instanceDates\":\"27 January-27 January\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"558001APHLPVBHPQQQJKSRTLMBNHBBGVN\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-01-27T19:30:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-01-27T19:30:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-01-27T19:30:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-01-27T19:30:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Talks & Discussions\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Adult Education\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false},{\"description\":\"Surviving bar-to-bar on anecdotes and the ‘good old days’, two blustery 50-somethings hatch a plan to change their luck by digging up the cash their old pal buried before he left for Argentina. En route to the airport, they come across a shy architecture student whose view of life will transform as they take him under their wing on a road trip across the Venetian plains. Duration: 100 minutes Rating: 15 Director: Francesco Sossai Cast: Filippo Scotti, Sergio Romano, Pierpaolo Capovilla Year: 2025 Language: Italian Subtitles: English https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=970EvAbQ3qI\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":101,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"The Last One for the Road\",\"instanceDates\":\"31 July-31 July\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"640802AHRLGHVNCHBHTPDGMLQHVRSPTCL\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-07-31T15:00:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-07-31T14:00:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-07-31T15:00:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-07-31T14:00:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false,\"attribute_Genre\":\"Cinema\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"The riveting biography of 102-year-old CIA spymaster Peter Sichel who passed away earlier this year, revealing for the first time the epic and unvarnished history of the US foreign intelligence service from the inside. With a good dose of wit and humor to boot, Sichel unpacks the obscured roots of conflicts that plague today's world and the toll espionage took on his personal life. | Duration: 1h 31m, Rating: 15 Credits\\r\\nRating: 15\\r\\nGenre: Documentary\\r\\nDirector: Katharina Otto-Bernstein\\r\\nStars: Scott Anderson, Erick Arbenz, Carl Bernstein https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=IYB2lKY4yQY&pp=ygUXdGhlIGxhc3Qgc3B5IFVLIHRyYWlsZXI%3D\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":106,\"imageUrl\":\"https://system.spektrix.com/jw3/files/0e9e18d7-f038-4ce3-aea0-cb3afce28355.jpg\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"The Last Spy\",\"instanceDates\":\"26 April-4 June\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"https://system.spektrix.com/jw3/files/0e9e18d7-f038-4ce3-aea0-cb3afce28355-thumbnail.jpg\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"615801AGJDNNSVHQQDHCQTSSMKNDBPDTP\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-04-26T17:00:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-04-26T16:00:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-06-04T16:15:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-06-04T15:15:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Cinema\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false},{\"description\":\"2-3.30pm, building, £20 // Join Sir Peter Thornton, the first Chief Coroner of England and Wales and the author of The Later Years, alongside Jonathan Levy, a former Old Bailey judge and Chartered Accountant, for a practical and reassuring talk about how to get your affairs in order.  \\r\\n\\r\\nTogether, they will guide you through the essential steps for putting plans in place, from organising a will and a Lasting Power of Attorney to pensions, care options, inheritance planning and how to reduce stress for your loved ones.  \\r\\n\\r\\nWhether you’re planning ahead for yourself or supporting family members, you’ll leave with practical checklists, straightforward advice and the peace of mind that comes from knowing what needs to be done, and how to do it.  \",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":90,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"The Later Years\",\"instanceDates\":\"20 October-20 October\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"635802ACTNLRVLRCPMCRPKKPTLJGSBHSK\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-10-20T14:00:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-10-20T13:00:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-10-20T14:00:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-10-20T13:00:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false,\"attribute_Genre\":\"Talks & Discussions\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Adult Education\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"Jonathan Levy and Peter Thornton\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"7pm - 8.30pm, £20, in building // While widely known in Germany, the Royal Academy’s ‘Making Modernism’ exhibition in 2022 presented a rare opportunity to see a brilliant but small display of Paula Modersohn-Becker’s work.  \\r\\n \\r\\n\\r\\nThis talk will put into context how in the early 1900’s Modersohn-Becker created an approach to painting in less than a decade that was original to her time that defies category.  With themes focusing the landscape, portraiture, adolescence, self portraits, and motherhood. The vibrant work predates ‘German Expressionism,’ leaving contemporary trends of her time in the dust like the Worpswede Artist Colony.   \\r\\n \\r\\n\\r\\nHer work still resonates with a visceral energy to viewers today.  \",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":90,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"The Life and Art of Paula Modersohn-Becker\",\"instanceDates\":\"29 September-29 September\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"651801ACDTSGRGQDGJVHHVQHMHSRRPDTC\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-09-29T19:00:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-09-29T18:00:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-09-29T19:00:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-09-29T18:00:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false,\"attribute_Genre\":\"Talks & Discussions\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"Michael Ajerman\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"Mondays, 11am-12:15pm, hybrid, £20 per session or £198 for 11 weeks //\\r\\n\\r\\n Tracking events amongst the shifting sands of the Middle East over two decades, this course seeks to unravel and explain some of the moving alliances, and new leaderships happening across the region. Placing everything into a wider global context of international engagements and distractions this course looks at 20 years of Middle Eastern history to help to understand some of the key political events of the world today.  \\r\\n\\r\\nPaula Kitching is an historian and writer. Paula is a regular contributor to the Historian magazine of the Historical Association, and has written articles for commemorative publications for the Royal British Legion and the MOD.\\r\\n\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":75,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"The Making of the Modern Middle East 1959 to 1979 [In-Building]\",\"instanceDates\":\"5 January-23 March\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"558602ANBBVLTSSGBVDLNKQRBJCRNVKJG\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-01-05T11:00:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-01-05T11:00:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-03-23T11:00:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-03-23T11:00:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Classes & Courses\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"History & Politics Courses\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"Paula Kitching\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false},{\"description\":\"Mondays, 11am-12:15pm, hybrid, £20 per session or £198 for 11 weeks // Tracking events amongst the shifting sands of the Middle East over two decades, this course seeks to unravel and explain some of the moving alliances, and new leaderships happening across the region. Placing everything into a wider global context of international engagements and distractions this course looks at 20 years of Middle Eastern history to help to understand some of the key political events of the world today.   Paula Kitching is an historian and writer. Paula is a regular contributor to the Historian magazine of the Historical Association, and has written articles for commemorative publications for the Royal British Legion and the MOD.\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":75,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"The Making of the Modern Middle East 1959 to 1979 [Online]\",\"instanceDates\":\"5 January-23 March\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"558601AKBGDCTKVLRGKLHKVBSKDHHRSNQ\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-01-05T11:00:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-01-05T11:00:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-03-23T11:00:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-03-23T11:00:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Classes & Courses\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"True\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"History & Politics Courses\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"Paula Kitching\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false},{\"description\":\"Mondays, 11am-12.15pm, £180 for the 10-week course, in building section // Tracking events amongst the shifting sands of the Middle East over two decades, this course seeks to unravel and explain some of the moving alliances, and new leaderships happening across the region.  \\r\\n\\r\\nPaula will explore how the region developed during this period, the rise of the Arab nationalism and the divisions and territorial ambitions. \\r\\n\\r\\nPlacing everything into a wider global context of international engagements and distractions this course looks at 20 years of Middle Eastern history to help to understand some of the key political events of the world today.    \\r\\n\\r\\nPaula Kitching is an historian and writer. Paula is a regular contributor to the Historian magazine of the Historical Association and has written articles for commemorative publications for the Royal British Legion and the MOD.  \",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":75,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"The Making of the Modern Middle East: 1960-80 [In Building]\",\"instanceDates\":\"5 October-14 December\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"643001ANQTTJQGTDJLHHLVDRMCVBMQKBT\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-10-05T11:00:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-10-05T10:00:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-12-14T11:00:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-12-14T11:00:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false,\"attribute_Genre\":\"Classes & Courses\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"True\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"Paula Kitching\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"Mondays, 11am-12.15pm, £180 for the 10-week course, online section // Tracking events amongst the shifting sands of the Middle East over two decades, this course seeks to unravel and explain some of the moving alliances, and new leaderships happening across the region. Paula will explore how the region developed during this period, the rise of the Arab nationalism and the divisions and territorial ambitions. Placing everything into a wider global context of international engagements and distractions this course looks at 20 years of Middle Eastern history to help to understand some of the key political events of the world today. Paula Kitching is an historian and writer. Paula is a regular contributor to the Historian magazine of the Historical Association and has written articles for commemorative publications for the Royal British Legion and the MOD.\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":75,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"The Making of the Modern Middle East: 1960-80 [Online]\",\"instanceDates\":\"5 October-5 October\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"643201APHTDNDQBQNSSPCNCJMCCJKSLSQ\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-10-05T11:00:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-10-05T10:00:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-10-05T11:00:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-10-05T10:00:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false,\"attribute_Genre\":\"Classes & Courses\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"True\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"Paula Kitching\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"7pm-9pm, £16 in building, £10 online, hybrid // Over the past three years, Ciara Shalome has been collecting oral testimonies pertaining to the multi-faceted lived experiences of Mizrahi Jews - aiming to spotlight these underrepresented voices and stories via social media.   \\r\\n Today, with over 100,000 followers on Instagram, Ciara has played a vital role in ensuring that the testimonies of Jewish people from the Middle East and North Africa are uplifted and remembered for generations to come.   \\r\\n\\r\\nDuring ‘The Mizrahi Story Live’, a few of the most compelling voices from Ciara’s platform , across two generations, will come together for a live, intimate interview. Seated around a communal table, they will share personal stories, memories, traditions, and the challenges they’ve faced.   \\r\\n\\r\\nBefore the event begins, guests are invited to explore a vibrant lively Shuk featuring community-made art, crafts, and speciality vegan Kubbeh tasting by Mazal.\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":120,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"The Mizrahi Story: Live [In Building]\",\"instanceDates\":\"29 January-29 January\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"574201ASQRMSLVKLMQHDNMJTCPGKMSJCG\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-01-29T19:00:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-01-29T19:00:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-01-29T19:00:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-01-29T19:00:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Arts & Culture\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false},{\"description\":\"7pm-9pm, £10 online, £16 in building, hybrid // After soaring past the 100,000 follower mark, The Mizrahi Story - the premier digital platform dedicated to bringing underrepresented Mizrahi narratives to a worldwide audience - is hosting its first-ever In Real Life (IRL) event!\\r\\nExperience an evening that engages all your senses through live, intimate interviews. Meet Mizrahi Jews featured on the MizrahiStory page, including Niran Basson from Iraq and Lisette Stalbow from Egypt, along with other intergenerational Mizrahi voices speak candidly with The Mizrahi Story Founder, Ciara Shalome.\\r\\nTo complete this cultural celebration, the event will also feature:\\r\\nShuk-Style Market Stalls selling unique Mizrahi crafts and items.\\r\\n(Darbuka Roll!) A special Kubbeh tasting session prepared by the legendary MAZAL!\\r\\nYes, this entire experience is included in your ticket price!\\r\\n🌐 Can't Make It in Person?\\r\\nFor dedicated followers across the pond or in the Arab Peninsula, you can still join the conversation! Purchase an online streaming ticket to tune in live (we apologize, but the Kubbeh tasting is reserved for our in-person guests).\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":120,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"The Mizrahi Story: Live [Online]\",\"instanceDates\":\"29 January-29 January\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"579401ANCQNDNBVTGKLJSLPNPMCGBSKLQ\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-01-29T19:00:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-01-29T19:00:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-01-29T19:00:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-01-29T19:00:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Arts & Culture\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false},{\"description\":\"7.15pm-8.30pm, £20, in building, Wednesday 29 April 2026 // The Second Commandment forbids creating and worshipping “graven images” or likenesses of the Divine. \\r\\n\\r\\nThis prohibition has inspired modern Jewish artists to imagine a new visual language, to reach beyond representation and provoke the deepest questions of human existence. \\r\\n\\r\\nOften drawing from Jewish folklore and personal history, Marc Chagall, Amedeo Modigliani, and Chaim Soutine depicted floating figures, and distorted perspectives to express a sense of identity and memory.\\r\\n\\r\\nMark Rothko, Barnett Newman, Lee Krasner, and Louise Nevelson, explored vast colour fields, powerful gestures and abstract forms to create immersive experiences that evoke spirituality, and the sublime.\\r\\n\\r\\nThis talk will examine how the emigrant experience and Talmudic influences have played significant roles to probe the limits of our visual experience, and transform our expectations of art.\\r\\n\\r\\nSophie is an art historian, writer, and lecturer, with a special interest in visual culture and architecture. She has worked with leading institutions in the culture and heritage sectors across Europe and brings a rich, interdisciplinary perspective to her talks.\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":75,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"The Modern Tapestry of Jewish Abstraction\",\"instanceDates\":\"29 April-29 April\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"594401ADJBGLJKJQSLHMCCPVHJHVDRLBH\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-04-29T19:15:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-04-29T18:15:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-04-29T19:15:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-04-29T18:15:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Talks & Discussions\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Adult Education\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"Sophie Lachowsky\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false},{\"description\":\"7pm-8.15pm, £15, in building, ages 13+ // Join Natalie Livingstone as she discusses her new book, a landmark history revealing the untold female legacy of the Nuremberg Trials.\\r\\n\\r\\nMarking 80 years since the Nuremberg Trials, The Nuremberg Women offers a powerful new perspective on postwar justice. Drawing on overlooked and international sources, Natalie Livingstone tells the story of eight women whose work, as lawyers, journalists, interpreters, artists and witnesses, helped shape the trials.\\r\\n\\r\\nWhile Nuremberg is often remembered through its leading men, this landmark history brings into focus the women who prepared cases, documented proceedings and gave testimony that revealed the reality of Nazi crimes. Their stories illuminate the trials as complex, contested and profoundly human.\\r\\n\\r\\nThe event will be followed by a reception with light refreshments and a book signing. \\r\\n\\r\\nNatalie Livingstone is a Sunday Times bestselling historian and journalist, and the author of The Mistresses of Cliveden and The Women of Rothschild. A graduate of Christ’s College, Cambridge, she is also the founder and chairman of the Cliveden Literary Festival.\\r\\n\\r\\nNatalie will be in conversation with Kate Weinberg. Kate studied English at Oxford and creative writing in East Anglia. She has worked as a slush pile reader, a bookshop assistant, a journalist and a ghost writer. She is the author of The Truants and There’s Nothing Wrong With Her.\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":75,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"The Nuremberg Women: The Trials that Brought the Nazis to Justice\",\"instanceDates\":\"5 May-5 May\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"605001ACGKKRDSRVLBJDSMNRHHTKTPLRP\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-05-05T19:00:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-05-05T18:00:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-05-05T19:00:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-05-05T18:00:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Talks & Discussions\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Holocaust Learning\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"Natalie Livingstone\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false},{\"description\":\"Drummer Ollie Usiskin celebrates three decades of jazz, returning to his roots with a quartet blending Klezmer’s soulful energy and classic jazz sophistication. Sit back and enjoy reimagined standards, vibrant Klezmer gems, and high-energy improvisation in this musical homecoming.\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":120,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"The Ollie Usiskin Quartet \",\"instanceDates\":\"1 July-1 July\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"613601ARPQBHCNPSVNRPRJCJRVGNGJQSQ\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-07-01T19:30:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-07-01T18:30:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-07-01T19:30:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-07-01T18:30:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Music\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Arts & Culture\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false},{\"description\":\"While people across 1990's Iraq struggle to survive, 9-year old Lamia has been selected to prepare a cake to celebrate the President's birthday. In a landscape of fear and scarcity, where basic ingredients are nearly impossible to find, Lamia sets out on a determined journey throughout the big city in search of eggs, flour, and sugar. Accompanied by her grandmother, her loyal friend Saeed, and her pet rooster Hindi, she navigates vendors and police officers along the way. | This film is in Arabic with English subtitles | Duration: 1h 45m, Rating: 12A\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":105,\"imageUrl\":\"https://system.spektrix.com/jw3/files/9cf1715a-9b56-46ee-87cc-95ca577a5002.jpg\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"The President's Cake\",\"instanceDates\":\"8 March-19 March\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"https://system.spektrix.com/jw3/files/9cf1715a-9b56-46ee-87cc-95ca577a5002-thumbnail.jpg\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"606601AMHMMRNJQCVDKCTDGSRKCLTQDTD\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-03-08T12:20:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-03-08T12:20:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-03-19T11:00:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-03-19T11:00:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Cinema\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false},{\"description\":\"7-8.15pm, £15, building, age 13+ //   Author Catherine Ostler joins journalist Natalie Livingstone to discuss The Renoir Girls, an astonishing true story of splendour, scandal and tragedy in Golden Age Paris.  In 1881, Pierre-Auguste Renoir painted two young sisters from the Jewish banking dynasty Cahen d’Anvers at their home in Paris’s grand 8th arrondissement. The resulting portrait, Pink and Blue, captures Elisabeth and Alice Cahen d’Anvers in a fleeting moment of innocence and beauty, and remains one of Renoir’s most celebrated works.  The painting evokes the glamour of the Belle Époque: days at the races, nights at the opera, sun-soaked châteaux and brilliant salons filled with art, music and conversation. But beneath the glittering surface lay a growing current of resentment. The same society illuminated by progress and culture was also shadowed by division, prejudice and rising antisemitism.  Drawing on letters, diaries and exclusive new research, Ostler uncovers the intimate lives behind the portrait and the family secrets hidden within it. From the aftermath of the Franco-Prussian War to the Dreyfus Affair and the devastation of two world wars, The Renoir Girls tells a powerful story of love, courage and identity in conflict with the forces of history.  Chosen by The Times as a book to look out for in 2026, this event offers a vivid journey into a dazzling world on the edge of rupture.\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":75,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"The Renoir Girls\",\"instanceDates\":\"9 September-9 September\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"638801AVDBKMHKKRQRBBSPVVLVSQVQMBP\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-09-09T19:00:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-09-09T18:00:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-09-09T19:00:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-09-09T18:00:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false,\"attribute_Genre\":\"Talks & Discussions\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Holocaust Learning\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"Natalie Livingstone, Catherine Ostler\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"7.30-9.30pm, £20, building // Following our sell-out screening of No 6 in the film series on the Syrian Jewish Community, JW3 and HARIF are proud to present the final part in the series, the  Rescue of the Jews of Syria (90 minutes).\\r\\nThis documentary describes the harsh and restrictive life of the Jews who were still trapped in Syria in the 1970s, the international human rights response to their plight  and how the Sephardi community in Brooklyn came together to free the remaining few thousand Jews, leading to their release in the 1990s.\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":120,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"The Rescue of the Jews of Syria (1970-1994)\",\"instanceDates\":\"8 December-8 December\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"651401ANGGTLTVPMQTCVDTCDTRCJHGDVL\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-12-08T19:30:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-12-08T19:30:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-12-08T19:30:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-12-08T19:30:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false,\"attribute_Genre\":\"Talks & Discussions\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Adult Education\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"Celebrate Purim with this cult classic! Sweethearts Brad and Janet, stuck with a flat tire during a storm, discover the eerie mansion of the charismatic scientist, Dr. Frank-N-Furter. As their innocence is lost, Brad and Janet meet a houseful of wild characters, including a rocking biker and a creepy butler. Through elaborate dances and rock songs, Frank-N-Furter unveils his latest creation: a muscular man named \\\"Rocky.\\\" | Duration: 1h 40m, Rating: 12A Credits\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":100,\"imageUrl\":\"https://system.spektrix.com/jw3/files/04d55418-a0e8-408e-be9a-6011c8e52923.jpg\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"The Rocky Horror Picture Show\",\"instanceDates\":\"5 March-8 March\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"https://system.spektrix.com/jw3/files/04d55418-a0e8-408e-be9a-6011c8e52923-thumbnail.jpg\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"606201ARVBQPVVTRQLHDLBNPKJVQVMMDQ\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-03-05T20:00:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-03-05T20:00:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-03-08T20:30:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-03-08T20:30:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Cinema\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false},{\"description\":\"7pm-8.15pm, £12.5, in building, Tuesday 9 June 2026 // The Sassoon story begins in the 19th century. Born in Baghdad, the extraordinary entrepreneur David Sassoon made his fortune in India and set up satelllite businesses all over the Far East. But his descendants   craved acceptance in British society. Edward and his son Philip Sassoon became MPs, Siegfried Sassoon a famous poet. Hannah Gubbay was a socialite and influential collector and Rachel Beer became the first female editor of the Observer and the Sunday Times. Today, only one branch of the family remains Jewish: the descendants of Flora Sassoon and her son, David Solomon Sassoon, whose famous Judaica library was housed at his hoime  in Letchworth .\\r\\n\\r\\nIn this Harif lecture for Jewish Culture Month, Lyn Julius will describe some of these colourful characters and consider their legacy.\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":75,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"The Sassoons: from Baghdad to Britain\",\"instanceDates\":\"9 June-9 June\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"592201AQBTTMMLTDHPLNLQNMKLLLJHCKJ\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-06-09T19:00:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-06-09T18:00:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-06-09T19:00:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-06-09T18:00:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Talks & Discussions\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Adult Education\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"Lyn Julius\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false},{\"description\":\"\\\"19:00 // 29 Sep 2026 // £15 // A staged reading inspired by the life, work and silencing of Moyshe Kulbak, the Belarusian-Jewish Yiddish writer, poet and dramatist who was executed during Stalin’s Great Purge in 1937.\\r\\n\\r\\nRead in Russian with English subtitles. Poetry performed in Yiddish.\\\"\\r\\n\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":90,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"The Scattering Ravens\",\"instanceDates\":\"29 September-29 September\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"633201AMPDLJJVGRPJNGMJHMPQCLGLSMD\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-09-29T19:00:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-09-29T18:00:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-09-29T19:00:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-09-29T18:00:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false,\"attribute_Genre\":\"Performance\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"Twelve-year-old Khaled has lived his entire life just miles from the Mediterranean, yet he has never seen the sea. When Israeli authorities deny him entry at a border checkpoint, his disappointment turns into a dangerous resolve. Determined to reach the water, Khaled sneaks across the border alone, embarking on a high-stakes journey through a landscape where he is considered a trespasser.\\r\\nAs Khaled chases the horizon, his father, Ribhi, desperately tries to trace his path. Driven by a father's love, Ribhi risks his job and his own freedom to find his son before the authorities do. The Sea is a gripping, poignant drama about the boundaries that divide us and a child’s simple, powerful dream to reach the shore. | This film is in Arabic and Hebrew with English subtitles. | Duration: 1h 33m\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":93,\"imageUrl\":\"https://system.spektrix.com/jw3/files/4ed9d8bd-751d-4367-bade-b1e8068e3896.jpg\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"The Sea\",\"instanceDates\":\"10 May-10 May\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"https://system.spektrix.com/jw3/files/4ed9d8bd-751d-4367-bade-b1e8068e3896-thumbnail.jpg\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"618601ANDLJNMCSQTPTSKBHHBMDSRKDHC\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-05-10T19:30:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-05-10T18:30:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-05-10T19:30:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-05-10T18:30:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Cinema\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Seret Film Festival\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false},{\"description\":\"Marcelo, a technology expert in his early 40s, is on the run. Hoping to reunite with his son, he travels to Recife during Carnival but soon realizes that the city is not the safe haven he was expecting. | Duration: 2h 41m, Rating: 15\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":161,\"imageUrl\":\"https://system.spektrix.com/jw3/files/aafa663b-20d6-4476-b491-3f1fe751238f.jpg\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"The Secret Agent\",\"instanceDates\":\"15 March-19 March\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"https://system.spektrix.com/jw3/files/aafa663b-20d6-4476-b491-3f1fe751238f-thumbnail.jpg\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"606801ASLPRBTGHSLMTMRMDLRKDLNRJJD\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-03-15T18:30:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-03-15T18:30:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-03-19T14:30:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-03-19T14:30:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Cinema\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false},{\"description\":\"Set high in the majestic French Pyrenees, The Shepherd and the Bear explores a conflict provoked by the reintroduction of brown bears in the midst of a traditional shepherding community. The film follows an aging shepherd who struggles to find a successor as bears prey on his flock, and a teenage boy who becomes obsessed with tracking the bears. Through its breathtaking cinematography and immersive storytelling, The Shepherd and the Bear is a modern folktale about tradition, community and humanity’s relationship with a vanishing natural world. | Duration: 2h 37m, Rating: 15 | Films may be preceded by up to 20 minutes of advertisements and trailers. Specific timings will vary with each screening. We always recommend arriving on time.\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":101,\"imageUrl\":\"https://system.spektrix.com/jw3/files/c05c67c4-9823-4bce-943d-d2d72822f1d1.jpg\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"The Shepherd and the Bear\",\"instanceDates\":\"22 February-26 February\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"https://system.spektrix.com/jw3/files/c05c67c4-9823-4bce-943d-d2d72822f1d1-thumbnail.jpg\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"589001AGRRBBMLRMDKDNJGHMPVPKKRHSM\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-02-22T12:30:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-02-22T12:30:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-02-26T11:00:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-02-26T11:00:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Cinema\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false},{\"description\":\"7pm-8.45pm, £15, in building // With a tender eye for the magic woven through everyday British Jewish life, writer–director Lewis Rose crafts stories that balance humour, heartbreak and a distinctly whimsical sensibility. Since 2012, Rose has been creating award‑winning short films that explore identity, belonging and the strange, shimmering spaces where tradition meets the modern world. Lewis' shorts have played at over 400 film festivals worldwide, won over 75 awards to date, and been purchased for screening by Disney+ and Canal+. \\r\\n\\r\\nIn this special conversation with critic-turned-producer Jason Solomons, Rose presents three of his most celebrated works: The Chop (2016), Pops (2021), Beshert (2025)  \\r\\n\\r\\n A must‑see showcase of one of the community’s most distinctive cinematic voices offering a rich, witty and heartfelt portrait of UK Jewish experience.\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":105,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"The Short Films of Lewis Rose\",\"instanceDates\":\"15 April-15 April\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"613801AVVJRJTMLSPDJQMBTJHKPRCNKSQ\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-04-15T19:00:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-04-15T18:00:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-04-15T19:00:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-04-15T18:00:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Talks & Discussions\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Arts & Culture\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false},{\"description\":\"The Shoshani Riddle is a captivating documentary that traces director Michael Grynszpan’s obsessive search for the truth behind one of the 20th century’s most enigmatic figures. Known only as “Mr. Shoshani,” this extraordinary nomad was a genius fluent in around thirty languages, versed in philosophy, mathematics, and sacred texts, and a teacher to luminaries like Nobel laureate Elie Wiesel and philosopher Emmanuel Levinas. Despite his vast intellect and influence, Shoshani lived without a home, adopted multiple identities, and left almost no concrete evidence of his life. Over ten years, Grynszpan travels the world interviewing witnesses, uncovering lost manuscripts, and piecing together the legend and legacy of a man who has become both myth and mystery. | This film is in Hebrew, English and French with English subtitles. | Duration: 1h 28m \",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":88,\"imageUrl\":\"https://system.spektrix.com/jw3/files/c9b8a28a-f4eb-4659-9694-fdcc9ef93a2b.jpg\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"The Shoshani Riddle\",\"instanceDates\":\"12 May-12 May\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"https://system.spektrix.com/jw3/files/c9b8a28a-f4eb-4659-9694-fdcc9ef93a2b-thumbnail.jpg\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"619401ACNSVQPPRHGBCNKQKKJGTBTGKJH\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-05-12T15:00:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-05-12T14:00:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-05-12T15:00:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-05-12T14:00:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Cinema\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Seret Film Festival\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false},{\"description\":\"In French Algeria, Meursault drifts through life and love with mysterious detachment. When he stands accused of murdering an Arab man, indifference is his only alibi in François Ozon's fresh take on Albert Camus's classic novel. | This film is in French with English subtitles | Duration: 2h 2m, Rating: 15 Credits\\r\\nRating: 15\\r\\nGenre: Crime, Drama\\r\\nDirector: François Ozon\\r\\nStars: Benjamin Voisin, Rebecca Marder, Pierre Lottin https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=nLoFzIoLpQA&pp=ygUXdGhlIHN0cmFuZ2VyIFVLIHRyYWlsZXI%3D\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":110,\"imageUrl\":\"https://system.spektrix.com/jw3/files/ca7bcfed-b643-4ac1-9ee2-006550993d24.jpg\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"The Stranger\",\"instanceDates\":\"26 April-3 June\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"https://system.spektrix.com/jw3/files/ca7bcfed-b643-4ac1-9ee2-006550993d24-thumbnail.jpg\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"616401ADKNSMQTKRNGNTVGLNHTPNSGJBT\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-04-26T19:30:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-04-26T18:30:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-06-03T11:00:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-06-03T10:00:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Cinema\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false},{\"description\":\"The Syrian Bride (2004) is an evocative, award-winning drama from acclaimed Israeli filmmaker Eran Riklis that turns a single wedding day into an unforgettable exploration of borders — both real and emotional. Set in the Golan Heights, the film follows Mona, a young Druze woman preparing to marry a Syrian actor, only to face a daunting truth: once she crosses the volatile border to begin her life with him, she may never return home. \\r\\nAs bureaucratic absurdity, political tension and family tensions collide, Riklis weaves humor and pathos into a richly human story that reflects the universal longing for connection amid geopolitical fracture. With a vivid ensemble of characters and keen emotional depth, The Syrian Bride reveals how personal lives are shaped — and sometimes shattered — by the sweeping forces of history. The screening will be followed by a Q&A with director Eran Riklis.| This film is in Arabic, English, Hebrew, Russian and French with English subtitles | Duration: 1h 33m\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":98,\"imageUrl\":\"https://system.spektrix.com/jw3/files/184e13d6-01a1-4b33-82c4-547234b7e2ac.jpg\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"The Syrian Bride + Q&A\",\"instanceDates\":\"10 May-10 May\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"https://system.spektrix.com/jw3/files/184e13d6-01a1-4b33-82c4-547234b7e2ac-thumbnail.jpg\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"618001AHJVJNJPNBSGTHNBJGHPMJSHPQQ\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-05-10T12:00:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-05-10T11:00:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-05-10T12:00:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-05-10T11:00:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Cinema\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Seret Film Festival\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false},{\"description\":\"Based on Margot Wölk’s extraordinary real-life account, this film sees a group of women risk their lives as Hitler’s ‘food tasters’. | Duration: 2h 3m, Rating: 15\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":123,\"imageUrl\":\"https://system.spektrix.com/jw3/files/8fac0ad9-3b20-419c-98d6-40f4210ba4c3.jpg\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"The Tasters\",\"instanceDates\":\"29 March-19 April\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"https://system.spektrix.com/jw3/files/8fac0ad9-3b20-419c-98d6-40f4210ba4c3-thumbnail.jpg\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"605402APPNLTGQCHJBQVBHSKVBKBTJLSJ\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-03-29T14:30:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-03-29T13:30:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-04-19T12:45:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-04-19T11:45:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Cinema\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false},{\"description\":\"Mondays 10.30am-12noon, £180 for the 10-week course, in building // What can the earliest stages of life teach us about ourselves, our relationships, and our purpose? \\r\\n\\r\\nIn this thought-provoking series, we'll explore life's journey through the lens of Jewish wisdom, drawing on insights from the Bible, rabbinic teachings and modern psychology. Together, we'll discover how everyday experiences can deepen our understanding of ourselves, the world around us, and our Jewish identity. \\r\\n\\r\\nStage 1: Birth, Babies & Childhood focuses on the beginning of life. We'll examine different perspectives on birth, early development and childhood and explore what these formative years can reveal about growth, learning, potential, and the meaning of life. \\r\\n\\r\\nJoin us as we begin our journey through The Time of Our Life. \\r\\n\\r\\nWhat You’ll Learn \\r\\n\\r\\nExplore Jewish and psychological perspectives on birth, babies, and childhood.  \\r\\n\\r\\nDiscover how early life experiences shape identity, values, and relationships.  \\r\\n\\r\\nReflect on what childhood can teach us about personal growth, potential, and the meaning of life. \\r\\n\\r\\nWho It’s For \\r\\n\\r\\nThis course is anyone interested in exploring life's journey through Jewish wisdom, psychology, and personal reflection. No prior knowledge is required—just curiosity and a willingness to learn and share ideas. \\r\\n\\r\\nWho Delivers It? \\r\\n\\r\\nAngela Gluck has worked as a teacher, trainer and consultant to schools and local authorities. She has written over 40 books on aspects of religion and history and broadcasted on these subjects. She devotes part of her work to teaching children, young people and adults in cross-communal settings. She is an active trustee of The Separated Child Foundation.  \",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":90,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"The Time of Our Life: Birth, Babies & Childhood\",\"instanceDates\":\"5 October-5 October\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"642801AVSHLLMSVPLRMGMHBKNMVSRTCPB\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-10-05T10:30:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-10-05T09:30:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-10-05T10:30:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-10-05T09:30:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false,\"attribute_Genre\":\"Classes & Courses\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"True\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"Angela Gluck\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"10.30-11.20am, building, £7, age 3-7 // A forest race is about to begin, and all the animals are excited. But the announcement puts the strong friendship between the tortoise and the hare to the test. \\r\\n\\r\\nWill they manage to persevere and find their way back to one another? \\r\\nWill they learn to embrace the healing power of forgiveness and find peace in their hearts and souls? \\r\\n\\r\\nPresented by the Israeli House. \",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":50,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"The Tortoise and the Hare\",\"instanceDates\":\"1 February-1 February\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"567801AKVKTKHTVSVMHCPSRPBHMQDGNHM\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-02-01T10:30:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-02-01T10:30:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-02-01T10:30:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-02-01T10:30:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Families & Youth\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Festival of Spoken Ivrit\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false},{\"description\":\"12.30-1.20pm, building, £7, ages 3-7 // A moving one-actor show based on the beloved tale of transformation and self-discovery, brought to life through innovative multimedia. It encourages children to embrace their unique qualities and those of others. Part of the Festival of Spoken Ivrit.\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":50,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"The Ugly Duckling\",\"instanceDates\":\"1 February-1 February\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"568001ASRGJBKKSLTHVSCRPHCPKDDRHQL\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-02-01T12:30:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-02-01T12:30:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-02-01T12:30:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-02-01T12:30:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Families & Youth\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Festival of Spoken Ivrit\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false},{\"description\":\"See the new explosive film, Theodor Herzl: The Man Behind Israel, followed by a Q&A with the film's producers, Sir Bernard Zissman and Geoff Morrow.\\r\\n\\r\\nFollowing a preview at BAFTA in July and the sold out screening in UKJF this is a rare opportunity to see the landmark documentary about legendary Theodor Herzl, regarded as the Founder of the State of Israel.\\r\\n\\r\\nTheodor Herzl:The Man Behind Israel is a bold and timely new documentary that traces the visionary, conflicted, and ultimately tragic life of the man who imagined a Jewish homeland long before it became a reality. Herzl’s journey is narrated by David Baddiel, with Stephen Fry voicing the words of Herzl.\\r\\n\\r\\nAlongside archival materials and expert commentary, the documentary includes powerful testimonies from both Palestinians and those who witnessed and survived the Holocaust, offering viewers a broad, human lens on a history that continues to shape lives today.\\r\\n\\r\\nThe film brings together a diverse range of voices: historians, writers, diplomats, survivors, and everyday citizens who help trace the echo of Herzl’s vision into the present. The team travelled across continents to build a documentary that is as visually compelling as it is emotionally resonant.\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":120,\"imageUrl\":\"https://system.spektrix.com/jw3/files/f64beea8-bba5-4cc0-b165-7f87f4f7e052.jpg\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Theodor Herzl: The Man Behind Israel\",\"instanceDates\":\"21 January-21 January\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"https://system.spektrix.com/jw3/files/f64beea8-bba5-4cc0-b165-7f87f4f7e052-thumbnail.jpg\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"539801APRGGTCJNGGBPDBGGDQDDMDTMJG\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-01-21T19:30:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-01-21T19:30:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-01-21T19:30:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-01-21T19:30:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Cinema\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false},{\"description\":\"Regular screenings // Renowned Icelandic poet and author Andri Snær Magnason is chasing something elusive. As the glacial ice of his homeland melts, he constructs a cinematic time capsule to hold onto this moment and send it to the future, before everything he loves slips away. Using his own collected archives, his grandparents' photographs, and films, as well as traditional songs and folktales, Andri interlaces his family’s story with that of the land around him. From Academy Award-nominated director Sara Dosa, Time and Water is a universal reflection on the power of home and what it means to be alive amid profound epochal change. \\r\\n\\r\\n \\r\\n\\r\\nDuration: 93 minutes \\r\\n\\r\\nRating: PG \\r\\n\\r\\nDirector: Andri Snær Magnason \\r\\n\\r\\nYear: 2024 \\r\\n\\r\\nLanguage: English / Icelandic \\r\\nSubtitles: English  \",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":93,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Time and Water\",\"instanceDates\":\"28 June-29 June\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"629401AJBDHKPPPMCJJVJGHSNCGSNDLGR\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-06-28T12:15:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-06-28T11:15:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-06-29T15:15:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-06-29T14:15:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Cinema\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false},{\"description\":\"7pm - 9.25pm, £7.50 // How do we say goodbye to what we never thought we could lose? Join us for a special screening of Time and Water, the breathtaking documentary by Oscar-nominated director Sara Dosa. The film follows celebrated Icelandic author Andri Snær Magnason as he weaves together family archives, folklore, and the stark reality of his homeland's melting glaciers to create a poignant time capsule for future generations.  Following the screening, our panel of Jewish climate thought leaders will bridge the film's themes with Jewish tradition. Presented in partnership with EcoJudaism, this event explores how water, ritual, and landscape shape our understanding of climate responsibility, intergenerational memory, and our sacred duty to the planet.\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":145,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Time and Water: Screening + Panel\",\"instanceDates\":\"21 June-21 June\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"626401ANJTNDPKPLNQRCPJMBJDRMDQBMB\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-06-21T19:00:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-06-21T18:00:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-06-21T19:00:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-06-21T18:00:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Cinema\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false},{\"description\":\"Wednesdays, 7-8.30pm, £110 for the 5-week course, online only // This engaging five-part course explores Jewish family history through migration, memory, and storytelling. Rather than focusing solely on traditional genealogy research, the course examines the wider historical forces that shaped Jewish journeys across Europe, the Middle East, and beyond. Participants will discover how migration, displacement, identity, and resilience are reflected in family records, archives, and personal stories. \\r\\n\\r\\nSessions combine practical genealogy skills with historical insight, helping learners uncover family connections while understanding the broader Jewish experience across generations. The course concludes with a dedicated storytelling session, supporting participants to bring their discoveries to life. \\r\\n\\r\\nWho It’s For \\r\\n\\r\\nThis course is suitable for beginners and anyone curious about Jewish ancestry, migration histories, and family storytelling. It is ideal for: \\r\\n\\r\\nIndividuals beginning their Jewish genealogy journey  \\r\\n\\r\\nLearners interested in Jewish social and migration history  \\r\\n\\r\\nPeople wanting to understand family records and archives  \\r\\n\\r\\nThose wishing to preserve and share family stories  \\r\\n\\r\\nAnyone with an interest in identity, heritage, and memory  \\r\\n\\r\\nNo prior genealogy experience is required. \\r\\n\\r\\nWhat You’ll Learn / Outcomes \\r\\n\\r\\nUnderstand major patterns of Jewish migration across Europe, the Middle East, and the Americas.  \\r\\n\\r\\nCourse Fornat:  \\r\\n\\r\\n5-week course on Zoom \\r\\n\\r\\nDates:  \\r\\n\\r\\nTuesday 11 November - Getting Started with Genealogy \\r\\n\\r\\nTuesday 18 November - Researching Family History in the UK \\r\\n\\r\\nTuesday 25 November - Jewish Genealogy in Europe and Beyond \\r\\n\\r\\nTuesday 2 December - Tracing Family During and after the Holocaust  \\r\\n\\r\\nTuesday 9 December - Telling the Story – Bringing It All Together \",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":90,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Tracing Your Jewish Family History [Online Only]\",\"instanceDates\":\"11 November-11 November\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"644601AHNMMHCSCHKMPLNVSPTDCDSCKJC\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-11-11T19:00:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-11-11T19:00:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-11-11T19:00:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-11-11T19:00:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false,\"attribute_Genre\":\"Classes & Courses\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"True\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"Jeanette R. Rosenberg\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"A gifted piano tuner's meticulous skills for tuning pianos lead him to discover an unexpected aptitude for cracking safes, turning his life upside down. //\\r\\n\\r\\nDuration: 132m \\r\\nRating: 15 \\r\\nDirector: Daniel Roher \\r\\nStars: Leo Woodall, Havana Rose Liu, Lior Raz  \",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":132,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Tuner\",\"instanceDates\":\"7 June-10 July\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"628201AQVDGHGJBQVCSVRHRKKGTNCTMMB\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-06-07T13:45:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-06-07T12:45:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-07-10T13:00:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-07-10T12:00:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Cinema\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false},{\"description\":\"Soviet Union, 1937. Thousands of letters from detainees falsely accused by the regime are burned in a prison cell. Against all odds, one of them reaches its destination, upon the desk of the newly appointed local prosecutor, Alexander Kornyev. Kornyev does his utmost to meet the prisoner, a victim of agents of the secret police, the NKVD. A dedicated Bolshevik of integrity, the young prosecutor suspects foul play. His quest for justice will take him all the way to the office of the Attorney General in Moscow. In the age of the great Stalinist purges, this is the plunge of a man into the corridors of a totalitarian regime that does not bear said name. | This film is in Russian and Ukrainian with English subtitles | Duration: 1h 58m, Rating: 12A Credits\\r\\nRating:12A\\r\\nGenre: History, Drama\\r\\nDirector: Sergei Loznitsa\\r\\nStars: Alexander Kuznetsov, Anatoliy Beliy, Dmitrijus Denisiukas https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=rzYfw1M9qT4&pp=ygUadHdvIHByb3NlY3V0b3JzIFVLIHRyYWlsZXI%3D\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":113,\"imageUrl\":\"https://system.spektrix.com/jw3/files/d9887d06-99e9-4c7b-95e8-26785e158767.jpg\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Two Prosecutors\",\"instanceDates\":\"14 April-23 April\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"https://system.spektrix.com/jw3/files/d9887d06-99e9-4c7b-95e8-26785e158767-thumbnail.jpg\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"616601ACLRDTLDNKPQMBLRQKGHMBDQVDN\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-04-14T19:30:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-04-14T18:30:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-04-23T13:20:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-04-23T12:20:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Cinema\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false},{\"description\":\"18:30 // 11 Oct 2026 // £20 // Join Israeli metal pioneer Kobi Farhi (Orphaned Land) at JW3 for the exclusive launch of his memoir, The Jewish Muezzin. Featuring an in-depth interview by Dr. Keith Kahn-Harris, live music from Geva Alon, and a post-show book signing.\\r\\n\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":150,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"UK Book Launch: \\\"The Jewish Muezzin\\\" by Kobi Farhi\",\"instanceDates\":\"11 October-11 October\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"631801AVPNKQMPRPPSPBTHTBQDSJTCPGL\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-10-11T18:30:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-10-11T17:30:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-10-11T18:30:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-10-11T17:30:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false,\"attribute_Genre\":\"Music\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"David and his fiancée Meg are about to have their parents meet for the first time over a Shabbat dinner on New York’s Upper West Side when an accidental death (or murder?) gets in the way. With Meg's Catholic parents due any moment, this family dinner soon spirals into a hilarious disaster.  //\\r\\n\\r\\n \\r\\n\\r\\nDuration: 84 minutes \\r\\n\\r\\nRating: 15 \\r\\n\\r\\nDirector: Daniel Robbins \\r\\n\\r\\nCast: Kyra Sedgwick, Milana Vayntrub, Ashley Zukerman \\r\\n\\r\\nYear: 2024 \\r\\n\\r\\nLanguage: English \",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":84,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"UK Jewish Film and JW3 Present: Bad Shabbos\",\"instanceDates\":\"23 June-5 July\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"628202ANCGPJBHLCBCCBVVHBTBSQTGJBH\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-06-23T15:45:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-06-23T14:45:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-07-05T19:50:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-07-05T18:50:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":true,\"attribute_Genre\":\"Cinema\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"9-13 November\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":60,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":false,\"name\":\"UK Jewish Film Festival 2025\",\"instanceDates\":\"9 November-13 November\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"331601ACPQBMBNVDDVGRDVKQGHPSCHDGS\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-11-09T16:30:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2025-11-09T16:30:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2025-11-13T19:00:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2025-11-13T19:00:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Cinema\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false},{\"description\":\"12.30-5pm, building, £15, age 9+ // It's more than just a movie! After a special screening of the Minecraft Movie, we're hosting a communal tech hangout. Connect with other players and build something amazing together—just bring your portable device. \\r\\n\\r\\nHey gamers! Are you ready for an afternoon of epic proportions? \\r\\n\\r\\nJoin us at JW3 Cinema for a super special event just for ages 9 and up! \\r\\n\\r\\nFirst, we're taking you on an incredible journey to the Overworld with a screening of the Minecraft Movie! Experience the blocky world like never before on the big screen. \\r\\n\\r\\nThen, the adventure continues! After the credits roll, we're inviting you to hang out with fellow fans for a communal Minecraft tech session. Bring your portable devices—laptops, tablets, or whatever you use to play—and let's build, mine, and explore together. It's the perfect chance to show off your creations, collaborate on a new project, or just chill with some real-life fellow Minecrafters. \\r\\n\\r\\nAs always there's the free crafting happening too for younger ones - but also with a special Minecraft theme !\\r\\n\\r\\nIt's an afternoon of film and fun you won't want to miss!\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":270,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Ultimate Minecraft Meet-Up\",\"instanceDates\":\"25 January-25 January\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"566601AKRKBGPGBRJBCRHKHBGHGGPGPVS\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-01-25T12:30:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-01-25T12:30:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-01-25T12:30:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-01-25T12:30:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Families & Youth\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Families\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false},{\"description\":\"9am-10am, suggested £5 donation, online only // Recommended 14+ // Join journalist and author Anshel Pfeffer for his insights into the current war between Israel, the US and Iran. \\r\\nSince 2024 Anshel has been The Economist's Israel Correspondent. Before that he was a columnist ad senior correspondent for Ha'aretz. He is the author of the acclaimed biography Bibi: The Turbulent Life and Times of Benjamin Netanyahu. He will be joined by Justin Cohen, News Editor of the Jewish News.\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":60,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"US, Israel & Iran Conflict: Online Briefing\",\"instanceDates\":\"17 April-17 April\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"615001AVTVCLPJLCGHLPSNLCJQNQSQCBB\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-04-17T09:00:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-04-17T08:00:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-04-17T09:00:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-04-17T08:00:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Talks & Discussions\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"David Patrikarakos\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false},{\"description\":\"2-2.45pm, building, £7 per child, £5 per adult £15 family of 3 or more, age 7 and under // Get ready to bust out your best moves at the ultimate family dance party!\\r\\n\\r\\nJoin us for a Valentine's Family Disco that's all about love, laughter, and serious grooves. We're teaming up with the one and only Ilana Bana from Lana Land to bring you an epic afternoon of music and fun for the whole family.\\r\\n\\r\\nWhether you're a tiny dancer or a grown-up disco king, you'll have a blast with amazing tunes, awesome activities, and a dance floor ready for everyone under 7 and their favourite grown-ups. It's the perfect way to celebrate Valentine's Day with the ones you love most! Come make some magical memories with us.\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":45,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Valentine's Family Disco\",\"instanceDates\":\"15 February-15 February\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"566801ALPJRRSJQNVLQRSHGMBBPSCQRBH\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-02-15T14:00:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-02-15T14:00:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-02-15T14:00:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-02-15T14:00:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false,\"attribute_Genre\":\"Families & Youth\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Families\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"Ilana Banana\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"2-4pm, £20, building // Early 20th century Europe was fertile ground for new ideas, and a Jewish perspective, expressed through thinkers, artists and architects, was fundamental to concepts that would shape the century ahead. As anti-Semitism rose across mainland Europe, many left in search of a better life. \\r\\n\\r\\nThis two-part lecture traces the Jewish architect émigrés who made pre-war Britain their home, bringing with them radical ideas that left a rich legacy now being fully recognized, one that formed the backbone of the welfare state Architecture. \\r\\n\\r\\nConcurrently, many émigrés found a home in an emerging Jewish State. There, the British Garden City movement's progressive planning ideas merged with a radical new architectural style then budding in continental Europe. Imported by Jews fleeing persecution, this style resonated deeply with the dream of building an infrastructure for a Socialist Zionist state. \\r\\n\\r\\nThe lecture will explore the common ideas, and the buildings that were built that contributed to the shaping of the two countries. \",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":120,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Virtual Tour: A Tale of Two Cities, One Legacy\",\"instanceDates\":\"29 November-29 November\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"636401ARHMNBNGNJSDLKRVTCQDLCDMTSV\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-11-29T14:00:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-11-29T14:00:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-11-29T14:00:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-11-29T14:00:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false,\"attribute_Genre\":\"Talks & Discussions\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Adult Education\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"Ittai Frank\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"2.30-4pm, £20, in building // On this virtual tour, held at JW3, we visit the last resting place of both the famous and the unknown whose varied lives produce for us stories that are enthralling, inspiring, tragic and even humorous. \\r\\n\\r\\nFrom the comfort of your seats at JW3 – and with a whole host of film slides - we will stroll through this 140-year-old cemetery and come across the famous scientist, robbed of the glory of one of the 20th century’s greatest discoveries;  four former chief rabbis each with revealing stories;  the father and son Rothschilds who could not have been more different;  the London teenager who emigrated to the other side of the world and became a Prime Minister;  the royal illusionist, inventor of the saw the lady in half trick;  two business giants, one in groceries and one in furniture;  Lady Chutzpah who continually stunned the world with her flamboyance;  the son of an East End second hand clothes dealer who literally went from rags to riches;  and there are many other fascinating lives to celebrate and tragic young deaths to lament on this virtual tour.\\r\\n\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":90,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Virtual Tour: Willesden Jewish Cemetery, Legends in Jewish History\",\"instanceDates\":\"1 December-1 December\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"636003ACDRCDGHPCRCRMLMMDGCMKTBTKV\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-12-01T14:30:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-12-01T14:30:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-12-01T14:30:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-12-01T14:30:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false,\"attribute_Genre\":\"Talks & Discussions\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Adult Education\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"Stephen Burstin\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"20:00 // 15 Nov 2026 // 50 tickets at £35 the rest at £40 // A tribute to legendary composer Mati Caspi, featuring Riki Gal performing iconic songs from their celebrated collaborations, alongside an ensemble of London-based Israeli musicians.\\r\\n\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":90,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"West from Here / מערבה מכאן  A tribute to Mati Caspi\",\"instanceDates\":\"15 November-15 November\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"632001AMLKNJDDBKHBSJRTMDRKBGCGQQQ\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-11-15T20:00:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-11-15T20:00:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-11-15T20:00:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-11-15T20:00:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false,\"attribute_Genre\":\"Music\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"Thursdays, 10.30am-12noon, £90 for the 5 week course, in building // What is Jewish Film and how has it developed from the early years of Yiddish cinema to today? Join Dr Julia Wagner on this 5-week course to explore how films reflect Jewish cultural shifts, crises and successes. Lectures include clips and discussion, offering new perspectives on film history and Jewish identities. No previous knowledge is necessary to participate.  \\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nWeek 1. Pioneers: Jewish filmmaking and representation in early silent film and classic Hollywood  \\r\\n\\r\\nWeek 2. Holocaust films: What are the major movements, and ethical considerations, of representations of the Holocaust? \\r\\n\\r\\nWeek 3. Israeli cinema: Nation building and cultural identity \\r\\n\\r\\nWeek 4. Heroes and schlemiels: Jewish masculinity on screen \\r\\n\\r\\nWeek 5. ‘I’ll have what she’s having’: Trailblazing Jewish women in film \\r\\n\\r\\nDr Julia Wagner is a lecturer and writer specialising in Jewish-interest film and television. She holds a PhD in Film Studies and is a member of the London Film Critics’ Circle. Julia is author of the BFI Film Classics book, Hester Street (Bloomsbury 2025).\\r\\n\\r\\nImage of Barbra Streisand: Photo by Hulton Archive/Getty Images\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":90,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"What is Jewish Film?\",\"instanceDates\":\"15 January-12 February\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"563401AKCHMHTBKBNSGDQNGTTNSHBCQBC\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-01-15T10:30:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-01-15T10:30:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-02-12T10:30:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-02-12T10:30:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Classes & Courses\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"True\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"History & Politics Courses\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"Julia Wagner\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false},{\"description\":\"Wednesdays, 7-8.30pm, £14 per session, in building only // What makes Jewish stories different from all others? Why did the Book of Esther get a holiday, and the story of Joseph get a musical?  \\r\\n\\r\\n This workshop series explores the cyclical nature of Jewish storytelling, the oral tradition, contemporary Jewish stories, and gives participants practical tools to share their own. \\r\\n\\r\\n \\r\\n\\r\\nWho It's For   \\r\\n\\r\\nAll welcome. \\r\\n\\r\\nWhat You'll Learn / Outcomes  \\r\\n\\r\\nThe skills, knowledge, or takeaways that participants can expect by the end of the course.  \\r\\n\\r\\nCourse Format  \\r\\n\\r\\nIn-person workshop series, looking at different storytelling forms (writing, oral, performance, ritual) with examples from Judaism and popular culture, and using these as a basis to develop our own individual storytelling styles and forms. \",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":90,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"What is Jewish Storytelling?\",\"instanceDates\":\"9 September-21 October\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"644801ASNPPKDCSCTTCNJQTKMHPPRKPPG\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-09-09T19:00:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-09-09T18:00:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-10-21T19:00:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-10-21T18:00:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false,\"attribute_Genre\":\"Classes & Courses\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"Kayla Feldman\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"Mondays, 10.30am-12noon, in building // £180 for the course // Peace is not an absence of war,” wrote Jewish philosopher Baruch Spinoza, in the 1600s.  “It’s a virtue, a state of mind, a tendency to kindness and justice.” \\r\\n\\r\\n \\r\\n\\r\\nToday, with the presence—not the absence—of wars and other kinds of conflicts, what form might virtues, states of mind and tendencies take? What wisdom can we find in Jewish, Christian and Islamic traditions? And is there common ground in their views of peace and their ways of peace? In the end, is peace a feeling or an action? \\r\\n\\r\\n  \\r\\n\\r\\nThis course will look at the presence and absence of peace at various levels and in a range of situations—interpersonal, intercultural, international. \\r\\n\\r\\n \\r\\n\\r\\nWhat You’ll Learn \\r\\n\\r\\nDiscuss the different conceptions of peace and how it manifests (or doesn’t) in various levels of society.   \\r\\n\\r\\nExplore how different religious traditions understand peace and examine their connections. \\r\\n\\r\\nDiscover practical ways ideas like kindness, justice, and forgiveness can shape how we respond to conflict in everyday life and in the wider world.  \\r\\n\\r\\nWho It’s For \\r\\n\\r\\nThis course is anyone interested in ethics, religion and conflict transformation. It’s also for anyone seeking deeper insight into how ancient wisdom can help us respond to contemporary conflicts today.  \\r\\n\\r\\nWho Delivers It? \\r\\n\\r\\nAngela Gluck has worked as a teacher, trainer and consultant to schools and local authorities. She has written over 40 books on aspects of religion and history and broadcasted on these subjects. She devotes part of her work to teaching children, young people and adults in cross-communal settings. She is an active trustee of The Separated Child Foundation.   \",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":90,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"What on Earth is Peace on Earth? \",\"instanceDates\":\"27 April-13 July\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"596401AGRSPKKHDSSLHNQLLRHPDPLRGDB\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-04-27T10:30:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-04-27T09:30:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-07-13T10:30:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-07-13T09:30:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Classes & Courses\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"True\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"History & Politics Courses\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"Angela Gluck\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false},{\"description\":\"7.30-9pm, hybrid, £20 // Join us for this enlightening event as we delve into the Qur'an's teachings about Jews, Judaism and the Bible, presented by  Rick Sopher with Dr Abdulla Galadari (online). There will be an opportunity to ask questions\\r\\n\\r\\nRick Sopher is emerging as a key figure in interfaith scriptural dialogue. With his background as a Jew whose family lived in Babylon (Iraq) from ancient times, Rick has forged new ways of understanding the links between the Bible and the Qur'an. Beginning in November 2020 he convened a reading group comprising the world's leading authorities on religious texts to discuss the themes contained in the book. He has engaged in discussions with Muslim Imams in the UK comparing Jewish and Muslim texts, which have appeared online in podcasts. He graduated from Christ's College, Cambridge in 1981 and had a career on finance, rising to CEO of Edmond de Rothschild Capital Holdings. In 2007, for his work in religious education, he was awarded the Chevalier de la Legion d'Honneur by French President Jacques Chirac.\\r\\n\\r\\nAbdulla Galadari is an Associate Professor of Islamic Studies at Khalifa University and holds a PhD in Arabic and Islamic Studies from the University of Aberdeen. His field is in Qur'anic hermeneutics and the Qur'an's possible engagement with Near Eastern traditions in Late Antiquity including biblical and rabbinic literature. He uses a multidisciplinary approach to the Qur'an that includes historical and philological methods to understand the Qur'an's milieu and its conversation with different audiences and traditions. He is the author of Qur'anic Hermeneutics: Between Science, History, and the Bible (2018), Metaphors of Death and Resurrection in the Qur'an: An Intertextual Approach with Biblical and Rabbinic Literature (2021).\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":90,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"What the Qur’an says about Jews, Judaism and the Torah\",\"instanceDates\":\"3 February-3 February\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"559601ARQHDCGMRMTVJVJNLLGLPPGMQSH\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-02-03T19:30:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-02-03T19:30:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-02-03T19:30:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-02-03T19:30:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Talks & Discussions\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Adult Education\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false},{\"description\":\"7.30pm-9pm, £30, in building, 18 plus, Thursday 7 May 2026 // Join us for a very special evening with Tal Sunderland-Cohen, Chairman of the Wine Guild of the United Kingdom, as we explore the dynamic world of Israeli whisky and wine innovation.\\r\\nFor the first time in London, JW3 is proud to host an exclusive Whisky Masterclass showcasing a remarkable line-up from M&H – Milk & Honey Distillery, Israel’s pioneering and internationally acclaimed whisky producer.\\r\\nDiscover extraordinary expressions matured in some of the most unique environments on earth:\\r\\nThe Galilee – cool, elevated, refined\\r\\nThe Dead Sea – the lowest place on the planet, where extreme conditions create intensely accelerated ageing\\r\\nA selection of hand-crafted casks – including red wine, STR, sherry, pomegranate, and more\\r\\nEvery whisky you’ll taste is fully kosher and crafted with passion, precision, and unmistakable Israeli innovation.\\r\\nThis is a rare opportunity to sample the whisky that stunned the industry by winning World’s Best Single Malt 2023, alongside several limited-edition expressions rarely available in the UK.\\r\\nJoin us at JW3 for an unforgettable evening of flavour, discovery, and storytelling with M&H.\\r\\nSpaces are limited – book now before it sells out!\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":90,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Whiskey Masterclass\",\"instanceDates\":\"7 May-7 May\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"591801ACQVTTBPGKMJJMSHDBTKJBPLHQH\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-05-07T19:30:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-05-07T18:30:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-05-07T19:30:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-05-07T18:30:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Talks & Discussions\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Adult Education\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"Tal Sunderland-Cohen\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false},{\"description\":\"11am-1pm, £20, off-site // Join Rachel Kolsky on a walking tour of the East End, uncovering stories of Jewish and non-Jewish women alike who made a significant impact. \\r\\n\\r\\nMarking International Women's Day, you will explore the backstreets of Whitechapel and Spitalfields, hearing stories like that of Alice Model and her maternity hospital, Miriam Moses and her youth work, the philanthropy of the Rothschild ladies, suffragette and local politician Minnie Lansbury, and local GP, Hannah Billig.\\r\\n\\r\\nThis tour is dedicated to Sophie Spielman, one of the Women of Worth profiled on the tour, who recently passed away shortly before her 101st birthday.\\r\\n\\r\\nThis tour will not depart from JW3; the meeting location will be provided upon booking.\\r\\n\\r\\nPlease wear comfortable shoes and dress for the weather! \",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":120,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Women of Worth\",\"instanceDates\":\"8 March-8 March\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"554002AVTBQHTVTCMQVQHNTKKSTPRMDHR\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-03-08T11:00:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-03-08T11:00:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-03-08T11:00:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-03-08T11:00:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Walks\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Walking Tours\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false},{\"description\":\"A bold and original imagining of one of the greatest love stories of all time, Emerald Fennell’s Wuthering Heights stars Margot Robbie and Jacob Elordi. | Duration: 2h 16m, Rating: 15 \",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":136,\"imageUrl\":\"https://system.spektrix.com/jw3/files/8a25f3e0-d5da-4f25-910f-14df7b585968.jpg\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Wuthering Heights\",\"instanceDates\":\"8 March-18 March\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"https://system.spektrix.com/jw3/files/8a25f3e0-d5da-4f25-910f-14df7b585968-thumbnail.jpg\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"606802AVRTMJDTLRSNSRNGRSRNCNPGMBR\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-03-08T17:00:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-03-08T17:00:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-03-18T19:00:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-03-18T19:00:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Cinema\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false},{\"description\":\"7pm-8.15pm, free, in building // Memorial event for the Israeli soldiers and victims of terror. The ceremony will be conducted in English and feature personal stories and songs.\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":75,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Yom HaZikaron Memorial\",\"instanceDates\":\"19 April-19 April\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"616801ARKSGDGBDLHHGCTKJSLKNGJHMML\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-04-19T19:00:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-04-19T18:00:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-04-19T19:00:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-04-19T18:00:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Special Events\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false},{\"description\":\"19:00 // 12 Nov 2026 // £6 // Tickets via UKJF website // Don’t miss UK Jewish Film's Young Jury of filmmakers and film enthusiasts celebrating some of the best short films of this year’s festival. Aged 18-30, the jury has selected their top choices from the variety of wonderful short films screening this year. They’ll be screening their favourite films, awarding the winner and explaining their choices in a post-screening panel discussion. Followed by a complimentary drink and an after-party in the bar.\\r\\n\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":180,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":false,\"name\":\"Young JW3 & UK Jewish Film Festival present: Young Jury Award for Best Short Film 2026\",\"instanceDates\":\"12 November-12 November\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"634201ARSRRCTQGGLHQVRVKJJSSTNSPJN\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-11-12T19:00:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-11-12T19:00:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-11-12T19:00:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-11-12T19:00:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false,\"attribute_Genre\":\"Young Professionals\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"\\\"6.30pm-7.45pm, £15, in building, 20s & 30s, Wednesday 1 July 2026 // Join us for an early evening yoga session on the JW3 Beach. \\r\\n\\r\\nConnect with your body, cultivate mindfulness and invite in light and wellbeing as you move. An open-air experience where city sounds, beach and sky meet peaceful, restorative practice.\\\"\\r\\n\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":95,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Young JW3 Beach Yoga: Evening Flow\",\"instanceDates\":\"1 July-1 July\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"599801AVNNJLPCKMDMTNHKVDCCKSCTMCS\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-07-01T18:30:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-07-01T17:30:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-07-01T18:30:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-07-01T17:30:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Young Professionals\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Young JW3\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"Maxine Levy\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false},{\"description\":\"15:00 29/03/2026\\r\\n £14 ////\\r\\n \\\"Young JW3’s crafternoon series continues with this joyful lino printing social. Lino printing is a hands-on form of relief printmaking, where you carve a design into a linoleum block, roll ink onto the raised surface, and press it onto paper or fabric to create a print. This simple yet satisfying technique lets you produce multiple copies of your artwork.\\r\\n\\r\\nNo art experience needed - just come as you are, enjoy a hot drink and a pastry, and get creative in great company.\\r\\n\\r\\nAbout MANOMAKE:\\r\\nTo put it simply, MANOMAKE is a creative community enterprise that strives to bring affordable and unique events to the creatives of London. Each event we explore a different activity, from collaging to mug painting to poetry. Everyone is welcome - regardless of skill level! Hopefully by joining in you'll even discover a creative side that you never knew you had!\\\"\\r\\n\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":120,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Young JW3 Craft Café: Lino Printing\",\"instanceDates\":\"29 March-29 March\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"554401ABCJMNTMLMTCQSQDGGCMNMNBGVC\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-03-29T15:00:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-03-29T14:00:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-03-29T15:00:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-03-29T14:00:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Young Professionals\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Young JW3\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"MANOMAKE\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false},{\"description\":\"15:00 25/01/2026\\r\\n £14 // \\\"We’re kicking off 2026 with the first in Young JW3's new series of cosy crafternoons, hosted by artist Eliza - founder of the MANOMAKE craft club. In this relaxed collage social, we’ll be creating mood and vision boards to set our intentions for the year ahead, helping us visualise and attract all the good things we hope to invite into 2026. No art experience needed; just come as you are, enjoy a hot drink and pastry, and get creative in great company. We can’t wait to welcome you!\\r\\n\\r\\nAbout MANOMAKE:\\r\\nTo put it simply, MANOMAKE is a creative community enterprise that strives to bring affordable and unique events to the creatives of London. Each event we explore a different activity, from collaging to mug painting to poetry. Everyone is welcome - regardless of skill level! Hopefully by joining in you'll even discover a creative side that you never knew you had!\\\"\\r\\n\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":120,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Young JW3 Craft Café: New Year's Collage Social\",\"instanceDates\":\"25 January-25 January\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"554201AQPRSDDLSJRVDSTKNSHKJGVKSQC\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-01-25T15:00:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-01-25T15:00:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-01-25T15:00:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-01-25T15:00:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Young Professionals\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Young JW3\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"MANOMAKE\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false},{\"description\":\"3pm, £16 // Young JW3’s Craft Café returns with a relaxed, creative social - perfect for welcoming in spring.\\r\\nIn this session, we’ll create small seasonal flower arrangements to use as inspiration for our own still life paintings in different media. Whether you enjoy carefully painting what you see or prefer to take a more abstract, expressive approach, this is a chance to experiment with new techniques, unwind, and explore your creativity in a supportive, social setting. No experience needed - just come ready to make, paint, and enjoy. Light refreshments included.\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":120,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Young JW3 Craft Café: Spring Flowers - Creative Painting\",\"instanceDates\":\"26 April-26 April\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"555801ALSMPCRTMBLLVCQLMGCVDKTRNDR\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-04-26T15:00:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-04-26T14:00:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-04-26T15:00:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-04-26T14:00:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Young Professionals\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Young JW3\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"MANOMAKE\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false},{\"description\":\"Early bird (£25) till 5th Oct\\r\\n\\r\\nGeneral sale (£30) till 2nd Nov\\r\\n\\r\\nLast call (£35) till 17th Nov. // A winter Shabbat dinner with good food and warm conversations, preceded by Embodied Light, an optional guided meditation and breathwork session. Rooted in Kavannah, it uses movement, breath and stillness to help you arrive, reset and prepare for Shabbat.\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":180,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Young JW3 Friday Night Dinner\",\"instanceDates\":\"20 November-20 November\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"634601ALDPJGHJDCRGQKHMLMPHDPDSRGD\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-11-20T19:00:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-11-20T19:00:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-11-20T19:00:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-11-20T19:00:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false,\"attribute_Genre\":\"Young Professionals\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"Maxine Levy\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"13:00 // 20 Dec 2026 // Ticket price: £25 Panto / £20 pickling workshop / £40 both // End the year Young JW3-style with a festive two-part winter afternoon of theatre and hands-on creativity. Start with JW3's own Pantomime, Dick Whittingberg Gets Into a Pickle, then continue with an interactive pickling workshop. Book one or both for a discounted full-afternoon experience.\\r\\n\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":240,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Young JW3 Pickle Party: Pantomime Outing & Pickling Workshop\",\"instanceDates\":\"20 December-20 December\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"634401AKQBVPTTCTSHDKGPBHVNVGPJJNN\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-12-20T13:00:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-12-20T13:00:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-12-20T13:00:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-12-20T13:00:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false,\"attribute_Genre\":\"Young Professionals\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"Hey! Food Is Ready\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"6.30pm - Pizza party\\r\\n7.15pm - Film starts\\r\\n9:30pm - Film ends\\r\\n\\r\\nThis is a safe space for queer Jews, so whether you're queer or just happy to be here, come and join us!\\r\\n\\r\\nVegan pizza available upon request - please purchase the appropriate ticket.\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":180,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Young JW3 Queer Movie & Pizza Night: Call Me By Your Name\",\"instanceDates\":\"21 October-21 October\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"634801ANLHBVBSHMNDDSRHGDJJTRMKDRP\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-10-21T18:30:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-10-21T17:30:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-10-21T18:30:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-10-21T17:30:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false,\"attribute_Genre\":\"Young Professionals\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"6.30pm - Pizza party\\r\\n7.15pm - Film starts\\r\\n8.50pm - Film ends\\r\\n\\r\\nThis is a safe space for queer Jews, so whether you're queer or just happy to be here, come and join us!\\r\\n\\r\\nVegan pizza available upon request - please purchase the appropriate ticket.\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":150,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Young JW3 Queer Movie & Pizza Night: Theatre Camp\",\"instanceDates\":\"16 December-16 December\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"635001ATDVRCKSKBMMVDVGTSHJMKJPTHV\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-12-16T18:30:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-12-16T18:30:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-12-16T18:30:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-12-16T18:30:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false,\"attribute_Genre\":\"Young Professionals\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"6pm-10pm, £25/£30/£35, in building, 20s & 30s, Friday 14 August 2026 // A magical summer BBQ Shabbat dinner under the open sky on our JW3 Beach. Enjoy live music, a delicious spread of grilled favourites and a warm?atmosphere. Come hungry, bring your friends, and let's make it a night to remember!?\\r\\n\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":240,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Young JW3 Summer BBQ Friday Night Dinner\",\"instanceDates\":\"14 August-14 August\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"599601ADGPCNSDBBBPVHDNSSPLSMRNPMM\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-08-14T18:00:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-08-14T17:00:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-08-14T18:00:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-08-14T17:00:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Young Professionals\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Young JW3\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false},{\"description\":\"19:00 12/02/2026 £20 //\\r\\n\\r\\n\\\"Looking for something a little different this Valentine’s season? Join us for a unique social featuring themed drinks, new connections, and an immersive escape room experience you won’t forget.\\r\\n\\r\\nYou’ll team up with fellow guests to solve \\\"\\\"Murder at the Mill\\\"\\\", a gripping, vintage-style escape game by Pier Pressure, brought specially for Young JW3 for one night only.\\r\\n\\r\\nWe'll have detective-themed props and costume items for you to get into character, or feel free to come dressed in your own favourite sleuthing gear: trench coats and magnifying glasses welcome!\\r\\n\\r\\nWhether you're coming with friends or flying solo, this is the perfect chance to meet new people, test your puzzle-solving skills, and enjoy a cocktail or two in a fun, relaxed setting. Love may or may not be in the air… but mystery definitely is.\\\"\\r\\n\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":150,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Young JW3 Valentine's Mixer & Murder Mystery Escape Room\",\"instanceDates\":\"12 February-12 February\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"555001APMGJLMJNLJJLJPVCRJVLJMJQGH\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-02-12T19:00:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-02-12T19:00:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-02-12T19:00:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-02-12T19:00:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Young Professionals\",\"attribute_Language\":\"English\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Young JW3\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"Pier Pressure - Welwyn Escape Rooms\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false},{\"description\":\"\\\"4pm-5.30pm, £12, in building, 20s & 30s, Sunday 26 July 2026 // Led by a student Soferet (scribe), this relaxed, hands-on workshop will give you the chance to learn about the traditional way to write our sacred texts. You'll learn how to write in the Beit Yosef script, a common Ashkenazi script, starting off with calligraphy marker pens and then writing with quill pens and oak gall ink. You'll also have the chance to ask any questions about the work and traditions of Jewish Scribal Art. No prior knowledge is necessary, but if you want to try your hand at writing you will need to be familiar with the Hebrew Aleph-Bet.\\r\\n\\r\\nQueer Yeshiva leads rigorous, immersive and inclusive Jewish learning in the UK, wrestling with Jewish knowledge and tradition through an explicitly Queer lens. We unlock Talmud and other sacred texts through events, courses and resources, by Queer Jews, for Queer Jews.\\\"\\r\\n\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":90,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Young JW3 x Queer Yeshiva: Jewish Scribal Art\",\"instanceDates\":\"26 July-26 July\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"599401AGTQCTSDRHMVHNSBSCJVPBTJHKJ\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-07-26T16:00:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-07-26T15:00:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-07-26T16:00:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-07-26T15:00:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Young Professionals\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Young JW3\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"Queer Yeshiva\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false},{\"description\":\"Join us for an hour of learning and discussion in Yiddish and English about the erotic, surprising and queer Shir HaShirim (Song of Songs). Led in Yiddish with live English translation, we will look at the original Hebrew text of Shir HaShirim alongside Yiddish and English translations. This bilingual workshop is for any level of Yiddish, including total beginners!\\r\\n\\r\\nאױף דער װאַרשטאַט פֿון אײן שעה, װעט מען לערנען און דיסקוטירן שיר השירים, אַן עראָטישער, חידושדיקער און קװירער פּאָעטישער טעקסט פֿון תּנך. די צװײ־שפּראַכיקע װאַרשטאַט װעט מען אָנפֿירן אױף ייִדיש און ענגליש בײדע, ניצנדיק דעם אָריגינעלן לשון־קדוש טעקסט צוזאַמען מיט זײַנע ייִדיש און ענגליש איבערזעצונגען. אַלע זײַנען שטאַרק פֿאַרבעטן, נישט קוקנדיק אױף דער .מדרגה פֿון ייִדיש  \\r\\n\\r\\nTamara Micner is a Yiddish educator, playwright and performer in London. She teaches at the University of Cambridge, Workers' Circle, Jewish Care and elsewhere. She also co-founded and co-leads Di londoner shpilers (The London Yiddish Players), London's first Yiddish theatre company in decades. She participated in Queer Yeshiva (gleefully) in 2025.\\r\\n\\r\\nQueer Yeshiva leads rigorous, immersive and inclusive Jewish learning in the UK, wrestling with Jewish knowledge and tradition through an explicitly Queer lens. We unlock Talmud and other sacred texts through events, courses and resources, by Queer Jews, for Queer Jews.\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":90,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Young JW3 x Queer Yeshiva: Shir HaShirim in Yiddish\",\"instanceDates\":\"21 June-21 June\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"599201AHJSSNNKHTHQLJSDMMJVPGLKBSP\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-06-21T16:00:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-06-21T15:00:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-06-21T16:00:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-06-21T15:00:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Young Professionals\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Young JW3\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"Tamara Micner\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false},{\"description\":\"\\\"4pm-5.30pm, £12, in building, 20s & 30s, Sunday 31 May 2026 // Who owns the Torah? Who gets to decide how it’s interpreted? The answer is… you!\\r\\n\\r\\nJoin us for an hour of fun, interactive Talmud study led by Queer Yeshiva, as we discuss radical and queer approaches to traditional Jewish texts through a Talmudic story of Moses arguing with the angels about who the Torah is really for. If you've ever been curious about Talmud study but not sure it's for you, this relaxed workshop is the perfect opportunity to give it a go.\\r\\n\\r\\nNo prior knowledge is required, but there will be the opportunity to dig into the text in the original Hebrew/Aramaic for anyone who wants to. So whether you’re Talmud-curious or an experienced Yeshivanik we’re excited to welcome you all. \\r\\n\\r\\nQueer Yeshiva leads rigorous, immersive and inclusive Jewish learning in the UK, wrestling with Jewish knowledge and tradition through an explicitly Queer lens. We unlock Talmud and other sacred texts through events, courses and resources, by Queer Jews, for Queer Jews.\\\"\\r\\n\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":90,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Young JW3 x Queer Yeshiva: Tea and Talmud\",\"instanceDates\":\"31 May-31 May\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"598801ALTDDCTVDPGJQTNPTNHSMGDVKCB\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-05-31T16:00:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-05-31T15:00:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-05-31T16:00:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-05-31T15:00:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Young Professionals\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Young JW3\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"Queer Yeshiva\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false},{\"description\":\"\\\"6pm-10pm, £25/£30/£35, in building, 20s & 30s, Friday 3 July 2026 // Join us for a vibrant Friday night dinner and Israeli dancing on the JW3 Beach, a joyful, safe space celebrating love, community, and Jewish pride. LGBTQ+ people and allies welcome. Dress festive, eat, dance, and celebrate together during London Pride weekend!\\r\\n\\r\\nMore about Sapphic Shabbat:\\r\\n\\r\\nSapphic Shabbat is a Jewish sapphic group, inclusive of non-binary and trans folk who identify as lesbian, bisexual, pansexual, wlw, transmasc, and transfemme. They organise curated Shabbat dinners for small groups so guests can make new connections in a low-pressure environment. Sapphic Shabbat also hosts open meet-ups that welcome the wider Jewish queer community and allies.\\r\\n\\r\\nFollow Sapphic Shabbat on Instagram: https://www.instagram.com/sapphic.shabbat/\\\"\\r\\n\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":240,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Young JW3 x Sapphic Shabbat: Beach, Please - It's Shabbat!\",\"instanceDates\":\"3 July-3 July\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"598201ASJBLRMRVSNMRDMGGKLRNNHMNSH\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-07-03T18:00:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-07-03T17:00:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-07-03T18:00:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-07-03T17:00:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Young Professionals\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Young JW3\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"Liat Oberlander\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false},{\"description\":\"15:00\\r\\n 15/02/2026 £14 //// \\\"In this special LGBTQ+ social, hosted in collaboration with Sapphic Shabbat, we’ll be diving into some joyful Valentine’s crafting. No art experience needed — just come as you are, sip on a hot drink, enjoy a pastry, and get creative in great company.\\r\\n\\r\\nNow in its third year, Sapphic Shabbat curates events for queer Jews to build community in a warm, low-pressure space. This social celebrates queer love in all its forms — the perfect chance to meet new people, make lasting friendships… or maybe even something more.\\r\\n\\r\\nAbout MANOMAKE:\\r\\nThis is the second in Young JW3’s new series of cosy crafternoons, hosted by artist Eliza — founder of the MANOMAKE craft club. To put it simply, MANOMAKE is a creative community enterprise that strives to bring affordable and unique events to the creatives of London. Each event we explore a different activity, from collaging to mug painting to poetry. Everyone is welcome - regardless of skill level! Hopefully by joining in you'll even discover a creative side that you never knew you had!\\r\\n\\r\\nMore about Sapphic Shabbat:\\r\\nSapphic Shabbat is a Jewish sapphic group, inclusive of non-binary and trans folk who identify as lesbian, bisexual, pansexual, wlw, transmasc, transfemme and more. They organise a range of events for members - including Shabbat dinners, picnics and book club meetings - as well as open meet-ups that welcome the wider LGBTQIA+ community and allies.\\r\\nFollow Sapphic Shabbat on Instagram: @sapphic.shabbat\\\"\\r\\n\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":120,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Young JW3 x Sapphic Shabbat: Hearts & Crafts: LGBTQ+ Valentine's Social\",\"instanceDates\":\"15 February-15 February\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"555002AQCTDRHSCRSTTKDQTQGDMCTKSDB\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-02-15T15:00:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-02-15T15:00:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-02-15T15:00:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-02-15T15:00:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Young Professionals\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Young JW3\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"MANOMAKE\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false},{\"description\":\"7pm-10pm, £15, in building, 20s & 30s, Tuesday 12 May 2026 // Join us for an unforgettable Eurovision Semi-Finals watch party! A safe, welcoming space to celebrate Eurovision, show solidarity with Israel, and schmooze with other Eurovision fans. Bring friends, flags, and get ready to party!\\r\\nWe’ll be screening all the action as the most exciting performances from across the world battle it out for a spot in the grand final. Whether you're there for the epic performances, hilarious commentary, or just to cheer on your favourite contestants, this is the place to be.\\r\\n \\r\\nTimings:\\r\\n19:00 - Doors open for sushi, drinks & mingling\\r\\n20:00 - Eurovision watch party\\r\\n \\r\\nPlease email Batsheva with any dietary requirements as soon as possible: batsheva.haber@ujia.org.\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":180,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Young JW3 x Young UJIA: Eurovision Semi-Finals Watch Party\",\"instanceDates\":\"12 May-12 May\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"603601ACCGBSRVKVDBJRPLBDBGBHRHRQB\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-05-12T19:00:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-05-12T18:00:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-05-12T19:00:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-05-12T18:00:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Young Professionals\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Young JW3\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false},{\"description\":\"The Israeli Film Club, a partnership between Young UJIA and Young JW3, uses cinema to spark conversation, connection, and fresh perspectives on Israel and Zionism. From cutting-edge contemporary films to beloved classics, it’s a chance to experience the richness of Israeli storytelling and meet fellow film lovers at JW3. The Israeli Film Club is generously sponsored by Young UJIA.\\r\\n\\r\\nWe will be screening Entebbe (2018). Entebbe tells the story of the 1976 hijacking of an Air France flight by Palestinian and German militants, who divert the plane to Uganda and hold passengers hostage. As the crisis unfolds, the film follows both the hijackers and Israeli leaders grappling with difficult moral and strategic decisions. While negotiations continue, Israel secretly plans a high-risk rescue operation. The film culminates in the famous raid at Entebbe airport, where Israeli commandos attempt to free the hostages. It emphasises the human motivations, fears, and political complexities behind the historic event. [Can cut down the summary.]\\r\\n\\r\\n[Insert trailer]\\r\\n\\r\\nTimings:\\r\\n6:30pm - food, drinks & schmoozing\\r\\n7:15pm - film starts\\r\\n\\r\\nBooking in advance helps us cater accordingly. Please email gianina@jw3.org.uk with any access or additional dietary requirements.\\r\\n\\r\\nAbout Young UJIA:\\r\\nYoung UJIA is UJIA’s home for young Jewish adults in their 20s and 30s: bringing people together through philanthropy, education, culture, leadership and community. It’s a space to meet others, explore big questions, and be part of a generation shaping the next generations connection to Israel and Jewish life.\\r\\n\\r\\nAbout UJIA:\\r\\nUJIA is dedicated to ensuring that young Jewish people in the UK forge a personal relationship with Israel, so that they have a strong sense of belonging to the Jewish people. This is our mission and vision.\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":150,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Young JW3 x Young UJIA: Film Club: Entebbe\",\"instanceDates\":\"27 July-27 July\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"639801ADTCTPTNLCTQBQCPRQKRDDLKVML\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-07-27T18:30:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-07-27T17:30:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-07-27T18:30:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-07-27T17:30:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false,\"attribute_Genre\":\"Young Professionals\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"6.30pm-9pm, £8.50 film & pizza, £8.50 film & vegan pizza, in building // The Israeli Film Club, a partnership between Young UJIA and Young JW3, uses cinema to spark conversation, connection, and fresh perspectives on Israel and Zionism. From cutting-edge contemporary films to beloved classics, it’s a chance to experience the richness of Israeli storytelling and meet fellow film lovers at JW3. The Israeli Film Club is generously sponsored by Young UJIA.\\r\\n\\r\\nWe will be screening Exodus (1960). Ari Ben Canaan, a passionate member of the Jewish paramilitary group Haganah, attempts to transport 600 Jewish refugees on a dangerous voyage from Cyprus to Palestine on a ship named the Exodus. He faces obstruction from British forces, who will not grant the ship passage to its destination.\\r\\n\\r\\n[Insert trailer: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=JMZ9bjInqwI]\\r\\n\\r\\nTimings:\\r\\n6:30pm - food, drinks & schmoozing\\r\\n7:15pm - film starts\\r\\n\\r\\nBooking in advance helps us cater accordingly. Please email gianina@jw3.org.uk with any access or additional dietary requirements.\\r\\n\\r\\nAbout Young UJIA:\\r\\nYoung UJIA is UJIA’s home for young Jewish adults in their 20s and 30s: bringing people together through philanthropy, education, culture, leadership and community. It’s a space to meet others, explore big questions, and be part of a generation shaping the next generations connection to Israel and Jewish life.\\r\\n\\r\\nAbout UJIA:\\r\\nUJIA is dedicated to ensuring that young Jewish people in the UK forge a personal relationship with Israel, so that they have a strong sense of belonging to the Jewish people. This is our mission and vision.\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":150,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Young JW3 x Young UJIA: Israeli Film Club - Exodus\",\"instanceDates\":\"27 April-27 April\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"620801AMVNKTBSQGHBVSHCVDLDPSRKKBB\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-04-27T18:30:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-04-27T17:30:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-04-27T18:30:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-04-27T17:30:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Young Professionals\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Young JW3\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false},{\"description\":\"19:00 15/01/2026 £20 // \\r\\n \\\"Shake up your New Year at our Dry January mocktail mixer!\\r\\n\\r\\nJoin us for a refreshing, alcohol-free evening of creativity and connection. Learn how to craft delicious mocktails with a pro, then sip, mix, and mingle in great company.\\\"\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":120,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Young JW3: Cheers to the New Year: A Mocktail Masterclass\",\"instanceDates\":\"15 January-15 January\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"553801AMDSGSKTSGQMJPNHTMQKVCRKHGP\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-01-15T19:00:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-01-15T19:00:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-01-15T19:00:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-01-15T19:00:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Young Professionals\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Young JW3\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"Nini\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false},{\"description\":\"\\\"6.30pm-8pm, £12 for workshop. £7.50 (50% discount) ticket for Kosher Giraffes after the workshop // Young JW3 presents an immersive drawing workshop hosted by artist, filmmaker and musician Hugo Max. \\r\\n\\r\\nThis small group session is open to those in their 20s and 30s with no prior artistic experience required. The session will unfold through a series of playful exercises in graphite and charcoal that embrace experimentation and collaboration.\\r\\n\\r\\nEngaging with different sensory approaches to drawing, whether through touch or deep listening, the workshop will focus on process rather than product to ask questions about the role of improvisation in daily experience. \\r\\n\\r\\nThis Improvisational Drawing workshop precedes Kosher Giraffes & Other Tails, a screening of Max’s experimental films featuring live improvised soundtracks at JW3 Cinema. The workshop will provide a unique perspective on the film programme.\\r\\n\\r\\nPlus, you'll get 50% off your ticket to Kosher Giraffes & Other Tails if you book the improvisational drawing workshop. \\r\\n\\r\\nArtist Biography\\r\\n\\r\\nHugo Max is a filmmaker, painter and musician based in London. His films have been programmed by the Austrian Filmmuseum, TIFF Cinematheque and Modern Art Oxford, screening at festivals in the UK, Northern Ireland, Germany and South Korea.\\r\\nMax has presented four UK tours accompanying silent films with live soundtracks on solo viola, regularly appearing at London's Prince Charles Cinema and Picturehouse Cinemas, and has devised performances at the BFI Southbank, Holywell Music Room and Locarno Film Festival. He has been a visiting lecturer on improvisation and interdisciplinary practice at the Royal Birmingham Conservatoire.  \",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":90,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Young JW3: Improvisational Drawing\",\"instanceDates\":\"11 June-11 June\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"600001ALNDQTNHNLSQJNVPDQQGQLJPTLR\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-06-11T18:30:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-06-11T17:30:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-06-11T18:30:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-06-11T17:30:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Young Professionals\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Young JW3\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"Hugo Max\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false},{\"description\":\"6-9.50pm, £25/£30/£35  //  Shabbat x Mimouna: A Moroccan-inspired celebration!\\r\\n\\r\\nJoin us for a special Friday night dinner that blends the beauty of Shabbat with the joyful spirit of Mimouna, the traditional North African Jewish celebration that marks the end of Passover. We’ll enjoy Moroccan-style food with vibrant flavours, warm hospitality, and an atmosphere full of simcha as we move from matzah to mufleta and celebrate freedom, abundance, and togetherness.\\r\\n\\r\\nWhether you grew up with Mimouna or it’s your first time, all are welcome at the table.\\r\\n\\r\\n£25 - early bird (until 2nd March)\\r\\n£30 - general sale (until 30th March)\\r\\n£35 - last chance (until 14th April)\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":200,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Young JW3: Mimouna Friday Night Dinner\",\"instanceDates\":\"17 April-17 April\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"555201ABQVDCVBPMGTRTLBKNGRTPJSDQM\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-04-17T18:00:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-04-17T17:00:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-04-17T18:00:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-04-17T17:00:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Young Professionals\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Young JW3\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false},{\"description\":\"19:30 01/03/2026 £20 //\\r\\n\\r\\n \\r\\n \\\"Join Young JW3 for a stylish Purim cocktail party, honouring the festival’s spirit of hidden miracles and joyful surprises with some impressive close-up magic.\\r\\n\\r\\nWear your favourite black and white outfit (smart-casual dress code) and enjoy handcrafted drinks while mingling and soaking up the atmosphere. Our walkaround magician will be mixing in clever illusions throughout the night to keep things fun, mysterious, and delightfully unexpected.\\r\\n\\r\\nCelebrate the magic of Purim with us - a night where nothing is quite as it seems!\\r\\n\\\"\\r\\n\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":90,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Young JW3: Purim After Dark: Cocktails & Magic\",\"instanceDates\":\"1 March-1 March\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"554001AHPSTKJKQKKCHVNNJBJLKPTVPLM\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-03-01T19:30:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-03-01T19:30:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-03-01T19:30:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-03-01T19:30:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Young Professionals\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Young JW3\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false},{\"description\":\"14:00 26/04/2026 £6\\r\\n///\\r\\n \\r\\n\\\"Queer Café: A Sunday Social for LGBTQ+ Folks\\r\\n\\r\\nJoin us for a relaxed and friendly Sunday afternoon hangout at Queer Café - an open space for LGBTQ+ people across the spectrum to chat and unwind. Whether you’re coming solo or with friends, it’s a chance to enjoy a hot drink, meet like-minded people, and share easy conversation in a private, welcoming setting.\\r\\n\\r\\nStick around afterwards if you'd like to get creative at our Young JW3 Spring Crafternoon from 3-5pm [insert booking link] - no pressure, just a fun option to keep the good vibes going.\\r\\n\\r\\nCome as you are - we can’t wait to see you there!\\\"\\r\\n\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":60,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Young JW3: Queer Café\",\"instanceDates\":\"26 April-26 April\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"555601ACSSLDLPHPDTPKJCCPHQHMQKJGJ\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-04-26T14:00:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-04-26T13:00:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-04-26T14:00:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-04-26T13:00:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Young Professionals\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Young JW3\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false},{\"description\":\"6.30pm-9pm, £10 film / £16 film & pizza (regular or vegan) // Join us for our next queer pizza party and movie screening (But I'm a Cheerleader - 1999) in our Cinema!\\r\\n\\r\\nIn this cult classic satirical comedy, high school cheerleader Megan is sent to a conversion therapy camp when her parents suspect she might be a lesbian. At \\\"True Directions,\\\" she meets a group of quirky teens and begins to question everything she’s been told about love and identity. With its campy aesthetic and sharp wit, But I’m a Cheerleader is a bold, hilarious, and heartfelt celebration of queer self-discovery.\\r\\n\\r\\n6.30pm - Pizza party\\r\\n7.15pm - Film starts\\r\\n8.45pm - Film ends\\r\\n\\r\\nThis is a safe space for queer Jews, so whether you're queer or just happy to be here, come and join us!\\r\\n\\r\\nVegan pizza available upon request - please purchase the appropriate ticket.\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":150,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Young JW3: Queer Movie & Pizza Night: But I'm A Cheerleader\",\"instanceDates\":\"19 March-19 March\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"568601AVVDCNCQMDLCKCLDGBCDCGTKTQL\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-03-19T18:30:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-03-19T18:30:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-03-19T18:30:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-03-19T18:30:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Young Professionals\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Young JW3\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false},{\"description\":\"12:30 22/02/2026 £15 ////\\r\\n \\r\\n\\\"Join us for Tai Chi & Chai Tea, a unique wellness event designed to cultivate and harmonise mind and body through gentle and flowing movements. Begin with a warm cup of chai tea and social in our Café, then transition into a gentle Tai Chi Chaun taster session.\\r\\n\\r\\nImmerse yourself in the flowing, meditative movements of Tai Chi Chaun, an ancient Chinese art that promotes flexibility, coordination, strength, and balance. No prior experience is necessary - this session is for everyone! \\r\\n\\r\\nOur instructor, a member of the Tai Chi Union of Great Britain, will guide you through the basics in a welcoming and supportive environment. It's the perfect way to nourish both your body and mind while meeting new people.\\\"\\r\\n\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":90,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Young JW3: Tai Chi & Chai Tea\",\"instanceDates\":\"22 February-22 February\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"554602APRGHJLGBHGCRSTRVMDMBDVHLLM\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-02-22T12:30:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-02-22T12:30:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-02-22T12:30:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-02-22T12:30:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Young Professionals\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Young JW3\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"Shira Klasmer\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false},{\"description\":\"A creative Rosh Hashanah craft workshop centred around renewal, second chances and self-expression. Explore Jewish symbols in art, then carve your own printmaking designs to upcycle old clothes and accessories with fabric ink. No experience needed.\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":120,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Young JW3: The Art of Renewal: A Rosh Hashanah Printmaking & Upcycling Workshop\",\"instanceDates\":\"17 September-17 September\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"634001ALLRHHMMRVBBMQVNHVJVRGDJPSV\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-09-17T18:30:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-09-17T17:30:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-09-17T18:30:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-09-17T17:30:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false,\"attribute_Genre\":\"Young Professionals\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"Tal Paley\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\"},{\"description\":\"6pm // 20s and 30s // Celebrate Tu B’Shvat with a Friday Night Dinner rooted in tradition!\\r\\n\\r\\nJoin us for a special Shabbat dinner in honour of Tu B’Shvat, the Jewish New Year for trees. This festival marks the start of the growing season in Israel and invites us to reflect on our connection to the earth, renewal, and sustainability.\\r\\n\\r\\nWe’ll come together for a delicious, seasonal Friday night meal with meaningful conversation and a warm, welcoming atmosphere.\\r\\n\\r\\n£25 - early bird (until 4th Jan)\\r\\n£30 - general sale (until 19th Jan)\\r\\n£35 - last chance (until 27th Jan)\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":230,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Young JW3: Tu B'Shvat Friday Night Dinner\",\"instanceDates\":\"30 January-30 January\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"554601AMQRKRPSCSLNBNDTNHKHHSCTHBT\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-01-30T18:00:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-01-30T18:00:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-01-30T18:00:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-01-30T18:00:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Young Professionals\",\"attribute_Language\":\"English\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Young JW3\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false},{\"description\":\"7pm-10pm, £10, in building, 20s & 30s, Sunday 19 July 2026 // Watch the World Cup Final on the big screen in the JW3 cinema! ? Enjoy beers, snacks, and a friendly, social atmosphere - perfect for fans and friends to cheer, celebrate, and soak up the excitement together.\\r\\n\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":180,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Young JW3: World Cup Final Watch Party\",\"instanceDates\":\"19 July-19 July\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"597601AKBTDSRSKCKHLLMCMBNCRDVBGDJ\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-07-19T19:00:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-07-19T18:00:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-07-19T19:00:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-07-19T18:00:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Young Professionals\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Young JW3\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false},{\"description\":\"18:30 22/04/2026 £15\\r\\n ////\\r\\n\\r\\nJoin us for a lively, social evening celebrating Yom Ha’atzmaut, Israel’s Independence Day!\\r\\n \\r\\nKick things off with a high-energy Israeli folk dance class, led by Liat Oberlander from the Israeli Dance Institute. No matter your experience level, it’s a fun way to explore Israeli culture and move to joyful music.\\r\\n \\r\\nAfter the class, stay for drinks, nibbles, and a chance to soak up the atmosphere on the JW3 Piazza. We’ll keep the Israeli theme going with opportunities to hear and speak a little Hebrew while connecting with others. Open to everyone - whether you’re fluent, a beginner, or just curious.\\r\\n \\r\\nTimings\\r\\n6:30pm - Dance class (please arrive a few minutes early so we can start promptly)\\r\\n7:15pm - Drinks & nibbles\\r\\n\\r\\nWear comfy clothes and shoes, and bring a water bottle (which you can refill here).\\r\\n \\r\\nPlease contact gianina@jw3.org.uk as soon as possible if you have any dietary or access requirements.\\r\\n\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":105,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Young JW3: Yom Ha'atzmaut Israeli Dance Class\",\"instanceDates\":\"22 April-22 April\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"555401AGDBPGHVQJBHCSTQCNDPSMMLRGP\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-04-22T18:30:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-04-22T17:30:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-04-22T18:30:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-04-22T17:30:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_Genre\":\"Young Professionals\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"Young JW3\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false},{\"description\":\"19:00 // 21 Oct 2026 // £15 // Experience the boundary-blurring sound of ZOHARA at JW3 this October. Blending electronica with Middle Eastern textures, the Oi Va Voi frontwoman delivers an immersive, high-energy performance. pairing oud, darbuka and synths with emotional energy and fearless songwriting.\",\"htmlDescription\":\"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\"duration\":150,\"imageUrl\":\"\",\"isOnSale\":true,\"name\":\"Zohara\",\"instanceDates\":\"21 October-21 October\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"\",\"webEventId\":null,\"id\":\"632201ASKJBNTMGQHQVBSDRGCQMDQKGBM\",\"firstInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-10-21T19:00:00\",\"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-10-21T18:00:00Z\",\"lastInstanceDateTime\":\"2026-10-21T19:00:00\",\"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\":\"2026-10-21T18:00:00Z\",\"altText\":\"\",\"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\":false,\"attribute_Genre\":\"Music\",\"attribute_Language\":\"\",\"attribute_TessituraId\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\":\"\",\"attribute_GatedEventFree\":\"\",\"attribute_SeriesBooking\":\"\",\"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\":\"\"}]",
