          "content": {
            "mimeType": "application/json",
            "text": "{\n  \"description\": \"Exhibition on Screen were deeply saddened to hear of the death of brilliant artist David Hockney, who they worked closely with to make a film about his work back in 2017. As a tribute to David Hockney this film has been made theatrically available again at certain cinemas & galleries. Widely considered Britain’s most popular artist, David Hockney was a global sensation with exhibitions in London, New York, Paris and beyond, attracting millions of visitors worldwide. Featuring intimate and in-depth interviews with Hockney, this revealing film focuses on two blockbuster exhibitions held in 2012 and 2016 at the Royal Academy of Art in London. Director Phil Grabsky secured privileged access to craft this cinematic celebration of a 21st century master of creativity. Duration: 30 minutes Director: Phil Grabsky Year: 2017 https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=WGRjOzQ-S40\",\n  \"htmlDescription\": \"<div id>\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\",\n  \"duration\": 85,\n  \"imageUrl\": \"\",\n  \"isOnSale\": true,\n  \"name\": \"Exhibition on Screen: Remembering David Hockney\",\n  \"instanceDates\": \"3 July-16 July\",\n  \"thumbnailUrl\": \"\",\n  \"webEventId\": null,\n  \"id\": \"641802ANCGMMPMCJLDBVTGMKLKMCKDQJS\",\n  \"firstInstanceDateTime\": \"2026-07-03T14:00:00\",\n  \"firstInstanceDateTimeUtc\": \"2026-07-03T13:00:00Z\",\n  \"lastInstanceDateTime\": \"2026-07-16T16:00:00\",\n  \"lastInstanceDateTimeUtc\": \"2026-07-16T15:00:00Z\",\n  \"altText\": \"\",\n  \"attribute_CinemaMembershipExclusion\": false,\n  \"attribute_Genre\": \"Cinema\",\n  \"attribute_Language\": \"\",\n  \"attribute_TessituraId\": \"\",\n  \"attribute_SeriesOrFestival\": \"\",\n  \"attribute_GatedEventFree\": \"\",\n  \"attribute_SeriesBooking\": \"\",\n  \"attribute_TeacherOrLecturer\": \"\",\n  \"instances\": [\n    {\n      \"isOnSale\": true,\n      \"planId\": \"4401APLLPBSHLDJVTLGBDQTQBHJDJSHCM\",\n      \"priceList\": {\n        \"id\": \"148802AKTKTJGVTJVDRDBTJLHNRDT